одукты.","position":4,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l1","label":"a bottle of water"},{"id":"l2","label":"a loaf of bread"},{"id":"l3","label":"a kilo of rice"},{"id":"l4","label":"a cup of tea"}],"right":[{"id":"r1","label":"бутылка воды"},{"id":"r2","label":"буханка хлеба"},{"id":"r3","label":"килограмм риса"},{"id":"r4","label":"чашка чая"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l1":"r1","l2":"r2","l3":"r3","l4":"r4"}},"reference_answer":{"l1":"r1","l2":"r2","l3":"r3","l4":"r4"},"incorrect_answer":{"l1":"r2","l2":"r3","l3":"r4","l4":"r1"},"explanation":"Слова bottle, loaf, kilo и cup позволяют назвать измеримую порцию продукта."},{"id":"8dc23816-5451-5508-966c-55fe5ff2b349","lesson_id":"e9f8202e-a60b-5e65-a242-1d02190f8f83","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что ещё нужно купить для ужина?","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Milk."},{"id":"o2","label":"Eggs."},{"id":"o3","label":"Rice."}],"passage":"Maya checks the kitchen before she goes shopping. There are a few potatoes and plenty of rice, but there are no eggs. She writes eggs on her list. She does not buy any milk because there is enough in the fridge."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Яиц нет, и Maya записывает eggs в список. Риса и молока достаточно."},{"id":"fb63d6bf-a6a7-5b70-9991-b64459085da6","lesson_id":"e9f8202e-a60b-5e65-a242-1d02190f8f83","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь вопрос о количестве воды.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"How many water do you drink?"},"answer_key":{"accepted":["How much water do you drink?"]},"reference_answer":"How much water do you drink?","incorrect_answer":"How much tea do you drink?","explanation":"С неисчисляемым water нужно much. Tea изменило бы предмет вопроса."},{"id":"65fed62f-92b7-58fc-9b77-32a15fd171aa","lesson_id":"e9f8202e-a60b-5e65-a242-1d02190f8f83","kind":"response_choice","prompt":"Попроси чек после оплаты.","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The receipt is hungry."},{"id":"o2","label":"Could I have the receipt, please?"},{"id":"o3","label":"I am a receipt."}],"context":"That’s eight pounds. Thank you."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Receipt — чек; Could I have …? — вежливая просьба."},{"id":"a96908f6-fc0f-5550-ad86-057eccd3e859","lesson_id":"e9f8202e-a60b-5e65-a242-1d02190f8f83","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи сообщение о достаточном количестве.","position":8,"public_payload":{"source":"У нас достаточно хлеба."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["We have enough bread.","We've got enough bread."]},"reference_answer":"We have enough bread.","incorrect_answer":"We do not have any bread.","explanation":"Enough bread — достаточно хлеба; отрицание any bread означало бы, что хлеба нет."},{"id":"398fdfb2-6d28-5f52-86bd-eb24e6041c71","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Как сказать «У меня болит голова»?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"I do a headache."},{"id":"o2","label":"I am a headache."},{"id":"o3","label":"I have a headache."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"В стандартном выражении о головной боли используется have a headache."},{"id":"c2e1b424-6058-5e9b-a8be-a1e6700aeaab","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери грамматически правильный совет уставшему человеку.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"should resting"},{"id":"o2","label":"should to rest"},{"id":"o3","label":"should rest"}],"sentence":"You look tired. You ___."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"После should нужна начальная форма без to."},{"id":"d5ae73af-cc6b-515b-9830-682f37d88bbc","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни просьбу записать на приём.","position":3,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I would like to make an ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["appointment"]},"reference_answer":"appointment","incorrect_answer":"apartment","explanation":"Appointment — запись на приём; apartment — квартира."},{"id":"107f1890-1aa1-5ba6-b250-4b65ff05e51f","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери ответ на вопрос о самочувствии.","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"I feel a little better, thanks."},{"id":"o2","label":"It costs six pounds."},{"id":"o3","label":"I am at seven o’clock."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Friend","text":"How are you feeling today?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Вопрос о самочувствии требует ответа о состоянии, а не цене или времени."},{"id":"d7cccb16-d57a-5a58-9c45-46373ce42882","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"reading","prompt":"Когда назначен приём Норы?","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Tuesday at twelve."},{"id":"o2","label":"Tuesday at ten."},{"id":"o3","label":"Monday at ten."}],"passage":"Nora feels unwell and calls the clinic. She asks for an appointment on Monday, but there are no free times that day. The receptionist offers Tuesday at ten. Nora accepts and writes the time in her diary."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Она принимает предложение Tuesday at ten, хотя сначала спрашивает о понедельнике."},{"id":"1011b695-9fef-50df-b91c-5fbeec7c6dfa","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи описание состояния.","position":6,"public_payload":{"source":"Сегодня я чувствую себя лучше."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I feel better today.","I am feeling better today."]},"reference_answer":"I feel better today.","incorrect_answer":"I feel worse today.","explanation":"Better — лучше; worse означает хуже и меняет смысл."},{"id":"71955c2a-e980-5d1f-bbac-a3bc42c758ca","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Составь вежливую просьбу о записи на приём.","position":7,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"appointment,"},{"id":"t2","label":"make"},{"id":"t3","label":"an"},{"id":"t4","label":"I"},{"id":"t5","label":"Can"},{"id":"t6","label":"please?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t5","t4","t2","t3","t1","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t5","t4","t2","t3","t1","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t4","t2","t3","t1","t6","t5"],"explanation":"Make an appointment — записаться на приём; Can I …, please? — вежливая просьба."},{"id":"2976a21a-7c60-5eec-b24b-4aefdafdc781","lesson_id":"09e339df-4a4e-5484-9797-0e4640e6d1aa","kind":"unit_test","prompt":"Повтори грамматику и ситуации уровня A2.","position":8,"public_payload":{"questions":[{"id":"q1","prompt":"Какой вопрос о вчерашнем дне верен?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Did you go out yesterday?"},{"id":"o2","label":"Did you went out yesterday?"}]},{"id":"q2","prompt":"Как спросить количество молока?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"How many milk?"},{"id":"o2","label":"How much milk?"}]},{"id":"q3","prompt":"Как выразить запланированное намерение?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"We are going to travel."},{"id":"o2","label":"We going travel."}]}]},"answer_key":{"answers":{"q1":"o1","q2":"o2","q3":"o1"},"explanations":{"q1":"После did используется go.","q2":"Milk неисчисляемое: much.","q3":"Нужна полная конструкция are going to travel."}},"reference_answer":{"q1":"o1","q2":"o2","q3":"o1"},"incorrect_answer":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o2","q3":"o1"},"explanation":"Контрольный блок засчитывается при всех верных ответах. Разбор каждого вопроса показан отдельно."},{"id":"2f0992cd-0996-55cf-a869-2eab56349a23","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"tenses","prompt":"Выбери форму для вопроса о жизненном опыте.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Did you ever went"},{"id":"o2","label":"Have you ever been"},{"id":"o3","label":"Are you ever been"}],"sentence":"___ to Scotland?"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Have you ever been …? спрашивает, случалось ли бывать в месте, без конкретной даты."},{"id":"10ab2778-fceb-595c-8e5f-bc41729731ca","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"tenses","prompt":"Выбери форму с завершённым периодом last year.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"visited"},{"id":"o2","label":"have been visiting"},{"id":"o3","label":"have visited"}],"sentence":"I ___ Edinburgh last year."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Last year — законченный период, поэтому visited."},{"id":"41feebfb-f5a5-57a8-b55e-4ccabcd4299f","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово, означающее «никогда».","position":3,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I have ___ tried surfing, but I would like to."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["never"]},"reference_answer":"never","incorrect_answer":"already","explanation":"Never отрицает наличие опыта. Already означало бы, что опыт уже есть."},{"id":"1a333346-b17d-5eba-8d74-805b563d6e17","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи сообщение об уже выполненной работе.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Я уже отправил письмо."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I have already sent the email.","I've already sent the email."]},"reference_answer":"I have already sent the email.","incorrect_answer":"I have not sent the email yet.","explanation":"Already подчёркивает, что письмо уже отправлено; not … yet означало бы обратное."},{"id":"615f05dd-598c-5ead-8d7e-63023b655c64","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какой вывод об опыте Марты соответствует тексту?","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"She stopped working for the company three years ago."},{"id":"o2","label":"She visited Japan last spring."},{"id":"o3","label":"The Tokyo trip would be her first visit to Japan."}],"passage":"Marta has worked for a small travel company for three years. She has visited several countries for work, but she has never been to Japan. Last spring she spent a week in Italy. Her manager has just offered her a trip to Tokyo, and she is looking forward to her first visit."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Она never been to Japan и ждёт first visit. Last spring относится к Италии."},{"id":"b5e7f13a-31a0-5f91-88cc-d43a6944affd","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери ответ о конкретной дате опыта.","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"I have never taken one."},{"id":"o2","label":"I took one last summer."},{"id":"o3","label":"I have taken one yesterday."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Ali","text":"Have you ever taken a night train?"},{"speaker":"Bea","text":"Yes, I have."},{"speaker":"Ali","text":"When did you take it?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"После уточнения When …? и last summer нужен Past Simple: took."},{"id":"6c83e81d-4928-5e6e-a752-884da50caf9f","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь время, сохранив указание yesterday.","position":7,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I have finished the report yesterday."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I finished the report yesterday."]},"reference_answer":"I finished the report yesterday.","incorrect_answer":"I have finished the report already.","explanation":"Yesterday требует Past Simple. В корректном ответе сохраняется исходное обстоятельство."},{"id":"465c4336-f33b-50b9-bcea-b31e64f195f3","lesson_id":"56b186bb-4b11-539e-b5b2-f46b7d853676","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Собери вопрос «Ты когда-нибудь жил за границей?»","position":8,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"abroad?"},{"id":"t2","label":"you"},{"id":"t3","label":"lived"},{"id":"t4","label":"Have"},{"id":"t5","label":"ever"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t4","t2","t5","t3","t1"]},"reference_answer":["t4","t2","t5","t3","t1"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t5","t3","t1","t4"],"explanation":"В Present Perfect have стоит перед подлежащим, lived — после ever."},{"id":"b3e2affb-fc4e-545a-8fe9-915e4beb99c5","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Дополни реальное условие о погоде.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"rains"},{"id":"o2","label":"would rain"},{"id":"o3","label":"will rain"}],"sentence":"If it ___ tomorrow, we will stay indoors."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"В придаточном с if для реального будущего нужен Present Simple: rains."},{"id":"ebe932d8-f15b-5e79-a449-6eaf286ac6dd","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни главное предложение о возможной задержке.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If the train is late, we ___ call you."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["will"]},"reference_answer":"will","incorrect_answer":"would","explanation":"Will call — ожидаемое действие при реальном будущем условии."},{"id":"b8a25fb0-b08b-5c8e-af26-d6219e915394","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Какой смысл у Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"If you hurry, you will miss the bus."},{"id":"o2","label":"You missed the bus because you hurried."},{"id":"o3","label":"If you do not hurry, you will miss the bus."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Unless = if not. Это условие будущего, а не сообщение о прошлом."},{"id":"d12c1cd0-957b-5d8c-9906-55790f279db9","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что группа сделает при отмене лодочной экскурсии?","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"They will take the boat even in strong wind."},{"id":"o2","label":"They will lose all their money."},{"id":"o3","label":"They will visit the science museum."}],"passage":"A group of friends has booked a boat trip for Saturday. The company says the trip will go ahead unless the wind is too strong. If it is cancelled, the group will receive a refund. They have agreed to visit the science museum instead, so the day will not be wasted."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Запасной план прямо указан: visit the science museum instead; при отмене будет refund."},{"id":"f55f1740-02cc-587d-a633-8289f99cfa56","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи реальное условие о билете.","position":5,"public_payload":{"source":"Если я найду билет, я тебе позвоню."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["If I find a ticket, I will call you.","If I find a ticket, I'll call you."]},"reference_answer":"If I find a ticket, I will call you.","incorrect_answer":"If I found a ticket, I would call you.","explanation":"Find + will call описывает реальную будущую возможность; found + would меняет тип условия."},{"id":"3ca70ed4-abf8-5a02-a0ae-1a182370160e","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Предложи запасной план.","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"We already went next week."},{"id":"o2","label":"If it cancelled yesterday, we go tomorrow."},{"id":"o3","label":"If it is cancelled, we can go to the cinema."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Dan","text":"The outdoor concert may be cancelled."},{"speaker":"Lia","text":"What shall we do if that happens?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"If it is cancelled задаёт реальное условие; can предлагает возможный вариант действий."},{"id":"2fecdb60-3682-50f5-8862-0f1b2ac7c197","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь форму после unless.","position":7,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Unless you will leave now, you will be late."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Unless you leave now, you will be late."]},"reference_answer":"Unless you leave now, you will be late.","incorrect_answer":"Unless you leave now, you will not be late.","explanation":"После unless в таком условии нужен Present Simple. Отрицание в главной части изменило бы смысл."},{"id":"3f113ebd-4876-5eec-8dab-5ad1e25c2cb1","lesson_id":"0f24909a-f2ba-55ee-b85d-2dec43be12e3","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери оба корректных реальных условия.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"We will wait unless you call."},{"id":"o2","label":"If I see Maya, I will tell her."},{"id":"o3","label":"If I will see Maya, I will tell her."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o1","o2"]},"reference_answer":["o2","o1"],"incorrect_answer":["o3"],"explanation":"После if/unless о реальном будущем используем Present Simple, а не will."},{"id":"b16f5792-5a85-5524-90d1-89191ed74a1f","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"response_choice","prompt":"Выбери вежливый ответ на запрос коллеги.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Why you not do it yesterday?"},{"id":"o2","label":"I am a report."},{"id":"o3","label":"Certainly. I will send it this afternoon."}],"context":"Could you send me the updated report, please?"},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Certainly + конкретный срок отвечает на вежливую просьбу по делу."},{"id":"41651201-ace2-5ca7-b7e4-7f6a926c1c43","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь относительное местоимение для человека.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The colleague ___ helped me works in sales."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["who","that"]},"reference_answer":"who","incorrect_answer":"which","explanation":"Who или that может относиться к человеку; which обычно относится к предмету."},{"id":"f11483d5-9b23-5e6d-9971-2a0c1d9881b1","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово о документе в электронном письме.","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"platform"},{"id":"o2","label":"attachment"},{"id":"o3","label":"appointment"}],"sentence":"Please see the ___ for the updated timetable."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Attachment — вложение в письмо."},{"id":"2d563b6a-ad20-51de-b5d4-0c5c08d72371","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что адресат должен подтвердить?","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Whether the room should be changed."},{"id":"o2","label":"Whether the workshop can start an hour later."},{"id":"o3","label":"Whether Tuesday is convenient for the team."}],"passage":"Hello Priya, I have attached the revised schedule for next week’s workshop. We have moved the opening session from Monday to Tuesday because the speaker is travelling on Monday. Could you confirm that the new date is convenient for your team? The room and the start time remain unchanged. Best wishes, Owen."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Просят подтвердить удобство новой даты. Комната и время начала не меняются."},{"id":"303895ba-6603-5432-88d2-8a89a028215b","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери запрос «Могли бы вы подтвердить срок сдачи?»","position":5,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"Could"},{"id":"t2","label":"the"},{"id":"t3","label":"you"},{"id":"t4","label":"please?"},{"id":"t5","label":"confirm"},{"id":"t6","label":"deadline,"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t3","t5","t2","t6","t4"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t3","t5","t2","t6","t4"],"incorrect_answer":["t3","t5","t2","t6","t4","t1"],"explanation":"Could you confirm …, please? — вежливый запрос уточнения."},{"id":"b8ae8c88-ec0a-5aff-99cf-35fb9b86a375","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи сообщение о приложенном документе.","position":6,"public_payload":{"source":"Я приложил документ, который вам нужен."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I have attached the document that you need.","I have attached the document which you need."]},"reference_answer":"I have attached the document that you need.","incorrect_answer":"I have deleted the document that you need.","explanation":"Attached — приложил, а не deleted. Для документа допустимы that и which."},{"id":"2834e912-ab1d-5cdc-8459-a9741ea870b9","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"error_identification","prompt":"Найди неверное относительное местоимение.","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"yesterday"},{"id":"o2","label":"helped"},{"id":"o3","label":"which"}],"sentence":"The person which helped me yesterday is my manager."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"О человеке, который помог, говорят who/that helped me."},{"id":"d5289ae9-9d1f-5ac7-abc2-b31a65e90f80","lesson_id":"34070c74-c481-5c27-94f6-d42ea8c572a9","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери близкое по смыслу слово для confirm в контексте договорённости.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"cancel"},{"id":"o2","label":"verify"},{"id":"o3","label":"ignore"}],"word":"confirm","relation":"synonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Confirm и verify могут означать подтвердить/проверить достоверность; cancel — отменить."},{"id":"f316308c-7d5f-5a5d-8df1-301494298f16","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"tenses","prompt":"Выбери фоновое действие в прошлом.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"have walked"},{"id":"o2","label":"walked every day"},{"id":"o3","label":"was walking"}],"sentence":"I ___ home when my phone rang."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Was walking описывает процесс, во время которого зазвонил телефон."},{"id":"d9d3197c-033f-5360-9f18-185079747350","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь прошедшую форму be для they.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"They ___ waiting outside when the doors opened."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["were"]},"reference_answer":"were","incorrect_answer":"was","explanation":"С they используется were в Past Continuous."},{"id":"a4694d90-be20-58ee-8c06-f1bc209c85b0","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему Эмма сначала не заметила остановку автобуса?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"She had already left the bus."},{"id":"o2","label":"She was talking to the driver the whole time."},{"id":"o3","label":"She was looking at a message on her phone."}],"passage":"Emma was travelling home after a long day. She was reading a message on her phone while the bus was moving through the town centre. When she looked up, she realised that the bus had stopped at a different place because the usual road was closed. She asked the driver how to reach her street."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"В начале Emma was reading a message, поэтому не следила за остановкой."},{"id":"4e7f1ace-257f-54d3-9c8f-1d16c15af9de","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Собери описание прерванного действия.","position":4,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"I"},{"id":"t2","label":"lights"},{"id":"t3","label":"when"},{"id":"t4","label":"was"},{"id":"t5","label":"cooking"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"out."},{"id":"t8","label":"went"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t4","t5","t3","t6","t2","t8","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t4","t5","t3","t6","t2","t8","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t4","t5","t3","t6","t2","t8","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Was cooking — фон; went out — краткое событие, прервавшее его."},{"id":"dbfb4593-879b-56a2-adaa-07bd519bcdf1","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь фоновую форму прошедшего времени.","position":5,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We was having lunch when she arrived."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["We were having lunch when she arrived."]},"reference_answer":"We were having lunch when she arrived.","incorrect_answer":"We are having lunch when she arrives.","explanation":"После we нужна were; обе части остаются в прошлом."},{"id":"85650a55-121c-504a-a74f-6500c4a64a5f","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери объяснение того, что происходило в момент звонка.","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"I will take a shower tomorrow."},{"id":"o2","label":"I take a shower every day."},{"id":"o3","label":"I was taking a shower."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Mum","text":"Why didn’t you answer the phone at eight?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Was taking описывает процесс в указанный прошлый момент."},{"id":"2b875bec-f775-5403-b99d-aadb56f3ec10","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи фразу о двух одновременных действиях в прошлом.","position":7,"public_payload":{"source":"Пока я готовил, она читала."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["While I was cooking, she was reading.","She was reading while I was cooking."]},"reference_answer":"While I was cooking, she was reading.","incorrect_answer":"While I am cooking, she is reading.","explanation":"Оба процесса относятся к прошлому: was cooking и was reading."},{"id":"80cedade-0997-57eb-bae6-6710c9d8c1bc","lesson_id":"129e7446-e579-576a-9cce-c4e324ef708f","kind":"word_review","prompt":"Повтори значение слова suddenly в рассказе.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"обычно"},{"id":"o2","label":"заранее"},{"id":"o3","label":"вдруг"}],"word":"suddenly"},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Suddenly обозначает неожиданное появление события."},{"id":"fe2763d6-003a-5e16-8af4-664f33d24fa7","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери глагол о присмотре за ребёнком.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"look for"},{"id":"o2","label":"look after"},{"id":"o3","label":"look up"}],"sentence":"Could you ___ my little brother while I am out?"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Look after — присматривать, заботиться; look for означало бы искать."},{"id":"04de69aa-2638-5eaa-bed3-1b5b4d99d2f2","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"matching","prompt":"Сопоставь фразовые глаголы и значения.","position":2,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l1","label":"give up"},{"id":"l2","label":"find out"},{"id":"l3","label":"turn off"},{"id":"l4","label":"pick up"}],"right":[{"id":"r1","label":"забрать, подобрать"},{"id":"r2","label":"бросить занятие"},{"id":"r3","label":"выяснить"},{"id":"r4","label":"выключить"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l1":"r2","l2":"r3","l3":"r4","l4":"r1"}},"reference_answer":{"l1":"r2","l2":"r3","l3":"r4","l4":"r1"},"incorrect_answer":{"l1":"r3","l2":"r4","l3":"r1","l4":"r2"},"explanation":"Фразовые глаголы нужно понимать в контексте; здесь pick up — забрать человека или предмет."},{"id":"7c7a76da-87dc-5ab6-84bd-8d4e0414e8c7","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему Зак позвонил в офис?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"To give up his job."},{"id":"o2","label":"To ask someone to look after a child."},{"id":"o3","label":"To check if he could collect the parcel at six."}],"passage":"Zack was going to pick up a parcel after work. Before leaving, he found out that the collection office had changed its opening hours. He called to check whether it would still be open at six. The employee explained that it closed at five, so Zack arranged to collect the parcel the next morning."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Он уточняет часы работы, чтобы забрать посылку. Остальные значения не соответствуют ситуации."},{"id":"b00887a3-9a02-5a15-a788-71da668ae1f9","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Какое предложение с местоимением правильно?","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Please it turn off."},{"id":"o2","label":"Please turn it off."},{"id":"o3","label":"Please turn off it."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"В отделяемом turn off местоимение it ставится между глаголом и частицей."},{"id":"f7fbbfaf-d0e3-5076-9823-b7d166d94ddb","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи обещание заботиться о кошке.","position":5,"public_payload":{"source":"Я присмотрю за твоей кошкой."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I will look after your cat.","I'll take care of your cat."]},"reference_answer":"I will look after your cat.","incorrect_answer":"I will look for your cat.","explanation":"Look after / take care of означает заботиться; look for — искать, это другой смысл."},{"id":"262a85de-d388-559c-be87-a3efe48345bf","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"dictation","prompt":"Запиши вопрос о том, что удалось выяснить.","position":6,"public_payload":{"text":"Did you find out the answer?","lang":"en-US"},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Did you find out the answer?"]},"reference_answer":"Did you find out the answer?","incorrect_answer":"Did you give up the answer?","explanation":"Find out the answer — выяснить ответ; замена на give up не передаёт исходный смысл."},{"id":"d4ed7bf1-8e56-5ce7-9572-384cbcd1adc4","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"response_choice","prompt":"Ответь на просьбу выключить свет.","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Sure, I will turn it off."},{"id":"o2","label":"Sure, I will look it after."},{"id":"o3","label":"Sure, I found it tomorrow."}],"context":"Could you turn off the light before you leave?"},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Turn it off — корректная конструкция с местоимением it."},{"id":"3897e7a3-6636-56bd-824d-3df7de11bd87","lesson_id":"ff4a54ea-65f9-5ee9-96cb-975bddcb7240","kind":"unit_test","prompt":"Проверь опыт, условия и связность речи B1.","position":8,"public_payload":{"questions":[{"id":"q1","prompt":"Выбери форму с yesterday.","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"I have seen her yesterday."},{"id":"o2","label":"I saw her yesterday."}]},{"id":"q2","prompt":"Выбери реальное условие о будущем.","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"If I get home early, I will call."},{"id":"o2","label":"If I will get home early, I call."}]},{"id":"q3","prompt":"Какой вариант о заботе верен?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"She looks after her grandmother."},{"id":"o2","label":"She looks up her grandmother every day."}]}]},"answer_key":{"answers":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o1","q3":"o1"},"explanations":{"q1":"Завершённое время yesterday требует Past Simple.","q2":"В if-части используется Present Simple.","q3":"Look after выражает заботу в этом контексте."}},"reference_answer":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o1","q3":"o1"},"incorrect_answer":{"q1":"o1","q2":"o1","q3":"o1"},"explanation":"Контрольный блок засчитывается при всех верных ответах. Разбор каждого вопроса показан отдельно."},{"id":"e7c79939-bb27-50fb-bbe9-c3fd409ffda6","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"tenses","prompt":"Выбери форму для альтернативного прошлого.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"would know"},{"id":"o2","label":"had known"},{"id":"o3","label":"have known"}],"sentence":"If I ___ about the meeting, I would have attended."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Для нереального условия в прошлом нужен Past Perfect: had known."},{"id":"b02abc8d-3d50-5071-b8d0-b290e4615c31","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни следствие нереальной ситуации в настоящем.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If I lived closer, I ___ walk to work."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["would"]},"reference_answer":"would","incorrect_answer":"will","explanation":"Would walk выражает гипотетическое следствие; will описывало бы другой тип условия."},{"id":"5ffd019e-fe07-5258-ad64-c47b52a60359","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какой вывод о подаче заявки следует из текста?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"He did not apply because he misunderstood the eligibility rules."},{"id":"o2","label":"He submitted a project but the judges rejected it."},{"id":"o3","label":"The text proves that he would have won."}],"passage":"When a design competition was announced, Felix decided not to apply because he assumed that only experienced professionals were eligible. After the deadline, he discovered that students could enter too. He had a strong project ready and now regrets not checking the rules. He says that, if he had read them carefully, he would have submitted his work. There is no suggestion that his project would definitely have won."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Он не подавал заявку из-за неверного предположения. Возможность участия не гарантирует победу."},{"id":"bc26afa3-a9f4-57cb-8211-996d5eeb2412","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи нереальное условие о настоящем.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Если бы у меня было больше времени, я бы чаще путешествовал."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["If I had more time, I would travel more often.","I would travel more often if I had more time."]},"reference_answer":"If I had more time, I would travel more often.","incorrect_answer":"If I have more time, I will travel more often.","explanation":"Had + would travel выражает гипотезу о настоящем; have + will — реальную будущую возможность."},{"id":"0f562809-7c32-53f4-9b9b-5f87efe3dfc7","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь if-часть альтернативного прошлого.","position":5,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If she would have left earlier, she would have caught the train."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["If she had left earlier, she would have caught the train."]},"reference_answer":"If she had left earlier, she would have caught the train.","incorrect_answer":"If she leaves earlier, she will catch the train.","explanation":"В if-части third conditional нужен had left, не would have left. Время события сохраняется прошлым."},{"id":"e0e4710e-c8b8-5eba-ba58-c8c7b4a8b458","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"response_choice","prompt":"Ответь гипотетическим советом о нынешней ситуации.","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"If I am you, I asked yesterday."},{"id":"o2","label":"If I were you, I would ask for clarification."},{"id":"o3","label":"If I had known yesterday, I would have asked."}],"context":"I do not understand the new instructions. What should I do now?"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"If I were you, I would … — стандартный гипотетический совет здесь и сейчас."},{"id":"9184e9aa-0c79-537d-84d9-1c1962c45f94","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Собери альтернативное следствие прошлого.","position":7,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"had"},{"id":"t2","label":"earlier"},{"id":"t3","label":"have"},{"id":"t4","label":"We"},{"id":"t5","label":"would"},{"id":"t6","label":"we"},{"id":"t7","label":"arrived"},{"id":"t8","label":"taxi."},{"id":"t9","label":"a"},{"id":"t10","label":"taken"},{"id":"t11","label":"if"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t4","t5","t3","t7","t2","t11","t6","t1","t10","t9","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t4","t5","t3","t7","t2","t11","t6","t1","t10","t9","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t5","t3","t7","t2","t11","t6","t1","t10","t9","t8","t4"],"explanation":"Would have arrived сочетается с had taken для альтернативного прошлого."},{"id":"1b496974-1cca-58a8-ae2b-89c41282180a","lesson_id":"0c184e75-e4af-5511-b8f8-5d92ec0403b5","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два корректных нереальных условия.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"If I would know, I would tell you."},{"id":"o2","label":"If he had called, I would have answered."},{"id":"o3","label":"If I were taller, I could reach the shelf."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o2","o3"]},"reference_answer":["o3","o2"],"incorrect_answer":["o1"],"explanation":"Первые два примера корректно разделяют условие и следствие; would обычно не ставится в такой if-части."},{"id":"121665b5-26a1-5609-b852-3636940b8b75","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Как грамматически передать «Считается, что компания прибыльна»?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The company believes to be profitable."},{"id":"o2","label":"The company is believe profitable."},{"id":"o3","label":"The company is believed to be profitable."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Reporting passive: is believed + to be. Это сообщение об убеждении, а не гарантия прибыли."},{"id":"9e01d248-0218-5d6c-a2c7-417be7272678","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни передачу сообщения об открытии здания.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The new centre is expected ___ open in June."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["to"]},"reference_answer":"to","incorrect_answer":"for","explanation":"После is expected для действия используется инфинитив с to."},{"id":"0dd6709e-a1a1-5acc-b3ea-c7ca51347e21","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что читатель вправе считать подтверждённым?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The town has definitely been selected."},{"id":"o2","label":"The company is considering possible locations."},{"id":"o3","label":"Construction will certainly start next month."}],"passage":"A local newspaper reports that a manufacturer may open a new plant near the town. The company has confirmed that it is examining several possible locations, but it has not announced a final decision. The council says the project could create jobs if it goes ahead. An anonymous source claims that construction will begin next month, yet no planning application has been published. The article therefore distinguishes official statements from an unverified prediction."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Официально подтверждено только рассмотрение площадок. Срок строительства приписан анонимному источнику и не проверен."},{"id":"402a4448-0126-521f-93c9-0ddeaa255e51","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи сообщение, сохранив его осторожный характер.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Сообщается, что проект задерживается."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The project is reported to be delayed.","It is reported that the project is delayed."]},"reference_answer":"The project is reported to be delayed.","incorrect_answer":"The project is definitely cancelled.","explanation":"Reported передаёт источник сообщения; definitely cancelled добавляет неподтверждённую отмену."},{"id":"131cf282-730a-52e3-aa54-eeafd24cb710","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, которое явно указывает на источник сообщения.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"reportedly"},{"id":"o2","label":"personally"},{"id":"o3","label":"certainly"}],"sentence":"The director has ___ resigned, although the company has not confirmed the news."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Reportedly — по сообщениям; certainly выражает уверенность, а personally — личную позицию."},{"id":"08ec99a7-0952-569d-8a30-a6a673a10146","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь форму пассива.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The decision was announce yesterday."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The decision was announced yesterday."]},"reference_answer":"The decision was announced yesterday.","incorrect_answer":"The decision will be announced tomorrow.","explanation":"Пассив прошедшего времени: was + announced. Нельзя менять yesterday на tomorrow."},{"id":"bcf98d9b-d8b2-570e-824a-2464bac24016","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери сообщение о предполагаемом прошлом событии.","position":7,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"He"},{"id":"t2","label":"the"},{"id":"t3","label":"have"},{"id":"t4","label":"left"},{"id":"t5","label":"said"},{"id":"t6","label":"country."},{"id":"t7","label":"to"},{"id":"t8","label":"is"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t8","t5","t7","t3","t4","t2","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t8","t5","t7","t3","t4","t2","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t8","t5","t7","t3","t4","t2","t6","t1"],"explanation":"To have left показывает, что предполагаемое отбытие предшествует нынешнему сообщению."},{"id":"dbd57a48-54ee-5592-9fc3-0d47d6f12670","lesson_id":"f3d5e543-c83d-5ae9-a85c-d320eb8c55b1","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери антоним confirm в контексте истинности утверждения.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"refute"},{"id":"o2","label":"corroborate"},{"id":"o3","label":"verify"}],"word":"confirm","relation":"antonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Refute — опровергать; verify и corroborate направлены на проверку или подтверждение."},{"id":"cd5ee355-8db5-57ac-bc24-b733f6ded14d","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери связку перед существительным the cost.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Although"},{"id":"o2","label":"Despite"},{"id":"o3","label":"Because"}],"sentence":"___ the cost, the training was useful."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Despite the cost — несмотря на стоимость; although требовало бы полноценного придаточного."},{"id":"bb2933b7-cb89-52ec-84e0-75eb9bc5cb18","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь although в придаточное уступки.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"___ the system is faster, it is not easier to use."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Although","although"]},"reference_answer":"Although","incorrect_answer":"Despite","explanation":"После although следует the system is faster; despite в такой структуре не подходит."},{"id":"75ae5090-e2c3-54da-a2a5-47dc675da76c","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какой вывод лучше всего отражает позицию автора?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Remote-working policies should reflect the requirements of different roles."},{"id":"o2","label":"Remote work has no advantages."},{"id":"o3","label":"Every employee should work from home permanently."}],"passage":"Working from home can reduce commuting time and allow employees to organise some tasks more flexibly. However, these advantages do not remove every difficulty. New staff may find it harder to learn informally from colleagues, and some roles require access to equipment at the workplace. A policy that works for an experienced designer may not suit a laboratory assistant. The writer therefore favours decisions based on the needs of a role rather than a single rule for everyone."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Автор признаёт плюсы и ограничения и предлагает учитывать требования роли, а не универсальное правило."},{"id":"32f5ddf6-e184-57c7-b2ac-a2b3cbadbdea","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи уступку, сохранив обе идеи.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Хотя решение дорогое, оно может сэкономить время."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Although the solution is expensive, it may save time.","The solution may save time although it is expensive."]},"reference_answer":"Although the solution is expensive, it may save time.","incorrect_answer":"Because the solution is cheap, it will always save time.","explanation":"Although выражает уступку; may сохраняет возможность, а не гарантию результата."},{"id":"cc5caea5-bb1d-518e-b2ba-749a9224d6a2","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два осторожных, не абсолютных утверждения.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The results suggest a possible improvement."},{"id":"o2","label":"The change may benefit some teams."},{"id":"o3","label":"The change will solve every problem without exception."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o1","o2"]},"reference_answer":["o2","o1"],"incorrect_answer":["o3"],"explanation":"May, some и suggest a possible ограничивают вывод. Every problem without exception необоснованно абсолютно."},{"id":"50475cfd-3ce7-586a-853b-f61d469b5ae1","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"response_choice","prompt":"Сформулируй конструктивное возражение на совещании.","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"That may be true, but we should also consider the cost."},{"id":"o2","label":"There are no costs in any project."},{"id":"o3","label":"You are always wrong about everything."}],"context":"This software will make the team more efficient."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Первый ответ признаёт возможную правоту собеседника и добавляет конкретный аспект."},{"id":"dd7af806-7d81-5916-9ce9-88adb6d12823","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь структуру с despite, сохранив уступку.","position":7,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Despite it was raining, we continued the survey."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Although it was raining, we continued the survey.","Despite the rain, we continued the survey."]},"reference_answer":"Although it was raining, we continued the survey.","incorrect_answer":"Because it was raining, we cancelled the survey.","explanation":"Допустимы although + придаточное и despite + существительное. Continued нельзя заменять cancelled."},{"id":"0c0a6b62-d3c0-5748-8865-822b6d558de6","lesson_id":"cbd16cfa-daf2-5b00-a00f-73ae3d170d55","kind":"word_review","prompt":"Повтори значение drawback при обсуждении решения.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"недостаток"},{"id":"o2","label":"разрешение"},{"id":"o3","label":"гарантия"}],"word":"drawback"},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Drawback — недостаток или отрицательная сторона решения."},{"id":"d38e8e61-03e3-5fb1-8b59-d36e3e8652fb","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери конструкцию вероятного, но не уверенного объяснения.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"must miss"},{"id":"o2","label":"can’t missing"},{"id":"o3","label":"might have missed"}],"sentence":"She has not replied. She ___ the message."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Might have missed допускает, что человек пропустил сообщение, не утверждая это наверняка."},{"id":"eb21c6ce-88f8-54e9-b43b-6fd0e868ca6f","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни сильный вывод о прошлом.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The ground is wet. It must ___ rained."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["have"]},"reference_answer":"have","incorrect_answer":"has","explanation":"После must о прошлом используется have + причастие, а не has."},{"id":"e2b833af-abb9-5904-b249-6aa90a899a32","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему автор допускает несколько объяснений?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The available clues do not establish a single certain explanation."},{"id":"o2","label":"An empty room always means a meeting was cancelled."},{"id":"o3","label":"The cups prove that no meeting took place."}],"passage":"When Karim returned to the office, the meeting room was empty and the lights were off. He initially assumed that the meeting had been cancelled. Then he noticed that the chairs had been rearranged and there were used cups on the table. The meeting might already have finished, or the group could have moved to another room. Karim decided to check the calendar and ask a colleague rather than treat his first assumption as a fact."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Признаки допускают несколько версий, поэтому Karim решает уточнить, а не объявить первую догадку фактом."},{"id":"1570e65a-48ad-5ccd-b560-fb61bb07faca","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Что означает He can’t have written this yesterday?","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"He was not allowed to write anything yesterday."},{"id":"o2","label":"He will probably write it tomorrow."},{"id":"o3","label":"The speaker believes it was impossible for him to write it yesterday."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Can’t have written — вывод о невозможности события в прошлом, не запрет."},{"id":"18d7ce89-6364-5d3b-a7f7-2dfaa7f7241d","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи осторожное предположение.","position":5,"public_payload":{"source":"Возможно, они забыли о встрече."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["They might have forgotten about the meeting.","They may have forgotten about the meeting."]},"reference_answer":"They might have forgotten about the meeting.","incorrect_answer":"They definitely cancelled the meeting.","explanation":"Might/may have forgotten сохраняет предположение; definitely cancelled добавляет уверенность и другой факт."},{"id":"24a486c0-e1a1-5f11-82aa-ceb3d792a75e","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Собери сильный вывод о потерянном ключе.","position":6,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"your"},{"id":"t2","label":"must"},{"id":"t3","label":"You"},{"id":"t4","label":"key"},{"id":"t5","label":"left"},{"id":"t6","label":"have"},{"id":"t7","label":"at"},{"id":"t8","label":"home."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t3","t2","t6","t5","t1","t4","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t3","t2","t6","t5","t1","t4","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t6","t5","t1","t4","t7","t8","t3"],"explanation":"Must have left — вывод о том, что произошло раньше."},{"id":"b9dc0db7-c96e-58b6-bf1b-ba71374352ec","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь конструкцию вывода о прошлом.","position":7,"public_payload":{"sentence":"She must has misunderstood the question."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["She must have misunderstood the question."]},"reference_answer":"She must have misunderstood the question.","incorrect_answer":"She must understand the question tomorrow.","explanation":"После модального must используется have, даже с she; misunderstood сохраняет прошлое."},{"id":"b2e88410-3f37-5665-a0ab-6d879017ffb2","lesson_id":"ec5a99eb-159c-5c3a-9ec9-ea412352e7c5","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Ответь, сохранив неуверенность в причине опоздания.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"He must be arrive yesterday."},{"id":"o2","label":"He definitely invented all the traffic."},{"id":"o3","label":"He might have been delayed by traffic."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Rae","text":"Why was Oliver late?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Might have been delayed выражает возможное объяснение без неподтверждённой уверенности."},{"id":"495ed0f6-33e1-5ce1-a875-0e3c4992da7d","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери естественное сочетание с concern.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"do"},{"id":"o2","label":"perform"},{"id":"o3","label":"raise"}],"sentence":"I would like to ___ a concern about the schedule."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Устойчивое сочетание — raise a concern."},{"id":"703af24a-7f4e-5dcc-8e74-d09c538ac1a9","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери близкое по смыслу выражение в рабочей переписке.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"respond later"},{"id":"o2","label":"reject immediately"},{"id":"o3","label":"arrive earlier"}],"word":"get back to someone","relation":"synonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Get back to someone в этом контексте означает ответить или связаться позже."},{"id":"9011db8c-05c2-5967-b7ec-6144725ba95d","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери уместную просьбу руководителю о переносе срока.","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"I have never had any deadlines anywhere."},{"id":"o2","label":"Would it be possible to extend the deadline until Monday?"},{"id":"o3","label":"Give me more time, or else."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Manager","text":"Is everything on track for Friday?"},{"speaker":"Analyst","text":"I need more time to check the figures."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Would it be possible …? — вежливая конкретная просьба; угроза неуместна."},{"id":"ca291aab-07da-5ecf-ba32-e32ac325fd9a","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую разницу в тоне объясняет текст?","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Longer messages are automatically more accurate."},{"id":"o2","label":"The same deadline can be expressed with different degrees of politeness."},{"id":"o3","label":"A professional message must always avoid stating a deadline."}],"passage":"Two colleagues need the same information from a supplier. One writes, “Send the figures today.” The other writes, “Could you please send the figures by the end of today?” Both messages state a deadline, but the second frames the request more politely. This does not mean that every business message should be long or indirect. A short message can still be professional if it gives the necessary context and shows reasonable consideration for the reader."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Обе просьбы задают срок, но вторая вежливее. Автор не утверждает, что длина гарантирует качество."},{"id":"b72a0ef4-c8f3-5a73-80e6-15c30362f453","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи просьбу учесть расходы.","position":5,"public_payload":{"source":"Пожалуйста, учтите дополнительные расходы."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Please take the additional costs into account.","Please take into account the additional costs.","Please consider the additional costs."]},"reference_answer":"Please take the additional costs into account.","incorrect_answer":"Please ignore the additional costs.","explanation":"Take into account / consider означает учитывать; ignore — противоположное действие."},{"id":"8d6a99aa-d56e-57b0-b452-351506bbf216","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь устойчивое сочетание.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We need to do a decision before Friday."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["We need to make a decision before Friday."]},"reference_answer":"We need to make a decision before Friday.","incorrect_answer":"We need to avoid a decision before Friday.","explanation":"Говорят make a decision, а не do a decision. Смысл необходимости решения сохраняется."},{"id":"577894dc-f6c1-5d32-845c-fc3a92d76128","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери вежливое уточнение срока ответа.","position":7,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"response?"},{"id":"t2","label":"me"},{"id":"t3","label":"can"},{"id":"t4","label":"you"},{"id":"t5","label":"when"},{"id":"t6","label":"Could"},{"id":"t7","label":"know"},{"id":"t8","label":"let"},{"id":"t9","label":"a"},{"id":"t10","label":"I"},{"id":"t11","label":"expect"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t6","t4","t8","t2","t7","t5","t10","t3","t11","t9","t1"]},"reference_answer":["t6","t4","t8","t2","t7","t5","t10","t3","t11","t9","t1"],"incorrect_answer":["t4","t8","t2","t7","t5","t10","t3","t11","t9","t1","t6"],"explanation":"Could you let me know …? — вежливый запрос; внутри косвенного вопроса порядок I can expect."},{"id":"cab8ea60-f5ef-516a-a9c8-2286a1acc819","lesson_id":"cce4a02c-5a44-5170-8f1e-0327811bc161","kind":"unit_test","prompt":"Проверь гипотезы, осторожность и связность B2.","position":8,"public_payload":{"questions":[{"id":"q1","prompt":"Выбери альтернативное прошлое.","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"If I would have checked, I had noticed."},{"id":"o2","label":"If I had checked, I would have noticed."}]},{"id":"q2","prompt":"Как выразить возможность в прошлом?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"They might have left early."},{"id":"o2","label":"They certainly must leaving early."}]},{"id":"q3","prompt":"Выбери верную уступительную структуру.","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Despite we were late, we finished."},{"id":"o2","label":"Despite the delay, we finished."}]}]},"answer_key":{"answers":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o1","q3":"o2"},"explanations":{"q1":"If + Past Perfect сочетается с would have + причастие.","q2":"Might have left допускает событие, но не подтверждает его.","q3":"После despite подходит существительное; для придаточного нужен although."}},"reference_answer":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o1","q3":"o2"},"incorrect_answer":{"q1":"o1","q2":"o1","q3":"o2"},"explanation":"Контрольный блок засчитывается при всех верных ответах. Разбор каждого вопроса показан отдельно."},{"id":"d44d9fe9-6966-56d8-b439-b6a9b170ff11","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери порядок слов после начального ограничения.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"we did realise"},{"id":"o2","label":"we realised did"},{"id":"o3","label":"did we realise"}],"sentence":"Only then ___ how serious the problem was."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"После Only then в главной части нужен вспомогательный did перед we."},{"id":"d784bf49-130b-5b90-85aa-21bcc7e7ec2d","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни инверсию с отрицательным наречием.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Never ___ I seen such a thorough analysis."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["have"]},"reference_answer":"have","incorrect_answer":"I","explanation":"После начального Never вспомогательный have ставится перед I."},{"id":"01b53b1e-6447-5894-9786-785d08d52990","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что подчёркивает начальное Only after в позиции автора?","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The review proved that every record was false."},{"id":"o2","label":"No employee had ever noticed any individual discrepancy."},{"id":"o3","label":"A broader understanding emerged only following the independent review."}],"passage":"Only after the independent reviewers examined the original records did the team recognise the extent of the reporting problem. Before that review, each department had assumed that the inconsistencies were confined to its own files. The reviewers did not discover a single dramatic error; rather, they showed that many small discrepancies pointed in the same direction. The opening phrase therefore matters: it identifies the review as the point at which a broader understanding became possible. It does not claim that every record was unreliable, nor does it imply that no member of staff had previously noticed any discrepancy at all."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Ограничение относится к общему осознанию масштаба, а не к отсутствию любых прежних наблюдений."},{"id":"0cf12583-ce93-59ad-a97a-6935e63121b6","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи условие формальной инверсией или обычным if.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Если бы я знал об ограничении, я бы упомянул его."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Had I known about the limitation, I would have mentioned it.","If I had known about the limitation, I would have mentioned it."]},"reference_answer":"Had I known about the limitation, I would have mentioned it.","incorrect_answer":"If I know about the limitation, I will mention it.","explanation":"Had I known = If I had known; следствие остаётся would have mentioned в нереальном прошлом."},{"id":"604dd494-826b-56a9-a1cf-7c9f46b01f1e","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь порядок слов после Only after.","position":5,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Only after the audit we understood the risk."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Only after the audit did we understand the risk."]},"reference_answer":"Only after the audit did we understand the risk.","incorrect_answer":"We understood the risk before the audit.","explanation":"После начального ограничительного оборота нужна инверсия did we understand. Before меняет временной смысл."},{"id":"c82b204e-13ca-5019-9582-4e55f6fb43c6","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Собери формальный запрет с инверсией.","position":6,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"files"},{"id":"t2","label":"confidential"},{"id":"t3","label":"no"},{"id":"t4","label":"be"},{"id":"t5","label":"Under"},{"id":"t6","label":"shared."},{"id":"t7","label":"circumstances"},{"id":"t8","label":"should"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t5","t3","t7","t8","t2","t1","t4","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t5","t3","t7","t8","t2","t1","t4","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t3","t7","t8","t2","t1","t4","t6","t5"],"explanation":"После Under no circumstances модальный should предшествует подлежащему; be shared — пассив."},{"id":"a5cdb770-6025-51d6-9f95-c7c479d0dbc1","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Какой обычный условный оборот соответствует Had the data been available, we would have used it?","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Because the data was available, we used it."},{"id":"o2","label":"If the data is available, we use it."},{"id":"o3","label":"If the data had been available, we would have used it."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Had the data been available — инверсия условного Past Perfect, не утверждение о доступности данных."},{"id":"78ecfabd-55ad-5e95-a818-c2ffdf14089f","lesson_id":"0303140c-00c8-53b6-b2ad-5a4ce6c8a747","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два корректных примера ограничительной инверсии.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Not until Friday did they publish the results."},{"id":"o2","label":"Seldom we have seen such a detailed response."},{"id":"o3","label":"Rarely do we encounter such a clear explanation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o1","o3"]},"reference_answer":["o3","o1"],"incorrect_answer":["o2"],"explanation":"Rarely do we … и Not until … did they … используют инверсию; в третьем примере её нет."},{"id":"f05fd5c3-19db-557e-acbe-7d33cc5e0328","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери существительное для формального описания внедрения.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"implementation"},{"id":"o2","label":"implication"},{"id":"o3","label":"imitation"}],"sentence":"The ___ of the policy took six months."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Implementation of a policy — внедрение политики; implication означает следствие."},{"id":"026c9521-9c10-5ecc-b3fd-3cbc89114f80","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую проблему редактор видит в исходной фразе?","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Every noun phrase is unsuitable for professional writing."},{"id":"o2","label":"The revision itself was necessarily a mistake."},{"id":"o3","label":"The noun-heavy wording obscures the actor and the action."}],"passage":"The draft report stated that “the implementation of the revision of the allocation procedure was undertaken.” A reader could see that something had happened, but not who had done what. The editor replaced the sentence with “The finance team revised the allocation procedure.” This version sacrifices some of the abstract formality while making the responsible actor and the main action visible. The editor did not argue that nominalisation should disappear from professional writing. In a heading such as “Implementation costs”, a noun phrase may be economical and useful. The objection was to an unnecessary chain of nouns that obscured responsibility in a particular sentence."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Критика относится к перегруженной фразе, скрывающей ответственность; не ко всем существительным и не к факту пересмотра."},{"id":"09b5fa60-ac4c-5da4-aedc-c7e2187b3f0d","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи формальное сообщение о снижении затрат.","position":3,"public_payload":{"source":"Снижение затрат не привело к потере качества."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The reduction in costs did not lead to a loss of quality.","Reducing costs did not result in a loss of quality."]},"reference_answer":"The reduction in costs did not lead to a loss of quality.","incorrect_answer":"The reduction in costs caused a loss of quality.","explanation":"Важны отсутствие потери качества и сохранение причинного отношения; cause без отрицания меняет смысл."},{"id":"7b6fb660-0a95-5520-a4e9-b9be939fccca","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"correction","prompt":"Сделай фразу яснее, назвав уже указанного исполнителя.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The carrying out of the review was done by the committee."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The committee carried out the review.","The committee conducted the review."]},"reference_answer":"The committee carried out the review.","incorrect_answer":"The committee cancelled the review.","explanation":"Оба варианта раскрывают действие глаголом и сохраняют committee как исполнителя. Cancelled — другое действие."},{"id":"0f68e0af-a398-5e9b-b62f-df5f8f35742a","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"matching","prompt":"Сопоставь абстрактные существительные и значения.","position":5,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l1","label":"implementation"},{"id":"l2","label":"allocation"},{"id":"l3","label":"accountability"},{"id":"l4","label":"revision"}],"right":[{"id":"r1","label":"подотчётность"},{"id":"r2","label":"пересмотр"},{"id":"r3","label":"внедрение"},{"id":"r4","label":"распределение"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l1":"r3","l2":"r4","l3":"r1","l4":"r2"}},"reference_answer":{"l1":"r3","l2":"r4","l3":"r1","l4":"r2"},"incorrect_answer":{"l1":"r4","l2":"r1","l3":"r2","l4":"r3"},"explanation":"Эти существительные часто встречаются в деловых текстах; accountability не тождественно просто blame — обвинению."},{"id":"6e16432a-12f9-598f-a626-1982b905190f","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Какая редактура сохраняет исполнителя и действие?","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The responses were never collected."},{"id":"o2","label":"An analysis existed somewhere."},{"id":"o3","label":"The research team analysed the responses."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Первый вариант ясно называет команду и действие, не добавляя отсутствия данных."},{"id":"e4eac101-4092-545e-aeeb-0c0a5c8c22ed","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери вывод о стиле без абсолютного запрета.","position":7,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"can"},{"id":"t2","label":"be"},{"id":"t3","label":"it"},{"id":"t4","label":"useful"},{"id":"t5","label":"when"},{"id":"t6","label":"a"},{"id":"t7","label":"clear"},{"id":"t8","label":"serves"},{"id":"t9","label":"Nominalisation"},{"id":"t10","label":"purpose."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t9","t1","t2","t4","t5","t3","t8","t6","t7","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t9","t1","t2","t4","t5","t3","t8","t6","t7","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t1","t2","t4","t5","t3","t8","t6","t7","t10","t9"],"explanation":"Can и when ограничивают вывод: уместность зависит от функции, а не от механического правила."},{"id":"3c61a528-ea53-5b4d-8272-1368aecf0616","lesson_id":"b6f7588f-b44e-5845-8b1a-a786d911e8d5","kind":"word_review","prompt":"Что означает accountability в управленческом контексте?","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"гарантия отсутствия любых ошибок"},{"id":"o2","label":"обязанность объяснять решения и отвечать за них"},{"id":"o3","label":"полное отсутствие полномочий"}],"word":"accountability"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Accountability — подотчётность и ответственность за решения, а не обещание безошибочности."},{"id":"b2791536-5567-55ab-b3d0-f686ec48922c","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какой вывод соответствует ограничениям исследования?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The tool is proven to improve productivity in every organisation."},{"id":"o2","label":"The results offer tentative evidence of a benefit in the tested setting."},{"id":"o3","label":"The researchers have demonstrated that scheduling tools never work."}],"passage":"A small company tested a new scheduling tool with twelve volunteers from one department. Most participants reported that planning their week became easier, but there was no comparison group and the test lasted only a fortnight. The researchers wrote that the findings “may indicate a practical benefit in this setting”. They deliberately avoided claiming that the tool would improve productivity in every organisation. A larger sample would not automatically remove every limitation: differences in roles and the absence of a comparison group would still require attention. The cautious wording therefore reflects the design of the study rather than a desire to conceal an unfavourable result."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Ограниченная добровольная выборка без группы сравнения поддерживает лишь осторожный контекстный вывод."},{"id":"c309b937-2593-5a3a-a7a3-75becacafa1a","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери формулировку, соразмерную предварительным данным.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"may suggest"},{"id":"o2","label":"conclusively prove"},{"id":"o3","label":"inevitably guarantee"}],"sentence":"These preliminary observations ___ that further investigation is worthwhile."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"May suggest сохраняет предварительный характер наблюдения."},{"id":"ae2b9102-3d6f-5bf0-9a7c-ebbebadd2c0b","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни оговорку об ограниченной выборке.","position":3,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The findings should be interpreted ___ caution."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["with"]},"reference_answer":"with","incorrect_answer":"without","explanation":"With caution — с осторожностью; without caution означало бы противоположный подход."},{"id":"37e8b44c-5f2f-5a23-ac3f-0b289460cce4","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи осторожный вывод, не усиливая его.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Результаты могут указывать на связь, но не доказывают причинность."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The results may indicate an association, but they do not prove causation.","The findings may suggest an association, but they do not demonstrate causation."]},"reference_answer":"The results may indicate an association, but they do not prove causation.","incorrect_answer":"The results prove that one factor causes the other.","explanation":"Association — связь; causation — причинность. Оговорка об отсутствии доказательства обязательна."},{"id":"65ef7196-82e9-53f7-a272-f0dac4c3cef5","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери две формулировки с явно ограниченной областью вывода.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The pattern must occur in every population."},{"id":"o2","label":"In this sample, the pattern was observed twice."},{"id":"o3","label":"The findings may not generalise to other settings."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o2","o3"]},"reference_answer":["o3","o2"],"incorrect_answer":["o1"],"explanation":"In this sample и may not generalise явно ограничивают область применимости."},{"id":"29c5cdce-d640-5e75-9017-3f0134221415","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"response_choice","prompt":"Ответь коллеге, который чрезмерно обобщил результат.","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"No result can ever provide any useful information."},{"id":"o2","label":"The evidence is promising, but the design does not support that broad a claim."},{"id":"o3","label":"Exactly; twelve volunteers prove every possible outcome."}],"context":"So this proves that the tool will work for everyone, doesn’t it?"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Первый ответ признаёт ценность данных и ограничивает силу вывода без другой крайности."},{"id":"c3edc451-c723-5058-be77-b9482ef05fe8","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"correction","prompt":"Согласуй глагол с множественным findings, сохранив осторожность.","position":7,"public_payload":{"sentence":"These findings suggests that the approach may help."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["These findings suggest that the approach may help."]},"reference_answer":"These findings suggest that the approach may help.","incorrect_answer":"These findings prove that the approach always works.","explanation":"С findings нужен suggest. Замена на prove и always необоснованно усиливает вывод."},{"id":"7adee2fd-6fbd-562c-b4af-96c3add9a017","lesson_id":"f072de5a-e807-5a58-a715-dbcf97b37659","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери ближайший синоним tentative для вывода.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"provisional"},{"id":"o2","label":"irrelevant"},{"id":"o3","label":"conclusive"}],"word":"tentative","relation":"synonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Tentative и provisional обозначают предварительный характер; conclusive означает окончательный."},{"id":"0ec99aa7-b768-5bd4-8c1b-5035d058175f","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какие сведения лучше всего помогли бы сравнить предложения?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"A larger number of enthusiastic slogans."},{"id":"o2","label":"The assumption that every pilot is directly transferable."},{"id":"o3","label":"Measurements of comparable tasks under stated conditions."}],"passage":"Two suppliers claim that their software will reduce administrative work. The first provides enthusiastic customer testimonials but no details about how time savings were measured. The second describes a pilot and lists the tasks included in its calculation, although the pilot took place in a larger organisation than the buyer’s. Neither proposal can simply be accepted at face value. The procurement team asks both suppliers for measurements of comparable tasks under clearly stated conditions. This request is not a claim that testimonials are dishonest or that pilots are useless. It aims to create a basis on which differences between the proposals can be interpreted fairly."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Команда запрашивает сопоставимые измерения, а не отвергает все отзывы или пилоты."},{"id":"3e50d2ef-f217-55df-9d22-c02aa4bf1c0f","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово о независимом подтверждении утверждения.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"corroborate"},{"id":"o2","label":"postpone"},{"id":"o3","label":"decorate"}],"sentence":"We need independent evidence to ___ the supplier’s claim."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Corroborate a claim — подтвердить его дополнительными данными."},{"id":"1a872622-d25e-5296-abdd-c41ec4ede095","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи просьбу о сопоставимых данных.","position":3,"public_payload":{"source":"Можете ли вы предоставить данные, полученные в сопоставимых условиях?"},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Could you provide data collected under comparable conditions?","Can you provide data gathered under comparable conditions?"]},"reference_answer":"Could you provide data collected under comparable conditions?","incorrect_answer":"Could you hide the data from comparable trials?","explanation":"Provide data — предоставить данные; comparable conditions — сопоставимые условия, не сокрытие данных."},{"id":"92888611-c268-547a-bc23-aef9c1e1265d","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Уточни утверждение поставщика профессионально.","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Which tasks and time period does that figure cover?"},{"id":"o2","label":"Thirty per cent is always the same in every role."},{"id":"o3","label":"So no other evidence will ever be necessary."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Supplier","text":"Our clients save thirty per cent of their time."},{"speaker":"Buyer","text":"That sounds useful, but we need to understand the calculation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Конкретный вопрос уточняет охват показателя и помогает оценить сопоставимость."},{"id":"9dac0353-46bf-590e-9153-16a4753c6619","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два вопроса, которые помогают оценить достоверность сравнения.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Can we ignore the measurement method if the headline is attractive?"},{"id":"o2","label":"How were the participants selected?"},{"id":"o3","label":"Were the same tasks measured?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o2","o3"]},"reference_answer":["o3","o2"],"incorrect_answer":["o1"],"explanation":"Сопоставимость задач и отбор участников влияют на интерпретацию; привлекательный заголовок не заменяет метод."},{"id":"26174021-531b-56db-bfaa-d11c6700633c","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Собери рекомендацию о проверке утверждения.","position":6,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"should"},{"id":"t2","label":"The"},{"id":"t3","label":"be"},{"id":"t4","label":"evidence."},{"id":"t5","label":"assessed"},{"id":"t6","label":"against"},{"id":"t7","label":"independent"},{"id":"t8","label":"claim"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t2","t8","t1","t3","t5","t6","t7","t4"]},"reference_answer":["t2","t8","t1","t3","t5","t6","t7","t4"],"incorrect_answer":["t8","t1","t3","t5","t6","t7","t4","t2"],"explanation":"Assessed against evidence — оценено с опорой на данные; should be assessed — пассивная рекомендация."},{"id":"18c0bbc2-4452-51c1-b1d1-576956d29079","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь устойчивое сочетание при оценке предложения.","position":7,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We should not take the figures at face price."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["We should not take the figures at face value."]},"reference_answer":"We should not take the figures at face value.","incorrect_answer":"We should take all figures as proven facts.","explanation":"At face value означает принимать без дополнительной проверки. Face price здесь не употребляется."},{"id":"9f25a2b4-ab07-5be3-b41f-44cb05b817a6","lesson_id":"d7d86ac8-bfd7-5760-979f-dd08aa72b0de","kind":"word_review","prompt":"Что означает like-for-like comparison?","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"сравнение только понравившихся результатов"},{"id":"o2","label":"сравнение сопоставимых объектов и условий"},{"id":"o3","label":"выбор самого короткого документа"}],"word":"like-for-like comparison"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Like-for-like требует сопоставимой основы, а не отбора удобных результатов."},{"id":"0e11f5b3-c83e-573f-a6f6-8cf75dbfefaf","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери связку контраста между двумя подходами.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Whereas"},{"id":"o2","label":"Unless"},{"id":"o3","label":"Because of"}],"sentence":"___ one team prioritises speed, the other emphasises reliability."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Whereas сопоставляет контрастирующие позиции; because of не вводит такое придаточное."},{"id":"93752162-f6d6-51fc-9bf2-c927e471e428","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что автор признаёт, не отказываясь от предложения?","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The scheme should immediately be imposed across the organisation."},{"id":"o2","label":"Popularity alone will prove long-term feasibility."},{"id":"o3","label":"The scheme has a real staffing cost, but a limited trial may still be worthwhile."}],"passage":"The committee accepts that the proposed mentoring scheme would require staff time that is already in short supply. Nonetheless, it recommends a limited trial, arguing that the current lack of support for new colleagues also has a cost. The recommendation is deliberately narrower than immediate organisation-wide adoption. Participants would be drawn from two departments, and the trial would be reviewed after one term. Even if the trial proved popular, the committee says that popularity alone would not settle the question of long-term feasibility. The argument therefore concedes a genuine resource constraint while proposing a way to gather information before making a larger commitment."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Автор признаёт ресурсное ограничение и предлагает небольшой проверяемый пилот, а не немедленное внедрение повсюду."},{"id":"a7f91070-0dda-510a-8937-8a3994a3dcf6","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни связку сохранения вывода вопреки трудности.","position":3,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The proposal is demanding; ___, it deserves consideration."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["nonetheless","nevertheless"]},"reference_answer":"nonetheless","incorrect_answer":"therefore","explanation":"Nonetheless / nevertheless — тем не менее. Therefore выражало бы следствие, а не уступку."},{"id":"bf8f3ea6-cf13-57d0-8e09-a791a994528f","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи условие, которое не меняет решения.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Даже если расходы возрастут, мы не откажемся от проверки безопасности."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Even if costs rise, we will not abandon the safety review.","We will not abandon the safety review even if costs increase."]},"reference_answer":"Even if costs rise, we will not abandon the safety review.","incorrect_answer":"Because costs have risen, we have abandoned the safety review.","explanation":"Even if не утверждает, что расходы уже выросли, и сохраняет отрицание will not abandon."},{"id":"b2a27230-ba8a-5c03-8136-9df980c3f41d","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Что подразумевает Even if the trial succeeds, further evaluation will be needed?","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Further evaluation will be unnecessary after success."},{"id":"o2","label":"Success would not remove the need for further evaluation."},{"id":"o3","label":"The trial has already succeeded."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Even if представляет допущение, при котором необходимость оценки сохраняется."},{"id":"b92e6430-d7c9-54e2-8c53-eceb8268be16","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь структуру уступки после in spite of.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"In spite of the scheme was popular, its cost remained uncertain."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Although the scheme was popular, its cost remained uncertain.","In spite of the scheme’s popularity, its cost remained uncertain."]},"reference_answer":"Although the scheme was popular, its cost remained uncertain.","incorrect_answer":"Because the scheme was unpopular, its cost was known.","explanation":"In spite of требует именной группы; although вводит придаточное. Исходная неопределённость затрат сохраняется."},{"id":"b16cb750-1994-5d3c-a033-bcd122cec117","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери осторожную уступительную рекомендацию.","position":7,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"trial"},{"id":"t2","label":"still"},{"id":"t3","label":"limited,"},{"id":"t4","label":"be"},{"id":"t5","label":"evidence"},{"id":"t6","label":"is"},{"id":"t7","label":"While"},{"id":"t8","label":"small"},{"id":"t9","label":"the"},{"id":"t10","label":"may"},{"id":"t11","label":"a"},{"id":"t12","label":"justified."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t7","t9","t5","t6","t3","t11","t8","t1","t10","t2","t4","t12"]},"reference_answer":["t7","t9","t5","t6","t3","t11","t8","t1","t10","t2","t4","t12"],"incorrect_answer":["t9","t5","t6","t3","t11","t8","t1","t10","t2","t4","t12","t7"],"explanation":"While здесь уступительное; may still сохраняет ограниченный, а не категоричный вывод."},{"id":"d7acd018-b27e-5071-9802-4cee9242c96d","lesson_id":"836a38b3-271d-51e7-b452-17062cee67d4","kind":"unit_test","prompt":"Проверь точность академической и профессиональной речи C1.","position":8,"public_payload":{"questions":[{"id":"q1","prompt":"Выбери корректную инверсию.","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Only then did we understand the issue."},{"id":"o2","label":"Only then we did understood the issue."}]},{"id":"q2","prompt":"Какой вывод осторожнее?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The findings prove every possible causal link."},{"id":"o2","label":"The findings may indicate an association."}]},{"id":"q3","prompt":"Как читать even if?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"It introduces a condition that does not alter the main conclusion."},{"id":"o2","label":"It confirms that the condition has definitely occurred."}]}]},"answer_key":{"answers":{"q1":"o1","q2":"o2","q3":"o1"},"explanations":{"q1":"После Only then нужна инверсия did we understand.","q2":"May indicate соразмеряет уверенность ограниченным данным.","q3":"Even if не утверждает фактическое выполнение условия."}},"reference_answer":{"q1":"o1","q2":"o2","q3":"o1"},"incorrect_answer":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o2","q3":"o1"},"explanation":"Контрольный блок засчитывается при всех верных ответах. Разбор каждого вопроса показан отдельно."},{"id":"7ab0e96d-c7db-5bf4-be6f-8bc9c99be176","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"reading","prompt":"В чём заключается ирония рецензента?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The board has made indecision more efficient while presenting it as progress."},{"id":"o2","label":"The reviewer proves that every member is deliberately dishonest."},{"id":"o3","label":"The reviewer approves of the board’s substantive decision."}],"passage":"The reviewer congratulates the board on its “remarkable efficiency”: a decision postponed at six consecutive meetings has finally been postponed without the inconvenience of a meeting at all. Read in isolation, the opening compliment might suggest approval. The surrounding account reverses that expectation. The board has streamlined the procedure for avoiding a decision, not the work the procedure was meant to accomplish. Yet the reviewer stops short of alleging that every member is deliberately obstructive. A later paragraph acknowledges that the proposal contains genuine uncertainties. The target is the institution’s self-congratulatory language, which presents the removal of an administrative step as though it were substantive progress. The humour depends on preserving that distinction rather than merely treating every positive word as a negative one."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Похвала относится к эффективности уклонения от решения. Текст не доказывает намеренную нечестность всех членов совета."},{"id":"49bb56be-1fd5-5802-8c77-5a964c1a4e35","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое ограничение критики автор явно сохраняет?","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The proposal contains real uncertainties, and universal bad faith is not alleged."},{"id":"o2","label":"Administrative changes can never have any value."},{"id":"o3","label":"All positive language must always be interpreted ironically."}],"passage":"The reviewer congratulates the board on its “remarkable efficiency”: a decision postponed at six consecutive meetings has finally been postponed without the inconvenience of a meeting at all. Read in isolation, the opening compliment might suggest approval. The surrounding account reverses that expectation. The board has streamlined the procedure for avoiding a decision, not the work the procedure was meant to accomplish. Yet the reviewer stops short of alleging that every member is deliberately obstructive. A later paragraph acknowledges that the proposal contains genuine uncertainties. The target is the institution’s self-congratulatory language, which presents the removal of an administrative step as though it were substantive progress. The humour depends on preserving that distinction rather than merely treating every positive word as a negative one."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Автор признаёт реальные неопределённости и не приписывает всем участникам умышленное препятствование."},{"id":"26e251fd-8b90-50f6-b3eb-58de746291e0","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Определи наиболее обоснованный подтекст замечания.","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The member has formally approved the tripled budget."},{"id":"o2","label":"The member doubts whether enthusiasm is justified before the costs are examined."},{"id":"o3","label":"The member wants the presentation to contain more colours."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Chair","text":"The budget has tripled, but the presentation is certainly colourful."},{"speaker":"Member","text":"Perhaps we could cost the proposal before celebrating it."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Противопоставление celebrating и costing делает сомнение в обоснованности энтузиазма явным."},{"id":"6f12e3e5-54d1-5ce5-8d73-c745e8c45ab9","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи сдержанную оценку, не превращая её в восторг или полное отрицание.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Предложение не лишено достоинств, но его преимущества преувеличены."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The proposal is not without merit, but its benefits have been overstated.","The proposal has some merit, but its advantages have been exaggerated."]},"reference_answer":"The proposal is not without merit, but its benefits have been overstated.","incorrect_answer":"The proposal is worthless and has no advantages.","explanation":"Not without merit — ограниченная положительная оценка; overstated критикует масштаб заявленных выгод."},{"id":"bea1efff-5461-5db2-bff2-696a81786149","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово для намеренно сдержанного описания серьёзной проблемы.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"specification"},{"id":"o2","label":"endorsement"},{"id":"o3","label":"understatement"}],"sentence":"Calling the collapse of the entire schedule “a slight inconvenience” is an ___."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Understatement — преуменьшение; endorsement было бы одобрением."},{"id":"b06b03eb-afb9-5946-8e2d-c40615301e83","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два вывода, допустимых при анализе иронического комментария.","position":6,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"A criticism can be ironic without accusing everyone of bad faith."},{"id":"o2","label":"Every polite adjective proves that the writer means its exact opposite."},{"id":"o3","label":"Context can reverse the apparent force of a compliment."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o1","o3"]},"reference_answer":["o3","o1"],"incorrect_answer":["o2"],"explanation":"Ирония зависит от контекста; механическое обращение любого прилагательного в противоположность неверно."},{"id":"263cf25c-a79a-5c41-b741-b688e906d085","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь модальный инфинитив, сохранив ретроспективную критику.","position":7,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The board ought to has examined the figures before praising the outcome."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The board ought to have examined the figures before praising the outcome."]},"reference_answer":"The board ought to have examined the figures before praising the outcome.","incorrect_answer":"The board ought to praise the figures without examining them.","explanation":"Ought to have examined выражает оценку прошлого; has после to здесь невозможно."},{"id":"9bed37ae-d55a-5d96-b4e7-325d69b04e54","lesson_id":"91628438-0914-524a-ae2c-77665a7f5aa6","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери ближайшее значение qualified в qualified praise.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"officially certified"},{"id":"o2","label":"limited by reservations"},{"id":"o3","label":"unreservedly enthusiastic"}],"word":"qualified","relation":"synonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Qualified praise — похвала с оговорками, а не безусловный восторг."},{"id":"e5c889e8-4d17-5175-add6-1180245c4fcf","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какая переформулировка сохраняет условие уведомления?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"You can always leave without paying, regardless of notice."},{"id":"o2","label":"You can leave without a fee if written notice arrives at least fourteen days before the event."},{"id":"o3","label":"You must leave exactly fourteen days before the event."}],"passage":"A fictional agreement states that a participant may withdraw without a fee provided that written notice is received at least fourteen days before the scheduled event. A later clause allows the organiser to waive the fee in exceptional circumstances even when that period has not been met. An editor is asked to make the wording easier to follow. “You can always leave without paying” is shorter, but it erases the notice requirement and turns a discretionary exception into a universal entitlement. The problem is not that plain language is inherently imprecise. A faithful revision can use familiar words while retaining the deadline, the requirement for writing, and the organiser’s limited discretion. This passage is a language exercise, not advice about an actual agreement."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Сохраняются письменная форма, крайний срок и условность освобождения от платы."},{"id":"a13464d0-fbd3-5b6f-b49b-b8129bb8e1ba","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери фразу, сохраняющую условность одобрения.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"in defiance of"},{"id":"o2","label":"subject to"},{"id":"o3","label":"regardless of"}],"sentence":"The arrangement will proceed ___ final approval."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Subject to approval — при условии одобрения; regardless of исключило бы зависимость от него."},{"id":"b2fdcee2-cf78-57ef-bd91-fb17b92255ef","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи оговорку без превращения возможности в обязанность.","position":3,"public_payload":{"source":"Организатор может отменить сбор в исключительных обстоятельствах."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The organiser may waive the fee in exceptional circumstances.","The organizer may waive the fee in exceptional circumstances."]},"reference_answer":"The organiser may waive the fee in exceptional circumstances.","incorrect_answer":"The organiser must waive the fee in all circumstances.","explanation":"May сохраняет усмотрение; must и all circumstances неоправданно усиливают правило."},{"id":"60acadd9-472a-55b1-a687-da9094631a76","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери точное редакторское замечание.","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"it makes the original condition more explicit."},{"id":"o2","label":"it preserves every restriction exactly."},{"id":"o3","label":"it removes a condition rather than merely simplifying the wording."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Writer","text":"I shortened “provided that written notice is received” to “whenever you like”."},{"speaker":"Editor","text":"The revision is shorter, but …"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Whenever you like устраняет требование уведомления, а не просто заменяет сложные слова простыми."},{"id":"3162e6b9-e40c-52dd-b6b8-b54c7e9b61f7","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два элемента, которые нужно сохранить при верной переформулировке условия.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Whether an exception is discretionary or automatic."},{"id":"o2","label":"The deadline for receiving notice."},{"id":"o3","label":"The exact number of syllables in every sentence."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o1","o2"]},"reference_answer":["o2","o1"],"incorrect_answer":["o3"],"explanation":"Смысловые условия важны; длина слов и слогов не обязана совпадать."},{"id":"889e6ad6-a958-5be6-8a54-fc6dc8971bbf","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь относительную конструкцию, не меняя ограничение.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The fee may be waived only in circumstances which the organiser considers them exceptional."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The fee may be waived only in circumstances which the organiser considers exceptional.","The fee may be waived only in circumstances that the organiser considers exceptional."]},"reference_answer":"The fee may be waived only in circumstances which the organiser considers exceptional.","incorrect_answer":"The fee must be waived in every circumstance.","explanation":"Which/that уже выполняет роль объекта considers; дополнительное them избыточно. Only и may сохраняются."},{"id":"8928b1cd-d257-57f8-aac7-bf5cf2bfd25c","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"word_review","prompt":"Что означает waiver в формальном документе?","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"обязательное увеличение платы"},{"id":"o2","label":"доказательство преступления"},{"id":"o3","label":"отказ от применения определённого права или требования"}],"word":"waiver"},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Waiver означает отказ от права/требования или его применения, в зависимости от контекста."},{"id":"5ed986f9-2042-5dd2-aeb0-e0c1037233ff","lesson_id":"38338103-b846-50c5-9c9d-2bc97e9f0d26","kind":"word_order","prompt":"Собери оговорку, сохранив разрешение и условие.","position":8,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"waived"},{"id":"t2","label":"is"},{"id":"t3","label":"provided"},{"id":"t4","label":"be"},{"id":"t5","label":"may"},{"id":"t6","label":"requirement"},{"id":"t7","label":"the"},{"id":"t8","label":"that"},{"id":"t9","label":"met."},{"id":"t10","label":"The"},{"id":"t11","label":"notice"},{"id":"t12","label":"fee"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t10","t12","t5","t4","t1","t3","t8","t7","t11","t6","t2","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t10","t12","t5","t4","t1","t3","t8","t7","t11","t6","t2","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t12","t5","t4","t1","t3","t8","t7","t11","t6","t2","t9","t10"],"explanation":"May сохраняет возможность, provided that — условие; перепорядочивание не должно менять их связь."},{"id":"7d987639-2947-53bc-a5ec-445d0e1a32e8","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какова функция уступки о неполноте архива?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"It proves that missing documents support the historian."},{"id":"o2","label":"It limits the strength of the reconstruction without making all accounts equally plausible."},{"id":"o3","label":"It makes every reconstruction worthless."}],"passage":"For all its gaps, the archive remains the most detailed record currently available of the negotiations. A critic is right to note that several private exchanges were never recorded. It does not follow, however, that the surviving material tells us nothing, or that every reconstruction is equally plausible. The historian’s argument is comparative: one account fits the available letters and minutes better than its rivals, while still leaving room for revision if new documents emerge. Even were the missing correspondence to contradict part of that account, the consequences would depend on what it contradicted. The concession narrows the claim to a defensible one; it is not a covert assertion that the missing material must support the preferred interpretation."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Автор ограничивает уверенность и сохраняет сравнительное преимущество одной реконструкции; содержание пропущенных документов неизвестно."},{"id":"70563784-3c64-58cd-9986-4766d8f7f40e","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что утверждает оборот Even were the missing correspondence to contradict …?","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The missing correspondence has already been found and analysed."},{"id":"o2","label":"Any contradiction would automatically invalidate every historical statement."},{"id":"o3","label":"A hypothetical contradiction would need to be assessed for its specific significance."}],"passage":"For all its gaps, the archive remains the most detailed record currently available of the negotiations. A critic is right to note that several private exchanges were never recorded. It does not follow, however, that the surviving material tells us nothing, or that every reconstruction is equally plausible. The historian’s argument is comparative: one account fits the available letters and minutes better than its rivals, while still leaving room for revision if new documents emerge. Even were the missing correspondence to contradict part of that account, the consequences would depend on what it contradicted. The concession narrows the claim to a defensible one; it is not a covert assertion that the missing material must support the preferred interpretation."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Это гипотетическое допущение, причём последствия зависели бы от конкретного содержания противоречия."},{"id":"0f17ded4-b7e7-58fa-b99c-834f739eb1a8","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери уступительный оборот со значением «несмотря на все ограничения».","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"For all its"},{"id":"o2","label":"In order to its"},{"id":"o3","label":"Because of all its"}],"sentence":"___ limitations, the account remains informative."},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"For all its limitations — несмотря на ограничения; сам оборот не отменяет последующий положительный вывод."},{"id":"51097ff1-54bd-54b1-9817-cac169a82f29","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи оговорку, не добавляя полной достоверности.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Это ослабляет аргумент, но не опровергает его полностью."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["This weakens the argument, but it does not refute it entirely.","This undermines the argument, but it does not completely refute it."]},"reference_answer":"This weakens the argument, but it does not refute it entirely.","incorrect_answer":"This conclusively proves that the argument is entirely correct.","explanation":"Weakens/undermines — ослабляет; does not entirely refute сохраняет предел критики."},{"id":"12e4d572-6699-553d-9c6e-e973664b5c2f","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два логически допустимых прочтения уступки.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"A hypothetical counterexample is not necessarily an established fact."},{"id":"o2","label":"Acknowledging a limitation can make a claim more precisely bounded."},{"id":"o3","label":"Any conceded weakness proves that the opposite thesis is wholly true."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o1","o2"]},"reference_answer":["o2","o1"],"incorrect_answer":["o3"],"explanation":"Уступка ограничивает тезис; она не доказывает автоматически полную истинность противоположного тезиса."},{"id":"1211e11e-f0cf-560a-a666-e1ed40b9617b","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь формальное гипотетическое условие.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Even were the documents to contradict the account, it would not necessarily follows that every detail is false."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Even were the documents to contradict the account, it would not necessarily follow that every detail is false."]},"reference_answer":"Even were the documents to contradict the account, it would not necessarily follow that every detail is false.","incorrect_answer":"The documents prove that every detail is false.","explanation":"После would not нужна начальная форма follow, не follows. Necessarily и every сохраняют предел вывода, а не превращают допущение в факт."},{"id":"a491fef9-eb85-5109-97ae-ec6f174b1805","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери антоним contingent в значении зависимости вывода от обстоятельств.","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"dependent"},{"id":"o2","label":"unconditional"},{"id":"o3","label":"conditional"}],"word":"contingent","relation":"antonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Unconditional — безусловный; contingent, conditional и dependent передают зависимость."},{"id":"a119364e-1e49-5ec9-b2fc-493fb541451f","lesson_id":"0f2bab4d-9b53-57ca-8b86-f45ec49eb9d1","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери ответ, который сохраняет предел уступки.","position":8,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"it proves that every competing account is equally sound."},{"id":"o2","label":"we still need to ask which claims the surviving evidence can support."},{"id":"o3","label":"it guarantees that no new evidence could matter."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Critic","text":"You admit that the source is incomplete. Surely that settles the issue."},{"speaker":"Historian","text":"It establishes a limitation, but …"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Уместно уточнить, какие выводы поддерживает оставшаяся информация, а не объявить все версии равными."},{"id":"34f0e0e2-0090-5986-ac40-76d9c9b57db4","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что конкретно поддерживает метафору moving the goalposts?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The panel merely repeated an unchanged criterion."},{"id":"o2","label":"The metaphor proves a secret intention to favour one team."},{"id":"o3","label":"A substantial new requirement was introduced after applications had relied on the original criteria."}],"passage":"The editorial accuses the funding panel of “moving the goalposts”. Applicants were first told that proposals would be judged on their potential public benefit. After the shortlist was announced, the panel introduced a requirement for an existing commercial partner, which several shortlisted teams could not meet within the remaining week. The writer distinguishes this change from a routine clarification of ambiguous wording: it added a substantial condition after applicants had acted on the published criteria. The metaphor draws attention to that sequence. It does not, by itself, prove that the panel intended to favour a particular team, and the editorial supplies no evidence for such a motive. A reader can accept the procedural criticism without endorsing an allegation that has not been made or substantiated."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Основание — новая существенная обязанность после начала отбора. Мотив фаворитизма текстом не доказан."},{"id":"2d94a819-dd93-5eea-84a2-a4ca0388b590","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово для критерия оценки, не для оправдания.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"afterthought"},{"id":"o2","label":"pretext"},{"id":"o3","label":"yardstick"}],"sentence":"Public benefit was supposed to be the principal ___ for assessing proposals."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Yardstick — мерило или критерий; pretext — предлог/отговорка."},{"id":"0e5239bd-8ab7-5abc-bd87-4525d2928986","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи процедурную критику без неподтверждённого обвинения в мотиве.","position":3,"public_payload":{"source":"Изменение ставит под вопрос справедливость процедуры, но не доказывает фаворитизм."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The change calls the fairness of the procedure into question, but it does not prove favouritism.","The change raises questions about the fairness of the process, but it does not demonstrate favoritism."]},"reference_answer":"The change calls the fairness of the procedure into question, but it does not prove favouritism.","incorrect_answer":"The change proves that the panel secretly favoured one team.","explanation":"Сохраняется различие между сомнением в процедуре и недоказанным мотивом."},{"id":"6c1270d3-d18b-5f70-96eb-f74f3de09796","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери ответ на чрезмерное прочтение метафоры.","position":4,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"It criticises the changing criteria; the motive would require separate evidence."},{"id":"o2","label":"No, it means the panel physically moved sports equipment."},{"id":"o3","label":"Yes, any metaphor establishes a criminal motive."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Reader","text":"So “moving the goalposts” proves that the panel was corrupt?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o1"},"reference_answer":"o1","incorrect_answer":"o2","explanation":"Образ описывает процедуру; мотив требует отдельных данных. Буквальное спортивное чтение также неверно."},{"id":"f45a495c-0cb7-5070-878d-2d63768e2fc5","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два признака внимательного критического прочтения.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Treating every vivid metaphor as independent proof."},{"id":"o2","label":"Separating an observable sequence from an inferred motive."},{"id":"o3","label":"Checking whether the new requirement changes substance or only clarifies wording."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o2","o3"]},"reference_answer":["o3","o2"],"incorrect_answer":["o1"],"explanation":"Образность не заменяет проверку фактов; последовательность и мотив — разные уровни утверждения."},{"id":"80ac5128-eec2-5229-a4c3-334103a6a621","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь согласование в формальном аргументе.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The introduction of additional criteria undermine confidence in the procedure."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The introduction of additional criteria undermines confidence in the procedure."]},"reference_answer":"The introduction of additional criteria undermines confidence in the procedure.","incorrect_answer":"The additional criteria guarantee confidence in the procedure.","explanation":"Главное подлежащее — introduction в единственном числе, поэтому undermines; criteria не определяет согласование."},{"id":"753028f0-90ae-58cc-a370-8f51768a1277","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери ближайший синоним substantiated для обвинения.","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"merely repeated"},{"id":"o2","label":"supported by evidence"},{"id":"o3","label":"deliberately vague"}],"word":"substantiated","relation":"synonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Substantiated означает подкреплённый доказательствами, а не просто повторённый."},{"id":"e2a504ec-0ae3-5098-ba59-4e7f8c379ea0","lesson_id":"12f5e759-0d8e-5f0a-b562-11d83627b1ac","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери ограниченный вывод о процедуре и мотиве.","position":8,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t1","label":"not"},{"id":"t2","label":"claim"},{"id":"t3","label":"sequence"},{"id":"t4","label":"a"},{"id":"t5","label":"definitive"},{"id":"t6","label":"procedural"},{"id":"t7","label":"supports"},{"id":"t8","label":"a"},{"id":"t9","label":"about"},{"id":"t10","label":"criticism,"},{"id":"t11","label":"The"},{"id":"t12","label":"motive."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t11","t3","t7","t8","t6","t10","t1","t4","t5","t2","t9","t12"]},"reference_answer":["t11","t3","t7","t8","t6","t10","t1","t4","t5","t2","t9","t12"],"incorrect_answer":["t3","t7","t8","t6","t10","t1","t4","t5","t2","t9","t12","t11"],"explanation":"Not противопоставляет две силы вывода: процедурное основание и недоказанный мотив."},{"id":"d5ea9ea4-4bb6-58f3-bc81-55350470d7dd","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую мысль автор защищает, различая два отрицательных вывода?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"The report asks for reviewers who will not read the evidence."},{"id":"o2","label":"An inconclusive result warrants neither a proven benefit nor a proven absence of benefit."},{"id":"o3","label":"Every inconclusive result confirms that an intervention works."}],"passage":"An evaluation found no clear improvement after a small pilot. In the report, the result was described as inconclusive: the measures were too imprecise and the sample too limited to distinguish a modest benefit from no benefit. A summary then announced that the pilot had “proved the intervention ineffective”. That is a stronger claim. The original report had not established a benefit, but neither had it demonstrated the absence of one. This distinction is not an invitation to assume that the intervention works. It is a requirement to keep the conclusion within what the evidence can discriminate. The same report also called for disinterested reviewers, meaning reviewers without a stake in the outcome, not people who could not be bothered to examine it."},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Неопределённый результат не доказывает ни пользу, ни её отсутствие; беспристрастность не равна равнодушию."},{"id":"d3867c54-77ef-5c78-ad55-ce20331d7af9","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"В формальном контексте выбери слово о рецензенте без личной выгоды от результата.","position":2,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"inadvertent"},{"id":"o2","label":"uninterested"},{"id":"o3","label":"disinterested"}],"sentence":"The panel needs a ___ reviewer who has no financial stake in the outcome."},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Здесь disinterested означает беспристрастный; uninterested означало бы отсутствие интереса."},{"id":"e91787ca-9019-5ae9-b1d8-1b52893ebcd1","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"synonym_antonym","prompt":"Выбери ближайший синоним inadvertent при описании ошибки.","position":3,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"unrelated"},{"id":"o2","label":"unavoidable"},{"id":"o3","label":"unintentional"}],"word":"inadvertent","relation":"synonym"},"answer_key":{"value":"o3"},"reference_answer":"o3","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Inadvertent — непреднамеренный. Unavoidable означало бы неизбежный — это другое утверждение."},{"id":"4697bf5d-12d0-58cb-ba7b-f39f7bf6fc8c","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"translation","prompt":"Переведи осторожное описание результата.","position":4,"public_payload":{"source":"Исследование не установило эффект; это не равнозначно доказательству его отсутствия."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The study did not establish an effect; this is not equivalent to proving its absence.","The study failed to establish an effect; that is not the same as proving that there was none."]},"reference_answer":"The study did not establish an effect; this is not equivalent to proving its absence.","incorrect_answer":"The study conclusively proved that there was no effect.","explanation":"Нужно сохранить различие между failed to establish и proved absence; conclusively неоправданно усиливает вывод."},{"id":"4846f65f-a3f5-551c-801b-529fb223355c","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Выбери два точных различия значений.","position":5,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"A disinterested reviewer need not be an uninterested reviewer."},{"id":"o2","label":"An inconclusive result is always proof of complete ineffectiveness."},{"id":"o3","label":"An inadvertent error need not be an unavoidable error."}]},"answer_key":{"value":["o1","o3"]},"reference_answer":["o3","o1"],"incorrect_answer":["o2"],"explanation":"Непреднамеренность не означает неизбежность; беспристрастность не означает отсутствие интереса."},{"id":"fe249a39-12a7-5f18-8274-f12915791699","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь согласование, сохранив осторожный вывод.","position":6,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The absence of clear findings do not establish that the intervention is ineffective."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The absence of clear findings does not establish that the intervention is ineffective."]},"reference_answer":"The absence of clear findings does not establish that the intervention is ineffective.","incorrect_answer":"The absence of clear findings proves that the intervention is ineffective.","explanation":"Подлежащее absence в единственном числе требует does not. Осторожный смысл нельзя заменять на proves."},{"id":"8ed6d33e-d200-5d8d-ac72-807739283f5a","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери ответ, который не подменяет отсутствие доказательств доказательством отсутствия.","position":7,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"o1","label":"No; an undetected benefit must therefore exist."},{"id":"o2","label":"Not on that basis alone; we need to consider what effects the study could reliably detect."},{"id":"o3","label":"Yes; any failure to detect something proves it impossible."}],"lines":[{"speaker":"Colleague","text":"The pilot did not establish a benefit. Can we say there is definitely none?"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"o2"},"reference_answer":"o2","incorrect_answer":"o1","explanation":"Нужно учитывать различающую способность исследования; ни отсутствие, ни наличие пользы автоматически не доказано."},{"id":"0b239d81-4273-5a5d-b903-9a2ac8a1fc83","lesson_id":"18df9422-22c8-5cc5-ad3d-915b70fa0d15","kind":"unit_test","prompt":"Проверь подтекст, оговорки и точность C2.","position":8,"public_payload":{"questions":[{"id":"q1","prompt":"Что означает qualified praise в аналитическом тексте?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Praise without any reservation."},{"id":"o2","label":"Praise limited by reservations."}]},{"id":"q2","prompt":"Что нужно сохранить при упрощении формального условия?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"Only the shortest possible wording."},{"id":"o2","label":"Its exceptions, conditions and modal force."}]},{"id":"q3","prompt":"Что позволяет заключить один лишь inconclusive result?","options":[{"id":"o1","label":"That one side has been conclusively proved."},{"id":"o2","label":"That the available evidence does not settle the issue."}]}]},"answer_key":{"answers":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o2","q3":"o2"},"explanations":{"q1":"Qualified ограничивает похвалу оговорками.","q2":"Простота не оправдывает потерю условий, исключений и модальной силы.","q3":"Inconclusive — не позволяющий решить вопрос на имеющихся данных."}},"reference_answer":{"q1":"o2","q2":"o2","q3":"o2"},"incorrect_answer":{"q1":"o1","q2":"o2","q3":"o2"},"explanation":"Контрольный блок засчитывается при всех верных ответах. Разбор каждого вопроса показан отдельно."},{"id":"5b403298-4069-5997-9db2-71b2048116e7","lesson