806","label":"The mechanic replaced the tyres instead."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vac8dafaea686"},"reference_answer":"vac8dafaea686","incorrect_answer":"v725cf760283f","explanation":"The chain replaced в конструкции had the chain replaced сообщает о замене цепи."},{"id":"9a04adb4-8ff7-558c-b662-2b2a1b1b1341","lesson_id":"f80cc913-eb26-5bee-a633-7d5095d1ba83","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему шины не заменили?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"Before a long cycling trip, Eva took her bicycle to a repair shop. She had the brakes checked and the chain replaced. The mechanic said that the tyres were still in good condition, so replacing them was unnecessary. Eva had expected a larger bill and appreciated the explanation. She kept the receipt in case a problem appeared during the shop’s warranty period. The visit prepared the bicycle for the journey, although it could not remove every possible risk on the road.","options":[{"id":"v5917fb3ef3d6","label":"The shop had lost the receipt."},{"id":"v897bd4e9a663","label":"The warranty prohibited all tyre repairs."},{"id":"vac28deeda6db","label":"They were still in good condition."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vac28deeda6db"},"reference_answer":"vac28deeda6db","incorrect_answer":"v5917fb3ef3d6","explanation":"Механик счёл замену ненужной из-за состояния шин."},{"id":"f687a38c-9bad-5248-b247-d6abd7c8844e","lesson_id":"f80cc913-eb26-5bee-a633-7d5095d1ba83","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Уточни, что работу выполнил приглашённый специалист.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Did you paint the kitchen yourself?"}],"options":[{"id":"va47eb7da03f5","label":"No, I had it painted by a local decorator."},{"id":"vda6e7f1407ea","label":"No, I had it paint by a local decorator."},{"id":"v56d9dab32dfd","label":"No, I was paint by a local decorator."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va47eb7da03f5"},"reference_answer":"va47eb7da03f5","incorrect_answer":"vda6e7f1407ea","explanation":"Had it painted by ... обозначает заказанную работу, а не самостоятельное выполнение."},{"id":"627f3e53-76bb-530c-8727-ea354d76c664","lesson_id":"f80cc913-eb26-5bee-a633-7d5095d1ba83","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A written promise to deal with certain faults during a set period is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v1459fd546b0b","label":"forecast"},{"id":"va1d97ae4d55c","label":"departure"},{"id":"vec8ada126c89","label":"warranty"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vec8ada126c89"},"reference_answer":"vec8ada126c89","incorrect_answer":"v1459fd546b0b","explanation":"Warranty — гарантийное обязательство с установленными условиями."},{"id":"b90eeb4f-6d35-5b9d-a4f8-6c85dca29294","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Several outlets now report a discovery made last week. The team is said ___ a new route.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vbc0ae562e015","label":"to have discovered"},{"id":"va39a0707395c","label":"to discovering"},{"id":"v832af2980a1c","label":"have discover"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbc0ae562e015"},"reference_answer":"vbc0ae562e015","incorrect_answer":"va39a0707395c","explanation":"Открытие предшествует нынешним сообщениям: to have discovered."},{"id":"0e310626-2389-51c0-8270-0caae253d5fc","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: reported / reporting.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"It is ___ that the bridge will reopen in May."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["reported"]},"reference_answer":"reported","incorrect_answer":"reporting","explanation":"В безличной пассивной конструкции требуется reported."},{"id":"4658d708-b1fe-57c0-b538-17d2c1b8fd46","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Считается, что архив содержит неопубликованные письма.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"is"},{"id":"t4","label":"believed"},{"id":"t5","label":"to"},{"id":"t6","label":"contain"},{"id":"t7","label":"unpublished"},{"id":"t8","label":"letters."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"archive"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Is believed приписывает утверждение существующему мнению и не доказывает его истинность."},{"id":"cecadb76-1d9b-56a6-a5f0-4c1dc4d22b37","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The researcher is said have found the original map."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The researcher is said to have found the original map."]},"reference_answer":"The researcher is said to have found the original map.","incorrect_answer":"The researcher is said have found the original map.","explanation":"После is said требуется to; to have found выражает более раннюю находку."},{"id":"c962ae54-7480-5af7-824b-df9d2b457940","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что подтвердил совет?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A local newspaper reported that a previously unknown footpath had been found near the coast. Several websites repeated the story, describing the path as an ancient trading route. The original article, however, quoted only one resident and included no archaeological assessment. The council confirmed that a path existed but said that its age and historical use had not been established. A careful summary would distinguish the confirmed existence of the path from the unverified claim about its role in trade.","options":[{"id":"vce632d621870","label":"That it was an ancient trading route."},{"id":"va78c8357e56b","label":"That an archaeological study had dated it."},{"id":"vb6f68347e200","label":"That a path existed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb6f68347e200"},"reference_answer":"vb6f68347e200","incorrect_answer":"vce632d621870","explanation":"Подтверждено существование пути, а не возраст и использование."},{"id":"5ce85000-ef55-590e-ba8b-333e5fd52718","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как лучше передать историческую версию?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A local newspaper reported that a previously unknown footpath had been found near the coast. Several websites repeated the story, describing the path as an ancient trading route. The original article, however, quoted only one resident and included no archaeological assessment. The council confirmed that a path existed but said that its age and historical use had not been established. A careful summary would distinguish the confirmed existence of the path from the unverified claim about its role in trade.","options":[{"id":"vcebd81ecd592","label":"As evidence that no path exists."},{"id":"v154b261c6359","label":"As an unverified claim, not an established fact."},{"id":"v3afbb748b1f5","label":"As proof accepted by archaeologists."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v154b261c6359"},"reference_answer":"v154b261c6359","incorrect_answer":"v3afbb748b1f5","explanation":"Нужно сохранить различие между подтверждённым фактом и непроверенной интерпретацией."},{"id":"347435d2-9e7e-509b-ae55-63ca691400c7","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани статус сообщения и незавершённой проверки.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can we say the painting is definitely authentic?"}],"options":[{"id":"v772090b3c65b","label":"Yes; reported means formally proved."},{"id":"ve2e557ce9c6b","label":"No; being examined means it is certainly fake."},{"id":"v83efc3bb9628","label":"Not yet; it is reported to be authentic, but experts are still examining it."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v83efc3bb9628"},"reference_answer":"v83efc3bb9628","incorrect_answer":"v772090b3c65b","explanation":"Reported не равнозначно proved; продолжающаяся проверка также не доказывает подделку."},{"id":"9eb16463-8c51-5a69-9665-cbe9e0195c22","lesson_id":"a01adf6c-e625-5e64-a761-e399fb828146","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To check whether a statement is accurate is to ___ it.","options":[{"id":"vfa690bdb63c7","label":"improvise"},{"id":"v0071682042e8","label":"verify"},{"id":"v611ebfb6e0b9","label":"overlook"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0071682042e8"},"reference_answer":"v0071682042e8","incorrect_answer":"v611ebfb6e0b9","explanation":"Verify означает проверить достоверность, а не просто повторить сообщение."},{"id":"e501aeb9-3879-5de3-a6a3-38157c3af7af","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: ___ the figures, the analyst sent the revised report.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v01e9634e1d93","label":"Have checking"},{"id":"v9027146cd987","label":"Had checks"},{"id":"v752ca41067f4","label":"Having checked"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v752ca41067f4"},"reference_answer":"v752ca41067f4","incorrect_answer":"v01e9634e1d93","explanation":"Having checked обозначает проверку, завершённую до отправки."},{"id":"43561dce-5ac3-5623-aa91-f0a6164452e0","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: received / receiving.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Having ___ approval, the group began the trial."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["received"]},"reference_answer":"received","incorrect_answer":"receiving","explanation":"После having требуется причастие received."},{"id":"f1ee1df9-914f-51ad-b204-f7cc8be9c3fe","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Пересмотрев черновик, редактор отправил его обратно.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"the"},{"id":"t4","label":"draft,"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"editor"},{"id":"t7","label":"sent"},{"id":"t8","label":"it"},{"id":"t9","label":"back."},{"id":"t1","label":"Having"},{"id":"t2","label":"revised"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Исполнитель обоих действий — the editor; пересмотр предшествует отправке."},{"id":"267a67e9-4746-52a8-bc45-846312cf5301","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Having checked the room, the missing key was found by Anna."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Having checked the room, Anna found the missing key."]},"reference_answer":"Having checked the room, Anna found the missing key.","incorrect_answer":"Having checked the room, the missing key was found by Anna.","explanation":"Начальный оборот относится к Anna, поэтому она должна быть подлежащим основной части."},{"id":"b4c857ce-212e-5380-b9b0-f44598d088fb","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что координатор сделала после сбора предложений?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A volunteer group prepared a grant application for a community garden. Having collected residents’ suggestions, the coordinator revised the original budget. She removed a decorative gate and added more accessible planting beds. The group then submitted the application. Receiving acknowledgement of the application did not mean that funding had been approved: the committee would assess all proposals the following month. The coordinator told residents that preparations were complete, while the decision about money remained outside the group’s control.","options":[{"id":"v1b39923aa1d6","label":"She stopped the application before submission."},{"id":"v2f5680df8060","label":"She revised the budget."},{"id":"v271a83ed8dc9","label":"She announced that funding was guaranteed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2f5680df8060"},"reference_answer":"v2f5680df8060","incorrect_answer":"v271a83ed8dc9","explanation":"Having collected ... задаёт предшествующее действие перед пересмотром бюджета."},{"id":"7131f907-c268-58d8-81fe-1aefb42029dc","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что подтверждало уведомление о получении?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A volunteer group prepared a grant application for a community garden. Having collected residents’ suggestions, the coordinator revised the original budget. She removed a decorative gate and added more accessible planting beds. The group then submitted the application. Receiving acknowledgement of the application did not mean that funding had been approved: the committee would assess all proposals the following month. The coordinator told residents that preparations were complete, while the decision about money remained outside the group’s control.","options":[{"id":"v9a22d85efa48","label":"Only that the application had been received."},{"id":"vc9e3fb3c890b","label":"That the project had won funding."},{"id":"v1e6466cb3a39","label":"That no other proposals would be considered."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9a22d85efa48"},"reference_answer":"v9a22d85efa48","incorrect_answer":"vc9e3fb3c890b","explanation":"Acknowledgement отличается от approval; решение будет позже."},{"id":"55a863c4-c877-5bdb-bbd0-4a0e960f71be","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери предложение без «повисшего» причастного оборота.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Which sentence clearly makes the same person do both actions?"}],"options":[{"id":"v6d1ac15c8a40","label":"Having read the proposal, the deadline expired."},{"id":"vec4edbf5b1b1","label":"Having read the proposal, Omar signed it."},{"id":"v23d6cee18995","label":"Having read the proposal, the signature was added."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vec4edbf5b1b1"},"reference_answer":"vec4edbf5b1b1","incorrect_answer":"v23d6cee18995","explanation":"В первом варианте читает и подписывает Omar; в остальных подлежащие не могут читать."},{"id":"13cc7b7f-c8be-50ba-b90c-522babd1d589","lesson_id":"766417de-547f-5fa7-9a5b-9d6e88e9546b","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The committee’s formal agreement to the plan would be its ___.","options":[{"id":"vf01750af7413","label":"approval"},{"id":"v32d47bbc0fe9","label":"acknowledgement of receipt"},{"id":"ve86f176923e8","label":"revision"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf01750af7413"},"reference_answer":"vf01750af7413","incorrect_answer":"v32d47bbc0fe9","explanation":"Approval означает одобрение; уведомление о получении его не заменяет."},{"id":"64183621-fbec-5147-9acd-82c4a6cf3759","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: It was the unexpected delay ___ caused the confusion.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v118c383e88ef","label":"whose"},{"id":"v5cd9b4550993","label":"that"},{"id":"v904eaff59cae","label":"what"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5cd9b4550993"},"reference_answer":"v5cd9b4550993","incorrect_answer":"v904eaff59cae","explanation":"В этой cleft-конструкции после выделенной причины используется that."},{"id":"1975d085-fb57-5695-b3ea-154e9fc203f4","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: What / That.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"___ we needed was a clearer explanation of the rules."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["What"]},"reference_answer":"What","incorrect_answer":"That","explanation":"What we needed образует подлежащую часть со значением «то, что нам было нужно»."},{"id":"b129c087-1974-51fe-9ae7-ca752189022b","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Комитет беспокоил именно выбор времени.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"the"},{"id":"t4","label":"timing"},{"id":"t5","label":"that"},{"id":"t6","label":"worried"},{"id":"t7","label":"the"},{"id":"t8","label":"committee."},{"id":"t1","label":"It"},{"id":"t2","label":"was"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Выделение the timing сужает фокус до времени, а не содержания решения."},{"id":"851a1532-6c20-582e-81ed-e0051054151b","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"It was the unclear wording what caused the problem."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["It was the unclear wording that caused the problem."]},"reference_answer":"It was the unclear wording that caused the problem.","incorrect_answer":"It was the unclear wording what caused the problem.","explanation":"В конструкции It was ... that нужен that, а не what."},{"id":"f5d7802f-1ef4-5e05-b067-e98fa6a097b9","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что было предметом возражения?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"When the committee discussed the new booking system, several members were described as opposing the change. Their written comments told a more specific story. They supported the system itself but objected to introducing it during the busiest week of the year. One member explained, “It was the timing that worried us, not the idea.” The chair later revised the public summary to reflect that distinction. The launch date changed, while the main features of the system remained the same.","options":[{"id":"v73b51c39f2e3","label":"The timing of the introduction."},{"id":"v229e6c77aaac","label":"Every feature of the system."},{"id":"v0f3ceb5b265f","label":"The existence of any booking system."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v73b51c39f2e3"},"reference_answer":"v73b51c39f2e3","incorrect_answer":"v229e6c77aaac","explanation":"Комментарий противопоставляет timing и idea."},{"id":"71436725-dfcd-5629-ad19-383a566ebe19","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как изменился план после обсуждения?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"When the committee discussed the new booking system, several members were described as opposing the change. Their written comments told a more specific story. They supported the system itself but objected to introducing it during the busiest week of the year. One member explained, “It was the timing that worried us, not the idea.” The chair later revised the public summary to reflect that distinction. The launch date changed, while the main features of the system remained the same.","options":[{"id":"v179b767837c1","label":"The system was abandoned entirely."},{"id":"v108fb748a87e","label":"The busiest week was removed from the calendar."},{"id":"v4a687612de69","label":"The date changed but the main features stayed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4a687612de69"},"reference_answer":"v4a687612de69","incorrect_answer":"v179b767837c1","explanation":"Перенесли запуск, сохранив основные функции."},{"id":"cba44a81-3ef4-5746-8666-5162a475c0ef","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Уточни с помощью cleft-конструкции, что беспокоили правила отмены.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Was it the price that made you hesitate?"}],"options":[{"id":"vd037e4a82cfe","label":"No, it was the unclear cancellation policy that concerned me."},{"id":"v2166d58e8513","label":"No, it what unclear policy concerned."},{"id":"v631d627951fa","label":"No, it was concerned me the unclear policy."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd037e4a82cfe"},"reference_answer":"vd037e4a82cfe","incorrect_answer":"v2166d58e8513","explanation":"It was ... that выделяет конкретную причину сомнений."},{"id":"622a8a96-0291-5ee2-940b-64dbf148e7ec","lesson_id":"d7a67fe3-c1fb-5427-adb5-4f98d2fc51d3","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A request to explain an unclear statement is a request for ___.","options":[{"id":"vae5f5a26db03","label":"cancellation"},{"id":"v87eea29da06a","label":"competition"},{"id":"va09ea76e8a81","label":"clarification"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va09ea76e8a81"},"reference_answer":"va09ea76e8a81","incorrect_answer":"vae5f5a26db03","explanation":"Clarification означает прояснение смысла, а не отмену решения."},{"id":"16eeed5b-b024-545a-85be-0733d42e059e","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: ___ the heavy rain, attendance remained high.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vefc416a43cf4","label":"Despite"},{"id":"vd8a7a934c030","label":"Although"},{"id":"v597d0cbabc91","label":"Despite of"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vefc416a43cf4"},"reference_answer":"vefc416a43cf4","incorrect_answer":"vd8a7a934c030","explanation":"После despite стоит именная группа the heavy rain; although потребовало бы целую часть."},{"id":"26bf7db3-c0a6-5625-8ec8-150ab328de0f","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: was / being.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Although the venue ___ small, the organisers welcomed every registered guest."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["was"]},"reference_answer":"was","incorrect_answer":"being","explanation":"После although здесь требуется конечная форма was с подлежащим the venue."},{"id":"8b6687ab-2f96-5686-a716-80bcd1a52d5e","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Несмотря на потерю спонсора, фестиваль состоялся.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"a"},{"id":"t4","label":"sponsor,"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"festival"},{"id":"t7","label":"went"},{"id":"t8","label":"ahead."},{"id":"t1","label":"Despite"},{"id":"t2","label":"losing"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Despite принимает -ing-форму losing."},{"id":"06244241-7c1c-5d92-b2f2-7ada8741df02","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Despite of the delay, the meeting finished on time."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Despite the delay, the meeting finished on time."]},"reference_answer":"Despite the delay, the meeting finished on time.","incorrect_answer":"Despite of the delay, the meeting finished on time.","explanation":"Despite не требует предлога of."},{"id":"d001b12f-6b19-50bc-a248-b1a0ea1c2819","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как организаторы сократили расходы?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A neighbourhood festival lost one of its sponsors a month before opening. Despite this setback, the organisers decided not to cancel. They reduced the number of printed programmes and borrowed equipment from a nearby school. Attendance was lower than the previous year, although most scheduled activities took place. The organisers described the event as worthwhile but financially difficult. Their report did not call the festival a complete success or a failure; it recorded both the community benefit and the remaining budget problem.","options":[{"id":"vd50a5896df44","label":"They cancelled all scheduled activities."},{"id":"v26e138bde372","label":"They secured a larger sponsor immediately."},{"id":"va427eb5f7a49","label":"They printed fewer programmes and borrowed equipment."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va427eb5f7a49"},"reference_answer":"va427eb5f7a49","incorrect_answer":"vd50a5896df44","explanation":"Обе меры названы в тексте как ответ на потерю спонсора."},{"id":"8093c835-7157-5891-9d12-5b527990b9f8","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое резюме сохраняет баланс отчёта?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A neighbourhood festival lost one of its sponsors a month before opening. Despite this setback, the organisers decided not to cancel. They reduced the number of printed programmes and borrowed equipment from a nearby school. Attendance was lower than the previous year, although most scheduled activities took place. The organisers described the event as worthwhile but financially difficult. Their report did not call the festival a complete success or a failure; it recorded both the community benefit and the remaining budget problem.","options":[{"id":"v56392a819f99","label":"No activities took place because the sponsor left."},{"id":"v2ed0977760e5","label":"The event benefited the community despite financial difficulty."},{"id":"v71005e7db596","label":"High attendance solved every budget problem."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2ed0977760e5"},"reference_answer":"v2ed0977760e5","incorrect_answer":"v71005e7db596","explanation":"Нужно сохранить пользу события и финансовые сложности одновременно."},{"id":"6424e620-9d3d-5bfd-92b3-caaa2834bcea","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери уступку с правильной структурой.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How can we acknowledge the problem and still describe the result?"}],"options":[{"id":"v4b60e5fc5118","label":"Despite the start was delayed, the workshop finished on time."},{"id":"v95ae639b9a5b","label":"Although the delay, the workshop finished on time."},{"id":"v486f8242f7ba","label":"Although the start was delayed, the workshop finished on time."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v486f8242f7ba"},"reference_answer":"v486f8242f7ba","incorrect_answer":"v4b60e5fc5118","explanation":"Although + the start was delayed — полноценная часть с подлежащим и глаголом."},{"id":"243df77b-b56b-5727-a259-edf082fa8f3b","lesson_id":"973dc33e-9998-54d3-b74e-467a88176fbc","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We had to ___ the match until Saturday rather than cancel it.","options":[{"id":"va81526623e71","label":"complete"},{"id":"v15c619cc9c29","label":"postpone"},{"id":"vbec897440fd9","label":"abandon permanently"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v15c619cc9c29"},"reference_answer":"v15c619cc9c29","incorrect_answer":"vbec897440fd9","explanation":"Postpone означает перенести на более позднее время, а не отменить навсегда."},{"id":"8bee4fea-1803-52bd-bdee-b19dd1a67483","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: ___ the defect been disclosed earlier, the purchase might have been delayed.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vf5b6d6666789","label":"Should"},{"id":"v254e0f2f86e9","label":"Were to"},{"id":"v6bad5905d304","label":"Had"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v6bad5905d304"},"reference_answer":"v6bad5905d304","incorrect_answer":"vf5b6d6666789","explanation":"Had the defect been disclosed = If the defect had been disclosed; речь о прошлом."},{"id":"383179ab-fea9-5b52-876e-a18e4098d0e1","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: require / required.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Should you ___ further assistance, please contact the coordinator."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["require"]},"reference_answer":"require","incorrect_answer":"required","explanation":"После should в такой условной инверсии нужен инфинитив require."},{"id":"2b492b0a-e4e0-5667-8427-41c52349ca98","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Если бы риски тогда были понятнее, мы, возможно, пересмотрели бы решение.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"risks"},{"id":"t4","label":"been"},{"id":"t5","label":"clearer,"},{"id":"t6","label":"we"},{"id":"t7","label":"might"},{"id":"t8","label":"have"},{"id":"t9","label":"reconsidered."},{"id":"t1","label":"Had"},{"id":"t2","label":"the"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Had ... been выражает нереальное прошлое, might сохраняет неопределённость результата."},{"id":"3008eed4-8ad0-5573-99c3-8e144b281e43","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Had we knew about the restriction, we would have applied elsewhere."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Had we known about the restriction, we would have applied elsewhere."]},"reference_answer":"Had we known about the restriction, we would have applied elsewhere.","incorrect_answer":"Had we knew about the restriction, we would have applied elsewhere.","explanation":"После инвертированного had требуется причастие known, не knew."},{"id":"edd9aa6f-ed22-5fa0-aa9e-5d7c66ef633e","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"reading","prompt":"Зачем в ответе сохранено might?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The supplier’s letter acknowledged that an inspection had identified a fault before the equipment was shipped. It did not say when the purchasing team had been informed. “Had the defect been disclosed prior to dispatch, we might have reconsidered acceptance,” the buyer replied. The wording deliberately left two matters open: whether timely disclosure had occurred and what decision the buyer would then have made. A colleague proposed replacing might with would, but the legal adviser objected. The available records supported concern about the process, not certainty about an alternative decision. The final response therefore requested the dated inspection report rather than alleging deliberate concealment.","options":[{"id":"v64450ba1cd77","label":"To confirm deliberate concealment by the supplier."},{"id":"v64c2bca1e782","label":"To avoid claiming certainty about a hypothetical decision."},{"id":"v2bb35ff3fe86","label":"To state that the defect never existed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v64c2bca1e782"},"reference_answer":"v64c2bca1e782","incorrect_answer":"v2bb35ff3fe86","explanation":"Might не превращает возможный пересмотр в гарантированное альтернативное решение."},{"id":"6043c0c0-4086-5570-8667-77fa8b60b8ef","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какие сведения запросили в итоге?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"The supplier’s letter acknowledged that an inspection had identified a fault before the equipment was shipped. It did not say when the purchasing team had been informed. “Had the defect been disclosed prior to dispatch, we might have reconsidered acceptance,” the buyer replied. The wording deliberately left two matters open: whether timely disclosure had occurred and what decision the buyer would then have made. A colleague proposed replacing might with would, but the legal adviser objected. The available records supported concern about the process, not certainty about an alternative decision. The final response therefore requested the dated inspection report rather than alleging deliberate concealment.","options":[{"id":"v134a439dbe6a","label":"The dated inspection report."},{"id":"v45c66adff451","label":"A statement admitting deliberate concealment."},{"id":"ve6cb7ee65779","label":"Proof that the buyer would certainly have refused acceptance."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v134a439dbe6a"},"reference_answer":"v134a439dbe6a","incorrect_answer":"v45c66adff451","explanation":"Запрос направлен на недостающую хронологию, а не на заранее установленную вину."},{"id":"a6a91a96-4668-5684-bd35-34e8bf19b6dd","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери формальное условие о возможных затруднениях.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How should we offer help in a formal conditional?"}],"options":[{"id":"v6dbd30fd3618","label":"Had any difficulties arise tomorrow, please notify the project lead."},{"id":"v3e098b4ebf84","label":"Should any difficulties arise, please notify the project lead."},{"id":"v8d2f8686fa43","label":"Should any difficulties arose, please notify the project lead."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3e098b4ebf84"},"reference_answer":"v3e098b4ebf84","incorrect_answer":"v8d2f8686fa43","explanation":"Should + подлежащее + arise описывает возможную будущую ситуацию."},{"id":"01ef208c-660f-5d13-801c-7d7aaa5e703f","lesson_id":"e63a36c0-a88d-5258-bec4-8c6ebd192880","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Information given before dispatch constitutes ___ disclosure.","options":[{"id":"vc785b8819896","label":"prior"},{"id":"vdd19ea6f72e4","label":"subsequent"},{"id":"v2527f2ffc14f","label":"simultaneous only"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc785b8819896"},"reference_answer":"vc785b8819896","incorrect_answer":"vdd19ea6f72e4","explanation":"Prior означает предшествующий; subsequent — последующий."},{"id":"8d58848f-27ab-587f-8522-6edec63b7839","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Choose neutral contrastive fronting: “The financial cost ___; the delay we could not.”","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vcd3283ec0759","label":"we could absorbed"},{"id":"v9c981c6ab1fe","label":"we could absorb"},{"id":"ve85e65b6dcdd","label":"could we absorb"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9c981c6ab1fe"},"reference_answer":"v9c981c6ab1fe","incorrect_answer":"ve85e65b6dcdd","explanation":"При выносе объекта the financial cost сохраняется we could absorb."},{"id":"653ed516-0918-511b-b98f-af983c8819fe","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: could / must to.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The budget we could revise; the legal deadline we ___ not change."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["could"]},"reference_answer":"could","incorrect_answer":"must to","explanation":"Модальный could с not change обозначает отсутствие возможности изменить срок."},{"id":"87f6c7b8-3711-51bd-a722-120f9ee8a163","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Расходы мы могли взять на себя, а задержку — нет.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"we"},{"id":"t4","label":"could"},{"id":"t5","label":"absorb;"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"delay"},{"id":"t8","label":"we"},{"id":"t9","label":"could"},{"id":"t10","label":"not."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"cost"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t1"],"explanation":"Два вынесенных объекта противопоставляют приемлемую и неприемлемую стороны решения."},{"id":"d7b2b179-78d0-58e0-90a9-e179808b84be","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The revised budget could we accept; the revised deadline we could not."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The revised budget we could accept; the revised deadline we could not."]},"reference_answer":"The revised budget we could accept; the revised deadline we could not.","incorrect_answer":"The revised budget could we accept; the revised deadline we could not.","explanation":"В заданном контрастивном выносе объекта нет основания для could we."},{"id":"bd75df82-80d1-5c05-b9cc-11300407da57","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую функцию выполняет контраст в цитате?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A transport charity considered replacing its booking software midway through a busy season. The new system promised lower running costs, but migration would require a week without online bookings. In the board discussion, the treasurer said, “The additional training cost we could absorb; the interruption to service we could not.” This was not a rejection of the software’s long-term value. It distinguished a manageable expense from a short-term constraint that conflicted with the charity’s obligations. The board postponed migration until winter, when telephone demand was lower. Its minutes recorded a decision about timing and feasibility, rather than a conclusion that the proposed system was intrinsically unsuitable.","options":[{"id":"vd732d1ed777a","label":"It separates an affordable cost from an unacceptable interruption."},{"id":"v64b2e69b5170","label":"It claims that all costs and delays are equally manageable."},{"id":"vcd1f3ea0c55a","label":"It reverses the charity’s obligation to provide a service."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd732d1ed777a"},"reference_answer":"vd732d1ed777a","incorrect_answer":"v64b2e69b5170","explanation":"Вынос training cost и interruption подчёркивает разные оценки этих факторов."},{"id":"0a58afea-3874-562c-8920-49f35bc89131","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что было решено о самом программном обеспечении?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A transport charity considered replacing its booking software midway through a busy season. The new system promised lower running costs, but migration would require a week without online bookings. In the board discussion, the treasurer said, “The additional training cost we could absorb; the interruption to service we could not.” This was not a rejection of the software’s long-term value. It distinguished a manageable expense from a short-term constraint that conflicted with the charity’s obligations. The board postponed migration until winter, when telephone demand was lower. Its minutes recorded a decision about timing and feasibility, rather than a conclusion that the proposed system was intrinsically unsuitable.","options":[{"id":"v021ea3aad265","label":"It was judged intrinsically unsuitable in every season."},{"id":"v14302dc2940e","label":"It was installed immediately without interruption."},{"id":"v1b2c27f958e8","label":"Its long-term value was not rejected; migration was postponed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1b2c27f958e8"},"reference_answer":"v1b2c27f958e8","incorrect_answer":"v021ea3aad265","explanation":"Решение касалось сроков и осуществимости перехода, а не полного отказа."},{"id":"04647a42-dd29-55f6-ab51-e344f2d898e5","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани контраст между идеей и сроками.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “The proposal we welcomed; the timetable we questioned” reject everything?"}],"options":[{"id":"vdcc24c064583","label":"No; it accepts the proposal while challenging the timetable."},{"id":"v5ea09e5c2f55","label":"Yes; both parts must express rejection."},{"id":"v7600e5dc3c27","label":"No; it guarantees approval of every later revision."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vdcc24c064583"},"reference_answer":"vdcc24c064583","incorrect_answer":"v5ea09e5c2f55","explanation":"Welcomed и questioned имеют разные объекты; общее одобрение всех будущих изменений не следует."},{"id":"b24bbd92-6c6d-5b0f-93a7-28c0b98061ec","lesson_id":"9c2f10a0-899f-5898-80a1-6da9b84b612d","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Balancing lower cost against a slower service involves a ___.","options":[{"id":"vfd19ab9123fd","label":"guarantee"},{"id":"v5341fa589733","label":"typographical error"},{"id":"v2fcf80652e14","label":"trade-off"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2fcf80652e14"},"reference_answer":"v2fcf80652e14","incorrect_answer":"vfd19ab9123fd","explanation":"Trade-off — выбор между конкурирующими преимуществами и недостатками."},{"id":"6619b040-fc9e-5e8b-9670-4e44d6de3ecf","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Several participants withdrew, ___ reduced the sample size.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v986238326cef","label":"which"},{"id":"v736b64ca18d0","label":"who"},{"id":"v3571a04642c6","label":"whose"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v986238326cef"},"reference_answer":"v986238326cef","incorrect_answer":"v736b64ca18d0","explanation":"Which относится к факту выбывания, а не заменяет обозначение людей who."},{"id":"0b046a3c-d748-560f-aaeb-12e7b99b9d16","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: This / These.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The trial ended early. ___ limited the conclusions researchers could draw."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["This"]},"reference_answer":"This","incorrect_answer":"These","explanation":"This отсылает к целой ситуации досрочного завершения."},{"id":"a60e6865-e5b5-5fb7-945d-39f6546877cf","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Выборка сократилась, что ослабило сравнение.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"shrank,"},{"id":"t4","label":"which"},{"id":"t5","label":"weakened"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"comparison."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"sample"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Which оценивает следствие всей предшествующей части."},{"id":"c380a6e0-a1fd-5bb2-acdc-2db348cb8bac","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The funding was withdrawn, who forced the team to stop."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The funding was withdrawn, which forced the team to stop."]},"reference_answer":"The funding was withdrawn, which forced the team to stop.","incorrect_answer":"The funding was withdrawn, who forced the team to stop.","explanation":"Отсылка к ситуации требует which, а не личного who."},{"id":"d3d5d638-deaa-577f-a658-1149464b2552","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"reading","prompt":"К чему относится This во втором смысловом звене?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A report described a training trial involving volunteers from three departments. Several participants left after a change in their work schedules. This reduced the number of observations available for comparison, but the report did not attribute the departures to dissatisfaction with the training. One summary replaced “this” with “the training”, creating the impression that the programme itself had driven people away. The authors corrected that summary. Their concern was not simply grammatical elegance: an unclear reference had altered the implied explanation. They specified that schedule-related attrition limited the comparison and that the evidence did not establish how satisfied the departing volunteers had been.","options":[{"id":"v7bbfd49ed309","label":"A proven negative effect of the training."},{"id":"v62d10300b8e7","label":"A survey establishing dissatisfaction."},{"id":"v22d0d5730393","label":"The participants’ departure after schedule changes."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v22d0d5730393"},"reference_answer":"v22d0d5730393","incorrect_answer":"v7bbfd49ed309","explanation":"This подхватывает событие выбытия, а не утверждение о качестве программы."},{"id":"40267eb0-921a-53ee-ae57-4a92c462ebd1","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему исправление отсылки существенно?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A report described a training trial involving volunteers from three departments. Several participants left after a change in their work schedules. This reduced the number of observations available for comparison, but the report did not attribute the departures to dissatisfaction with the training. One summary replaced “this” with “the training”, creating the impression that the programme itself had driven people away. The authors corrected that summary. Their concern was not simply grammatical elegance: an unclear reference had altered the implied explanation. They specified that schedule-related attrition limited the comparison and that the evidence did not establish how satisfied the departing volunteers had been.","options":[{"id":"v314ee5ea67f0","label":"Every use of this is grammatically incorrect."},{"id":"v71424d5659c6","label":"The unclear reference had implied an unsupported cause."},{"id":"v7d22562cb5ea","label":"The authors wanted to hide a completed satisfaction survey."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v71424d5659c6"},"reference_answer":"v71424d5659c6","incorrect_answer":"v7d22562cb5ea","explanation":"Проблема в искажённой причинной интерпретации, не в запрете местоимения."},{"id":"ebf8ee0b-9edb-53a8-a859-5348578fed69","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Определи отсылку к целой ситуации.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"The session was cancelled. This disappointed the volunteers. What does “this” most naturally refer to?"}],"options":[{"id":"vff6ba6ae41e1","label":"The spelling of volunteers."},{"id":"v5f9cd1782e17","label":"A new claim that volunteers cancelled it themselves."},{"id":"v9d84e58cdf01","label":"The cancellation of the session."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9d84e58cdf01"},"reference_answer":"v9d84e58cdf01","incorrect_answer":"vff6ba6ae41e1","explanation":"Указательное местоимение подхватывает отмену; исполнитель отмены не уточняется."},{"id":"cef8e02d-7969-5a70-bfe3-a115d42c6f99","lesson_id":"eb6a9b2e-6fff-580b-9c29-a228936552b2","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Loss of participants during a study is known as ___.","options":[{"id":"v33429e89214b","label":"replication"},{"id":"v8759f0674290","label":"attrition"},{"id":"vde4da53bdd8a","label":"allocation"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8759f0674290"},"reference_answer":"v8759f0674290","incorrect_answer":"vde4da53bdd8a","explanation":"Attrition — выбывание; allocation — распределение, replication — повторение исследования."},{"id":"ac6473fc-d5f3-5500-b897-7eada8da2ebe","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The proposal would benefit ___ a clearer explanation of maintenance costs.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vad66253673d5","label":"of"},{"id":"vc192966280f5","label":"to"},{"id":"v54fae8647e60","label":"from"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v54fae8647e60"},"reference_answer":"v54fae8647e60","incorrect_answer":"vad66253673d5","explanation":"Устойчивое выражение benefit from указывает, какое улучшение было бы полезно."},{"id":"51b873bc-639c-5661-b97f-e77bad418be6","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: substantiated / substantiating.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The projected saving remains insufficiently ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["substantiated"]},"reference_answer":"substantiated","incorrect_answer":"substantiating","explanation":"После remains нужна характеристика утверждения: insufficiently substantiated."},{"id":"02d31847-7707-55ca-89f7-0f679a32563f","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Оценка требует дополнительного обоснования.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"requires"},{"id":"t4","label":"further"},{"id":"t5","label":"justification."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"estimate"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t1"],"explanation":"Критика относится к оценке, не приписывая автору личных недостатков."},{"id":"b074255d-7805-5daf-a4b5-539a4dc311f2","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The plan would benefit of a clearer risk assessment."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The plan would benefit from a clearer risk assessment."]},"reference_answer":"The plan would benefit from a clearer risk assessment.","incorrect_answer":"The plan would benefit of a clearer risk assessment.","explanation":"В этом значении нужно benefit from, а не benefit of."},{"id":"3af220bb-5784-55a2-a80c-5e2b0fa8b628","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что инженер поддерживала?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a design review, an engineer wrote that a proposal was “optimistic”. The project manager initially read this as a dismissive judgement of the whole team. In a follow-up note, the engineer specified that the projected savings excluded maintenance costs and depended on an untested assumption about demand. She supported a small pilot but did not recommend full implementation on the evidence available. The clarification made the disagreement actionable: the team could revise the calculation and test the assumption. It also preserved the distinction between questioning a forecast and questioning the competence or intentions of the people who had prepared it.","options":[{"id":"ve57b4c9e22ee","label":"Abandoning any attempt to revise the calculation."},{"id":"vb196c27bf31e","label":"A small pilot, rather than full implementation."},{"id":"v755ba16aaa01","label":"Immediate full implementation without further evidence."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb196c27bf31e"},"reference_answer":"vb196c27bf31e","incorrect_answer":"v755ba16aaa01","explanation":"Поддержка пилота не равна поддержке немедленного полномасштабного внедрения."},{"id":"3ceb16e6-50eb-50a5-9416-06097d057232","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему уточнение сделало критику практичной?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a design review, an engineer wrote that a proposal was “optimistic”. The project manager initially read this as a dismissive judgement of the whole team. In a follow-up note, the engineer specified that the projected savings excluded maintenance costs and depended on an untested assumption about demand. She supported a small pilot but did not recommend full implementation on the evidence available. The clarification made the disagreement actionable: the team could revise the calculation and test the assumption. It also preserved the distinction between questioning a forecast and questioning the competence or intentions of the people who had prepared it.","options":[{"id":"vb2c92c236fa1","label":"It identified omissions and an assumption that could be checked."},{"id":"v5595ec52f914","label":"It proved that the team had dishonest intentions."},{"id":"vc12d751aafe9","label":"It removed every disagreement about future demand."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb2c92c236fa1"},"reference_answer":"vb2c92c236fa1","incorrect_answer":"v5595ec52f914","explanation":"Указаны проверяемые элементы расчёта; личная нечестность не устанавливается."},{"id":"58ab9e52-e162-5676-a0af-f9d75b5d6a77","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери конструктивный запрос к основанию оценки.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Which reply challenges the claim without attacking its author?"}],"options":[{"id":"v76128cf3ca79","label":"Your intention must have been to mislead us."},{"id":"v92df5bf71c0f","label":"Could you explain how the estimate accounts for maintenance?"},{"id":"v252e395e423a","label":"Only an incompetent person would produce that estimate."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v92df5bf71c0f"},"reference_answer":"v92df5bf71c0f","incorrect_answer":"v252e395e423a","explanation":"Вопрос о методе расчёта проверяем; два других варианта приписывают личные качества и намерения."},{"id":"1bbb46d0-85b5-5e80-aa1b-ebab0c647a43","lesson_id":"3639bcf8-8237-50c3-97c7-f1d075ff3938","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A proposal that can realistically be carried out is ___.","options":[{"id":"v197c5da95a3e","label":"feasible"},{"id":"ve99b63333f58","label":"infallible"},{"id":"v21ac6de1e0d2","label":"retrospective"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v197c5da95a3e"},"reference_answer":"v197c5da95a3e","incorrect_answer":"ve99b63333f58","explanation":"Feasible означает осуществимый, а не безошибочный или относящийся к прошлому."},{"id":"35ba1135-627c-5882-9ea7-30a121ae3a96","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Not all reviewers supported the proposal. This means the support was ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v2aa053c4a356","label":"unanimously positive"},{"id":"vb8bbe91c93e0","label":"not unanimous"},{"id":"v9e07d3d8afcc","label":"entirely absent"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb8bbe91c93e0"},"reference_answer":"vb8bbe91c93e0","incorrect_answer":"v9e07d3d8afcc","explanation":"Not all исключает полное единодушие, но не утверждает отсутствие поддержки."},{"id":"c88908e5-d401-5189-b9bd-2329912cbff9","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: all / none.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Not ___ applicants met the additional requirement; several needed further training."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["all"]},"reference_answer":"all","incorrect_answer":"none","explanation":"Several ... needed показывает исключения из множества кандидатов; конструкция not all."},{"id":"e4753e99-d13c-5d0b-a633-9b63a390a8cd","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Не каждый участник выполнил оба раздела.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"participant"},{"id":"t4","label":"completed"},{"id":"t5","label":"both"},{"id":"t6","label":"sections."},{"id":"t1","label":"Not"},{"id":"t2","label":"every"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t1"],"explanation":"Отрицается универсальность; из этого не следует, что никто не выполнил оба раздела."},{"id":"a5d05238-a327-5398-8f15-78bef283e3ff","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Not all of the comments was critical."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Not all of the comments were critical."]},"reference_answer":"Not all of the comments were critical.","incorrect_answer":"Not all of the comments was critical.","explanation":"Comments — множественное число; количественное отрицание не меняет согласование were."},{"id":"0a781bf3-9bfc-5026-942b-526362456ce2","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что допускает исходная формулировка not all?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The consultation summary stated that not all respondents favoured extending the opening hours. A headline paraphrased this as “Residents reject longer hours”. The underlying responses did not support that generalisation: some welcomed later access, some preferred the existing schedule, and others supported an extension only on weekends. The summary did not provide a representative estimate of opinion across the entire town, because participation was voluntary. A careful account therefore needed to preserve both the range of views and the limits of the sample. Neither unanimous support nor universal opposition could legitimately be inferred from the phrase “not all”.","options":[{"id":"v442ebea65bc0","label":"A mixture of supportive and non-supportive responses."},{"id":"v76e65c5d019f","label":"Proof that nobody supported any extension."},{"id":"vbdc43e77bf44","label":"Proof of unanimous support."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v442ebea65bc0"},"reference_answer":"v442ebea65bc0","incorrect_answer":"v76e65c5d019f","explanation":"Not all отрицает универсальность, а текст затем прямо описывает разные мнения."},{"id":"6264067c-2fdc-55a8-a6e6-e4278cb6dc81","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое дополнительное ограничение есть у опроса?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"The consultation summary stated that not all respondents favoured extending the opening hours. A headline paraphrased this as “Residents reject longer hours”. The underlying responses did not support that generalisation: some welcomed later access, some preferred the existing schedule, and others supported an extension only on weekends. The summary did not provide a representative estimate of opinion across the entire town, because participation was voluntary. A careful account therefore needed to preserve both the range of views and the limits of the sample. Neither unanimous support nor universal opposition could legitimately be inferred from the phrase “not all”.","options":[{"id":"v327d7db2bbd0","label":"The responses prove exactly what every resident thinks."},{"id":"ve4ac7da7e9f2","label":"Weekend views were excluded from the responses."},{"id":"ve8632fb8b926","label":"Voluntary participation may not represent the whole town."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve8632fb8b926"},"reference_answer":"ve8632fb8b926","incorrect_answer":"v327d7db2bbd0","explanation":"Самоотбор участников ограничивает обобщение на всех жителей."},{"id":"a3563c45-7d01-5aa4-bf39-e40434526434","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани область действия отрицания без усиления.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Someone says “Not every reviewer found an error.” Which paraphrase is safest?"}],"options":[{"id":"v99700989d221","label":"It is not true that every reviewer found an error."},{"id":"v295da3b8c27b","label":"No reviewer found an error."},{"id":"v2caefd969915","label":"Every reviewer found the same error."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v99700989d221"},"reference_answer":"v99700989d221","incorrect_answer":"v295da3b8c27b","explanation":"Первый вариант повторяет логическое содержание; none и every создают другие утверждения."},{"id":"0aed09ca-509f-5637-a3ae-475bbc090dbe","lesson_id":"c2b35960-25cc-5573-b87d-d25077cc2541","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A decision supported by every member is ___.","options":[{"id":"v96bb96a843d5","label":"conditional"},{"id":"v6229a27582c3","label":"inconclusive"},{"id":"v5c506f3d05fe","label":"unanimous"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5c506f3d05fe"},"reference_answer":"v5c506f3d05fe","incorrect_answer":"v96bb96a843d5","explanation":"Unanimous обозначает согласие всех, в отличие от частичного или условного согласия."},{"id":"7a906a8a-28e1-5dfe-b28d-3f051ec9f5ce","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The new service is ___ reliable than its predecessor, though failures remain frequent.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v7119e47df455","label":"more"},{"id":"vc9f45dcc8e9e","label":"most"},{"id":"v0af307cc0b70","label":"much than"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7119e47df455"},"reference_answer":"v7119e47df455","incorrect_answer":"vc9f45dcc8e9e","explanation":"Comparative more reliable сравнивает две версии и не утверждает абсолютную надёжность."},{"id":"fc30156f-80c4-5345-a519-42e7c4d9ed7c","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: number / amount.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A higher percentage does not necessarily mean a larger ___ of replies."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["number"]},"reference_answer":"number","incorrect_answer":"amount","explanation":"Replies — исчисляемое существительное, a larger number of replies."},{"id":"2a9dd373-72f2-520f-9fcc-b5d14a71f11e","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Пересмотренная модель показала лучший результат, чем исходная.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"model"},{"id":"t4","label":"performed"},{"id":"t5","label":"better"},{"id":"t6","label":"than"},{"id":"t7","label":"the"},{"id":"t8","label":"original."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"revised"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Сравнение с оригиналом не доказывает достаточное абсолютное качество."},{"id":"c08c1010-d43e-509a-9ecf-430104ad4591","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The second group had a more higher response rate."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The second group had a higher response rate."]},"reference_answer":"The second group had a higher response rate.","incorrect_answer":"The second group had a more higher response rate.","explanation":"Higher уже сравнительная степень; дополнительное more не нужно."},{"id":"ae4dc882-e6f9-501d-add8-f8e17aad0d5d","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"reading","prompt":"В каком отделе выше доля ответов?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"Two departments tested different invitation messages. Department A received forty replies from one hundred invitations, while department B received thirty replies from fifty. The second department therefore had a higher response rate but fewer replies in absolute terms. A manager described B’s message as “twice as effective”, overlooking both the different group sizes and the fact that the recipients had not been randomly assigned. The results could justify testing the messages more systematically, but they did not isolate wording as the cause of the difference. A clear comparison would report both the numbers and the proportions, together with the limits of the design.","options":[{"id":"v048765c2deb0","label":"A: forty out of one hundred, or forty per cent."},{"id":"v149d3bf6d906","label":"The response rates are identical."},{"id":"v0ae9b4ae48c7","label":"B: thirty out of fifty, or sixty per cent."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0ae9b4ae48c7"},"reference_answer":"v0ae9b4ae48c7","incorrect_answer":"v048765c2deb0","explanation":"B: 30/50 = 60%; A: 40/100 = 40%, хотя абсолютных ответов у A больше."},{"id":"66c7c9f1-bd74-5e5a-a035-3fb823406e2b","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему нельзя уверенно приписать разницу формулировке?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"Two departments tested different invitation messages. Department A received forty replies from one hundred invitations, while department B received thirty replies from fifty. The second department therefore had a higher response rate but fewer replies in absolute terms. A manager described B’s message as “twice as effective”, overlooking both the different group sizes and the fact that the recipients had not been randomly assigned. The results could justify testing the messages more systematically, but they did not isolate wording as the cause of the difference. A clear comparison would report both the numbers and the proportions, together with the limits of the design.","options":[{"id":"vf3fb40e4cffd","label":"The higher percentage proves that all recipients prefer B."},{"id":"v8a5c451d02b5","label":"Recipients were not randomly assigned, so other differences may matter."},{"id":"v967c22e4c596","label":"Both groups received exactly the same number of invitations."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8a5c451d02b5"},"reference_answer":"v8a5c451d02b5","incorrect_answer":"v967c22e4c596","explanation":"Дизайн не изолирует влияние формулировки от различий групп. Кроме того, 60% — это в полтора, а не в два раза больше 40%."},{"id":"7b8c1d6e-d5a7-58aa-8616-14e448e5d6be","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Различи относительное удешевление и доступность по цене.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “less expensive than before” establish affordability?"}],"options":[{"id":"v8910492d97ed","label":"Yes; any price reduction makes a product affordable."},{"id":"vc3afc717030e","label":"Yes; comparative adjectives always set an absolute standard."},{"id":"v347d9a395698","label":"No; the previous price may have been extremely high."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v347d9a395698"},"reference_answer":"v347d9a395698","incorrect_answer":"v8910492d97ed","explanation":"Сравнительный ориентир сам может быть очень дорогим."},{"id":"f916cc81-a2b0-5a6f-a5bb-376aa05953d6","lesson_id":"50bf4244-860b-56c1-acef-797e55d67893","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An explicit standard against which performance is judged is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v2b823fde4361","label":"distraction"},{"id":"v8bc558eb188f","label":"benchmark"},{"id":"vbff55037a6f0","label":"guarantee"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8bc558eb188f"},"reference_answer":"v8bc558eb188f","incorrect_answer":"vbff55037a6f0","explanation":"Benchmark — точка сравнения; он не является гарантией результата."},{"id":"2f5fd5c0-93bd-5c9c-8f45-9e008d83dea0","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The timetable change may ___ to better attendance, but the study cannot isolate its effect.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v072aa2c40ae8","label":"has contributed"},{"id":"v5592c07d0577","label":"having contributed"},{"id":"v7edf9229404a","label":"have contributed"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7edf9229404a"},"reference_answer":"v7edf9229404a","incorrect_answer":"v072aa2c40ae8","explanation":"После may нужен have contributed; may сохраняет неопределённость вклада."},{"id":"bc92d130-3356-5ffb-ae8d-a44061e69002","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: establish / established.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The observed association does not ___ causation."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["establish"]},"reference_answer":"establish","incorrect_answer":"established","explanation":"После does not требуется establish; смысл — не устанавливает причинную связь."},{"id":"17ea3dd2-0d94-584d-90e3-e2ae6f044f41","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Напоминание, возможно, способствовало улучшению.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"may"},{"id":"t4","label":"have"},{"id":"t5","label":"contributed"},{"id":"t6","label":"to"},{"id":"t7","label":"the"},{"id":"t8","label":"improvement."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"reminder"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"May have contributed допускает вклад, не объявляя его единственной доказанной причиной."},{"id":"738e3e35-baf3-532a-b9d7-b948167aff1a","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The findings suggests that several factors may be involved."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The findings suggest that several factors may be involved."]},"reference_answer":"The findings suggest that several factors may be involved.","incorrect_answer":"The findings suggests that several factors may be involved.","explanation":"Findings во множественном числе требует suggest; модальность вывода сохраняется."},{"id":"a33235fd-54a5-54bf-b8c4-b097bce85c43","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какие изменения совпали по времени с напоминаниями?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A clinic introduced text reminders and observed fewer missed appointments over the next two months. During the same period, it also extended evening opening hours and changed its booking procedure. The manager credited the reminders with the entire improvement. An analyst agreed that reminders were a plausible contributor but pointed out that the other changes offered alternative explanations. Without a comparison that separated these influences, the records could not establish how much of the improvement was attributable to each measure. The analyst recommended retaining the useful changes while designing a more informative evaluation, rather than treating uncertainty about causation as evidence that nothing had helped.","options":[{"id":"vd49f3cba8b79","label":"A controlled comparison isolated reminders from every other influence."},{"id":"vd409a3bd3935","label":"Evening hours and the booking procedure changed too."},{"id":"vaebceeb3f96a","label":"All appointments were abolished."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd409a3bd3935"},"reference_answer":"vd409a3bd3935","incorrect_answer":"vaebceeb3f96a","explanation":"Два дополнительных изменения могут влиять на посещаемость."},{"id":"969d6f00-8601-5bad-9c38-7e90d5c451db","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую позицию занимает аналитик?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A clinic introduced text reminders and observed fewer missed appointments over the next two months. During the same period, it also extended evening opening hours and changed its booking procedure. The manager credited the reminders with the entire improvement. An analyst agreed that reminders were a plausible contributor but pointed out that the other changes offered alternative explanations. Without a comparison that separated these influences, the records could not establish how much of the improvement was attributable to each measure. The analyst recommended retaining the useful changes while designing a more informative evaluation, rather than treating uncertainty about causation as evidence that nothing had helped.","options":[{"id":"v2a6c89e1b64b","label":"Keep useful changes while evaluating their separate contributions more carefully."},{"id":"v3cea913110b8","label":"Stop everything because causation has not been isolated."},{"id":"v4693d4ba7918","label":"Declare that the reminders certainly caused the entire improvement."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2a6c89e1b64b"},"reference_answer":"v2a6c89e1b64b","incorrect_answer":"v3cea913110b8","explanation":"Неопределённость вклада не равна доказательству бесполезности всех мер."},{"id":"3184719f-18fa-512d-8497-a041101ffc65","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани наблюдение и предел причинного вывода.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"What is the most defensible conclusion from an uncontrolled before-and-after comparison?"}],"options":[{"id":"v2469eb1cc612","label":"No intervention can ever be evaluated."},{"id":"vfdda0f7442ad","label":"The change coincided with improvement; its independent effect remains uncertain."},{"id":"v71bdd2b3ff81","label":"The change must be the only cause."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vfdda0f7442ad"},"reference_answer":"vfdda0f7442ad","incorrect_answer":"v71bdd2b3ff81","explanation":"Совпадение по времени не изолирует причинный эффект, но и не делает оценку принципиально невозможной."},{"id":"d8c6b45b-0dec-5432-8a97-f637ddfefd97","lesson_id":"f1612713-ccf6-51d5-8772-21c897d03597","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A factor that may distort an apparent causal relationship is a ___.","options":[{"id":"ve35729b71da6","label":"confounder"},{"id":"v0b28a2925cf8","label":"certificate"},{"id":"v2cb1ff53d2b1","label":"deadline"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve35729b71da6"},"reference_answer":"ve35729b71da6","incorrect_answer":"v0b28a2925cf8","explanation":"Confounder — фактор, связанный и с воздействием, и с результатом, который может искажать оценку их причинной связи."},{"id":"5f0b813c-3a9b-5297-b358-ecf4475060f6","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: According ___ the audit team, the records were incomplete.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v0caacb4d18cf","label":"by"},{"id":"vdd67cca6f4bd","label":"to"},{"id":"v1f60d3acf932","label":"with"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vdd67cca6f4bd"},"reference_answer":"vdd67cca6f4bd","incorrect_answer":"v1f60d3acf932","explanation":"According to — стандартная конструкция указания источника."},{"id":"fe9ce933-53b7-541f-ac24-e79b57072a09","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: corroborated / corroborating.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The account has not been independently ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["corroborated"]},"reference_answer":"corroborated","incorrect_answer":"corroborating","explanation":"Пассив has not been corroborated сообщает об отсутствии независимого подтверждения."},{"id":"8bb06fe8-aabf-5daa-b479-9397601f5c58","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Представитель отрицал, что данные были изменены.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"denied"},{"id":"t4","label":"that"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"figures"},{"id":"t7","label":"had"},{"id":"t8","label":"been"},{"id":"t9","label":"altered."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"spokesperson"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Отрицание представителя не равно независимому доказательству отсутствия изменений."},{"id":"925e9691-55b5-57f9-a66b-f279d6ad115f","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"According with the witness, the door was already open."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["According to the witness, the door was already open."]},"reference_answer":"According to the witness, the door was already open.","incorrect_answer":"According with the witness, the door was already open.","explanation":"Для приписывания сообщения свидетелю нужно according to."},{"id":"bb04306b-c497-54a4-b4b0-7783c83b7bdd","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"reading","prompt":"Кто первоначально выдвинул обвинение?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A newspaper quoted a former contractor who claimed that maintenance records had been altered. The company denied the allegation and said that an external review was underway. The article did not include the disputed records or a completed review report. In an internal summary, a reader wrote that the newspaper had “confirmed falsification”. That description collapsed attribution into endorsement: quoting a claim is not the same as establishing it. Equally, the company’s denial did not by itself settle the matter. A proportionate summary would identify the allegation, the denial and the unresolved review, without presenting any of them as a final independent finding.","options":[{"id":"v2b64595b3bf8","label":"A former contractor quoted by the newspaper."},{"id":"v9ebe2e6d09ac","label":"The external review’s completed report."},{"id":"vf3d77c29e695","label":"Every reader of the article."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2b64595b3bf8"},"reference_answer":"v2b64595b3bf8","incorrect_answer":"v9ebe2e6d09ac","explanation":"Источник обвинения — цитируемый бывший подрядчик; завершённого отчёта ещё нет."},{"id":"57185e1a-963c-5ac8-9293-0b2c63c9fbda","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое резюме точнее?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A newspaper quoted a former contractor who claimed that maintenance records had been altered. The company denied the allegation and said that an external review was underway. The article did not include the disputed records or a completed review report. In an internal summary, a reader wrote that the newspaper had “confirmed falsification”. That description collapsed attribution into endorsement: quoting a claim is not the same as establishing it. Equally, the company’s denial did not by itself settle the matter. A proportionate summary would identify the allegation, the denial and the unresolved review, without presenting any of them as a final independent finding.","options":[{"id":"v82c584ca7604","label":"Independent falsification has been conclusively confirmed."},{"id":"vcebcead946b2","label":"The denial alone proves that the records are accurate."},{"id":"v50ff0f2d91d3","label":"There is an allegation, a denial and an unresolved review."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v50ff0f2d91d3"},"reference_answer":"v50ff0f2d91d3","incorrect_answer":"v82c584ca7604","explanation":"Нужно различать утверждения сторон и ещё не завершённую проверку."},{"id":"86ebb81d-2a94-5a1c-af7e-4d15985852be","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Определи функцию указания источника.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “According to the applicant, the fee was waived” mean the writer independently verified it?"}],"options":[{"id":"v82759f2455b5","label":"No; it identifies the applicant as the source."},{"id":"va5e6de785084","label":"Yes; according to always means independently verified."},{"id":"v430c4fbd12da","label":"No; it proves the applicant is lying."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v82759f2455b5"},"reference_answer":"v82759f2455b5","incorrect_answer":"va5e6de785084","explanation":"Attribution не является ни независимой проверкой, ни доказательством лжи."},{"id":"606c0e7d-787e-5043-bd45-96de8bda4a04","lesson_id":"e64b825c-d1a7-5475-b3bb-f80adfeb3549","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Evidence from a separate source may ___ an account.","options":[{"id":"v3b8e822d3850","label":"postpone"},{"id":"v962f84eeed84","label":"translate automatically"},{"id":"v3ab64e4e1a93","label":"corroborate"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3ab64e4e1a93"},"reference_answer":"v3ab64e4e1a93","incorrect_answer":"v3b8e822d3850","explanation":"Corroborate означает подкрепить сообщение дополнительными данными."},{"id":"f53571a1-c56d-5ecb-bf5b-7a3d525037dc","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “The plan is not without merit, but its funding assumptions are untenable” expresses ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v1c5c7fb46b25","label":"qualified recognition with a substantive objection"},{"id":"v10a7e7d2bf4f","label":"unreserved approval of the funding"},{"id":"v637a91f8e8ba","label":"proof that the plan has no useful feature"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1c5c7fb46b25"},"reference_answer":"v1c5c7fb46b25","incorrect_answer":"v10a7e7d2bf4f","explanation":"Литота признаёт достоинства, а but вводит существенное возражение к финансированию."},{"id":"18873d22-3ea0-50e4-934a-ac020d32ad92","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: for / from.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Were it not ___ the unresolved funding gap, the recommendation would be favourable."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["for"]},"reference_answer":"for","incorrect_answer":"from","explanation":"Устойчивая условная конструкция were it not for означает «если бы не»."},{"id":"4b4ee7f9-5844-502a-b538-b65f8dfeb9b8","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Если бы не дефицит финансирования, рекомендация была бы благоприятной.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"not"},{"id":"t4","label":"for"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"funding"},{"id":"t7","label":"gap,"},{"id":"t8","label":"the"},{"id":"t9","label":"recommendation"},{"id":"t10","label":"would"},{"id":"t11","label":"be"},{"id":"t12","label":"favourable."},{"id":"t1","label":"Were"},{"id":"t2","label":"it"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t12"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t12"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t12","t1"],"explanation":"Конструкция представляет гипотезу; дефицит остаётся реальным ограничением."},{"id":"537f1b45-3fc3-5768-9b8c-8f4bbd05f925","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Were it not for the unresolved issue, the proposal will be acceptable."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Were it not for the unresolved issue, the proposal would be acceptable."]},"reference_answer":"Were it not for the unresolved issue, the proposal would be acceptable.","incorrect_answer":"Were it not for the unresolved issue, the proposal will be acceptable.","explanation":"Гипотетическому условию were it not for соответствует would, а не will."},{"id":"12b113fc-75c8-5da5-ad77-347858955cf1","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"reading","prompt":"В чём проблема сокращённой цитаты?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The panel’s chair described the proposal as “not without merit”, a phrase the publicity team immediately selected for its announcement. The rest of the sentence was less accommodating: the proposed benefits depended on funding commitments that had not been secured. A panel member objected to the abbreviated quotation, arguing that it converted a qualified acknowledgement into an apparent endorsement. The publicity team replied that every quoted word was accurate. That defence addressed literal transcription, not the implication created by omission. In the final notice, the chair’s reservation appeared alongside the acknowledgement of merit. Readers could then distinguish a potentially valuable idea from a recommendation to proceed under the conditions presently described. The panel had neither dismissed the idea outright nor licensed implementation.","options":[{"id":"v8e6e8c645b2b","label":"Every quoted word had been invented."},{"id":"v5abed2835201","label":"The panel had secretly approved unconditional implementation."},{"id":"vea0ed5d26ac7","label":"Accurate words implied a stronger endorsement once the reservation was omitted."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vea0ed5d26ac7"},"reference_answer":"vea0ed5d26ac7","incorrect_answer":"v8e6e8c645b2b","explanation":"Дословная точность слов не сохраняет смысл при удалении существенной оговорки."},{"id":"873f128f-6c00-559d-a3e6-b161c966b182","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какова позиция комиссии в полном контексте?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"The panel’s chair described the proposal as “not without merit”, a phrase the publicity team immediately selected for its announcement. The rest of the sentence was less accommodating: the proposed benefits depended on funding commitments that had not been secured. A panel member objected to the abbreviated quotation, arguing that it converted a qualified acknowledgement into an apparent endorsement. The publicity team replied that every quoted word was accurate. That defence addressed literal transcription, not the implication created by omission. In the final notice, the chair’s reservation appeared alongside the acknowledgement of merit. Readers could then distinguish a potentially valuable idea from a recommendation to proceed under the conditions presently described. The panel had neither dismissed the idea outright nor licensed implementation.","options":[{"id":"v46c1c8da5733","label":"Implementation has been authorised without further conditions."},{"id":"v757ba84abdea","label":"The idea has potential merit, but proceeding on the stated funding assumptions is not endorsed."},{"id":"vd49d4b16e2ed","label":"The proposal has no merit under any imaginable conditions."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v757ba84abdea"},"reference_answer":"v757ba84abdea","incorrect_answer":"vd49d4b16e2ed","explanation":"Текст исключает и полный отказ от идеи, и разрешение реализации на нынешних условиях."},{"id":"e983fef4-bf18-5d7b-ab7f-29df58ef30b5","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани силу условного одобрения.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can we describe “promising, subject to independent verification” simply as “approved”?"}],"options":[{"id":"vf559b0fd0a48","label":"Yes; subject to means regardless of verification."},{"id":"v8252551cf4a4","label":"Yes; promising always authorises implementation."},{"id":"v577aff3424d5","label":"No; that removes a condition on the favourable assessment."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v577aff3424d5"},"reference_answer":"v577aff3424d5","incorrect_answer":"vf559b0fd0a48","explanation":"Subject to делает проверку условием; promising не равно approved."},{"id":"28c42444-a012-5027-a34c-853d55e9b5e9","lesson_id":"f1e470e4-b32d-5d00-b954-3a7dab26747a","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An argument that can withstand reasoned criticism is ___.","options":[{"id":"vc19c942fd820","label":"unanimous"},{"id":"vf31b4f96ef2b","label":"tenable"},{"id":"v8db4a5a3d558","label":"infallible"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf31b4f96ef2b"},"reference_answer":"vf31b4f96ef2b","incorrect_answer":"v8db4a5a3d558","explanation":"Tenable — защищаемый аргумент; это не обещание безошибочности и не голосование."},{"id":"901fd7a7-8555-545a-bfab-89292ad1bb3d","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “The pattern would appear to support the account” is best understood as ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v29af49b558e4","label":"a binding promise of future support"},{"id":"vce8fb74e9e14","label":"a declaration that no alternative account is possible"},{"id":"v5eda5c7639a7","label":"a cautiously framed inference"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5eda5c7639a7"},"reference_answer":"v5eda5c7639a7","incorrect_answer":"v29af49b558e4","explanation":"Would appear to смягчает эпистемическую уверенность, а не обещает будущее действие."},{"id":"bfcec061-dd8c-56c2-8154-2820a9504c84","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: with / of.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The pattern is consistent ___ the hypothesis, though not uniquely explained by it."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["with"]},"reference_answer":"with","incorrect_answer":"of","explanation":"Consistent with означает совместимость, которая не устанавливает единственную причину."},{"id":"52154599-e6cf-5be8-9057-4c60c5c8399c","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «По-видимому, документы поддерживают более узкую интерпретацию.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"would"},{"id":"t4","label":"appear"},{"id":"t5","label":"to"},{"id":"t6","label":"support"},{"id":"t7","label":"a"},{"id":"t8","label":"narrower"},{"id":"t9","label":"interpretation."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"records"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Would appear to маркирует осторожный вывод, а не официальное окончательное установление."},{"id":"48a5b95d-2931-5caf-9045-7c15e84464ae","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The evidence is consistent to the account but does not establish it."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The evidence is consistent with the account but does not establish it."]},"reference_answer":"The evidence is consistent with the account but does not establish it.","incorrect_answer":"The evidence is consistent to the account but does not establish it.","explanation":"В этом значении используется consistent with."},{"id":"8d153731-e1e8-5266-8f14-2025f9aac9ce","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему формулировка «prove common authorship» слишком сильна?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"An archivist found that several letters had been copied in the same hand, although their signatures differed. One explanation was that a secretary had prepared correspondence for several authors. Another was that the letters were later copies made for the archive. The dates and paper stock were compatible with both accounts. In her catalogue note, the archivist wrote that the documents “would appear to reflect a shared copying practice”. A reviewer wanted this changed to “prove common authorship”. The archivist refused: a shared hand was an observation, while common authorship was one possible interpretation requiring additional evidence. Her caution did not deny the discovery’s significance. It prevented an attractive explanation from inheriting a degree of certainty that the surviving material could not sustain.","options":[{"id":"vffd2eaab410b","label":"The paper stock conclusively identified every author."},{"id":"va7577d44b8a3","label":"Shared handwriting is compatible with different explanations of authorship."},{"id":"v80a70c831e53","label":"The archivist found no similarity in handwriting."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va7577d44b8a3"},"reference_answer":"va7577d44b8a3","incorrect_answer":"v80a70c831e53","explanation":"Одинаковая рука могла принадлежать секретарю или позднему переписчику."},{"id":"01d7d281-d50c-5bf4-8b4f-3a5615feb28b","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как следует понимать осторожность архивиста?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"An archivist found that several letters had been copied in the same hand, although their signatures differed. One explanation was that a secretary had prepared correspondence for several authors. Another was that the letters were later copies made for the archive. The dates and paper stock were compatible with both accounts. In her catalogue note, the archivist wrote that the documents “would appear to reflect a shared copying practice”. A reviewer wanted this changed to “prove common authorship”. The archivist refused: a shared hand was an observation, while common authorship was one possible interpretation requiring additional evidence. Her caution did not deny the discovery’s significance. It prevented an attractive explanation from inheriting a degree of certainty that the surviving material could not sustain.","options":[{"id":"vaffec0533c52","label":"As a boundary on certainty, not a denial that the finding matters."},{"id":"v1a8ac50bed3c","label":"As proof that the letters are worthless."},{"id":"v846850ccb92f","label":"As a promise to reject any future evidence."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vaffec0533c52"},"reference_answer":"vaffec0533c52","incorrect_answer":"v1a8ac50bed3c","explanation":"Последние предложения прямо отделяют значимость наблюдения от силы вывода."},{"id":"ebb45b2a-e78f-55ee-94cf-3814826497c1","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Различи совместимость и однозначное доказательство.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Is evidence “compatible with” an explanation necessarily decisive for it?"}],"options":[{"id":"v49d6699bae1b","label":"Yes; a compatible account can never be revised."},{"id":"v2ac86fb649b5","label":"No; competing explanations may also accommodate the evidence."},{"id":"va3fdbda7e301","label":"Yes; compatibility excludes every competing explanation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2ac86fb649b5"},"reference_answer":"v2ac86fb649b5","incorrect_answer":"va3fdbda7e301","explanation":"Одни и те же данные могут согласовываться с несколькими версиями."},{"id":"c55011e1-77dc-59c9-b479-4a4daf3fbc65","lesson_id":"427394fd-47bc-56a0-8ebf-33b2dccd650e","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A proposition advanced without sufficient evidence for certainty is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v4a1959cd2740","label":"conjecture"},{"id":"v6d8e3ecd65cf","label":"verdict"},{"id":"v4c8dd80e54ed","label":"warranty"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4a1959cd2740"},"reference_answer":"v4a1959cd2740","incorrect_answer":"v6d8e3ecd65cf","explanation":"Conjecture — предположение, а не окончательное решение или гарантия."},{"id":"26ef1745-c8e4-50ba-9a22-92a295c17645","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “Only the external reviewers received the appendix” restricts ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v0e947d2d65f8","label":"whether any appendix existed"},{"id":"v418d9b5a27da","label":"who received the appendix"},{"id":"vc14ddd17f4f9","label":"which document the reviewers received"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v418d9b5a27da"},"reference_answer":"v418d9b5a27da","incorrect_answer":"vc14ddd17f4f9","explanation":"Only перед the external reviewers ограничивает получателей, не набор полученных документов."},{"id":"e0803b50-774a-5a90-8794-59ae8284a503","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: necessarily / necessary.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A lack of agreement does not ___ entail opposition to every clause."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["necessarily"]},"reference_answer":"necessarily","incorrect_answer":"necessary","explanation":"Not necessarily сохраняет возможность разных причин несогласия, а не утверждает их отсутствие."},{"id":"7bfe3c91-382f-527b-9baa-efe25372694d","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Конфиденциальное приложение получили только рецензенты.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"reviewers"},{"id":"t4","label":"received"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"confidential"},{"id":"t7","label":"appendix."},{"id":"t1","label":"Only"},{"id":"t2","label":"the"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Only ограничивает получателей; фраза не перечисляет все документы, полученные рецензентами."},{"id":"0b6f0464-143d-5349-8f47-c691c953b382","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The restriction does not necessary apply to every draft."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The restriction does not necessarily apply to every draft."]},"reference_answer":"The restriction does not necessarily apply to every draft.","incorrect_answer":"The restriction does not necessary apply to every draft.","explanation":"Нужна наречная форма necessarily, относящаяся к apply."},{"id":"91eb6628-d408-5196-8cc5-66ae56184249","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое утверждение не следует из исходного сообщения?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The editor’s message stated that only the external reviewers had received the confidential appendix. In a later account, this became “The reviewers received only the appendix”, which suggested that they had seen none of the main report. The original message made no such claim. Its restriction concerned recipients, not the set of documents supplied to those recipients. A second misunderstanding arose when the editor said that disagreement did not necessarily entail rejection: one participant paraphrased this as “Disagreement never means rejection”. Both errors replaced a limited statement with a different logical commitment. Clarifying the position of only and the force of necessarily restored the intended boundaries without resolving the substantive dispute about whether the report itself was persuasive.","options":[{"id":"v0017c20cca5f","label":"The reviewers received no part of the main report."},{"id":"v30afbc08e2a1","label":"The confidential appendix was received by external reviewers."},{"id":"v62c17f641cab","label":"The editor restricted the stated recipients of the appendix."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0017c20cca5f"},"reference_answer":"v0017c20cca5f","incorrect_answer":"v30afbc08e2a1","explanation":"Only ограничивало круг получателей, а не все полученные ими документы."},{"id":"67fd06e4-b48c-5799-9c00-b09a79c98086","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему never means rejection искажает not necessarily entail rejection?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"The editor’s message stated that only the external reviewers had received the confidential appendix. In a later account, this became “The reviewers received only the appendix”, which suggested that they had seen none of the main report. The original message made no such claim. Its restriction concerned recipients, not the set of documents supplied to those recipients. A second misunderstanding arose when the editor said that disagreement did not necessarily entail rejection: one participant paraphrased this as “Disagreement never means rejection”. Both errors replaced a limited statement with a different logical commitment. Clarifying the position of only and the force of necessarily restored the intended boundaries without resolving the substantive dispute about whether the report itself was persuasive.","options":[{"id":"v801a1ec97d2d","label":"The two expressions are exact logical equivalents."},{"id":"vd92a4164e99a","label":"It merely changes the tense without changing meaning."},{"id":"v3420ed0826e4","label":"It replaces denial of necessity with a universal exclusion."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3420ed0826e4"},"reference_answer":"v3420ed0826e4","incorrect_answer":"v801a1ec97d2d","explanation":"Not necessarily допускает разные случаи, never исключает связь во всех случаях."},{"id":"eea18420-2e81-59c9-bf75-296854b693f8","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани различие между отсутствием обязательного отрицания и доказанной истинностью.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “not necessarily false” establish truth?"}],"options":[{"id":"v25876cefc7d0","label":"No; it rejects a necessary falsity judgement without establishing truth."},{"id":"v6fb186f14b1f","label":"Yes; it always means conclusively true."},{"id":"v0423af6382d9","label":"Yes; uncertainty logically guarantees correctness."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v25876cefc7d0"},"reference_answer":"v25876cefc7d0","incorrect_answer":"v6fb186f14b1f","explanation":"Ограничение отрицательного вывода само по себе не доказывает противоположный."},{"id":"781c82fe-764a-5cf4-9826-1762ce71e8aa","lesson_id":"65d25549-e02a-5b5a-89d7-9d718affbdd8","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If a conclusion follows as a logical consequence, the premises ___ it.","options":[{"id":"v71b0a11911fe","label":"merely resemble"},{"id":"vc51dfed45a94","label":"postpone"},{"id":"vf050b98f38d3","label":"entail"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf050b98f38d3"},"reference_answer":"vf050b98f38d3","incorrect_answer":"v71b0a11911fe","explanation":"Entail описывает логическое следование, а не внешнее сходство."},{"id":"0e55b64f-4b98-5a69-af48-eb259bc343d7","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “Granted, the initial cost is lower; that does not settle the lifetime cost” concedes ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"va57ad867a52c","label":"one premise while resisting a broader conclusion"},{"id":"va679cd292ca5","label":"the whole case without reservation"},{"id":"v092a3af6e50c","label":"that lifetime cost is irrelevant"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va57ad867a52c"},"reference_answer":"va57ad867a52c","incorrect_answer":"va679cd292ca5","explanation":"Granted признаёт меньшую начальную цену, но не итоговую экономичность."},{"id":"45096703-fbf9-57b7-acbd-2afa2a493a14","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: if / despite.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Even ___ the forecast proves accurate, the distributional concern remains."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["if"]},"reference_answer":"if","incorrect_answer":"despite","explanation":"Even if вводит условную уступку; после despite полноценная часть так не присоединяется."},{"id":"40769b01-3110-5360-b447-81b3abcf6d1e","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Даже если экономия возникнет, проблема доступа останется.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"the"},{"id":"t4","label":"saving"},{"id":"t5","label":"materialises,"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"access"},{"id":"t8","label":"problem"},{"id":"t9","label":"remains."},{"id":"t1","label":"Even"},{"id":"t2","label":"if"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Уступка допускает экономию без принятия вывода о решённости всех проблем."},{"id":"331ab1a3-af22-5e5d-be12-cfef61ddd85f","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Even despite the estimates are correct, the policy needs revision."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Even if the estimates are correct, the policy needs revision."]},"reference_answer":"Even if the estimates are correct, the policy needs revision.","incorrect_answer":"Even despite the estimates are correct, the policy needs revision.","explanation":"Для полноценной условно-уступительной части здесь используется even if."},{"id":"15a8c179-751c-5d7b-90e8-5d73c763f4bd","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что выступающая признала?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"In a debate about replacing staffed counters with kiosks, one speaker conceded that kiosks could reduce the cost of routine transactions. She then argued that the saving did not answer the question of access for people unable to use them independently. Her opponent celebrated the concession as acceptance of the replacement policy. This conflated agreement on a possible efficiency gain with agreement on what should follow from it. The speaker’s argument was instead that, even if the saving materialised, an accessible alternative would still be required. She had not demonstrated that kiosks were always unsuitable, nor had she withdrawn the accessibility objection. Her concession narrowed the dispute to the conditions under which efficiency could justify a change in service.","options":[{"id":"vf88eba6bede8","label":"All staffed alternatives should immediately close."},{"id":"vfe73da6460a9","label":"Everyone can independently use a kiosk."},{"id":"v3911be344131","label":"Kiosks could reduce the cost of routine transactions."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3911be344131"},"reference_answer":"v3911be344131","incorrect_answer":"vf88eba6bede8","explanation":"Уступка касается возможной экономии, а не всей политики замены."},{"id":"11d7d2f5-c30a-533a-ae16-ee9bb88c3b49","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что остаётся предметом спора после уступки?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"In a debate about replacing staffed counters with kiosks, one speaker conceded that kiosks could reduce the cost of routine transactions. She then argued that the saving did not answer the question of access for people unable to use them independently. Her opponent celebrated the concession as acceptance of the replacement policy. This conflated agreement on a possible efficiency gain with agreement on what should follow from it. The speaker’s argument was instead that, even if the saving materialised, an accessible alternative would still be required. She had not demonstrated that kiosks were always unsuitable, nor had she withdrawn the accessibility objection. Her concession narrowed the dispute to the conditions under which efficiency could justify a change in service.","options":[{"id":"v07a9e7e5726f","label":"Whether the speaker has proved that all kiosks are unsuitable."},{"id":"v0b093ed66138","label":"Whether efficiency can justify the change without an accessible alternative."},{"id":"v814cbd736658","label":"Whether any transaction ever has a cost."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0b093ed66138"},"reference_answer":"v0b093ed66138","incorrect_answer":"v814cbd736658","explanation":"Спор сужен до условий оправданности изменения и сохранения доступности."},{"id":"16942c53-2b33-55fd-b5fa-0e9d4d20c469","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Отдели признанную посылку от итогового решения.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does conceding that a proposal has one advantage commit us to adopting it?"}],"options":[{"id":"v6b98f35a1c9a","label":"Yes; every conceded premise settles the conclusion."},{"id":"v187df43c3468","label":"Yes; a concession withdraws all unrelated objections."},{"id":"v0387df703854","label":"No; other considerations may still defeat the overall recommendation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0387df703854"},"reference_answer":"v0387df703854","incorrect_answer":"v6b98f35a1c9a","explanation":"Один плюс не устанавливает перевес над всеми существенными минусами."},{"id":"882809a6-b8c0-57fb-835f-29741d628a9c","lesson_id":"69bb566a-0188-5f0f-aa69-a0ed169576f4","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A conclusion that depends on specified circumstances is ___.","options":[{"id":"v6ac8984bd1dd","label":"self-evident"},{"id":"v21353bf49980","label":"contingent"},{"id":"v3d157262d60a","label":"unconditional"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v21353bf49980"},"reference_answer":"v21353bf49980","incorrect_answer":"v3d157262d60a","explanation":"Contingent означает зависящий от условий, в отличие от unconditional."},{"id":"d735a322-cff3-59b6-8514-a9b5101b9003","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “When did the office stop ignoring complaints?” presupposes ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v5b75344d9d9b","label":"only that the office has an address"},{"id":"v4c5b68f620ac","label":"that every complaint has been independently resolved"},{"id":"v03c219f46b22","label":"that the office had been ignoring complaints"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v03c219f46b22"},"reference_answer":"v03c219f46b22","incorrect_answer":"v5b75344d9d9b","explanation":"Форма stop ignoring содержит допущение о прежнем игнорировании."},{"id":"6eee8b77-7452-5ae7-b592-098df1235941","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: on / at.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The question rests ___ a premise that has not been established."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["on"]},"reference_answer":"on","incorrect_answer":"at","explanation":"Rest on a premise означает опираться на предпосылку."},{"id":"b87f949a-6cd4-5d24-9994-9e2755c003f4","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Вопрос предполагает, что раньше жалобы игнорировали.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"assumes"},{"id":"t4","label":"that"},{"id":"t5","label":"complaints"},{"id":"t6","label":"were"},{"id":"t7","label":"previously"},{"id":"t8","label":"ignored."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"question"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Нужно отделить встроенное допущение вопроса от отдельно подтверждённого факта."},{"id":"ca1b83e7-43d0-585b-8b13-87927c65f770","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The question presupposes of an earlier failure to respond."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The question presupposes an earlier failure to respond."]},"reference_answer":"The question presupposes an earlier failure to respond.","incorrect_answer":"The question presupposes of an earlier failure to respond.","explanation":"Presuppose — переходный глагол, поэтому of перед объектом не нужен."},{"id":"67875405-5756-519b-b5a2-ed4256dd4501","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему просьба «дать дату» проблематична?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"At a public meeting, a resident asked when the housing office had stopped ignoring repair requests. The chair initially invited the office manager to give a date. The manager instead challenged the question’s premise: requests had been recorded, she said, though some repairs had been delayed. That reply did not establish that the service had been adequate, and it did not erase the delays. It separated a claim about ignoring requests from a claim about completing repairs slowly. The chair then asked what records showed about response times and outstanding work. This reformulation made the issue investigable without requiring either party to accept a disputed characterisation simply in order to answer. The original dissatisfaction remained a legitimate subject of scrutiny.","options":[{"id":"v204ba3a705d9","label":"It proves that all repairs were completed promptly."},{"id":"v53eb75c4247a","label":"It accepts the disputed assumption that requests had been ignored."},{"id":"v22e3a4321be0","label":"Dates can never be relevant to public services."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v53eb75c4247a"},"reference_answer":"v53eb75c4247a","incorrect_answer":"v22e3a4321be0","explanation":"Ответ датой молчаливо принимает встроенную предпосылку вопроса."},{"id":"376b2e55-a562-5c12-992f-3f3546693c8f","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что не доказывает ответ менеджера?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"At a public meeting, a resident asked when the housing office had stopped ignoring repair requests. The chair initially invited the office manager to give a date. The manager instead challenged the question’s premise: requests had been recorded, she said, though some repairs had been delayed. That reply did not establish that the service had been adequate, and it did not erase the delays. It separated a claim about ignoring requests from a claim about completing repairs slowly. The chair then asked what records showed about response times and outstanding work. This reformulation made the issue investigable without requiring either party to accept a disputed characterisation simply in order to answer. The original dissatisfaction remained a legitimate subject of scrutiny.","options":[{"id":"v391788e6c5d6","label":"That the overall service had been adequate."},{"id":"v0519b1147192","label":"That she distinguishes recording requests from repair delays."},{"id":"v10d4b502b79a","label":"That the delays remain open to scrutiny."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v391788e6c5d6"},"reference_answer":"v391788e6c5d6","incorrect_answer":"v0519b1147192","explanation":"Оспаривание слова ignoring не устанавливает высокое качество всей работы."},{"id":"fc10915e-a698-50f2-b37d-d79b793c25b5","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери ответ, который не принимает спорную предпосылку.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How can we answer a question containing an unsupported assumption?"}],"options":[{"id":"ve933b5a40792","label":"Treat the question’s wording as conclusive evidence."},{"id":"vaaf0b231ea73","label":"Identify the assumption and ask for a formulation that does not take it for granted."},{"id":"v0f18c3dcae08","label":"Invent a date so that the question appears answered."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vaaf0b231ea73"},"reference_answer":"vaaf0b231ea73","incorrect_answer":"v0f18c3dcae08","explanation":"Уточнение предпосылки сохраняет возможность проверки фактов."},{"id":"b1b819f1-85c7-54d7-bc7a-6c0dc3ce098e","lesson_id":"5080e1ea-40a1-5aef-b104-445093ccfa7b","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To dispute an assumption explicitly is to ___ it.","options":[{"id":"v62b92f448b95","label":"challenge"},{"id":"v7c6e52a1f60c","label":"certify"},{"id":"v0c076e03ca60","label":"quietly endorse"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v62b92f448b95"},"reference_answer":"v62b92f448b95","incorrect_answer":"v7c6e52a1f60c","explanation":"Challenge означает оспорить, а не подтвердить или молча принять."},{"id":"ee2e7559-4bf0-5833-baa8-9bb1c343ac3b","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Calling a budget “a leaking bucket” primarily supplies ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v53300f470577","label":"a literal description of a container in the accounts"},{"id":"v42b0a8115b5c","label":"a frame that highlights loss"},{"id":"ve88e5f9e8423","label":"measurement proving every expense is waste"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v42b0a8115b5c"},"reference_answer":"v42b0a8115b5c","incorrect_answer":"ve88e5f9e8423","explanation":"Образ акцентирует утечки, но не заменяет анализ конкретных расходов."},{"id":"a4290b55-57fa-58d5-98d5-769c48936622","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: extent / extension.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The analogy is useful to the ___ that it reveals neglected costs."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["extent"]},"reference_answer":"extent","incorrect_answer":"extension","explanation":"To the extent that — устойчивая конструкция ограничения по степени."},{"id":"d864bb8c-4e02-57fb-9d92-8a8339a1fdf8","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Аналогия полезна в той мере, в какой она проясняет компромисс.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"is"},{"id":"t4","label":"useful"},{"id":"t5","label":"to"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"extent"},{"id":"t8","label":"that"},{"id":"t9","label":"it"},{"id":"t10","label":"clarifies"},{"id":"t11","label":"the"},{"id":"t12","label":"trade-off."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"analogy"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t12"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t12"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t12","t1"],"explanation":"Полезность ограничена конкретной функцией аналогии, а не объявлена абсолютной."},{"id":"b023cacb-aaaf-536e-9499-167ad521286f","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The analogy is persuasive to the extend that it fits the evidence."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The analogy is persuasive to the extent that it fits the evidence."]},"reference_answer":"The analogy is persuasive to the extent that it fits the evidence.","incorrect_answer":"The analogy is persuasive to the extend that it fits the evidence.","explanation":"В выражении to the extent that используется существительное extent."},{"id":"48df0fe5-b2a4-566c-a342-4105d291c0eb","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое ограничение «дырявого ведра» отмечает библиотекарь?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A councillor described the library budget as a leaking bucket, arguing that additional funding would merely disappear into an inefficient system. A librarian replied that the bucket image made waste salient while leaving the value of the service out of view. She did not deny that particular costs deserved scrutiny. Rather, she questioned whether an image of leakage could establish which expenditure was avoidable and which supported public access. Another councillor proposed a different metaphor, calling the library shared infrastructure. That image highlighted long-term benefit but could also obscure operational failings. The committee eventually requested itemised costs and usage evidence. Neither metaphor was prohibited; neither was allowed to substitute for the evidence needed to judge the budget.","options":[{"id":"v4914ca3c81cb","label":"It highlights waste without establishing which spending is avoidable."},{"id":"vc7fe61b836cf","label":"It proves that every item of expenditure has equal value."},{"id":"va39fc1e7444b","label":"It prevents anyone from asking about operational costs."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4914ca3c81cb"},"reference_answer":"v4914ca3c81cb","incorrect_answer":"vc7fe61b836cf","explanation":"Рамка делает потери заметными, но не различает конкретные виды расходов."},{"id":"2044746b-f635-51df-9ef5-940d2e7f822a","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему второй образ тоже недостаточен?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A councillor described the library budget as a leaking bucket, arguing that additional funding would merely disappear into an inefficient system. A librarian replied that the bucket image made waste salient while leaving the value of the service out of view. She did not deny that particular costs deserved scrutiny. Rather, she questioned whether an image of leakage could establish which expenditure was avoidable and which supported public access. Another councillor proposed a different metaphor, calling the library shared infrastructure. That image highlighted long-term benefit but could also obscure operational failings. The committee eventually requested itemised costs and usage evidence. Neither metaphor was prohibited; neither was allowed to substitute for the evidence needed to judge the budget.","options":[{"id":"v600a624cc079","label":"Shared infrastructure can never have public value."},{"id":"vc1fc45daf427","label":"Replacing one metaphor with another produces itemised evidence."},{"id":"v03bb33e00619","label":"It may highlight benefit while obscuring operational failings."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v03bb33e00619"},"reference_answer":"v03bb33e00619","incorrect_answer":"v600a624cc079","explanation":"Текст применяет симметричную критику: обе рамки выделяют часть ситуации."},{"id":"9e9ac0ae-49eb-5473-95f0-ac073475e839","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Различи убедительность образа и фактическое обоснование.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can an analogy settle the factual question merely by sounding apt?"}],"options":[{"id":"ve744d3e98053","label":"No; its explanatory appeal must be checked against relevant evidence."},{"id":"vdb3365266403","label":"Yes; vividness guarantees factual correspondence."},{"id":"v3b4aaaa549c8","label":"Yes; an analogy contains all the measurements it evokes."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve744d3e98053"},"reference_answer":"ve744d3e98053","incorrect_answer":"vdb3365266403","explanation":"Уместность сравнения не делает перенос всех свойств автоматически истинным."},{"id":"439d068c-cada-5efe-a350-7f66217b0b06","lesson_id":"057b2eca-8cda-5332-b845-c3cfe48f82ae","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A detail made especially noticeable by a particular description becomes ___.","options":[{"id":"ved762437d543","label":"irrelevant by definition"},{"id":"vdf2985dc31ba","label":"unrecorded"},{"id":"v7448984ce4d1","label":"salient"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7448984ce4d1"},"reference_answer":"v7448984ce4d1","incorrect_answer":"ved762437d543","explanation":"Salient — выделяющийся и заметный; это характеристика внимания, а не гарантия истинности."},{"id":"7f3c4e57-9350-55c1-b6be-c08bdb323af2","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: A review calls the account “lucid but methodologically thin”. A faithful plain-language summary is ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vbd4131cd8bcc","label":"It is clearly written, but its methods are insufficiently developed."},{"id":"v6fc45498bba6","label":"It is fully endorsed in both style and method."},{"id":"ve1b28f0fcf33","label":"It is unreadable and deliberately deceptive."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbd4131cd8bcc"},"reference_answer":"vbd4131cd8bcc","incorrect_answer":"v6fc45498bba6","explanation":"Нужно сохранить положительную оценку ясности и отрицательную оценку методов без приписывания обмана."},{"id":"15afbb5d-1847-512f-9e9b-c2e28227b7fe","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: interpret / interprets.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The caveat was retained lest readers ___ the comment as unqualified approval."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["interpret"]},"reference_answer":"interpret","incorrect_answer":"interprets","explanation":"После lest здесь подходит формальный базовый interpret с подлежащим readers."},{"id":"16e1d3d6-30f9-5ac4-8e9b-2a0c7ca9f5d6","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Оговорку сохранили, чтобы читатели не приняли ясность за строгость.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"was"},{"id":"t4","label":"retained"},{"id":"t5","label":"lest"},{"id":"t6","label":"readers"},{"id":"t7","label":"mistake"},{"id":"t8","label":"clarity"},{"id":"t9","label":"for"},{"id":"t10","label":"rigour."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"caveat"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t1"],"explanation":"Lest вводит предотвращаемую ошибку; clarity и rigour оценивают разные качества."},{"id":"d1b9fb0d-59aa-5ac7-8f42-7caa453d3f48","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The reviewer praised the clarity while question the method."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The reviewer praised the clarity while questioning the method."]},"reference_answer":"The reviewer praised the clarity while questioning the method.","incorrect_answer":"The reviewer praised the clarity while question the method.","explanation":"После while в сокращённой параллельной конструкции требуется questioning."},{"id":"cede6485-27ba-5cdb-9ca8-de607fec95b6","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему excellent introduction оказалось неточным?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"An editor asked an assistant to turn an academic review into a short description for a general audience. The reviewer had called the book lucid but methodologically thin, noting that its accessible examples were not matched by a convincing account of how the evidence had been selected. The assistant’s first version described it as an excellent introduction. That was readable, but it discarded the criticism rather than translating it. A second version called the book unreliable, which exceeded the reviewer’s narrower reservation. The final description praised the clarity and explained the concern about evidence selection in ordinary language. Simplifying the vocabulary had not required simplifying the judgement into either approval or rejection; the two dimensions of the assessment could remain distinct.","options":[{"id":"v61803b632d1f","label":"It faithfully explained the selection of evidence."},{"id":"v70bb0374adcf","label":"It retained every dimension of the reviewer’s judgement."},{"id":"v331725eb624b","label":"It removed the methodological reservation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v331725eb624b"},"reference_answer":"v331725eb624b","incorrect_answer":"v61803b632d1f","explanation":"Первая версия оставила похвалу и потеряла критику метода."},{"id":"04d5cd1b-1e27-5141-b261-5ef918aa3f55","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что делает итоговую версию более верной?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"An editor asked an assistant to turn an academic review into a short description for a general audience. The reviewer had called the book lucid but methodologically thin, noting that its accessible examples were not matched by a convincing account of how the evidence had been selected. The assistant’s first version described it as an excellent introduction. That was readable, but it discarded the criticism rather than translating it. A second version called the book unreliable, which exceeded the reviewer’s narrower reservation. The final description praised the clarity and explained the concern about evidence selection in ordinary language. Simplifying the vocabulary had not required simplifying the judgement into either approval or rejection; the two dimensions of the assessment could remain distinct.","options":[{"id":"vbc9119b00654","label":"It avoids giving readers any account of the criticism."},{"id":"v0d0b5bfb2d85","label":"It preserves both clarity and the specific concern in accessible language."},{"id":"va502bb9573f9","label":"It turns the reservation into a claim of deliberate deception."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0d0b5bfb2d85"},"reference_answer":"v0d0b5bfb2d85","incorrect_answer":"va502bb9573f9","explanation":"Смена регистра упрощает лексику, сохраняя разные измерения оценки."},{"id":"dd575b3d-4018-5c38-963d-47db64758abd","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери принцип точного пересказа для широкой аудитории.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Should a plain-language summary remove a caveat because it is difficult to phrase?"}],"options":[{"id":"ve27e037c4607","label":"Yes; readability permits reversing the conclusion."},{"id":"v83473e503422","label":"Yes; every caveat is merely decorative."},{"id":"ve37f1b02d54c","label":"No; explain the caveat more plainly while preserving its force."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve37f1b02d54c"},"reference_answer":"ve37f1b02d54c","incorrect_answer":"ve27e037c4607","explanation":"Доступность формулировки не требует утраты существенной оговорки."},{"id":"ff31f4cd-85dc-5364-b435-657cf76a9ae3","lesson_id":"08b2f050-c01e-5f00-ae05-c2455d3471e5","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A paraphrase that changes the scope or force of a claim may ___ it.","options":[{"id":"ve2df1cf40a0b","label":"quote verbatim"},{"id":"v177090bda759","label":"distort"},{"id":"vfa040106322e","label":"corroborate automatically"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v177090bda759"},"reference_answer":"v177090bda759","incorrect_answer":"vfa040106322e","explanation":"Distort — исказить содержание; это не независимое подтверждение и не дословная цитата."},{"id":"9deacb4f-84e0-5be2-9614-8608a5f7d6be","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “An informal agreement cannot be ruled out” commits the writer to ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vb96569ea4149","label":"judging it the most probable explanation"},{"id":"vdfc4bd9c5cf0","label":"claiming documentary proof of it"},{"id":"v05b06915deff","label":"retaining it as a possibility"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v05b06915deff"},"reference_answer":"v05b06915deff","incorrect_answer":"vb96569ea4149","explanation":"Cannot be ruled out не ранжирует вероятность и не объявляет доказательство."},{"id":"bb4d52f3-ca9a-5a67-8dad-609cba6032af","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь подходящее слово из пары: rule / rules.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The silence of a selective archive does not ___ out an unrecorded discussion."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["rule"]},"reference_answer":"rule","incorrect_answer":"rules","explanation":"После does not нужен rule; rule out означает исключить возможность."},{"id":"663f8fe6-0e5d-5d10-aa19-fd949f923bd1","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Неформальную договорённость исключить нельзя.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"agreement"},{"id":"t4","label":"cannot"},{"id":"t5","label":"be"},{"id":"t6","label":"ruled"},{"id":"t7","label":"out."},{"id":"t1","label":"An"},{"id":"t2","label":"informal"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Возможность остаётся открытой; вероятность или документальная подтверждённость не устанавливаются."},{"id":"62ffbf61-9f1f-57b0-89dc-705868e2467a","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь только ошибку в конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The missing entry does not proves that no meeting occurred."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The missing entry does not prove that no meeting occurred."]},"reference_answer":"The missing entry does not prove that no meeting occurred.","incorrect_answer":"The missing entry does not proves that no meeting occurred.","explanation":"После does not нужен инфинитив prove; смысл ограничивает вывод по отсутствующей записи."},{"id":"647d4dce-9a01-5265-85a1-0b8bd2bfb671","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему отсутствие записи не решает вопрос?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A historian found no record of a meeting in a committee’s surviving minute books. One commentator treated the omission as proof that the meeting had never occurred. The historian was more circumspect. The books were incomplete, informal discussions were rarely minuted, and two letters referred ambiguously to a conversation around the relevant date. None of this established that a meeting had taken place. It did, however, weaken the claim that archival silence decisively established its absence. The historian distinguished an unconfirmed possibility from a positive reconstruction, and an incomplete record from a recording system known to be comprehensive. Whether silence counted strongly against an event depended on what the archive would normally have been expected to preserve.","options":[{"id":"v345cb6599a3d","label":"The historian has shown that no meeting could ever be recorded."},{"id":"vb34f61ca9005","label":"The archive is incomplete and informal discussions were rarely recorded."},{"id":"v8b969cdb9d6c","label":"The letters conclusively prove a formal committee meeting."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb34f61ca9005"},"reference_answer":"vb34f61ca9005","incorrect_answer":"v8b969cdb9d6c","explanation":"Нужно учитывать полноту архива и обычную практику записи именно таких событий."},{"id":"e229a32d-7089-5074-bf10-9c35344ea9d0","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что историк всё же не утверждает?","position":6,"public_payload":{"passage":"A historian found no record of a meeting in a committee’s surviving minute books. One commentator treated the omission as proof that the meeting had never occurred. The historian was more circumspect. The books were incomplete, informal discussions were rarely minuted, and two letters referred ambiguously to a conversation around the relevant date. None of this established that a meeting had taken place. It did, however, weaken the claim that archival silence decisively established its absence. The historian distinguished an unconfirmed possibility from a positive reconstruction, and an incomplete record from a recording system known to be comprehensive. Whether silence counted strongly against an event depended on what the archive would normally have been expected to preserve.","options":[{"id":"vab8ef1afee92","label":"That a meeting has been positively established."},{"id":"v4f6510ad82c6","label":"That the surviving minute books are incomplete."},{"id":"v8d0a872aaaa4","label":"That the evidential weight of silence depends on expected recording."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vab8ef1afee92"},"reference_answer":"vab8ef1afee92","incorrect_answer":"v4f6510ad82c6","explanation":"Критика доказательства отсутствия не является позитивным доказательством события."},{"id":"0ae53938-d71a-5526-868e-37f85f37b261","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Не усиливай возможность до вероятности или доказанного факта.","position":7,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “we cannot rule it out” justify reporting that it probably happened?"}],"options":[{"id":"ve33ffbccbf24","label":"Yes; inability to exclude is documentary confirmation."},{"id":"v44fbba831baf","label":"No; non-exclusion alone does not establish probability."},{"id":"vcedb4e22b363","label":"Yes; any unexcluded possibility is the most likely one."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v44fbba831baf"},"reference_answer":"v44fbba831baf","incorrect_answer":"vcedb4e22b363","explanation":"Из открытой возможности не следует её преимущество перед альтернативами."},{"id":"2770fcff-46c4-56c7-a9c3-f198151eca60","lesson_id":"3c3a9c14-2821-57f5-96d7-87ae391cf6ab","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово, точно соответствующее контексту.","position":8,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An archive preserving some kinds of material much better than others is ___.","options":[{"id":"vcf8d55bd24aa","label":"selective"},{"id":"v3b18e04f3157","label":"comprehensive by definition"},{"id":"v73e90bc47872","label":"conclusive"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vcf8d55bd24aa"},"reference_answer":"vcf8d55bd24aa","incorrect_answer":"v3b18e04f3157","explanation":"Selective обозначает избирательность сохранения, а не полноту или окончательность вывода."},{"id":"9aad67c4-f12d-5e34-a76d-a6457fb3b494","lesson_id":"9606efc9-2661-5c58-abb7-4ecec9db2a3b","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: My aunt works in a hospital. She is ___ nurse.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v23e2d119d84f","label":"a"},{"id":"v43864058cfc8","label":"an"},{"id":"v8c5194330394","label":"of"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v23e2d119d84f"},"reference_answer":"v23e2d119d84f","incorrect_answer":"v43864058cfc8","explanation":"Nurse начинается с согласного звука, поэтому a nurse."},{"id":"4f4b4a71-279a-5b91-acee-1343dc280e4a","lesson_id":"9606efc9-2661-5c58-abb7-4ecec9db2a3b","kind":"gap","prompt":"Дополни предложение словом из пары: work / works.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"My brother ___ in an office."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["works"]},"reference_answer":"works","incorrect_answer":"work","explanation":"My brother заменяется he; в Present Simple нужна форма works."},{"id":"eba5d8a0-f104-5ed3-8db2-4743fd922251","lesson_id":"9606efc9-2661-5c58-abb7-4ecec9db2a3b","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предл