hree because of a class. They finally chose four at the library entrance, with a café nearby as another option if the library was closed.","options":[{"id":"v5d6b1a5c756c","label":"The library."},{"id":"v49e627522125","label":"Another outdoor park."},{"id":"vc9016c818be2","label":"An exhibition in a different city."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5d6b1a5c756c"},"reference_answer":"v5d6b1a5c756c","incorrect_answer":"v49e627522125","explanation":"Она предлагает помещение как альтернативу дождливому парку."},{"id":"2ed578f1-be1b-599b-89c1-1a7935890340","lesson_id":"5e6a6fd3-df13-50db-b17a-edf47d37f5a0","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l075b479ec389","label":"suggest"},{"id":"l907bb2390d8d","label":"agree"},{"id":"lef811cfdea65","label":"alternative"},{"id":"l541b5fb3350c","label":"indoors"}],"right":[{"id":"r3faf5d00d133","label":"другой вариант"},{"id":"r512b70df74d5","label":"в помещении"},{"id":"r0b347398cf69","label":"предлагать идею"},{"id":"r35e62152d90c","label":"соглашаться"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l075b479ec389":"r0b347398cf69","l907bb2390d8d":"r35e62152d90c","lef811cfdea65":"r3faf5d00d133","l541b5fb3350c":"r512b70df74d5"}},"reference_answer":{"l075b479ec389":"r0b347398cf69","l907bb2390d8d":"r35e62152d90c","lef811cfdea65":"r3faf5d00d133","l541b5fb3350c":"r512b70df74d5"},"incorrect_answer":{"l075b479ec389":"r35e62152d90c","l907bb2390d8d":"r0b347398cf69","lef811cfdea65":"r3faf5d00d133","l541b5fb3350c":"r512b70df74d5"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: suggest — предлагать идею; agree — соглашаться; alternative — другой вариант; indoors — в помещении."},{"id":"4381c2a9-e518-517f-b0d9-2339a6ba6bc8","lesson_id":"5e6a6fd3-df13-50db-b17a-edf47d37f5a0","kind":"reading","prompt":"На какое время в итоге договорились?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"Two friends planned to meet in the park, but the forecast showed rain. “How about meeting in the library instead?” asked Noor. Alex agreed, but suggested four rather than three because of a class. They finally chose four at the library entrance, with a café nearby as another option if the library was closed.","options":[{"id":"vb6d607d7561c","label":"Three."},{"id":"ve759d8f090cd","label":"No time was agreed."},{"id":"vc7c2f43a5a04","label":"Four."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc7c2f43a5a04"},"reference_answer":"vc7c2f43a5a04","incorrect_answer":"vb6d607d7561c","explanation":"Первоначальные три часа заменили четырьмя из-за занятия Алекса."},{"id":"8c87e1e5-2f96-55d5-ac79-8c49222aa135","lesson_id":"5e6a6fd3-df13-50db-b17a-edf47d37f5a0","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Предложи совместный визит правильной конструкцией.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"We need an idea for Saturday."}],"options":[{"id":"v4eaafa065f15","label":"How about visiting the new gallery?"},{"id":"v939e44d11484","label":"How about to visiting the new gallery?"},{"id":"v06c60425987a","label":"Let’s to visited the gallery."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4eaafa065f15"},"reference_answer":"v4eaafa065f15","incorrect_answer":"v939e44d11484","explanation":"How about + visiting — подходящая модель."},{"id":"6e82d356-a365-54ad-907f-3b4059a11dfb","lesson_id":"5e6a6fd3-df13-50db-b17a-edf47d37f5a0","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If the weather is bad, we can stay ___ rather than outside.","options":[{"id":"v5dc2ad345782","label":"upstairs in every case"},{"id":"v0bfdbc9f0a5a","label":"yesterday"},{"id":"vecb5eeaa4b43","label":"indoors"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vecb5eeaa4b43"},"reference_answer":"vecb5eeaa4b43","incorrect_answer":"v5dc2ad345782","explanation":"Indoors означает внутри помещения; upstairs — только наверху."},{"id":"9165f4ba-e52f-5269-8e28-5844ff715e2e","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: I ___ my neighbour since we started school together.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vc6bdb119cefa","label":"have known"},{"id":"v0b42bb2b6912","label":"have been knowing"},{"id":"vdc798e8b04ff","label":"am knowing"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc6bdb119cefa"},"reference_answer":"vc6bdb119cefa","incorrect_answer":"v0b42bb2b6912","explanation":"Know в значении знакомства обычно используется как состояние: have known."},{"id":"6f296c93-d212-5b49-a4b5-213e2b72bc7e","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: since / for.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We have known each other ___ ten years."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["for"]},"reference_answer":"for","incorrect_answer":"since","explanation":"Ten years — длительность, поэтому for."},{"id":"1a839782-3ed6-564d-b647-5016e8f58666","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Я знаю её с тех пор, как мы были детьми.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"known"},{"id":"t4","label":"her"},{"id":"t5","label":"since"},{"id":"t6","label":"we"},{"id":"t7","label":"were"},{"id":"t8","label":"children."},{"id":"t1","label":"I"},{"id":"t2","label":"have"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Have known связывает состояние знакомства с настоящим."},{"id":"9f738a68-2535-54f7-989b-62de1b8ac10d","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I have been knowing him for six years."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I have known him for six years."]},"reference_answer":"I have known him for six years.","incorrect_answer":"I have been knowing him for six years.","explanation":"Для состояния знакомства требуется have known, а не Continuous."},{"id":"7df6ca64-ceab-5b94-96f8-31269551b33d","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"reading","prompt":"Когда началось знакомство?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"I have known Omar since our first week at secondary school. We have lived in different towns for several years, but we still talk regularly. Last month, he moved to my neighbourhood. We now meet for a walk on Sundays. His move has changed how often we meet, not when our friendship began.","options":[{"id":"v6a3b3830d1d7","label":"When Omar moved last month."},{"id":"v5ada4331b6b1","label":"On their first Sunday walk this year."},{"id":"vda291dd5961a","label":"During their first week at secondary school."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vda291dd5961a"},"reference_answer":"vda291dd5961a","incorrect_answer":"v6a3b3830d1d7","explanation":"Since связывает начало знакомства со школой, а не с недавним переездом."},{"id":"d2c13dba-4ce1-5165-bad6-a8e8d5b58e4a","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l0e538748cf8c","label":"know"},{"id":"le0153dbca5b9","label":"since"},{"id":"lf5f3aac5a9bd","label":"for"},{"id":"l4379a777f2b7","label":"neighbour"}],"right":[{"id":"r61ccf855f919","label":"в течение"},{"id":"r1fef27f63c27","label":"сосед"},{"id":"r868c100fced9","label":"знать, быть знакомым"},{"id":"r2fc3245b05f9","label":"с указанного момента"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l0e538748cf8c":"r868c100fced9","le0153dbca5b9":"r2fc3245b05f9","lf5f3aac5a9bd":"r61ccf855f919","l4379a777f2b7":"r1fef27f63c27"}},"reference_answer":{"l0e538748cf8c":"r868c100fced9","le0153dbca5b9":"r2fc3245b05f9","lf5f3aac5a9bd":"r61ccf855f919","l4379a777f2b7":"r1fef27f63c27"},"incorrect_answer":{"l0e538748cf8c":"r2fc3245b05f9","le0153dbca5b9":"r868c100fced9","lf5f3aac5a9bd":"r61ccf855f919","l4379a777f2b7":"r1fef27f63c27"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: know — знать, быть знакомым; since — с указанного момента; for — в течение; neighbour — сосед."},{"id":"2d45aa7d-6011-5e19-89cc-674129f5b5a2","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что изменил переезд?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"I have known Omar since our first week at secondary school. We have lived in different towns for several years, but we still talk regularly. Last month, he moved to my neighbourhood. We now meet for a walk on Sundays. His move has changed how often we meet, not when our friendship began.","options":[{"id":"vd695e57a41e4","label":"The fact that they had never spoken before."},{"id":"v7bf0c30ff55d","label":"How often they can meet."},{"id":"v7f8bfa634ea5","label":"The original beginning of their friendship."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7bf0c30ff55d"},"reference_answer":"v7bf0c30ff55d","incorrect_answer":"v7f8bfa634ea5","explanation":"Последняя фраза отделяет частоту встреч от давнего начала дружбы."},{"id":"b81c7671-dfb1-50f8-aebe-09ae4d51808c","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Ответь о продолжающемся знакомстве.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How long have you known your colleague?"}],"options":[{"id":"v33b3ef7e0286","label":"I have been knowing her for three years."},{"id":"v4db13d5c455c","label":"I know her since three years."},{"id":"vbf69efb29e32","label":"I have known her for three years."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbf69efb29e32"},"reference_answer":"vbf69efb29e32","incorrect_answer":"v33b3ef7e0286","explanation":"Have known + for three years выражает состояние и длительность."},{"id":"235e2beb-f464-51c5-bdf8-a086536d7f5c","lesson_id":"f4ee18c1-bf64-553b-a8f0-d455c100e3eb","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Someone living next door is your ___.","options":[{"id":"v6085a09bdab7","label":"passenger"},{"id":"v149b74ecf784","label":"neighbour"},{"id":"v0f236ecd5912","label":"stranger by definition"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v149b74ecf784"},"reference_answer":"v149b74ecf784","incorrect_answer":"v0f236ecd5912","explanation":"Neighbour — человек, живущий рядом."},{"id":"d1b43c0f-781e-5820-a148-b6fffd09e34b","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The new volunteer introduced ___ to the group.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v3caadeef58f3","label":"her ownselves"},{"id":"vff4931b6672f","label":"she"},{"id":"v12aa99e9cc3d","label":"herself"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v12aa99e9cc3d"},"reference_answer":"v12aa99e9cc3d","incorrect_answer":"v3caadeef58f3","explanation":"Возвратное herself указывает, что она представила саму себя."},{"id":"5f3b2aec-c2ee-5ad9-bdc5-40bbb374813e","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: myself / me.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I completed the form by ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["myself"]},"reference_answer":"myself","incorrect_answer":"me","explanation":"By myself означает без посторонней помощи."},{"id":"77b2d87e-bfdd-5f42-85a5-cacf97ef6599","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Они сами организовали мероприятие.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"the"},{"id":"t4","label":"event"},{"id":"t5","label":"themselves."},{"id":"t1","label":"They"},{"id":"t2","label":"organised"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t1"],"explanation":"Themselves подчёркивает участие самих организаторов."},{"id":"abed8e41-a7c7-5943-9061-adeb7ee7376d","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"She looked at himself in the mirror."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["She looked at herself in the mirror."]},"reference_answer":"She looked at herself in the mirror.","incorrect_answer":"She looked at himself in the mirror.","explanation":"She требует согласованного возвратного herself."},{"id":"3f5376f6-4100-58c6-b5a1-4d5b91505c96","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую задачу Майя выполнила самостоятельно?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"At the first meeting, Maya introduced herself and explained that she was new to the area. Two volunteers showed her the booking system. A week later, she completed a booking by herself. She was pleased to work independently, but she still asked for help when a form contained an unfamiliar question. Working alone did not mean refusing all support.","options":[{"id":"v67d316d0fa50","label":"The whole first meeting without volunteers."},{"id":"ve804a58b4cc4","label":"A booking."},{"id":"v3d53eaf039b8","label":"Every repair in the building."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve804a58b4cc4"},"reference_answer":"ve804a58b4cc4","incorrect_answer":"v3d53eaf039b8","explanation":"A week later относится к самостоятельному оформлению брони."},{"id":"e9145927-731d-5ca2-8ceb-b914d860fa70","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"le441b24f5663","label":"myself"},{"id":"l7de558da884f","label":"herself"},{"id":"l33d5a07eb1f0","label":"themselves"},{"id":"lf2ea3a29044b","label":"independently"}],"right":[{"id":"r33c1c55e9238","label":"себя, сами (об they)"},{"id":"rbdc1a431e737","label":"самостоятельно"},{"id":"r5e0a0336cae5","label":"себя, сам (об I)"},{"id":"ra444e3171c44","label":"себя, сама (об she)"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"le441b24f5663":"r5e0a0336cae5","l7de558da884f":"ra444e3171c44","l33d5a07eb1f0":"r33c1c55e9238","lf2ea3a29044b":"rbdc1a431e737"}},"reference_answer":{"le441b24f5663":"r5e0a0336cae5","l7de558da884f":"ra444e3171c44","l33d5a07eb1f0":"r33c1c55e9238","lf2ea3a29044b":"rbdc1a431e737"},"incorrect_answer":{"le441b24f5663":"ra444e3171c44","l7de558da884f":"r5e0a0336cae5","l33d5a07eb1f0":"r33c1c55e9238","lf2ea3a29044b":"rbdc1a431e737"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: myself — себя, сам (об I); herself — себя, сама (об she); themselves — себя, сами (об they); independently — самостоятельно."},{"id":"f1b05a34-4d55-520d-97a2-a99ace14c008","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"reading","prompt":"Отказалась ли она от любой помощи?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"At the first meeting, Maya introduced herself and explained that she was new to the area. Two volunteers showed her the booking system. A week later, she completed a booking by herself. She was pleased to work independently, but she still asked for help when a form contained an unfamiliar question. Working alone did not mean refusing all support.","options":[{"id":"v482663915717","label":"No; she still asked about unfamiliar questions."},{"id":"v593c32ad9637","label":"Yes; she would never ask anything again."},{"id":"v41a85b07521e","label":"Yes; independently always means without any communication."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v482663915717"},"reference_answer":"v482663915717","incorrect_answer":"v593c32ad9637","explanation":"Последняя часть специально ограничивает смысл самостоятельности."},{"id":"db8b7e16-35a6-5eb2-a860-c9edd98cee8c","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Ответь о собственном самостоятельном действии.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Did anyone help you fill in the form?"}],"options":[{"id":"v8af5cdeecd58","label":"No, I filled it in by herself."},{"id":"vb2049d4e1bc1","label":"No, I filled it in by myself."},{"id":"v5059101d6b97","label":"No, I filled it in by me."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb2049d4e1bc1"},"reference_answer":"vb2049d4e1bc1","incorrect_answer":"v5059101d6b97","explanation":"By myself согласовано с I."},{"id":"ec4ff796-7469-5306-b519-034220e6628b","lesson_id":"d3ae9acb-3d9a-57fe-ba70-c0696441262b","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Doing a task without needing someone to direct every step means working ___.","options":[{"id":"v190fba6ed663","label":"independently"},{"id":"vb2e2918dea9f","label":"identically"},{"id":"ve1ec5feff629","label":"accidentally"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v190fba6ed663"},"reference_answer":"v190fba6ed663","incorrect_answer":"vb2e2918dea9f","explanation":"Independently описывает самостоятельность, не одинаковость или случайность."},{"id":"f8982cf4-e939-5a42-a9ac-9292d026c5a4","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0-5aec-acfe-edeb6355d3cc","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: All the seats are taken. There is ___ to sit.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v2e984d625a6e","label":"every person"},{"id":"vfb7c85e90510","label":"nowhere"},{"id":"vc19bf81478d8","label":"somebody"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vfb7c85e90510"},"reference_answer":"vfb7c85e90510","incorrect_answer":"vc19bf81478d8","explanation":"Nowhere обозначает отсутствие места для сидения."},{"id":"74ae47c1-694a-5c85-937d-07b4707e8652","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0-5aec-acfe-edeb6355d3cc","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: nowhere / somewhere.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I put the folder ___ safe, but I cannot remember where."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["somewhere"]},"reference_answer":"somewhere","incorrect_answer":"nowhere","explanation":"Папка помещена в какое-то безопасное место, хотя место забыто."},{"id":"60ffb672-c2f5-5536-b283-941164fa8214","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0-5aec-acfe-edeb6355d3cc","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Велосипеды негде оставить.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"nowhere"},{"id":"t4","label":"to"},{"id":"t5","label":"leave"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"bicycles."},{"id":"t1","label":"There"},{"id":"t2","label":"is"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Nowhere уже несёт отрицание."},{"id":"40b43512-a790-5372-be07-bbc4f82e84df","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0-5aec-acfe-edeb6355d3cc","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We could not find nowhere quiet."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["We could not find anywhere quiet."]},"reference_answer":"We could not find anywhere quiet.","incorrect_answer":"We could not find nowhere quiet.","explanation":"После could not используется anywhere, чтобы избежать двойного отрицания."},{"id":"8e90a1fb-46f1-5250-b571-7c1cb05fa0d5","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0-5aec-acfe-edeb6355d3cc","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что они искали?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The students wanted somewhere quiet to discuss their project. The café was crowded, and the library’s small rooms were booked. They looked for an empty classroom but could not find anywhere suitable. Finally, a tutor offered them her office for half an hour. They used the short time to divide the work and arranged to continue online later.","options":[{"id":"vecee7fe9bcad","label":"A quiet place for a project discussion."},{"id":"v99e346aa7b73","label":"A larger café to open."},{"id":"v85c2cbd66ffe","label":"A permanent office to rent."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vecee7fe9bcad"},"reference_answer":"vecee7fe9bcad","incorrect_answer":"v99e346aa7b73","explanation":"Somewhere quiet означает неопределённое тихое место; речь идёт об обсуждении проекта."},{"id":"5c74f174-a13f-5e33-8321-cb69b3da6975","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0-5aec-acfe-edeb6355d3cc","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"le9d0fb0b2f8d","label":"somewhere"},{"id":"lbf1328324121","label":"anywhere"},{"id":"l467df28f0e9b","label":"nowhere"},{"id":"l28eaf2da928f","label":"everywhere"}],"right":[{"id":"r878a971b09ed","label":"нигде"},{"id":"r72cd6e8427b5","label":"везде"},{"id":"r114f7b215df4","label":"где-то, куда-то"},{"id":"ref6ae8e3c65b","label":"где-либо"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"le9d0fb0b2f8d":"r114f7b215df4","lbf1328324121":"ref6ae8e3c65b","l467df28f0e9b":"r878a971b09ed","l28eaf2da928f":"r72cd6e8427b5"}},"reference_answer":{"le9d0fb0b2f8d":"r114f7b215df4","lbf1328324121":"ref6ae8e3c65b","l467df28f0e9b":"r878a971b09ed","l28eaf2da928f":"r72cd6e8427b5"},"incorrect_answer":{"le9d0fb0b2f8d":"ref6ae8e3c65b","lbf1328324121":"r114f7b215df4","l467df28f0e9b":"r878a971b09ed","l28eaf2da928f":"r72cd6e8427b5"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: somewhere — где-то, куда-то; anywhere — где-либо; nowhere — нигде; everywhere — везде."},{"id":"6b77c6b5-a734-5f4c-a799-dda5859d585f","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0-5aec-acfe-edeb6355d3cc","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему после встречи планировали продолжить онлайн?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The students wanted somewhere quiet to discuss their project. The café was crowded, and the library’s small rooms were booked. They looked for an empty classroom but could not find anywhere suitable. Finally, a tutor offered them her office for half an hour. They used the short time to divide the work and arranged to continue online later.","options":[{"id":"v83d983b30a04","label":"They had already lost every project file."},{"id":"v780a9d743511","label":"The tutor prohibited all discussion."},{"id":"v09c435797dc6","label":"They had the tutor’s office for only half an hour."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v09c435797dc6"},"reference_answer":"v09c435797dc6","incorrect_answer":"v83d983b30a04","explanation":"Ограничение времени объясняет разделение работы и последующее продолжение."},{"id":"aaee860f-676d-5893-ad82-f48a62d83316","lesson_id":"73c02726-9cb0