e display boards difficult. The larger room cost more but had a wide entrance. The group chose it because the boards were essential to the activity, while still recording cost as a disadvantage.","options":[{"id":"v5620e064d59b","label":"The larger room was impossible to reach."},{"id":"v14cc764426a3","label":"The display boards were not needed."},{"id":"v2f3ef20c9ab7","label":"The smaller room’s doorway was narrow."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2f3ef20c9ab7"},"reference_answer":"v2f3ef20c9ab7","incorrect_answer":"v5620e064d59b","explanation":"However вводит ограничение при наличии достоинств меньшей комнаты."},{"id":"cd774408-654f-5c7e-ae0e-51ee0266f428","lesson_id":"1426eaaf-b270-5cd7-9386-63aff29c4222","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l368fe1ff965f","label":"however"},{"id":"l8e6d59f433bb","label":"contrast"},{"id":"l2b1eff0cfc73","label":"continue"},{"id":"l1fb4f89ce79f","label":"reservation"}],"right":[{"id":"re067932419f3","label":"продолжать"},{"id":"rb4bef403b9e9","label":"оговорка, сомнение"},{"id":"rc33360684deb","label":"однако"},{"id":"r67132e38756c","label":"контраст"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l368fe1ff965f":"rc33360684deb","l8e6d59f433bb":"r67132e38756c","l2b1eff0cfc73":"re067932419f3","l1fb4f89ce79f":"rb4bef403b9e9"}},"reference_answer":{"l368fe1ff965f":"rc33360684deb","l8e6d59f433bb":"r67132e38756c","l2b1eff0cfc73":"re067932419f3","l1fb4f89ce79f":"rb4bef403b9e9"},"incorrect_answer":{"l368fe1ff965f":"r67132e38756c","l8e6d59f433bb":"rc33360684deb","l2b1eff0cfc73":"re067932419f3","l1fb4f89ce79f":"rb4bef403b9e9"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: however — однако; contrast — контраст; continue — продолжать; reservation — оговорка, сомнение."},{"id":"3755ff04-cf18-530e-883f-8fe25e62db31","lesson_id":"1426eaaf-b270-5cd7-9386-63aff29c4222","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как группа отнеслась к более высокой цене?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A local group considered two rooms for a workshop. The smaller room was cheaper and easy to reach. However, its narrow doorway made moving large display boards difficult. The larger room cost more but had a wide entrance. The group chose it because the boards were essential to the activity, while still recording cost as a disadvantage.","options":[{"id":"v9610edba5162","label":"It ignored every cost completely."},{"id":"v97f455de2c3f","label":"It still recognised it as a disadvantage."},{"id":"va24f71b97934","label":"It proved that the higher price had vanished."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v97f455de2c3f"},"reference_answer":"v97f455de2c3f","incorrect_answer":"va24f71b97934","explanation":"Выбор по другому критерию не отменяет признанного недостатка цены."},{"id":"74dc03f3-9fd0-559a-8b5e-0014c032fbbd","lesson_id":"1426eaaf-b270-5cd7-9386-63aff29c4222","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери правильно оформленный переход.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can I start a contrasting second sentence with however?"}],"options":[{"id":"vfd048fa005fd","label":"Yes: “However the route longer is.”"},{"id":"vbd92c5b471f2","label":"Yes: “However of the route is safer.”"},{"id":"v75bef77fd040","label":"Yes: “The route is longer. However, it is safer.”"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v75bef77fd040"},"reference_answer":"v75bef77fd040","incorrect_answer":"vfd048fa005fd","explanation":"В первом варианте две самостоятельные части и вводное However."},{"id":"f7e1770e-6ea8-5f62-80b5-f7565760c501","lesson_id":"1426eaaf-b270-5cd7-9386-63aff29c4222","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A difference presented between two ideas is a ___.","options":[{"id":"vb74acc06bd90","label":"deadline"},{"id":"ve4a4c8686710","label":"contrast"},{"id":"v798584b548dd","label":"receipt"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve4a4c8686710"},"reference_answer":"ve4a4c8686710","incorrect_answer":"v798584b548dd","explanation":"Contrast — сопоставленное различие."},{"id":"34ae94a6-e0ad-561f-abf1-09ec164e4cc6","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: She asked if ___ available on Friday.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v0cb7aa4f7862","label":"was I"},{"id":"v38b67439eb2f","label":"did I was"},{"id":"vd2adf839b5f5","label":"I was"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd2adf839b5f5"},"reference_answer":"vd2adf839b5f5","incorrect_answer":"v0cb7aa4f7862","explanation":"После if в пересказе вопроса нужен прямой порядок I was."},{"id":"cfa550fd-134d-5bcd-99cb-1f60356e00d5","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: was / did.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"He asked whether I ___ a student."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["was"]},"reference_answer":"was","incorrect_answer":"did","explanation":"Для исходного Are you a student? в заданном прошлом пересказе нужен was."},{"id":"2275572a-b01d-5a19-86ec-46de079282e9","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Она спросила, свободен ли я в пятницу.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"if"},{"id":"t4","label":"I"},{"id":"t5","label":"was"},{"id":"t6","label":"free"},{"id":"t7","label":"on"},{"id":"t8","label":"Friday."},{"id":"t1","label":"She"},{"id":"t2","label":"asked"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Asked if вводит косвенный yes/no-вопрос с прямым порядком слов."},{"id":"6415c28f-753b-5b56-9bb2-b93191dd1c49","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"He asked if was I ready."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["He asked if I was ready."]},"reference_answer":"He asked if I was ready.","incorrect_answer":"He asked if was I ready.","explanation":"В косвенной части восстанавливается I was."},{"id":"29c69a0a-b750-5e54-887d-560ce9d6ab3f","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"reading","prompt":"Был ли первый ответ Лины окончательным согласием?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"On Tuesday, the organiser asked Lina if she was available to help on Friday. Lina said she needed to check her work schedule. The organiser recorded this as a request awaiting a reply, not as confirmed help. Lina called back the next day and agreed to the afternoon only. The morning shift therefore still needed another volunteer.","options":[{"id":"v65869a60fbaa","label":"Yes; asking a question automatically creates agreement."},{"id":"vd5423ef63b98","label":"No; she needed to check her schedule."},{"id":"vde31f7040561","label":"Yes; she agreed to every shift immediately."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd5423ef63b98"},"reference_answer":"vd5423ef63b98","incorrect_answer":"vde31f7040561","explanation":"Сначала требовалась проверка расписания."},{"id":"ee412e0f-8e2e-5b55-b256-2b94b4c37a47","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l49ed37fac657","label":"enquire"},{"id":"lcd94e5d3d63b","label":"available"},{"id":"l83dc5d391a3a","label":"reply"},{"id":"l29fe44f47130","label":"schedule"}],"right":[{"id":"rb24a558f7f89","label":"отвечать"},{"id":"rc4f0d97bbc82","label":"расписание"},{"id":"rc294822ad79c","label":"спрашивать, узнавать"},{"id":"rcb1085113246","label":"свободный по времени"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l49ed37fac657":"rc294822ad79c","lcd94e5d3d63b":"rcb1085113246","l83dc5d391a3a":"rb24a558f7f89","l29fe44f47130":"rc4f0d97bbc82"}},"reference_answer":{"l49ed37fac657":"rc294822ad79c","lcd94e5d3d63b":"rcb1085113246","l83dc5d391a3a":"rb24a558f7f89","l29fe44f47130":"rc4f0d97bbc82"},"incorrect_answer":{"l49ed37fac657":"rcb1085113246","lcd94e5d3d63b":"rc294822ad79c","l83dc5d391a3a":"rb24a558f7f89","l29fe44f47130":"rc4f0d97bbc82"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: enquire — спрашивать, узнавать; available — свободный по времени; reply — отвечать; schedule — расписание."},{"id":"a3fea351-9117-5a2f-afb2-2af61031c23d","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"reading","prompt":"На какую смену ещё нужен человек?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"On Tuesday, the organiser asked Lina if she was available to help on Friday. Lina said she needed to check her work schedule. The organiser recorded this as a request awaiting a reply, not as confirmed help. Lina called back the next day and agreed to the afternoon only. The morning shift therefore still needed another volunteer.","options":[{"id":"v4c4ff4bc1457","label":"The morning shift."},{"id":"v91d9c10c209b","label":"The afternoon shift only."},{"id":"v1e637db6ea7c","label":"No shift, because all were filled."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4c4ff4bc1457"},"reference_answer":"v4c4ff4bc1457","incorrect_answer":"v91d9c10c209b","explanation":"Лина согласилась только на вторую половину дня."},{"id":"2dd02442-913e-5aa1-8b0f-6df39a9199eb","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Передай вопрос с whether и прямым порядком слов.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How can I report “Are you ready?” in the past?"}],"options":[{"id":"v19964f6522e1","label":"She asked whether did I ready."},{"id":"vbe3865ba03b5","label":"She asked whether I was ready."},{"id":"v0c058418b213","label":"She asked whether was I ready."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbe3865ba03b5"},"reference_answer":"vbe3865ba03b5","incorrect_answer":"v0c058418b213","explanation":"Whether I was ready сохраняет правильную структуру."},{"id":"9e851274-903d-5728-904a-f205de83385d","lesson_id":"9414688f-bcf6-5e1d-924f-a2602287e034","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To ask formally for information is to ___.","options":[{"id":"vaf5d82119fac","label":"enquire"},{"id":"v1423b971dc2b","label":"guarantee"},{"id":"v1cb325be67fb","label":"approve automatically"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vaf5d82119fac"},"reference_answer":"vaf5d82119fac","incorrect_answer":"v1423b971dc2b","explanation":"Enquire — запрашивать сведения, а не автоматически одобрять."},{"id":"06e7efa9-8973-5a33-8904-e71daa5b0201","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: She works nights and is used to ___ during the day.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v4d49e9f6aa50","label":"slept to"},{"id":"v023d200edea0","label":"sleeping"},{"id":"vcc243ee3f263","label":"sleep"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v023d200edea0"},"reference_answer":"v023d200edea0","incorrect_answer":"vcc243ee3f263","explanation":"После is used to нужен герундий sleeping."},{"id":"400d21d5-e416-5260-b8c3-4c884bfc15f3","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: work / working.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"It took several weeks to get used to ___ in a shared office."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["working"]},"reference_answer":"working","incorrect_answer":"work","explanation":"Get used to описывает привыкание; to здесь предлог."},{"id":"c77cb4e9-5d33-548a-a905-aa550c3bf7d3","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Я привык работать в небольшой команде.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"used"},{"id":"t4","label":"to"},{"id":"t5","label":"working"},{"id":"t6","label":"with"},{"id":"t7","label":"a"},{"id":"t8","label":"small"},{"id":"t9","label":"team."},{"id":"t1","label":"I"},{"id":"t2","label":"am"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Am used to working описывает привычность, не прежнюю отменённую привычку."},{"id":"d6656cca-735f-590d-9e2a-a73de94e752d","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"He is used to work with background noise."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["He is used to working with background noise."]},"reference_answer":"He is used to working with background noise.","incorrect_answer":"He is used to work with background noise.","explanation":"После is used to нужна -ing-форма working."},{"id":"3d9ba2d6-6ed0-5555-baea-dc5ef6bd01b0","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что описывает used to work в начале?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"Mina used to work alone in a quiet room. Her new job involved a shared office and regular interruptions. At first, she found it hard to concentrate, but gradually she got used to working with other people nearby. This did not mean that every interruption became helpful. She and her colleagues agreed on quiet periods for complex tasks. Becoming accustomed to the office involved both personal adjustment and a change in shared routines, rather than simply accepting every condition without discussion.","options":[{"id":"vc1a0da5f3e8b","label":"A previous working arrangement."},{"id":"v308f1fee5a3e","label":"A future promise to work alone forever."},{"id":"va3d3057874fb","label":"Proof that Mina enjoys every interruption."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc1a0da5f3e8b"},"reference_answer":"vc1a0da5f3e8b","incorrect_answer":"v308f1fee5a3e","explanation":"Used to work относится к прошлому рабочему порядку."},{"id":"942fe893-27eb-5392-80e0-2e2854aa46dc","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lbe2e6b7678d6","label":"accustomed"},{"id":"l9cf50aeb49d1","label":"adjust"},{"id":"l39adbf476981","label":"routine"},{"id":"l51a377d4410f","label":"unfamiliar"}],"right":[{"id":"ra13588384064","label":"привычный порядок"},{"id":"r8791841292e8","label":"незнакомый"},{"id":"r96fbd1b82619","label":"привыкший"},{"id":"r393a416e5ddd","label":"приспосабливаться"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lbe2e6b7678d6":"r96fbd1b82619","l9cf50aeb49d1":"r393a416e5ddd","l39adbf476981":"ra13588384064","l51a377d4410f":"r8791841292e8"}},"reference_answer":{"lbe2e6b7678d6":"r96fbd1b82619","l9cf50aeb49d1":"r393a416e5ddd","l39adbf476981":"ra13588384064","l51a377d4410f":"r8791841292e8"},"incorrect_answer":{"lbe2e6b7678d6":"r393a416e5ddd","l9cf50aeb49d1":"r96fbd1b82619","l39adbf476981":"ra13588384064","l51a377d4410f":"r8791841292e8"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: accustomed — привыкший; adjust — приспосабливаться; routine — привычный порядок; unfamiliar — незнакомый."},{"id":"685c29c9-111e-55b2-92ef-4e05fdb7e7c4","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"reading","prompt":"Означало ли привыкание согласие с любыми помехами?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"Mina used to work alone in a quiet room. Her new job involved a shared office and regular interruptions. At first, she found it hard to concentrate, but gradually she got used to working with other people nearby. This did not mean that every interruption became helpful. She and her colleagues agreed on quiet periods for complex tasks. Becoming accustomed to the office involved both personal adjustment and a change in shared routines, rather than simply accepting every condition without discussion.","options":[{"id":"v8481519dc1a9","label":"Yes; no shared routine changed."},{"id":"v591d39fb2ff6","label":"Yes; every interruption became useful."},{"id":"vf45260195a36","label":"No; the team also introduced quiet periods."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf45260195a36"},"reference_answer":"vf45260195a36","incorrect_answer":"v8481519dc1a9","explanation":"Текст различает личную адаптацию и согласованные изменения условий."},{"id":"29df3831-d91d-55fb-9a5e-424d597abf02","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Опиши продолжающееся привыкание.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Do you still find the early start difficult?"}],"options":[{"id":"v606a5158f9f0","label":"Less so; I am getting used to waking up early."},{"id":"ve41815e85cdd","label":"Less so; I am getting used to wake up early."},{"id":"vd5fe601bf89a","label":"Less so; I used getting wake up early."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v606a5158f9f0"},"reference_answer":"v606a5158f9f0","incorrect_answer":"ve41815e85cdd","explanation":"Getting used to + waking выражает процесс адаптации."},{"id":"f23bcdf5-11d7-5252-85ef-24b61ec40768","lesson_id":"35eddd75-a9f4-5b57-a37d-17bc6330e999","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A person who is familiar with a repeated situation is ___ to it.","options":[{"id":"v100c6b7ce009","label":"opposed by definition"},{"id":"vc0dd96473479","label":"entitled regardless"},{"id":"vb15a19a5f0d2","label":"accustomed"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb15a19a5f0d2"},"reference_answer":"vb15a19a5f0d2","incorrect_answer":"v100c6b7ce009","explanation":"Accustomed to означает привыкший к условиям."},{"id":"1f91e515-2a43-5fd7-8ef9-aff821a00dee","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: They ___ launch the service in May, but the inspection delayed it.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v24d1566bd051","label":"were going to"},{"id":"v5a05769694e6","label":"was going to"},{"id":"v8446959f4fdc","label":"were going launch"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v24d1566bd051"},"reference_answer":"v24d1566bd051","incorrect_answer":"v5a05769694e6","explanation":"They согласуется с were going to; последующая часть сообщает о препятствии."},{"id":"eaffbad7-9636-53f0-87d4-2cbb0d62da68","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: would / will to.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"She said she ___ contact us the next day."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["would"]},"reference_answer":"would","incorrect_answer":"will to","explanation":"Would передаёт будущее с точки зрения прошлого сообщения."},{"id":"4362b42f-7ab5-56ee-9bc8-e2ac766bfbd1","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Мы собирались открыться в мае.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"going"},{"id":"t4","label":"to"},{"id":"t5","label":"open"},{"id":"t6","label":"in"},{"id":"t7","label":"May."},{"id":"t1","label":"We"},{"id":"t2","label":"were"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Фраза сообщает о прошлом намерении; фактическая дата требует дополнительных сведений."},{"id":"8704f84e-00a5-5c0b-bc76-d0e68f54cb83","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The organiser was going open the hall in June."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The organiser was going to open the hall in June."]},"reference_answer":"The organiser was going to open the hall in June.","incorrect_answer":"The organiser was going open the hall in June.","explanation":"В конструкции going to необходимо to перед open."},{"id":"195ec217-691c-508f-8434-13fdec763502","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую ошибку сделал поздний бюллетень?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"In March, the organisers announced that they were going to open the community workshop in May. They expected the electrical inspection to finish in April. When the inspection identified a fault, the opening was postponed. A later newsletter accidentally repeated the original plan as though the workshop had already opened. The coordinator corrected it, explaining that the March announcement recorded an intention at that time, not the outcome after subsequent events. A revised date would be published only after the fault had been addressed.","options":[{"id":"v56dad57b9158","label":"It reported a revised date that had definitely been confirmed."},{"id":"v402e4f5eda35","label":"It denied that any plan had ever existed."},{"id":"v8dbfddbaf0a6","label":"It presented an earlier intention as a completed opening."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8dbfddbaf0a6"},"reference_answer":"v8dbfddbaf0a6","incorrect_answer":"v56dad57b9158","explanation":"Старый план был неверно превращён в сообщение о результате."},{"id":"967e07c1-6b12-5595-9bdd-862f3a92b7da","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l7f209b5a7676","label":"intention"},{"id":"lbb469bdadc2a","label":"subsequent"},{"id":"l688c0952048c","label":"revise"},{"id":"l39b97de92fa0","label":"postpone"}],"right":[{"id":"r7f8475c6efdb","label":"пересматривать"},{"id":"rb212d1738900","label":"откладывать"},{"id":"r095101f8ab0a","label":"намерение"},{"id":"r9f62fd2c6dba","label":"последующий"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l7f209b5a7676":"r095101f8ab0a","lbb469bdadc2a":"r9f62fd2c6dba","l688c0952048c":"r7f8475c6efdb","l39b97de92fa0":"rb212d1738900"}},"reference_answer":{"l7f209b5a7676":"r095101f8ab0a","lbb469bdadc2a":"r9f62fd2c6dba","l688c0952048c":"r7f8475c6efdb","l39b97de92fa0":"rb212d1738900"},"incorrect_answer":{"l7f209b5a7676":"r9f62fd2c6dba","lbb469bdadc2a":"r095101f8ab0a","l688c0952048c":"r7f8475c6efdb","l39b97de92fa0":"rb212d1738900"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: intention — намерение; subsequent — последующий; revise — пересматривать; postpone — откладывать."},{"id":"43c2bdf9-cd1a-5cd4-9bc7-d6ea0ffc9124","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"reading","prompt":"Когда обещали назвать новую дату?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"In March, the organisers announced that they were going to open the community workshop in May. They expected the electrical inspection to finish in April. When the inspection identified a fault, the opening was postponed. A later newsletter accidentally repeated the original plan as though the workshop had already opened. The coordinator corrected it, explaining that the March announcement recorded an intention at that time, not the outcome after subsequent events. A revised date would be published only after the fault had been addressed.","options":[{"id":"v0e2648795ac1","label":"Automatically on the original May date."},{"id":"vf3248bde3741","label":"After the fault had been addressed."},{"id":"vb83153119618","label":"Before any inspection took place."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf3248bde3741"},"reference_answer":"vf3248bde3741","incorrect_answer":"vb83153119618","explanation":"Указано условие новой публикации, а не безусловное сохранение старой даты."},{"id":"78ba0cb1-d021-5d7e-b0c8-2d9f85adf8e4","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Отдели намерение от выполнения.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “I was going to call” prove that the call happened?"}],"options":[{"id":"ve1c544e7f92a","label":"Yes; the intention guarantees the event."},{"id":"v640a02c7e662","label":"No; it proves the speaker never wanted to call."},{"id":"vec00efccd995","label":"No; it reports a past intention without confirming completion."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vec00efccd995"},"reference_answer":"vec00efccd995","incorrect_answer":"ve1c544e7f92a","explanation":"Was going to не устанавливает ни факт звонка, ни отсутствие желания."},{"id":"3f2fcfc8-cd77-5960-9228-c6353df55259","lesson_id":"70e3e02a-4dbf-5293-8f1d-04b4d2b8303e","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Events happening later than the original announcement are ___ events.","options":[{"id":"vc44946599fdc","label":"simultaneously earlier"},{"id":"v078ec3f6f42c","label":"subsequent"},{"id":"v380a699520b3","label":"prior"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v078ec3f6f42c"},"reference_answer":"v078ec3f6f42c","incorrect_answer":"v380a699520b3","explanation":"Subsequent — последующий, а prior — предшествующий."},{"id":"53d2ae61-af4c-5294-b28a-5e46b4a78c50","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The person to ___ the enquiry was sent has replied.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vb6070760ed84","label":"which"},{"id":"ve2769739e34c","label":"whose of"},{"id":"v3ef19c011859","label":"whom"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3ef19c011859"},"reference_answer":"v3ef19c011859","incorrect_answer":"vb6070760ed84","explanation":"После to о человеке в формальной модели нужно whom."},{"id":"e38c5c53-97c6-5b67-a929-9d30a008fd3e","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: who / which.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"This is the folder in ___ the copies are stored."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["which"]},"reference_answer":"which","incorrect_answer":"who","explanation":"Для папки после in используется which."},{"id":"f6812eb8-94fd-5219-b29c-415dc995898a","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Человек, которому я написал, ответил.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"to"},{"id":"t4","label":"whom"},{"id":"t5","label":"I"},{"id":"t6","label":"wrote"},{"id":"t7","label":"has"},{"id":"t8","label":"replied."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"person"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"To whom — формальная отсылка к получателю письма."},{"id":"c3c2fa98-4a90-5311-9e7a-1344f0fbf9e4","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The office to which I sent the form has reply."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The office to which I sent the form has replied."]},"reference_answer":"The office to which I sent the form has replied.","incorrect_answer":"The office to which I sent the form has reply.","explanation":"После has в Present Perfect требуется причастие replied; to which уже оформлено правильно."},{"id":"fde8c1e7-da81-56c8-af38-cc825be17dce","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какие роли различает архивист?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"An archivist traced a set of letters to the office to which they had originally been addressed. The recipient named on the envelopes was no longer employed there, but a register recorded the department responsible for answering enquiries. The archivist distinguished the person to whom a letter was addressed from the person who actually drafted the reply. That distinction mattered because an official signature did not necessarily identify the writer of every sentence. The catalogue note therefore described the correspondence precisely without assuming that recipient, signatory and author were always the same person.","options":[{"id":"v731ea378e055","label":"The author and all readers as necessarily identical."},{"id":"v86f55349311c","label":"The intended recipient and the person drafting the reply."},{"id":"vacfda3a0747b","label":"Only the colour and size of every envelope."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v86f55349311c"},"reference_answer":"v86f55349311c","incorrect_answer":"vacfda3a0747b","explanation":"Текст специально отделяет адресата, подписанта и составителя ответа."},{"id":"7d620db5-677d-5b9d-a59f-fff3d4f305b5","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lc52268912f13","label":"recipient"},{"id":"l9833f24c31fb","label":"correspondence"},{"id":"l7ba62b357349","label":"archive"},{"id":"l2265640817b4","label":"enquiry"}],"right":[{"id":"r096f5267211f","label":"архив"},{"id":"r5d5dc83c3e8e","label":"запрос сведений"},{"id":"r65e515794c7e","label":"получатель"},{"id":"rfe5057cca401","label":"переписка"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lc52268912f13":"r65e515794c7e","l9833f24c31fb":"rfe5057cca401","l7ba62b357349":"r096f5267211f","l2265640817b4":"r5d5dc83c3e8e"}},"reference_answer":{"lc52268912f13":"r65e515794c7e","l9833f24c31fb":"rfe5057cca401","l7ba62b357349":"r096f5267211f","l2265640817b4":"r5d5dc83c3e8e"},"incorrect_answer":{"lc52268912f13":"rfe5057cca401","l9833f24c31fb":"r65e515794c7e","l7ba62b357349":"r096f5267211f","l2265640817b4":"r5d5dc83c3e8e"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: recipient — получатель; correspondence — переписка; archive — архив; enquiry — запрос сведений."},{"id":"12b984b1-b4b5-5779-bb50-cce98ad5378a","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему подписи недостаточно для определения автора всех предложений?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"An archivist traced a set of letters to the office to which they had originally been addressed. The recipient named on the envelopes was no longer employed there, but a register recorded the department responsible for answering enquiries. The archivist distinguished the person to whom a letter was addressed from the person who actually drafted the reply. That distinction mattered because an official signature did not necessarily identify the writer of every sentence. The catalogue note therefore described the correspondence precisely without assuming that recipient, signatory and author were always the same person.","options":[{"id":"v57a2ffd6c1a3","label":"An official signatory may not have drafted the entire reply."},{"id":"ve21d8b189366","label":"A signature always proves that no reply exists."},{"id":"veee9ebcd7087","label":"Registers never contain department names."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v57a2ffd6c1a3"},"reference_answer":"v57a2ffd6c1a3","incorrect_answer":"ve21d8b189366","explanation":"Официальная подпись не гарантирует личное написание каждого предложения."},{"id":"8b5e8d41-c580-55a0-94a3-7714421a97ec","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Отнеси with к человеку в формальной конструкции.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Choose the formal version with the preposition first."}],"options":[{"id":"ve3d5201585e6","label":"The colleague with whose I worked has retired."},{"id":"va4ddbd35cd6a","label":"The colleague with whom I worked has retired."},{"id":"v464b5e37c26c","label":"The colleague with which I worked has retired."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va4ddbd35cd6a"},"reference_answer":"va4ddbd35cd6a","incorrect_answer":"v464b5e37c26c","explanation":"После with о человеке здесь используется whom."},{"id":"0db60830-8c9c-552f-a686-c512ce3a3063","lesson_id":"8ed530a6-c062-535d-8533-8a40fd15f449","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The person for whom a letter is intended is its ___.","options":[{"id":"v73a28710f7d9","label":"recipient"},{"id":"v11f6c9e0c3f3","label":"author necessarily"},{"id":"ve39f1083b728","label":"publisher necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v73a28710f7d9"},"reference_answer":"v73a28710f7d9","incorrect_answer":"v11f6c9e0c3f3","explanation":"Recipient — адресат или получатель, не обязательно автор или издатель."},{"id":"6ca8e04d-b665-5869-9350-ad099e31d583","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: ___ arrives first can collect the key from reception.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v5b85fc6588fd","label":"Which thing"},{"id":"v16c366febc54","label":"Whoever"},{"id":"ve6cc35725053","label":"Whatever"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v16c366febc54"},"reference_answer":"v16c366febc54","incorrect_answer":"ve6cc35725053","explanation":"Речь о человеке, поэтому Whoever."},{"id":"a0d08c77-4b1a-5ff6-ae96-6d13452b2eae","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: whatever / whoever.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Take ___ materials you need from this table."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["whatever"]},"reference_answer":"whatever","incorrect_answer":"whoever","explanation":"Materials — предметы, не люди."},{"id":"1d4a6b72-f6a8-578a-90bc-1c4c268b8f62","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Тот, кто закончит первым, может помочь следующей группе.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"first"},{"id":"t4","label":"can"},{"id":"t5","label":"help"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"next"},{"id":"t8","label":"group."},{"id":"t1","label":"Whoever"},{"id":"t2","label":"finishes"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Whoever вводит неопределённого по личности участника."},{"id":"b68b485d-73a0-58f4-a180-9030407ab4d9","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Whatever person arrives first can collects the key."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Whatever person arrives first can collect the key."]},"reference_answer":"Whatever person arrives first can collect the key.","incorrect_answer":"Whatever person arrives first can collects the key.","explanation":"После can убирается -s у collect; whatever person здесь допустимо как «любой человек»."},{"id":"37a2f44f-bf8e-5391-a9e5-7eb9e91fc9e6","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что означало take whatever they needed?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The workshop leader placed spare materials on a table and told groups to take whatever they needed for their own designs. This was permission to choose relevant materials, not an instruction to take the whole supply. Whoever finished the first stage could help another group, provided that their own tools had been put away safely. Several participants welcomed the flexibility, while the leader reminded them that an open choice still operated within the stated purpose and safety rules.","options":[{"id":"vab3ee3e209d7","label":"Choose materials relevant to their designs."},{"id":"vd5964ea650e7","label":"Take the entire supply regardless of need."},{"id":"vbcabcc16825a","label":"Ignore all safety rules."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vab3ee3e209d7"},"reference_answer":"vab3ee3e209d7","incorrect_answer":"vd5964ea650e7","explanation":"Need и контекст собственных проектов ограничивают цель выбора."},{"id":"2f65ff3e-c592-5258-97d2-466187584031","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l1253f743a3a5","label":"whatever"},{"id":"l3a00fe208afc","label":"whoever"},{"id":"l9c26f47a6307","label":"whichever"},{"id":"la30dc96f9513","label":"requirement"}],"right":[{"id":"r2d581c40a53a","label":"любой из ограниченного выбора"},{"id":"r6cb07fe32bd0","label":"требование"},{"id":"r98caf275593b","label":"всё, что"},{"id":"r743a56f9d44a","label":"любой, кто"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l1253f743a3a5":"r98caf275593b","l3a00fe208afc":"r743a56f9d44a","l9c26f47a6307":"r2d581c40a53a","la30dc96f9513":"r6cb07fe32bd0"}},"reference_answer":{"l1253f743a3a5":"r98caf275593b","l3a00fe208afc":"r743a56f9d44a","l9c26f47a6307":"r2d581c40a53a","la30dc96f9513":"r6cb07fe32bd0"},"incorrect_answer":{"l1253f743a3a5":"r743a56f9d44a","l3a00fe208afc":"r98caf275593b","l9c26f47a6307":"r2d581c40a53a","la30dc96f9513":"r6cb07fe32bd0"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: whatever — всё, что; whoever — любой, кто; whichever — любой из ограниченного выбора; requirement — требование."},{"id":"5ea7218b-81d1-5751-bb4f-fcd1a3520b84","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"reading","prompt":"При каком условии можно помочь другой группе?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The workshop leader placed spare materials on a table and told groups to take whatever they needed for their own designs. This was permission to choose relevant materials, not an instruction to take the whole supply. Whoever finished the first stage could help another group, provided that their own tools had been put away safely. Several participants welcomed the flexibility, while the leader reminded them that an open choice still operated within the stated purpose and safety rules.","options":[{"id":"v39cb75d8b484","label":"Before dealing with any of their own tools."},{"id":"v96b7d8e0ff6e","label":"Only after taking every material from the table."},{"id":"v9a3f3a109aac","label":"After putting away their own tools safely."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9a3f3a109aac"},"reference_answer":"v9a3f3a109aac","incorrect_answer":"v39cb75d8b484","explanation":"Требование безопасно убрать инструменты дано явно."},{"id":"e41040bc-c634-52b5-b17a-8cbdeacd63f7","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сформулируй правило для любого первого добровольца.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"We do not know which volunteer will arrive first."}],"options":[{"id":"veed361066936","label":"Whoever arrives first can open the room."},{"id":"v4073d570f544","label":"Whatever arrives first can open the room, referring to a volunteer."},{"id":"vc880743c77b6","label":"Whoever arrive first can opens the room."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"veed361066936"},"reference_answer":"veed361066936","incorrect_answer":"v4073d570f544","explanation":"Whoever относится к человеку; arrives и can open оформлены правильно."},{"id":"8899d931-cc18-5108-83fc-fee21fdfdbed","lesson_id":"c6361a77-ccdf-5d01-a273-7c893189b394","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"For an unspecified person satisfying a condition, use ___.","options":[{"id":"va6ca59e91ab9","label":"whatever"},{"id":"v1cae9ecec76b","label":"wherever"},{"id":"v714459bfbf29","label":"whoever"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v714459bfbf29"},"reference_answer":"v714459bfbf29","incorrect_answer":"va6ca59e91ab9","explanation":"Whoever — любой человек, который соответствует условию."},{"id":"4b0b182c-ce54-5693-903a-aff6ba5139bf","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The figures are not checked yet. I would rather you ___ before publishing them.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v8a7acc42cc67","label":"waited"},{"id":"v234b64eb873f","label":"to wait"},{"id":"vb1758d15d23a","label":"waiting"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8a7acc42cc67"},"reference_answer":"v8a7acc42cc67","incorrect_answer":"v234b64eb873f","explanation":"С отдельным you после would rather нужна форма waited для текущего предпочтения."},{"id":"4b643913-8415-5fb6-b13b-547c2ddfd584","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: to consult / consulted.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I would rather you ___ me before changing the schedule."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["consulted"]},"reference_answer":"consulted","incorrect_answer":"to consult","explanation":"Другой субъект you требует Past Simple в этой модели предпочтения."},{"id":"89cf2dac-14a7-5bb0-8ec1-f10230989f33","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Я бы предпочёл, чтобы ты дождался подтверждения.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"rather"},{"id":"t4","label":"you"},{"id":"t5","label":"waited"},{"id":"t6","label":"for"},{"id":"t7","label":"confirmation."},{"id":"t1","label":"I"},{"id":"t2","label":"would"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Waited здесь не доказывает уже совершённое ожидание в прошлом."},{"id":"2230e99d-e215-53ec-ab23-904c929ccac2","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I would rather you to ask before booking."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I would rather you asked before booking."]},"reference_answer":"I would rather you asked before booking.","incorrect_answer":"I would rather you to ask before booking.","explanation":"После would rather + you в данном предпочтении используется asked, не to ask."},{"id":"503e822f-3814-5e39-b60f-4eb245690155","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"reading","prompt":"К какому времени относится предпочтение координатора?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A coordinator received a draft announcement containing a provisional opening date. She told the assistant, “I would rather you waited for confirmation before posting it.” The assistant initially thought she was referring to something he had failed to do yesterday. She clarified that the past form expressed a current preference about a future action. The date remained provisional because the final inspection had not taken place. They agreed to prepare the announcement now but publish it only after confirmation, keeping preparation separate from public commitment.","options":[{"id":"v0d2688ee0243","label":"Only a completed action yesterday."},{"id":"v57ca64b2d353","label":"A statement that confirmation is unnecessary."},{"id":"v7347ecf30519","label":"A current preference about whether to publish next."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7347ecf30519"},"reference_answer":"v7347ecf30519","incorrect_answer":"v0d2688ee0243","explanation":"В тексте прямо объяснена разница грамматической формы и временного смысла."},{"id":"31805c40-7d45-54a4-aa2c-30ed3af02fc0","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l81c6dfdcda7d","label":"preference"},{"id":"lc4e8718a644b","label":"deadline"},{"id":"l9b2f67cf3aeb","label":"consult"},{"id":"lb3c77e8b8fb9","label":"provisional"}],"right":[{"id":"r9ccf4a9789ca","label":"советоваться"},{"id":"rb8756f9e6ae2","label":"предварительный"},{"id":"r18dcdbbb3851","label":"предпочтение"},{"id":"r66d97d437a9e","label":"срок"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l81c6dfdcda7d":"r18dcdbbb3851","lc4e8718a644b":"r66d97d437a9e","l9b2f67cf3aeb":"r9ccf4a9789ca","lb3c77e8b8fb9":"rb8756f9e6ae2"}},"reference_answer":{"l81c6dfdcda7d":"r18dcdbbb3851","lc4e8718a644b":"r66d97d437a9e","l9b2f67cf3aeb":"r9ccf4a9789ca","lb3c77e8b8fb9":"rb8756f9e6ae2"},"incorrect_answer":{"l81c6dfdcda7d":"r66d97d437a9e","lc4e8718a644b":"r18dcdbbb3851","l9b2f67cf3aeb":"r9ccf4a9789ca","lb3c77e8b8fb9":"rb8756f9e6ae2"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: preference — предпочтение; deadline — срок; consult — советоваться; provisional — предварительный."},{"id":"69ea9b20-4c25-5238-b330-79ad09ee0f8c","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"reading","prompt":"О чём договорились?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A coordinator received a draft announcement containing a provisional opening date. She told the assistant, “I would rather you waited for confirmation before posting it.” The assistant initially thought she was referring to something he had failed to do yesterday. She clarified that the past form expressed a current preference about a future action. The date remained provisional because the final inspection had not taken place. They agreed to prepare the announcement now but publish it only after confirmation, keeping preparation separate from public commitment.","options":[{"id":"v78d56271f964","label":"Delete every draft before preparing it."},{"id":"v0eb3d61540e5","label":"Prepare the notice now and publish after confirmation."},{"id":"vd4641f1e8305","label":"Publish immediately as a guaranteed date."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0eb3d61540e5"},"reference_answer":"v0eb3d61540e5","incorrect_answer":"vd4641f1e8305","explanation":"Подготовку отделили от обязательства перед публикой."},{"id":"96473d95-5dd4-5aa8-9e12-0b388b31c219","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Вырази предпочтение относительно действия другого человека.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can I share this unfinished estimate?"}],"options":[{"id":"v7a5ff3d18163","label":"I would rather you to check it first."},{"id":"vb5fa4919aef2","label":"I would rather you checking it first."},{"id":"vfb337ce2f631","label":"I would rather you checked it first."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vfb337ce2f631"},"reference_answer":"vfb337ce2f631","incorrect_answer":"v7a5ff3d18163","explanation":"Would rather you checked — правильная модель с отдельным субъектом."},{"id":"0c00c4b7-ebf4-5fe7-943c-c91d7ffb974f","lesson_id":"6a0cef7f-9215-5a38-951e-34cf636ed2d8","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A date that may still change is ___.","options":[{"id":"v16b19a8151e6","label":"expired necessarily"},{"id":"vaeea578d65e4","label":"provisional"},{"id":"v7f30cd01aebf","label":"irrevocably confirmed"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vaeea578d65e4"},"reference_answer":"vaeea578d65e4","incorrect_answer":"v7f30cd01aebf","explanation":"Provisional означает предварительный, а не окончательно подтверждённый."},{"id":"0bbde050-ffc8-529a-9ec4-a81c457e3f71","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The final figures ___ before publication.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v8a681fdbe000","label":"will checked"},{"id":"v76a59cba9112","label":"will be checking by"},{"id":"vfb0b9076afc7","label":"will be checked"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vfb0b9076afc7"},"reference_answer":"vfb0b9076afc7","incorrect_answer":"v8a681fdbe000","explanation":"Будущий пассив строится will be + причастие checked."},{"id":"d845134a-f29f-5575-9d94-53df467eb558","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: inspected / inspecting.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The equipment will be ___ next week."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["inspected"]},"reference_answer":"inspected","incorrect_answer":"inspecting","explanation":"Объект проверяют, поэтому inspected в пассиве."},{"id":"d3af0c8c-8d4d-509e-9021-8de41ea33bcd","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Черновик проверят перед выпуском.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"will"},{"id":"t4","label":"be"},{"id":"t5","label":"reviewed"},{"id":"t6","label":"before"},{"id":"t7","label":"release."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"draft"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Will be reviewed сообщает о будущей проверке, не о её завершении."},{"id":"fbeebfc1-b764-5caf-b137-c82ee200668d","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The results will checked by an independent reviewer."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The results will be checked by an independent reviewer."]},"reference_answer":"The results will be checked by an independent reviewer.","incorrect_answer":"The results will checked by an independent reviewer.","explanation":"Между will и причастием checked требуется be."},{"id":"cf07f685-347f-57d4-8dc8-24513b6533dd","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему сокращённая формулировка была неверна?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A project update said that the final figures would be checked by an independent reviewer before release. A colleague shortened this to “independently checked figures” in a presentation prepared the same day. The review had not yet happened. The project lead asked for the slide to be corrected, because a future commitment had been turned into a completed assurance. The team could describe the planned safeguard, but it needed separate evidence of completion before presenting the figures as reviewed. The release date remained conditional on that work.","options":[{"id":"v29910a50721f","label":"It said that no reviewer had been planned."},{"id":"vefeb344c2207","label":"It presented a planned review as already completed."},{"id":"vd5df434ba064","label":"It accurately reported a finished independent review."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vefeb344c2207"},"reference_answer":"vefeb344c2207","incorrect_answer":"vd5df434ba064","explanation":"Проверка ещё не состоялась; время и статус действия были изменены."},{"id":"7ead7a48-2890-5d58-a8a3-7b61ee29cc13","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lf3e8c541ba0c","label":"inspection"},{"id":"la8763cfe7b2a","label":"release"},{"id":"l693363c45119","label":"verify"},{"id":"l16cdaaee6f68","label":"completion"}],"right":[{"id":"rf9af60bc72de","label":"проверять"},{"id":"r4eddd2c1c561","label":"завершение"},{"id":"r9d0ffa6d3ab0","label":"проверка"},{"id":"r238c1d608ec3","label":"выпуск"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lf3e8c541ba0c":"r9d0ffa6d3ab0","la8763cfe7b2a":"r238c1d608ec3","l693363c45119":"rf9af60bc72de","l16cdaaee6f68":"r4eddd2c1c561"}},"reference_answer":{"lf3e8c541ba0c":"r9d0ffa6d3ab0","la8763cfe7b2a":"r238c1d608ec3","l693363c45119":"rf9af60bc72de","l16cdaaee6f68":"r4eddd2c1c561"},"incorrect_answer":{"lf3e8c541ba0c":"r238c1d608ec3","la8763cfe7b2a":"r9d0ffa6d3ab0","l693363c45119":"rf9af60bc72de","l16cdaaee6f68":"r4eddd2c1c561"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: inspection — проверка; release — выпуск; verify — проверять; completion — завершение."},{"id":"8d187ecb-716c-5670-93c4-1cac8a8833e9","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что нужно для заявления о проверенных данных?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A project update said that the final figures would be checked by an independent reviewer before release. A colleague shortened this to “independently checked figures” in a presentation prepared the same day. The review had not yet happened. The project lead asked for the slide to be corrected, because a future commitment had been turned into a completed assurance. The team could describe the planned safeguard, but it needed separate evidence of completion before presenting the figures as reviewed. The release date remained conditional on that work.","options":[{"id":"ve6a4b4ccdd38","label":"Evidence that the review has actually been completed."},{"id":"v300b897c1ebd","label":"Only the intention to arrange a review."},{"id":"v68cee62d25ef","label":"A shorter slide title regardless of timing."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve6a4b4ccdd38"},"reference_answer":"ve6a4b4ccdd38","incorrect_answer":"v300b897c1ebd","explanation":"Планируемая мера и доказательство её исполнения различаются."},{"id":"aedf7eb6-3086-5979-9195-832c97d4a8bb","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Отдели нынешнее состояние от запланированного действия.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Have these documents already been reviewed?"}],"options":[{"id":"v703570c59ede","label":"Not yet. They will reviewed tomorrow."},{"id":"v37302ede9cc4","label":"Not yet. They will be reviewed tomorrow."},{"id":"v782e26f0f451","label":"Yes. Will be reviewed always means completed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v37302ede9cc4"},"reference_answer":"v37302ede9cc4","incorrect_answer":"v782e26f0f451","explanation":"Not yet и will be reviewed сохраняют реальную последовательность."},{"id":"0dbcd61e-b90d-5e0a-9ed8-89c42e0c9ec9","lesson_id":"334ce837-cdca-5239-8730-7f6554988b47","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Finishing a task is its ___.","options":[{"id":"v641f0187ca5c","label":"completion"},{"id":"vc74a3e9eb4a6","label":"proposal"},{"id":"v3e53ed4c3e7a","label":"reservation"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v641f0187ca5c"},"reference_answer":"v641f0187ca5c","incorrect_answer":"vc74a3e9eb4a6","explanation":"Completion — завершение, в отличие от предложения или оговорки."},{"id":"1cf7ef9e-59ee-533b-8d6b-c02374cb225c","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: We do not know whether the grant will arrive. ___ it does, costs will still need checking.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v68e7ea4ec896","label":"Despite of"},{"id":"vee35fc4ff5f8","label":"Even if"},{"id":"v83055b5a3935","label":"Because of"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vee35fc4ff5f8"},"reference_answer":"vee35fc4ff5f8","incorrect_answer":"v83055b5a3935","explanation":"Неподтверждённое получение вводится как допущение even if."},{"id":"b9a13db1-f476-55e4-896c-f00270475090","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: of / though.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"It was definitely raining. We went ahead even ___ it was raining."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["though"]},"reference_answer":"though","incorrect_answer":"of","explanation":"Even though вводит признанный факт с полной придаточной частью."},{"id":"16a75840-d142-5f49-a5c4-51e0471bd31c","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Даже если грант поступит, нам потребуется аккуратный бюджет.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"the"},{"id":"t4","label":"grant"},{"id":"t5","label":"arrives,"},{"id":"t6","label":"we"},{"id":"t7","label":"will"},{"id":"t8","label":"need"},{"id":"t9","label":"a"},{"id":"t10","label":"careful"},{"id":"t11","label":"budget."},{"id":"t1","label":"Even"},{"id":"t2","label":"if"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t1"],"explanation":"Even if не подтверждает, что грант уже получен."},{"id":"c5acf0ce-3b8e-50de-9ca4-b9b88b261d04","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Even despite the grant was approved, the timetable remained difficult."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Even though the grant was approved, the timetable remained difficult."]},"reference_answer":"Even though the grant was approved, the timetable remained difficult.","incorrect_answer":"Even despite the grant was approved, the timetable remained difficult.","explanation":"Перед полной уступительной частью здесь нужно even though."},{"id":"b640a846-d9b2-52d4-9ed5-7e3a2ca12eac","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую ошибку внёс пересказ?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The organisers wrote, “Even if the grant is approved, we will need to reduce some costs.” A supporter repeated the message as “Even though the grant has been approved”, unintentionally presenting a possibility as a confirmed fact. The organiser corrected the wording. The funding decision was still pending, and the cost issue would remain relevant in either case. Accurate reporting required preserving the distinction between the hypothetical concession and an acknowledged event, rather than merely retaining the general idea that money alone would not solve every problem.","options":[{"id":"v613b960a9e25","label":"It treated possible approval as confirmed approval."},{"id":"vef9a14dab121","label":"It preserved the grant’s pending status exactly."},{"id":"v41797c3e58af","label":"It proved that the grant had been refused."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v613b960a9e25"},"reference_answer":"v613b960a9e25","incorrect_answer":"vef9a14dab121","explanation":"Смена even if на even though вместе со временем утверждает несуществующее подтверждение."},{"id":"ca685547-51b0-5e64-9ac7-3a426a978150","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l196005f3c2d3","label":"hypothesis"},{"id":"l722806ef257c","label":"concession"},{"id":"l1d93dcc1a523","label":"confirmed"},{"id":"l031d8c4ed42e","label":"contingency"}],"right":[{"id":"r3e492122ff83","label":"подтверждённый"},{"id":"rb6a678f8d88a","label":"непредвиденная ситуация"},{"id":"r493bbc6b53bb","label":"гипотеза"},{"id":"r10b7fa696652","label":"уступка"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l196005f3c2d3":"r493bbc6b53bb","l722806ef257c":"r10b7fa696652","l1d93dcc1a523":"r3e492122ff83","l031d8c4ed42e":"rb6a678f8d88a"}},"reference_answer":{"l196005f3c2d3":"r493bbc6b53bb","l722806ef257c":"r10b7fa696652","l1d93dcc1a523":"r3e492122ff83","l031d8c4ed42e":"rb6a678f8d88a"},"incorrect_answer":{"l196005f3c2d3":"r10b7fa696652","l722806ef257c":"r493bbc6b53bb","l1d93dcc1a523":"r3e492122ff83","l031d8c4ed42e":"rb6a678f8d88a"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: hypothesis — гипотеза; concession — уступка; confirmed — подтверждённый; contingency — непредвиденная ситуация."},{"id":"2e19d448-6768-5eed-b852-4a6ea51f4f35","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что остаётся общим при обоих вариантах решения?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The organisers wrote, “Even if the grant is approved, we will need to reduce some costs.” A supporter repeated the message as “Even though the grant has been approved”, unintentionally presenting a possibility as a confirmed fact. The organiser corrected the wording. The funding decision was still pending, and the cost issue would remain relevant in either case. Accurate reporting required preserving the distinction between the hypothetical concession and an acknowledged event, rather than merely retaining the general idea that money alone would not solve every problem.","options":[{"id":"v13590e040aa7","label":"Funding is already guaranteed."},{"id":"v9ad82830e6e5","label":"The organisers no longer need a budget."},{"id":"v01989001d2bb","label":"Some costs still need attention."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v01989001d2bb"},"reference_answer":"v01989001d2bb","incorrect_answer":"v13590e040aa7","explanation":"Проблема расходов остаётся, но это не снимает неопределённость самого финансирования."},{"id":"fe5eb1e4-0d4a-5b9a-9bb2-cbf7e918a90d","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани статус допущения.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can I report “Even if the plan works” as proof that it works?"}],"options":[{"id":"va65af1ea9b4a","label":"No; the clause introduces a hypothetical concession."},{"id":"v8a4619415eaa","label":"Yes; every if-clause establishes its content as fact."},{"id":"v0941a926cf6a","label":"Yes; even cancels all uncertainty."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va65af1ea9b4a"},"reference_answer":"va65af1ea9b4a","incorrect_answer":"v8a4619415eaa","explanation":"Even if не подтверждает истинность введённого условия."},{"id":"e02074dc-c7ca-562f-8119-2ac5949cc078","lesson_id":"6f3d318a-33d8-580a-8990-e7c3bc939252","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A possibility considered for planning is a ___.","options":[{"id":"vb23506c7a5e7","label":"completed guarantee"},{"id":"v28f93c9a0151","label":"verdict necessarily"},{"id":"v3cd8a37babc6","label":"contingency"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3cd8a37babc6"},"reference_answer":"v3cd8a37babc6","incorrect_answer":"vb23506c7a5e7","explanation":"Contingency — возможная ситуация, которую учитывают при планировании."},{"id":"c274c232-9c7a-5065-84d6-2798f3299c5b","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: I remember ___ the door: I can clearly recall turning the key.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v8badc71cefe3","label":"locking"},{"id":"v390d24ebf3b5","label":"to locking"},{"id":"v926fecfb94b0","label":"lock to"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8badc71cefe3"},"reference_answer":"v8badc71cefe3","incorrect_answer":"v390d24ebf3b5","explanation":"Воспоминание о выполненном действии выражается remember locking."},{"id":"101181a3-2c4b-5a63-a20b-df31a6fd2b19","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: to / for.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Please remember ___ lock the door before leaving."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["to"]},"reference_answer":"to","incorrect_answer":"for","explanation":"Просьба не забыть выполнить действие использует remember to lock."},{"id":"567fc316-aa6a-5bb8-a936-c33fb4943ddb","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Мы остановились, чтобы проверить карту.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"to"},{"id":"t4","label":"check"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"map."},{"id":"t1","label":"We"},{"id":"t2","label":"stopped"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t1"],"explanation":"Stop to check обозначает цель остановки другого действия, не прекращение проверки."},{"id":"0e8fe8d1-13c8-510b-b377-262c34d558d0","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Remember to turning off the lights."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Remember to turn off the lights."]},"reference_answer":"Remember to turn off the lights.","incorrect_answer":"Remember to turning off the lights.","explanation":"В просьбе не забыть нужен инфинитив to turn."},{"id":"9c021ec6-465b-5843-8dbf-3692d4b87995","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что означает stopped to check the map?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a long walk, the group stopped to check the map at a junction. Later, the leader asked everyone to stop checking their phones while crossing a busy road. The two uses of stop described different relationships between actions. At the end, she reminded a volunteer to lock the equipment cupboard. He replied that he remembered locking it before departure and described where he had put the key. His reply referred to a memory of a completed action, while her reminder concerned ensuring that the task was done.","options":[{"id":"v82762817f4ad","label":"They gave up checking maps forever."},{"id":"vd2a7f4bd9ac7","label":"They crossed without looking at anything."},{"id":"v24641c7307ef","label":"They paused the walk in order to check the map."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v24641c7307ef"},"reference_answer":"v24641c7307ef","incorrect_answer":"v82762817f4ad","explanation":"To check задаёт цель остановки прогулки."},{"id":"027d7801-4353-5dab-b89a-c61ea431bd4e","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l78aadf3a1876","label":"recall"},{"id":"l9ea95edb6c30","label":"reminder"},{"id":"ldbf51fdc9a07","label":"pause"},{"id":"l75dbe050bfff","label":"cease"}],"right":[{"id":"r9d108be7e231","label":"пауза"},{"id":"ra1b1c207bf09","label":"прекращать"},{"id":"r537829ea3ed4","label":"вспоминать"},{"id":"re50bfc2a3fcf","label":"напоминание"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l78aadf3a1876":"r537829ea3ed4","l9ea95edb6c30":"re50bfc2a3fcf","ldbf51fdc9a07":"r9d108be7e231","l75dbe050bfff":"ra1b1c207bf09"}},"reference_answer":{"l78aadf3a1876":"r537829ea3ed4","l9ea95edb6c30":"re50bfc2a3fcf","ldbf51fdc9a07":"r9d108be7e231","l75dbe050bfff":"ra1b1c207bf09"},"incorrect_answer":{"l78aadf3a1876":"re50bfc2a3fcf","l9ea95edb6c30":"r537829ea3ed4","ldbf51fdc9a07":"r9d108be7e231","l75dbe050bfff":"ra1b1c207bf09"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: recall — вспоминать; reminder — напоминание; pause — пауза; cease — прекращать."},{"id":"bfc472f8-00cb-5f70-b269-03a0356f4e8d","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"reading","prompt":"На что ссылался волонтёр с remembered locking?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a long walk, the group stopped to check the map at a junction. Later, the leader asked everyone to stop checking their phones while crossing a busy road. The two uses of stop described different relationships between actions. At the end, she reminded a volunteer to lock the equipment cupboard. He replied that he remembered locking it before departure and described where he had put the key. His reply referred to a memory of a completed action, while her reminder concerned ensuring that the task was done.","options":[{"id":"v8032e38812da","label":"An admission that he had never locked anything."},{"id":"v55bfe8323189","label":"A memory of having performed the action."},{"id":"v21551bf38b1c","label":"A promise that he might lock it next week."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v55bfe8323189"},"reference_answer":"v55bfe8323189","incorrect_answer":"v21551bf38b1c","explanation":"Locking представляет действие как уже совершённое и вспоминаемое."},{"id":"c95092eb-2b8b-5d24-8c5c-5c89714ac4a2","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани различие двух моделей.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"What is the difference between “stop talking” and “stop to talk”?"}],"options":[{"id":"vaf8253ed949d","label":"Both always mean ending every conversation permanently."},{"id":"ve11faffc0dfb","label":"The first always means start talking; the second means remain silent."},{"id":"v897085628e41","label":"The first ends talking; the second pauses another activity in order to talk."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v897085628e41"},"reference_answer":"v897085628e41","incorrect_answer":"vaf8253ed949d","explanation":"-ing обозначает прекращаемое действие, to-infinitive — цель остановки."},{"id":"fae5292c-8b5b-516f-8150-0333bb305889","lesson_id":"b51e3335-5f3a-5ca3-9505-8d886c1cc03a","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To bring a past event back to mind is to ___ it.","options":[{"id":"vb8d7d89ee715","label":"postpone"},{"id":"v206be824acbc","label":"recall"},{"id":"v344a4b96d86a","label":"guarantee in advance"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v206be824acbc"},"reference_answer":"v206be824acbc","incorrect_answer":"v344a4b96d86a","explanation":"Recall означает вспомнить уже произошедшее."},{"id":"1b0ee99c-8b79-5643-8f3a-e42e4b982e93","lesson_id":"0e307f7