e former owner sells books only upstairs."},{"id":"v487b4f4f8aa6","label":"Some neighbours still use the old name."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v487b4f4f8aa6"},"reference_answer":"v487b4f4f8aa6","incorrect_answer":"v58fafe946a83","explanation":"Старая привычка называния сохраняется после смены бизнеса."},{"id":"beb4bb11-a4c8-5d8f-bbc7-170a4c0050ea","lesson_id":"2b46fadf-d8b0-58ad-aeb7-378103dfa86b","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сообщи о прекращении посещения.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Do you still attend the Tuesday class?"}],"options":[{"id":"vacdc68751c07","label":"No, I do not attend it anymore."},{"id":"v9c2ab027fd85","label":"No, I not attend it still anymore."},{"id":"v210f86b70ba7","label":"No, I do not attends it anymore."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vacdc68751c07"},"reference_answer":"vacdc68751c07","incorrect_answer":"v9c2ab027fd85","explanation":"Do not attend ... anymore сохраняет отрицание и начальную форму."},{"id":"3ffd4ce7-15ba-500d-a856-8dbb1adb4572","lesson_id":"2b46fadf-d8b0-58ad-aeb7-378103dfa86b","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A person who held a role previously is a ___ holder of that role.","options":[{"id":"veee6a2f706e4","label":"current"},{"id":"v3cd1219c5b09","label":"future necessarily"},{"id":"v914fb4041211","label":"former"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v914fb4041211"},"reference_answer":"v914fb4041211","incorrect_answer":"veee6a2f706e4","explanation":"Former обозначает прежнюю, уже не текущую роль."},{"id":"c5133d16-7a43-593b-95f3-202922b90cae","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: If we had a larger room now, we ___ more guests.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v2a524a88fd83","label":"would invite"},{"id":"vacb4a0a70021","label":"will invited"},{"id":"vfd16b770c2e5","label":"would invited"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2a524a88fd83"},"reference_answer":"v2a524a88fd83","incorrect_answer":"vacb4a0a70021","explanation":"Гипотетическому условию о настоящем соответствует would invite."},{"id":"40643f45-e60f-5c45-99f1-f9e1369038fc","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: live / lived.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If I ___ closer, I would walk to work."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["lived"]},"reference_answer":"lived","incorrect_answer":"live","explanation":"В изучаемой нереальной гипотезе используется lived."},{"id":"daae1d11-2494-58a9-84b8-5aed50f5e3c2","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Если бы у меня была машина, я бы приезжал чаще.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"had"},{"id":"t4","label":"a"},{"id":"t5","label":"car,"},{"id":"t6","label":"I"},{"id":"t7","label":"would"},{"id":"t8","label":"visit"},{"id":"t9","label":"more"},{"id":"t10","label":"often."},{"id":"t1","label":"If"},{"id":"t2","label":"I"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t1"],"explanation":"Had и would visit описывают воображаемую нынешнюю ситуацию."},{"id":"10fde14f-7f6b-5c5d-82a8-02cb26b8a5bc","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If I had more time, I would studied another language."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["If I had more time, I would study another language."]},"reference_answer":"If I had more time, I would study another language.","incorrect_answer":"If I had more time, I would studied another language.","explanation":"После would требуется study."},{"id":"23d9b26e-2c32-5e0e-b007-510d0722954e","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что ограничивало первоначальный план Лии?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"Leah wanted to organise a reading group, but her flat was too small for eight people. She said that if she had more space, she would host it herself. Her friend suggested borrowing a room at the community centre instead. Leah liked the idea because it solved the practical problem without requiring her to move. Her conditional described an imagined alternative, not an actual change of home.","options":[{"id":"v6e9ffd3745b6","label":"A rule banning all reading."},{"id":"v27ce5a340e44","label":"An inability to contact any friend."},{"id":"v0995fbd997b5","label":"The size of her flat."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0995fbd997b5"},"reference_answer":"v0995fbd997b5","incorrect_answer":"v6e9ffd3745b6","explanation":"Квартира слишком мала для восьми человек."},{"id":"1436b900-2997-5d9c-8e41-988b36ad4fc3","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l1c1086568e31","label":"imagine"},{"id":"l8fdaee5d4ca2","label":"space"},{"id":"l920e8a3f720b","label":"choice"},{"id":"l2069bc72ed5b","label":"possibility"}],"right":[{"id":"rd120320a8cb8","label":"выбор"},{"id":"ree1bb82636ab","label":"возможность"},{"id":"r7f9fdafe514d","label":"представлять"},{"id":"rc2cf6e751365","label":"место"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l1c1086568e31":"r7f9fdafe514d","l8fdaee5d4ca2":"rc2cf6e751365","l920e8a3f720b":"rd120320a8cb8","l2069bc72ed5b":"ree1bb82636ab"}},"reference_answer":{"l1c1086568e31":"r7f9fdafe514d","l8fdaee5d4ca2":"rc2cf6e751365","l920e8a3f720b":"rd120320a8cb8","l2069bc72ed5b":"ree1bb82636ab"},"incorrect_answer":{"l1c1086568e31":"rc2cf6e751365","l8fdaee5d4ca2":"r7f9fdafe514d","l920e8a3f720b":"rd120320a8cb8","l2069bc72ed5b":"ree1bb82636ab"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: imagine — представлять; space — место; choice — выбор; possibility — возможность."},{"id":"38c695aa-c0ac-5440-8897-d1f8f6781ce5","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую реальную альтернативу предложили?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"Leah wanted to organise a reading group, but her flat was too small for eight people. She said that if she had more space, she would host it herself. Her friend suggested borrowing a room at the community centre instead. Leah liked the idea because it solved the practical problem without requiring her to move. Her conditional described an imagined alternative, not an actual change of home.","options":[{"id":"veef9ed272a02","label":"Buy a new flat immediately."},{"id":"veff36cd5e2ed","label":"Use a room at the community centre."},{"id":"v17daaefcc8a6","label":"Assume Leah had already moved."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"veff36cd5e2ed"},"reference_answer":"veff36cd5e2ed","incorrect_answer":"v17daaefcc8a6","explanation":"Предложение решает проблему места без переезда."},{"id":"6708a0f4-a087-5a8d-958d-7f7025a0d3a9","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Ответь на гипотетический вопрос.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"What would you do with an extra free day?"}],"options":[{"id":"vdac6c3854f72","label":"I would spent it visiting my family."},{"id":"v98e160f0db38","label":"I will spent it yesterday."},{"id":"vd2d66d70d95f","label":"I would spend it visiting my family."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd2d66d70d95f"},"reference_answer":"vd2d66d70d95f","incorrect_answer":"vdac6c3854f72","explanation":"Would spend использует начальную форму."},{"id":"919e0169-1f61-571d-bd00-10b7ed71c007","lesson_id":"7042ef9f-5001-599f-a0e6-4cef80ba0d27","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To form a picture of a situation that is not currently real is to ___ it.","options":[{"id":"v645defc20072","label":"record as completed"},{"id":"v79ad92cd8f28","label":"imagine"},{"id":"v739567330e49","label":"confirm as fact"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v79ad92cd8f28"},"reference_answer":"v79ad92cd8f28","incorrect_answer":"v739567330e49","explanation":"Imagine означает представить, не подтвердить реальность."},{"id":"31f03b16-9646-5292-b42c-c4a7e7ab8edd","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The organiser let us ___ the room early.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v19bce3a1fbc4","label":"to enter"},{"id":"v5607b1740708","label":"entered"},{"id":"v3e490137ac96","label":"enter"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3e490137ac96"},"reference_answer":"v3e490137ac96","incorrect_answer":"v19bce3a1fbc4","explanation":"После let us нужна начальная форма без to."},{"id":"c4c4bb37-4e1c-5688-bb30-8ed5a9739ad0","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: return / to return.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The missing form made me ___ to the office."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["return"]},"reference_answer":"return","incorrect_answer":"to return","explanation":"В активном make me return предлог to не ставится."},{"id":"c70f2f45-1fc7-526c-8891-470f730fdeb5","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Нам разрешили воспользоваться боковым входом.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"us"},{"id":"t4","label":"use"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"side"},{"id":"t7","label":"entrance."},{"id":"t1","label":"They"},{"id":"t2","label":"let"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Let us use — активная модель разрешения без to."},{"id":"48453195-e14a-59c5-8f70-8ac617835fc1","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The coach made us to repeat the exercise."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The coach made us repeat the exercise."]},"reference_answer":"The coach made us repeat the exercise.","incorrect_answer":"The coach made us to repeat the exercise.","explanation":"В активной конструкции make someone do убирается to."},{"id":"67559407-6961-545c-8f37-17068e370f56","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему волонтёры могли войти в восемь?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The venue normally opened at nine, but the organiser let the volunteers enter at eight to prepare. A missing delivery made them change the layout of the room. They used smaller tables near the wall and left a wider path through the middle. The change was inconvenient, but it did not prevent the event from starting on time.","options":[{"id":"v84fdb676d805","label":"The delivery driver forced every door open."},{"id":"vd8d737e2f51b","label":"The organiser gave them permission to prepare early."},{"id":"vda65f288bd22","label":"The public opening time had always been eight."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd8d737e2f51b"},"reference_answer":"vd8d737e2f51b","incorrect_answer":"vda65f288bd22","explanation":"Let выражает специальное разрешение, отличное от обычного открытия в девять."},{"id":"75ecd24b-952d-5f70-acb5-e8bddae7804e","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l77d68e901c8b","label":"let"},{"id":"l90397126a4ac","label":"make"},{"id":"laddd384d7592","label":"permission"},{"id":"l32b1693d158c","label":"requirement"}],"right":[{"id":"rc5cf36c3895e","label":"разрешение"},{"id":"r46da9c10bff9","label":"требование"},{"id":"r9f89cdf1fe55","label":"разрешать"},{"id":"r1363f7345dd4","label":"заставлять в этой конструкции"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l77d68e901c8b":"r9f89cdf1fe55","l90397126a4ac":"r1363f7345dd4","laddd384d7592":"rc5cf36c3895e","l32b1693d158c":"r46da9c10bff9"}},"reference_answer":{"l77d68e901c8b":"r9f89cdf1fe55","l90397126a4ac":"r1363f7345dd4","laddd384d7592":"rc5cf36c3895e","l32b1693d158c":"r46da9c10bff9"},"incorrect_answer":{"l77d68e901c8b":"r1363f7345dd4","l90397126a4ac":"r9f89cdf1fe55","laddd384d7592":"rc5cf36c3895e","l32b1693d158c":"r46da9c10bff9"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: let — разрешать; make — заставлять в этой конструкции; permission — разрешение; requirement — требование."},{"id":"5fcd6280-c573-57c1-ba7e-04b8523b3224","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что вынудило изменить расстановку?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The venue normally opened at nine, but the organiser let the volunteers enter at eight to prepare. A missing delivery made them change the layout of the room. They used smaller tables near the wall and left a wider path through the middle. The change was inconvenient, but it did not prevent the event from starting on time.","options":[{"id":"v4f015aa559ad","label":"A missing delivery."},{"id":"v4d2c181c6ff9","label":"A decision to cancel the event."},{"id":"v55edf9e1adca","label":"A rule requiring a late start."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4f015aa559ad"},"reference_answer":"v4f015aa559ad","incorrect_answer":"v4d2c181c6ff9","explanation":"Недоставленные предметы вызвали практическую адаптацию."},{"id":"e398100e-82b5-5582-9f32-b2b679fdbcd8","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сообщи о разрешении с let.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can we begin before the public arrives?"}],"options":[{"id":"va8e9d3c2dd4b","label":"The manager has let us starting early."},{"id":"v9bd0717ae4e6","label":"The manager has let us start early."},{"id":"vfc1447833f6e","label":"The manager has let us to start early."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9bd0717ae4e6"},"reference_answer":"v9bd0717ae4e6","incorrect_answer":"vfc1447833f6e","explanation":"Let us start использует инфинитив без to."},{"id":"8c8a659a-9eef-5fa4-984c-774cc621dfc8","lesson_id":"0e395cd6-aff9-5494-9382-d80e387dd398","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To allow an action is to ___ it.","options":[{"id":"v2adaf1ab071f","label":"permit"},{"id":"v3c3a0fec7f46","label":"prohibit"},{"id":"v9287b70413da","label":"prevent always"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2adaf1ab071f"},"reference_answer":"v2adaf1ab071f","incorrect_answer":"v3c3a0fec7f46","explanation":"Permit означает разрешать, в отличие от prohibit."},{"id":"f92c91e8-fedd-5eda-b996-d17c6ddf160a","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Which version can omit the relative pronoun?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v529b68de5ef6","label":"The bus that stops here is late."},{"id":"v62cb9f861c4e","label":"The book that I borrowed is here."},{"id":"vc90fe49af422","label":"The person who called is here."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v62cb9f861c4e"},"reference_answer":"v62cb9f861c4e","incorrect_answer":"vc90fe49af422","explanation":"В первом варианте that — объект при подлежащем I; в остальных местоимение — подлежащее."},{"id":"5cd3a77c-ddf4-5031-b075-c51d199f3233","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: who / that.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The film ___ we watched was short."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["that"]},"reference_answer":"that","incorrect_answer":"who","explanation":"Фильм — предмет; that здесь можно также опустить, но who не подходит."},{"id":"803b64cb-eab1-5324-9080-4831db4fc32b","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Книга, которую я взял, лежит на столе.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"I"},{"id":"t4","label":"borrowed"},{"id":"t5","label":"is"},{"id":"t6","label":"on"},{"id":"t7","label":"the"},{"id":"t8","label":"desk."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"book"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Пропущенное that является объектом borrowed, при этом I остаётся подлежащим."},{"id":"b194006a-5680-5c31-bcf1-72262315d35b","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The person called me yesterday is waiting outside."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The person who called me yesterday is waiting outside."]},"reference_answer":"The person who called me yesterday is waiting outside.","incorrect_answer":"The person called me yesterday is waiting outside.","explanation":"Нужно восстановить подлежащее who в определяющей части."},{"id":"b60c02c3-214b-5820-9f71-2627a19c0015","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"reading","prompt":"Кто рекомендовал руководство?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"At the club, Nina showed us a guide she had borrowed from the library. The person who recommended it was waiting nearby. We compared the route the guide described with a newer map. One footpath was missing from the map, so we decided to ask the visitor centre before using it. Omitting a relative object made some phrases shorter, but it did not remove the need to check the route itself.","options":[{"id":"v26b8a0add82c","label":"A person waiting nearby."},{"id":"v5aea08607d8b","label":"The guide itself."},{"id":"v7c3cc138dd86","label":"Every visitor at the centre."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v26b8a0add82c"},"reference_answer":"v26b8a0add82c","incorrect_answer":"v5aea08607d8b","explanation":"Who recommended it относится к человеку поблизости."},{"id":"63cd0a2e-8bf6-51e5-8545-897c44ec0bc5","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lb7fd579f295f","label":"borrow"},{"id":"l50e8bfea60e1","label":"lend"},{"id":"ldde4f627b9b0","label":"subject"},{"id":"l9108c79c2a77","label":"object"}],"right":[{"id":"rd87d4eea9463","label":"подлежащее"},{"id":"ra2159ce4997c","label":"дополнение"},{"id":"r244ded9497f3","label":"брать взаймы"},{"id":"ra273e04913b5","label":"давать взаймы"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lb7fd579f295f":"r244ded9497f3","l50e8bfea60e1":"ra273e04913b5","ldde4f627b9b0":"rd87d4eea9463","l9108c79c2a77":"ra2159ce4997c"}},"reference_answer":{"lb7fd579f295f":"r244ded9497f3","l50e8bfea60e1":"ra273e04913b5","ldde4f627b9b0":"rd87d4eea9463","l9108c79c2a77":"ra2159ce4997c"},"incorrect_answer":{"lb7fd579f295f":"ra273e04913b5","l50e8bfea60e1":"r244ded9497f3","ldde4f627b9b0":"rd87d4eea9463","l9108c79c2a77":"ra2159ce4997c"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: borrow — брать взаймы; lend — давать взаймы; subject — подлежащее; object — дополнение."},{"id":"6fb0369f-33ef-5419-8371-986ebf711bb7","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему решили уточнить маршрут?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"At the club, Nina showed us a guide she had borrowed from the library. The person who recommended it was waiting nearby. We compared the route the guide described with a newer map. One footpath was missing from the map, so we decided to ask the visitor centre before using it. Omitting a relative object made some phrases shorter, but it did not remove the need to check the route itself.","options":[{"id":"v2b02f3984413","label":"Every map had been lost."},{"id":"vf8cfec2c6874","label":"The guide had no routes in it."},{"id":"vac615622ab39","label":"One footpath was absent from the newer map."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vac615622ab39"},"reference_answer":"vac615622ab39","incorrect_answer":"v2b02f3984413","explanation":"Расхождение источников потребовало проверки."},{"id":"2313c597-896c-5629-9d94-f1342c8765bb","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери объяснение допустимого пропуска.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can I say “the letter I received” instead of “the letter that I received”?"}],"options":[{"id":"v1913171ad8c9","label":"Yes; the omitted pronoun is the object of received."},{"id":"va0a98090d1f8","label":"No; I cannot be a subject."},{"id":"v3b7d3e25a870","label":"Yes; every relative subject can always be omitted."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1913171ad8c9"},"reference_answer":"v1913171ad8c9","incorrect_answer":"va0a98090d1f8","explanation":"I — подлежащее, поэтому объектное that можно опустить."},{"id":"5a977017-5705-5b8f-898d-142c9712238f","lesson_id":"9b28ed25-2040-5abf-ace4-bde1f29f2125","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"In “I borrowed the book”, “the book” is the ___.","options":[{"id":"v793face9e6d0","label":"subject"},{"id":"vade95d301941","label":"speaker"},{"id":"vfeb090d60a7e","label":"object"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vfeb090d60a7e"},"reference_answer":"vfeb090d60a7e","incorrect_answer":"v793face9e6d0","explanation":"Book является объектом действия borrowed."},{"id":"779a3b40-6ba0-5e83-9a60-a4a588327568","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: As winter approached, the evenings became ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v772f92ee37c2","label":"colder and colder"},{"id":"v08292891b513","label":"more colder and colder"},{"id":"vd2e76d0332c1","label":"coldest and colder"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v772f92ee37c2"},"reference_answer":"v772f92ee37c2","incorrect_answer":"v08292891b513","explanation":"С коротким прилагательным повторяется сравнительная степень colder."},{"id":"5e4e9e43-7e05-518a-9acc-38998c33a38e","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: more / most.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"More and ___ visitors are using the online form."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["more"]},"reference_answer":"more","incorrect_answer":"most","explanation":"More and more обозначает рост числа посетителей."},{"id":"a6e6e7c6-3380-5f46-901c-7a533876ea6c","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Инструкции становились всё более подробными.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"became"},{"id":"t4","label":"more"},{"id":"t5","label":"and"},{"id":"t6","label":"more"},{"id":"t7","label":"detailed."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"instructions"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"More and more detailed описывает изменение степени признака."},{"id":"eceab85e-4c44-5e54-8ce5-73350240f469","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The queue became more longer and longer."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The queue became longer and longer."]},"reference_answer":"The queue became longer and longer.","incorrect_answer":"The queue became more longer and longer.","explanation":"Longer уже сравнительная степень, лишнее more убирается."},{"id":"141120a5-061e-5afb-a127-d8846549c68b","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какая тенденция описана?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"At first, only a few neighbours used the shared tool cupboard. Over several months, more and more people began borrowing equipment. The organiser added clearer labels and a booking sheet. As use increased, keeping track of returns became more and more important. The group did not assume that growth alone proved the system worked well; it also checked whether borrowed tools came back on time.","options":[{"id":"vd8f86ceeccf1","label":"Fewer and fewer tools were ever available, according to the text."},{"id":"vc8b77cb688ab","label":"Every neighbour stopped borrowing equipment."},{"id":"vb61746d4b5c6","label":"More people began using the cupboard."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb61746d4b5c6"},"reference_answer":"vb61746d4b5c6","incorrect_answer":"vd8f86ceeccf1","explanation":"More and more people прямо описывает рост использования."},{"id":"288ea69e-27cb-509c-8e17-3c03eeb4cfaf","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lcc61bc5c9e54","label":"gradually"},{"id":"l5be8840a2af3","label":"increase"},{"id":"lc0553d768111","label":"decrease"},{"id":"lda961ae357cb","label":"trend"}],"right":[{"id":"r9e399f0379f3","label":"уменьшаться"},{"id":"r40057655fe0b","label":"тенденция"},{"id":"r61bc374e95f8","label":"постепенно"},{"id":"r06a45ae8a986","label":"увеличиваться"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lcc61bc5c9e54":"r61bc374e95f8","l5be8840a2af3":"r06a45ae8a986","lc0553d768111":"r9e399f0379f3","lda961ae357cb":"r40057655fe0b"}},"reference_answer":{"lcc61bc5c9e54":"r61bc374e95f8","l5be8840a2af3":"r06a45ae8a986","lc0553d768111":"r9e399f0379f3","lda961ae357cb":"r40057655fe0b"},"incorrect_answer":{"lcc61bc5c9e54":"r06a45ae8a986","l5be8840a2af3":"r61bc374e95f8","lc0553d768111":"r9e399f0379f3","lda961ae357cb":"r40057655fe0b"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: gradually — постепенно; increase — увеличиваться; decrease — уменьшаться; trend — тенденция."},{"id":"48177e6d-d8cd-5293-a2f6-3572651d78ad","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что ещё проверяла группа помимо роста?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"At first, only a few neighbours used the shared tool cupboard. Over several months, more and more people began borrowing equipment. The organiser added clearer labels and a booking sheet. As use increased, keeping track of returns became more and more important. The group did not assume that growth alone proved the system worked well; it also checked whether borrowed tools came back on time.","options":[{"id":"vba3801020d5d","label":"Whether all labels had disappeared."},{"id":"vf75781a46231","label":"Whether tools were returned on time."},{"id":"ve480a5f040b7","label":"Only whether the cupboard was fashionable."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf75781a46231"},"reference_answer":"vf75781a46231","incorrect_answer":"ve480a5f040b7","explanation":"Рост числа пользователей не заменил проверку возвратов."},{"id":"d71f2762-5aa0-50ac-af30-bc599ec1df25","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Опиши постепенно растущую сложность.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How is the task changing?"}],"options":[{"id":"v75bb159425b6","label":"It is becoming more difficulter."},{"id":"v854af9ae6ef9","label":"It is becoming most and more difficult."},{"id":"v12908bb094d0","label":"It is becoming more and more difficult."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v12908bb094d0"},"reference_answer":"v12908bb094d0","incorrect_answer":"v75bb159425b6","explanation":"More and more difficult — правильная модель."},{"id":"5a264753-6ade-5c48-a399-3f7435d17f60","lesson_id":"6b4b3393-4f96-552e-8fe3-08f27b00bf2a","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A general direction of change over time is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v52de2f12a892","label":"receipt"},{"id":"v7bb30285a699","label":"trend"},{"id":"v75332243a6b7","label":"single exception only"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7bb30285a699"},"reference_answer":"v7bb30285a699","incorrect_answer":"v75332243a6b7","explanation":"Trend — тенденция, а не единичный случай."},{"id":"23729a79-50ec-531b-993d-e4531770a47d","lesson_id":"eac6d852-e19e-5dec-8e7e-f904cd93b4ba","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: I can swim. — ___ can I.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vea5b52154c9d","label":"Neither"},{"id":"vc7f18cafd494","label":"Either not"},{"id":"v07ce1ca1cfe0","label":"So"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v07ce1ca1cfe0"},"reference_answer":"v07ce1ca1cfe0","incorrect_answer":"vea5b52154c9d","explanation":"К положительному can swim присоединяется So can I."},{"id":"d00f8976-39d5-57f2-ab33-fc695d8e75ec","lesson_id":"eac6d852-e19e-5dec-8e7e-f904cd93b4ba","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: am / do.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I do not work on Sundays. — Neither ___ I."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["do"]},"reference_answer":"do","incorrect_answer":"am","explanation":"Нужен тот же вспомогательный do."},{"id":"8c7b9042-706f-5e6a-a96c-56aa04bfe724","lesson_id":"eac6d852-e19e-5dec-8e7e-f904cd93b4ba","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Я готов. Я тоже.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"ready."},{"id":"t4","label":"So"},{"id":"t5","label":"am"},{"id":"t6","label":"I."},{"id":"t1","label":"I"},{"id":"t2","label":"am"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t1"],"explanation":"So am I сохраняет be и правильный порядок ответа."},{"id":"538ddff1-b4e7-5574-9ca8-338fdd9de30f","lesson_id":"eac6d852-e19e-5dec-8e7e-f904cd93b4ba","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I am tired. So I am, says another tired person."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["I am tired. So am I, says another tired person."]},"reference_answer":"I am tired. So am I, says another tired person.","incorrect_answer":"I am tired. So I am, says another tired person.","explanation":"Для значения «я тоже» у другого человека требуется So am I."},{"id":"bd974409-885c-5f71-9dab-8f2ea53d4992","lesson_id":"eac6d852-e19e-5dec-8e7e-f904cd93b4ba","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что выражает первый ответ Бена?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"At the start of a training day, Noor said she was nervous. “So am I,” replied Ben. Later, Noor explained that she did not know the building well. “Neither do I,” Ben said, suggesting they find the room together. Their replies showed shared experiences rather than agreement about a factual claim that only one of them could verify.","options":[{"id":"vb7ddf1d168b3","label":"He says Noor must be wrong."},{"id":"v2aaa06f6fea1","label":"He is nervous too."},{"id":"vde9b341e08eb","label":"He is not nervous."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2aaa06f6fea1"},"reference_answer":"v2aaa06f6fea1","incorrect_answer":"vde9b341e08eb","explanation":"So am I добавляет такое же состояние у Бена."},{"id":"89a0e72a-f47c-56d8-a36e-270e083ad009","lesson_id":"eac6d852-e19e-5dec-8e7e-f904cd93b4ba","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l3aa03b28f542","label":"agree"},{"id":"l901bc09a0287","label":"positive"},{"id":"l1b1c46795233","label":"negative"},{"id":"l4ba323340106","label":"auxiliary"}],"right":[{"id":"r4e4283a1b1e2","label":"отрицательный"},{"id":"rbd60da7ecac7","label":"вспомогательный глагол"},{"id":"r19c4b63835c3","label":"соглашаться"},{"id":"rcd02e07108f7","label":"утвердительный"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l3aa03b28f542":"r19c4b63835c3","l901bc09a0287":"rcd02e07108f7","l1b1c46795233":"r4e4283a1b1e2","l4ba323340106":"rbd60da7ecac7"}},"reference_answer":{"l3aa03b28f542":"r19c4b63835c3","l901bc09a0287":"rcd02e07108f7","l1b1c46795233":"r4e4283a1b1e2","l4ba323340106":"rbd60da7ecac7"},"incorrect_answer":{"l3aa03b28f542":"rcd02e07108f7","l901bc09a0287":"