ul."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["detailed"]},"reference_answer":"detailed","incorrect_answer":"detail","explanation":"После how здесь требуется прилагательное detailed."},{"id":"89ad19ab-9f60-5d4b-a36d-13025a353b3f","lesson_id":"2568ea32-dd0c-5d12-b80f-00c3e444b097","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Как бы тщательно мы ни планировали, задержки всё равно возможны.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"how"},{"id":"t4","label":"carefully"},{"id":"t5","label":"we"},{"id":"t6","label":"plan,"},{"id":"t7","label":"delays"},{"id":"t8","label":"remain"},{"id":"t9","label":"possible."},{"id":"t1","label":"No"},{"id":"t2","label":"matter"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Уступка не объявляет планирование бесполезным; она сохраняет возможность задержки."},{"id":"3ce01c13-26ba-57fe-8d3e-2acc98acc1e3","lesson_id":"2568ea32-dd0c-5d12-b80f-00c3e444b097","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"No matter how careful are we, mistakes remain possible."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["No matter how careful we are, mistakes remain possible."]},"reference_answer":"No matter how careful we are, mistakes remain possible.","incorrect_answer":"No matter how careful are we, mistakes remain possible.","explanation":"В уступительной части используется прямой порядок we are."},{"id":"a13ded5f-f56e-5b7d-b09f-506d990768c7","lesson_id":"2568ea32-dd0c-5d12-b80f-00c3e444b097","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что неверно в прочтении первого читателя?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The organiser wrote that, no matter how detailed the schedule was, volunteers should keep a contact number for unexpected problems. One reader interpreted this as a claim that planning did not matter. The organiser clarified that the schedule still reduced confusion; the point was that preparation could not remove every contingency. The contact number complemented the plan rather than replacing it. The group therefore checked both the timetable and the backup arrangements before the event, recognising a limit without abandoning useful precautions.","options":[{"id":"v5c260dd4c98d","label":"It treats a limit on planning as a claim that planning is useless."},{"id":"v332f8eb01b3b","label":"It preserves the complementary role of the contact number."},{"id":"vc62884f83218","label":"It establishes that every possible problem has been removed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5c260dd4c98d"},"reference_answer":"v5c260dd4c98d","incorrect_answer":"v332f8eb01b3b","explanation":"Из ограничения эффективности не следует полная бесполезность."},{"id":"5cf5333f-6956-5509-a2a2-306bdfec5c00","lesson_id":"2568ea32-dd0c-5d12-b80f-00c3e444b097","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lc0187a087cbc","label":"regardless"},{"id":"lbb246d0dda7e","label":"thorough"},{"id":"ld93fcd7c16ec","label":"limitation"},{"id":"l7c5dd3ade109","label":"precaution"}],"right":[{"id":"rc0dfacd3f947","label":"ограничение"},{"id":"r82fc161ffa57","label":"мера предосторожности"},{"id":"rcd2dff8ada05","label":"независимо от"},{"id":"r97bae604c38e","label":"тщательный"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lc0187a087cbc":"rcd2dff8ada05","lbb246d0dda7e":"r97bae604c38e","ld93fcd7c16ec":"rc0dfacd3f947","l7c5dd3ade109":"r82fc161ffa57"}},"reference_answer":{"lc0187a087cbc":"rcd2dff8ada05","lbb246d0dda7e":"r97bae604c38e","ld93fcd7c16ec":"rc0dfacd3f947","l7c5dd3ade109":"r82fc161ffa57"},"incorrect_answer":{"lc0187a087cbc":"r97bae604c38e","lbb246d0dda7e":"rcd2dff8ada05","ld93fcd7c16ec":"rc0dfacd3f947","l7c5dd3ade109":"r82fc161ffa57"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: regardless — независимо от; thorough — тщательный; limitation — ограничение; precaution — мера предосторожности."},{"id":"22b70796-2b36-55b0-878e-a510c3c45a04","lesson_id":"2568ea32-dd0c-5d12-b80f-00c3e444b097","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как соотносятся контактный номер и план?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The organiser wrote that, no matter how detailed the schedule was, volunteers should keep a contact number for unexpected problems. One reader interpreted this as a claim that planning did not matter. The organiser clarified that the schedule still reduced confusion; the point was that preparation could not remove every contingency. The contact number complemented the plan rather than replacing it. The group therefore checked both the timetable and the backup arrangements before the event, recognising a limit without abandoning useful precautions.","options":[{"id":"veff3e2058a08","label":"The number proves the schedule is unnecessary."},{"id":"v8782000f849c","label":"The schedule prohibits any backup contact."},{"id":"v9def912fb628","label":"The contact number complements the plan."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9def912fb628"},"reference_answer":"v9def912fb628","incorrect_answer":"veff3e2058a08","explanation":"Резервная связь добавляет меру к планированию, а не отменяет его."},{"id":"d7fea13b-d0ed-5346-8a11-847bbaeaf1ca","lesson_id":"2568ea32-dd0c-5d12-b80f-00c3e444b097","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери грамматически правильную уступку.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can we acknowledge uncertainty without abandoning preparation?"}],"options":[{"id":"vf8b11d867f81","label":"Yes: no matter how thorough the plan is, keep a backup."},{"id":"v7d8418caecae","label":"Yes: no matter how is thorough the plan, keep a backup."},{"id":"v172d9e745947","label":"Yes: no matter thorough the plan to be backup."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf8b11d867f81"},"reference_answer":"vf8b11d867f81","incorrect_answer":"v7d8418caecae","explanation":"После how thorough нужен прямой порядок the plan is."},{"id":"4a1d595c-c71a-5e53-bbf4-c66a98177445","lesson_id":"2568ea32-dd0c-5d12-b80f-00c3e444b097","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An action taken in advance to reduce risk is a ___.","options":[{"id":"vfaa294d6e497","label":"conclusion automatically"},{"id":"va25a74c78e6f","label":"reimbursement"},{"id":"va87bdacb9ec9","label":"precaution"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va87bdacb9ec9"},"reference_answer":"va87bdacb9ec9","incorrect_answer":"vfaa294d6e497","explanation":"Precaution — предупредительная мера."},{"id":"9037ec4e-ffdb-5690-a376-8529faf3c1de","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The clearer labels are likely ___ confusion.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v3539a87294e8","label":"to reduce"},{"id":"v0b4d59228e2f","label":"reducing to"},{"id":"v881b63c34d1d","label":"reduce to"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3539a87294e8"},"reference_answer":"v3539a87294e8","incorrect_answer":"v0b4d59228e2f","explanation":"Likely to reduce — правильная модель вероятности."},{"id":"863001de-d431-5544-95b6-865eecdda726","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: to / for.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The change is bound ___ attract questions."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["to"]},"reference_answer":"to","incorrect_answer":"for","explanation":"Be bound to требует инфинитив с to."},{"id":"52d54286-85a6-5444-aec8-dcfeea9fee1b","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Пересмотренные инструкции, вероятно, помогут начинающим.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"instructions"},{"id":"t4","label":"are"},{"id":"t5","label":"likely"},{"id":"t6","label":"to"},{"id":"t7","label":"help"},{"id":"t8","label":"beginners."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"revised"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Likely не означает проверенное улучшение для каждого человека."},{"id":"c0004918-8198-508d-b9a6-2195c77e3f51","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The proposal is likely improve access."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The proposal is likely to improve access."]},"reference_answer":"The proposal is likely to improve access.","incorrect_answer":"The proposal is likely improve access.","explanation":"Между likely и improve требуется to."},{"id":"8d35763b-2702-5efd-af06-05e24606f4d6","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как рекламный черновик усилил исходный вывод?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A designer said that larger labels were likely to help visitors find the correct entrance. In a publicity draft, this became a promise that nobody would be confused again. The designer objected to the change. Her expectation was reasonable enough to test, but it had not established the experience of every future visitor. The team retained the new labels and observed a trial group before making a stronger claim. They treated an expected benefit as a reason for evaluation, not as a substitute for it.","options":[{"id":"v392074660e12","label":"It simply repeated the same degree of probability."},{"id":"vaeaf41227f7f","label":"It said that larger labels were already proved useless."},{"id":"va06e0304bf3b","label":"It changed a likely benefit into a guarantee for every visitor."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va06e0304bf3b"},"reference_answer":"va06e0304bf3b","incorrect_answer":"v392074660e12","explanation":"Likely to help слабее универсальной гарантии nobody would be confused."},{"id":"6aa44e89-7da2-5241-8b02-be666d37a3fa","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lc064acc9fbad","label":"likely"},{"id":"l9194d839c8e0","label":"expectation"},{"id":"l3060c6f9306c","label":"certainty"},{"id":"ledd2c6cc0df8","label":"assurance"}],"right":[{"id":"r0d110e954160","label":"уверенность"},{"id":"r48e5eeae37a1","label":"заверение"},{"id":"rb8d5fabdbc41","label":"вероятный"},{"id":"r9e5e890f6f7a","label":"ожидание"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lc064acc9fbad":"rb8d5fabdbc41","l9194d839c8e0":"r9e5e890f6f7a","l3060c6f9306c":"r0d110e954160","ledd2c6cc0df8":"r48e5eeae37a1"}},"reference_answer":{"lc064acc9fbad":"rb8d5fabdbc41","l9194d839c8e0":"r9e5e890f6f7a","l3060c6f9306c":"r0d110e954160","ledd2c6cc0df8":"r48e5eeae37a1"},"incorrect_answer":{"lc064acc9fbad":"r9e5e890f6f7a","l9194d839c8e0":"rb8d5fabdbc41","l3060c6f9306c":"r0d110e954160","ledd2c6cc0df8":"r48e5eeae37a1"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: likely — вероятный; expectation — ожидание; certainty — уверенность; assurance — заверение."},{"id":"a7d708b1-23af-5bbe-a19c-f53d106e46cc","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что команда сделала перед более сильным заявлением?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A designer said that larger labels were likely to help visitors find the correct entrance. In a publicity draft, this became a promise that nobody would be confused again. The designer objected to the change. Her expectation was reasonable enough to test, but it had not established the experience of every future visitor. The team retained the new labels and observed a trial group before making a stronger claim. They treated an expected benefit as a reason for evaluation, not as a substitute for it.","options":[{"id":"vb74eeb0b0280","label":"Removed every entrance sign."},{"id":"v2e12b78a1f85","label":"Observed a trial group."},{"id":"v58155016ef17","label":"Assumed all possible results were already known."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2e12b78a1f85"},"reference_answer":"v2e12b78a1f85","incorrect_answer":"v58155016ef17","explanation":"Было проведено наблюдение за пробной группой."},{"id":"0348c00d-9a9e-55f9-b7c7-328ce96f01cb","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани степень уверенности и время результата.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can I describe “likely to improve” as “has improved for everyone”?"}],"options":[{"id":"v70668e9b25a3","label":"Yes; likely always means tested on everyone."},{"id":"v02f9b0fdf9ed","label":"Yes; future expectation is identical to past measurement."},{"id":"v14e1ee75f016","label":"No; that changes probability into a completed universal result."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v14e1ee75f016"},"reference_answer":"v14e1ee75f016","incorrect_answer":"v70668e9b25a3","explanation":"Вероятность не равна завершённому измерению для всех."},{"id":"999e641a-6c12-55f9-9292-d1d6683d3700","lesson_id":"31bd7fdb-74e7-516a-b2bc-0a2a6dbac456","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Something expected to happen with substantial probability is ___.","options":[{"id":"vdd7b72741c88","label":"completed necessarily"},{"id":"v97de47662a5c","label":"likely"},{"id":"v280de4fe13f5","label":"impossible by definition"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v97de47662a5c"},"reference_answer":"v97de47662a5c","incorrect_answer":"v280de4fe13f5","explanation":"Likely обозначает вероятность, не обязательное завершение."},{"id":"49f004ae-350d-5ae7-b24a-26da047c2e04","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: By May, the team ___ on the archive for six months.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vfcfd3bb00909","label":"will been working"},{"id":"v1bd47e01216b","label":"will have working"},{"id":"v94020d653121","label":"will have been working"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v94020d653121"},"reference_answer":"v94020d653121","incorrect_answer":"vfcfd3bb00909","explanation":"Будущая длительность к границе выражается will have been working."},{"id":"6b3aca6d-4ea4-50af-a4de-1fdadd65112c","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: trained / training.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"By Friday, she will have been ___ for two weeks."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["training"]},"reference_answer":"training","incorrect_answer":"trained","explanation":"Для активного продолжающегося процесса нужна training."},{"id":"cea42f49-374b-5eb2-9699-15edf62346a0","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «К июню мы будем работать уже год.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"we"},{"id":"t4","label":"will"},{"id":"t5","label":"have"},{"id":"t6","label":"been"},{"id":"t7","label":"working"},{"id":"t8","label":"for"},{"id":"t9","label":"a"},{"id":"t10","label":"year."},{"id":"t1","label":"By"},{"id":"t2","label":"June,"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t1"],"explanation":"Форма обозначает накопленную длительность, не завершённость всего проекта."},{"id":"7862639f-4617-5366-91bb-4787b94a1ec9","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"By Monday, they will have working for a month."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["By Monday, they will have been working for a month."]},"reference_answer":"By Monday, they will have been working for a month.","incorrect_answer":"By Monday, they will have working for a month.","explanation":"После will have в этой длительной форме требуется been перед working."},{"id":"a6cc2913-f0c7-5794-877a-60e4a4a94223","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что измеряет сообщение о шести месяцах?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The archive team began its project in December. A progress note said that by June it would have been working for six months. A reader assumed this meant the whole archive would be ready in June. The coordinator explained that the sentence measured the duration of the work, not its completion. Some collections were already catalogued, while others required additional checking. The team would publish a separate completion estimate after assessing those remaining collections, rather than treating six months of activity as proof that every item would be finished.","options":[{"id":"v2a0a87043d9f","label":"The exact number of remaining documents."},{"id":"v68f0d57ec165","label":"The duration of the work by June."},{"id":"v682171300e61","label":"A confirmed completion date for every item."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v68f0d57ec165"},"reference_answer":"v68f0d57ec165","incorrect_answer":"v682171300e61","explanation":"Длительность и завершённость всего архива — разные сведения."},{"id":"3a5bdf83-aad4-55a0-b50c-61cab598b86c","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l684497511021","label":"duration"},{"id":"l6ccd48df33e9","label":"milestone"},{"id":"lfd8b308dd05a","label":"ongoing"},{"id":"l6258cb13aee5","label":"completion"}],"right":[{"id":"r1e77ce752dec","label":"продолжающийся"},{"id":"r1d2c9530afe5","label":"завершение"},{"id":"r1e8b1b986a49","label":"длительность"},{"id":"reeac395596f0","label":"контрольная точка"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l684497511021":"r1e8b1b986a49","l6ccd48df33e9":"reeac395596f0","lfd8b308dd05a":"r1e77ce752dec","l6258cb13aee5":"r1d2c9530afe5"}},"reference_answer":{"l684497511021":"r1e8b1b986a49","l6ccd48df33e9":"reeac395596f0","lfd8b308dd05a":"r1e77ce752dec","l6258cb13aee5":"r1d2c9530afe5"},"incorrect_answer":{"l684497511021":"reeac395596f0","l6ccd48df33e9":"r1e8b1b986a49","lfd8b308dd05a":"r1e77ce752dec","l6258cb13aee5":"r1d2c9530afe5"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: duration — длительность; milestone — контрольная точка; ongoing — продолжающийся; completion — завершение."},{"id":"f3f12c07-baaf-5c7a-91a7-ca9b9f11164c","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"reading","prompt":"Когда собирались дать оценку завершения?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The archive team began its project in December. A progress note said that by June it would have been working for six months. A reader assumed this meant the whole archive would be ready in June. The coordinator explained that the sentence measured the duration of the work, not its completion. Some collections were already catalogued, while others required additional checking. The team would publish a separate completion estimate after assessing those remaining collections, rather than treating six months of activity as proof that every item would be finished.","options":[{"id":"v0c39007154a7","label":"After assessing the remaining collections."},{"id":"v485162626886","label":"Automatically when six months had passed."},{"id":"v5744f4d4b918","label":"Before the project began, with no review."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0c39007154a7"},"reference_answer":"v0c39007154a7","incorrect_answer":"v485162626886","explanation":"Для оценки требовалось понять оставшийся объём проверки."},{"id":"ff51d31e-dcb0-58b0-8b3d-5e8ce2362ba6","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Отдели длительность процесса от окончания результата.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Will “we will have been building for a year” guarantee a finished building?"}],"options":[{"id":"v74cc279fd328","label":"Yes; for a year always means every task is finished."},{"id":"vb8222f692f83","label":"No; it states duration unless completion is separately established."},{"id":"v722284f5a67b","label":"Yes; every perfect continuous form guarantees completion."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb8222f692f83"},"reference_answer":"vb8222f692f83","incorrect_answer":"v722284f5a67b","explanation":"Perfect Continuous в этой модели не обещает завершение всей постройки."},{"id":"2bde9105-2bb8-5eae-a4f6-962e5cac0de7","lesson_id":"71d5aaa6-525e-5e17-ab2e-6f19f2b63890","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A task that continues over time is ___.","options":[{"id":"va5dff3578143","label":"ongoing"},{"id":"vb9559751ffec","label":"completed necessarily"},{"id":"v8f76678f263f","label":"cancelled automatically"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va5dff3578143"},"reference_answer":"va5dff3578143","incorrect_answer":"vb9559751ffec","explanation":"Ongoing — продолжающийся."},{"id":"b472020a-cb08-5328-a18b-ec217a0a6f64","lesson_id":"fe78a91a-38fb-53a4-b361-e1b60dbbd710","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The damaged lock needs ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v9ca25df27fa6","label":"be repair to"},{"id":"vaa09541e2a84","label":"to be repaired"},{"id":"v82a97a5c97b4","label":"to repairing"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vaa09541e2a84"},"reference_answer":"vaa09541e2a84","incorrect_answer":"v82a97a5c97b4","explanation":"Нужное действие направлено на замок: to be repaired."},{"id":"7ccbd518-406a-5914-b6d8-167b95607347","lesson_id":"fe78a91a-38fb-53a4-b361-e1b60dbbd710","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: checked / checking.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The figures need to be ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["checked"]},"reference_answer":"checked","incorrect_answer":"checking","explanation":"После be в пассивном инфинитиве требуется checked."},{"id":"1d186b7a-25c8-533c-9b4e-43abd63047a2","lesson