The two grammatical forms focused on the materials requiring action, not on who would carry it out. The team assigned each task to a named person and recorded completion separately once the checks and replacement had actually occurred.","options":[{"id":"v0fe6db066db8","label":"Assumed the passive meaning named everyone automatically."},{"id":"vd395bb9a88d2","label":"Removed the requirement to replace the attachment."},{"id":"v47b85fde0ccc","label":"Assigned tasks to named people."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v47b85fde0ccc"},"reference_answer":"v47b85fde0ccc","incorrect_answer":"v0fe6db066db8","explanation":"Грамматика фокусировала материалы; исполнителей назначили отдельно."},{"id":"610507fd-e17a-5f2f-a4b3-ccf73eec875c","lesson_id":"fe78a91a-38fb-53a4-b361-e1b60dbbd710","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сопоставь две допустимые модели.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Which two forms can express the need for a room to be cleaned?"}],"options":[{"id":"v4586f24c3c34","label":"It needs cleaning; it needs to be cleaned."},{"id":"vddf791959867","label":"It needs clean; it needs to cleaned."},{"id":"v84e99febff4b","label":"It need cleaning; it needs to be clean yesterday."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4586f24c3c34"},"reference_answer":"v4586f24c3c34","incorrect_answer":"vddf791959867","explanation":"Need + -ing и need to be + причастие могут выражать пассивную необходимость."},{"id":"ef14f53a-7c02-5dcc-ac90-b3035dff9921","lesson_id":"fe78a91a-38fb-53a4-b361-e1b60dbbd710","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A task not yet completed is ___.","options":[{"id":"vf2422c957780","label":"completed by definition"},{"id":"vca9ca560bc74","label":"irrelevant necessarily"},{"id":"ve7d6ba73da4d","label":"outstanding"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve7d6ba73da4d"},"reference_answer":"ve7d6ba73da4d","incorrect_answer":"vf2422c957780","explanation":"Outstanding в данном рабочем контексте означает остающийся невыполненным."},{"id":"fb83870f-6059-5e5b-abb7-5f3b02f21af9","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: With all the documents ___, the coordinator authorised submission.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v6df0f00acf5f","label":"checked"},{"id":"v2ec65c66760b","label":"checking themselves"},{"id":"v183f6dc83f1b","label":"to checking"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v6df0f00acf5f"},"reference_answer":"v6df0f00acf5f","incorrect_answer":"v2ec65c66760b","explanation":"Документы были проверены: checked выражает действие над ними."},{"id":"71b31ea2-a593-595d-b59c-ea5eb8088860","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: waited / waiting.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"With the visitors ___ outside, the staff opened the side door."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["waiting"]},"reference_answer":"waiting","incorrect_answer":"waited","explanation":"Посетители сами выполняют ожидание, поэтому waiting."},{"id":"c505b5d9-4236-5561-b8b0-71b0c987aba5","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «После проверки документов координатор подписал форму.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"documents"},{"id":"t4","label":"checked,"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"coordinator"},{"id":"t7","label":"signed"},{"id":"t8","label":"the"},{"id":"t9","label":"form."},{"id":"t1","label":"With"},{"id":"t2","label":"the"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Вводный оборот имеет свой участник documents, отличный от coordinator."},{"id":"3e46dd41-aee4-503c-9140-a2bd5e730c14","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"With the guests wait outside, the guide unlocked the hall."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["With the guests waiting outside, the guide unlocked the hall."]},"reference_answer":"With the guests waiting outside, the guide unlocked the hall.","incorrect_answer":"With the guests wait outside, the guide unlocked the hall.","explanation":"После with the guests для активного фонового процесса нужна форма waiting."},{"id":"c154bd29-cc1f-5533-a26c-7bb2b038cac7","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как проверка соотносится с подачей в первой цитате?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The coordinator’s note began, “With the documents checked, the application was submitted.” A later summary suggested that submission itself had verified the documents. The note described a different relationship: checking was presented as background already completed when submission occurred. Another sentence, “With several responses still pending, the committee postponed its decision,” described an unresolved situation instead. Neither construction named every person responsible for the background action. The reviewer therefore asked for the verification record as well as the submission date. A compact grammatical construction could organise the sequence clearly, but it could not by itself provide the independent evidence that the stated checking had actually taken place.","options":[{"id":"v090e03adeaa6","label":"It is caused automatically by the act of submission."},{"id":"vf4e5a93c819e","label":"It is stated to be impossible after any response."},{"id":"v116599f8b3df","label":"It is presented as completed background before submission."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v116599f8b3df"},"reference_answer":"v116599f8b3df","incorrect_answer":"v090e03adeaa6","explanation":"Оборот представляет проверку как предшествующее состояние, не как автоматический эффект подачи."},{"id":"1c1d8a56-665f-5e9e-b538-a1a3e0a42f1e","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"le18b1f026c9d","label":"background"},{"id":"lad7ec3a43463","label":"pending"},{"id":"l4d3809360ae3","label":"verify"},{"id":"ld66e522dda7f","label":"precondition"}],"right":[{"id":"r07baa42c66e3","label":"проверять"},{"id":"r7de538b20354","label":"предварительное условие"},{"id":"ra5089f53e06c","label":"фоновые обстоятельства"},{"id":"r50f5b0625ce7","label":"ожидающий решения"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"le18b1f026c9d":"ra5089f53e06c","lad7ec3a43463":"r50f5b0625ce7","l4d3809360ae3":"r07baa42c66e3","ld66e522dda7f":"r7de538b20354"}},"reference_answer":{"le18b1f026c9d":"ra5089f53e06c","lad7ec3a43463":"r50f5b0625ce7","l4d3809360ae3":"r07baa42c66e3","ld66e522dda7f":"r7de538b20354"},"incorrect_answer":{"le18b1f026c9d":"r50f5b0625ce7","lad7ec3a43463":"ra5089f53e06c","l4d3809360ae3":"r07baa42c66e3","ld66e522dda7f":"r7de538b20354"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: background — фоновые обстоятельства; pending — ожидающий решения; verify — проверять; precondition — предварительное условие."},{"id":"6c4c2540-627e-533f-bcc0-697fa2978239","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"reading","prompt":"Зачем запросили отдельную запись о проверке?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The coordinator’s note began, “With the documents checked, the application was submitted.” A later summary suggested that submission itself had verified the documents. The note described a different relationship: checking was presented as background already completed when submission occurred. Another sentence, “With several responses still pending, the committee postponed its decision,” described an unresolved situation instead. Neither construction named every person responsible for the background action. The reviewer therefore asked for the verification record as well as the submission date. A compact grammatical construction could organise the sequence clearly, but it could not by itself provide the independent evidence that the stated checking had actually taken place.","options":[{"id":"vd87a7d165e2c","label":"A submission date always names every verifier."},{"id":"v2f1e39a72d71","label":"The sentence states completion but is not itself independent proof of it."},{"id":"vcc89c65c0b49","label":"The grammar proves the documents were never checked."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2f1e39a72d71"},"reference_answer":"v2f1e39a72d71","incorrect_answer":"vcc89c65c0b49","explanation":"Сообщение о факте и независимое подтверждение факта — разные вещи."},{"id":"a934fb9d-6e90-5608-88c1-c70bcc3cdc54","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери активный фон с отдельным участником.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Which form describes visitors actively waiting?"}],"options":[{"id":"vfba19fa86e31","label":"With the visitors waited outside, we prepared the room."},{"id":"v465ca4c81f12","label":"With the visitors to waiting outside, we prepared the room."},{"id":"vaabcf970b1d2","label":"With the visitors waiting outside, we prepared the room."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vaabcf970b1d2"},"reference_answer":"vaabcf970b1d2","incorrect_answer":"vfba19fa86e31","explanation":"Waiting согласуется со смыслом активного действия visitors."},{"id":"00c81696-be8b-5ef1-a3a3-422364e04f8b","lesson_id":"490b38ae-26ea-5e8e-8ff4-36342ae44a44","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A condition that must be met before another step is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v3e53e5452775","label":"decoration"},{"id":"vd0eb3310dd9f","label":"precondition"},{"id":"vb525bc555268","label":"consequence necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd0eb3310dd9f"},"reference_answer":"vd0eb3310dd9f","incorrect_answer":"vb525bc555268","explanation":"Precondition — предварительное условие."},{"id":"7d0afb17-55d9-5acd-91e4-b4840cccdc28","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: В базовой сослагательной модели: It is essential that the report ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vd32abc1cb0fe","label":"is submitting yesterday"},{"id":"vd60619763f6d","label":"was to submitted"},{"id":"v8a20df512ac4","label":"be submitted on time"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8a20df512ac4"},"reference_answer":"v8a20df512ac4","incorrect_answer":"vd32abc1cb0fe","explanation":"Базовая форма be используется в пассивном требовании be submitted."},{"id":"a2b78ce7-7a83-55d4-9a91-4a3a14c3ee26","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: wear / wears.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"В базовой сослагательной модели: They requested that every visitor ___ a badge."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["wear"]},"reference_answer":"wear","incorrect_answer":"wears","explanation":"В указанной модели используется базовая форма wear даже после every visitor."},{"id":"db095f6c-4b68-5f7b-b7e8-7d3c81851151","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Необходимо, чтобы каждый участник был уведомлён.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"essential"},{"id":"t4","label":"that"},{"id":"t5","label":"every"},{"id":"t6","label":"member"},{"id":"t7","label":"be"},{"id":"t8","label":"informed."},{"id":"t1","label":"It"},{"id":"t2","label":"is"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Фраза задаёт требование, но сама не подтверждает уведомление всех участников."},{"id":"f7c8a38f-6707-5972-b354-b97df23631a0","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"It is essential that the notice be to displayed."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["It is essential that the notice be displayed."]},"reference_answer":"It is essential that the notice be displayed.","incorrect_answer":"It is essential that the notice be to displayed.","explanation":"В выбранном сослагательном пассиве нужно be displayed без to."},{"id":"1937e365-eb68-5ff9-9127-0c279cfa6d8c","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"reading","prompt":"В чём ошибка менеджера?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The procedure stated that it was essential that every participant be informed before the schedule changed. In an audit discussion, one manager cited that sentence as evidence that everyone had received notice. The auditor objected: a requirement described the standard to be met, not a record of compliance. Delivery logs showed that messages had been sent to most participants, while two addresses had failed. The team arranged direct contact with those participants and recorded the result. The grammatical form was appropriate for stating the rule; the error lay in treating the existence of that rule as sufficient evidence that each required action had occurred.","options":[{"id":"v5a68bcb1eeb8","label":"He proved that every address had failed."},{"id":"v800684b9d838","label":"He treated a requirement as evidence of completed compliance."},{"id":"v0138a91ad6e2","label":"He used the rule only as a standard for checking logs."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v800684b9d838"},"reference_answer":"v800684b9d838","incorrect_answer":"v0138a91ad6e2","explanation":"Текст требования не является записью об исполнении для каждого участника."},{"id":"655434a7-6d63-54ce-b94d-73289a5f1cf0","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l0af01d8c296c","label":"essential"},{"id":"lc890c1a4905f","label":"requirement"},{"id":"l648f888ec44c","label":"compliance"},{"id":"l0d89f021d46e","label":"mandate"}],"right":[{"id":"rc52a221ad5ff","label":"соблюдение требования"},{"id":"r6ceb1ea9ebb3","label":"предписание"},{"id":"r445431afde20","label":"необходимый"},{"id":"r6658325bac07","label":"требование"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l0af01d8c296c":"r445431afde20","lc890c1a4905f":"r6658325bac07","l648f888ec44c":"rc52a221ad5ff","l0d89f021d46e":"r6ceb1ea9ebb3"}},"reference_answer":{"l0af01d8c296c":"r445431afde20","lc890c1a4905f":"r6658325bac07","l648f888ec44c":"rc52a221ad5ff","l0d89f021d46e":"r6ceb1ea9ebb3"},"incorrect_answer":{"l0af01d8c296c":"r6658325bac07","lc890c1a4905f":"r445431afde20","l648f888ec44c":"rc52a221ad5ff","l0d89f021d46e":"r6ceb1ea9ebb3"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: essential — необходимый; requirement — требование; compliance — соблюдение требования; mandate — предписание."},{"id":"9eb7fff2-8f69-5a02-949b-f323f86d877b","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что выявили журналы доставки?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The procedure stated that it was essential that every participant be informed before the schedule changed. In an audit discussion, one manager cited that sentence as evidence that everyone had received notice. The auditor objected: a requirement described the standard to be met, not a record of compliance. Delivery logs showed that messages had been sent to most participants, while two addresses had failed. The team arranged direct contact with those participants and recorded the result. The grammatical form was appropriate for stating the rule; the error lay in treating the existence of that rule as sufficient evidence that each required action had occurred.","options":[{"id":"v1c897219beda","label":"Most messages were sent, but two addresses failed."},{"id":"vf3c1df3989b4","label":"Every participant necessarily read the message."},{"id":"v8b98694435bc","label":"No attempt to notify anyone existed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1c897219beda"},"reference_answer":"v1c897219beda","incorrect_answer":"vf3c1df3989b4","explanation":"Даже отправку нужно отличать от всеобщего получения; два сбоя указаны прямо."},{"id":"214f35ab-4dd5-571c-ab0e-65a7edeb8dd5","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани статус предписания.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “We require that the data be checked” establish that they have been checked?"}],"options":[{"id":"va5d2288be2e8","label":"Yes; require always means confirmed yesterday."},{"id":"veb93c7a89581","label":"No; it states a requirement, not its fulfilment."},{"id":"vc856bd57dc26","label":"Yes; the subjunctive makes every action completed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"veb93c7a89581"},"reference_answer":"veb93c7a89581","incorrect_answer":"vc856bd57dc26","explanation":"Требование и доказательство выполнения различаются."},{"id":"16f402d5-8d15-5c1a-9ea6-3c7208b48357","lesson_id":"f587154f-f4f6-5634-9a66-87d51f462972","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Following an established requirement is ___.","options":[{"id":"v986747f94b21","label":"compliance"},{"id":"v572c8542a497","label":"prediction"},{"id":"vd49c14b92470","label":"coincidence only"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v986747f94b21"},"reference_answer":"v986747f94b21","incorrect_answer":"v572c8542a497","explanation":"Compliance — соблюдение установленного требования."},{"id":"d5628973-87e9-5285-b1a9-a6f3495f8626","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The more examples we add, ___ the guide becomes.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"va6e8007f7d01","label":"most longer"},{"id":"vb1ae1683c7ad","label":"the longer"},{"id":"v4e32cc1ba236","label":"than longer"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb1ae1683c7ad"},"reference_answer":"vb1ae1683c7ad","incorrect_answer":"v4e32cc1ba236","explanation":"Парная конструкция требует the + сравнительная степень во второй части."},{"id":"163309ba-9cf2-57df-be52-d6b8b0d444f0","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: clearest / clearer.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The ___ the wording, the fewer questions readers asked in this trial."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["clearer"]},"reference_answer":"clearer","incorrect_answer":"clearest","explanation":"Используется сравнительная степень clearer."},{"id":"06dd1f54-9829-541f-841a-cee4aea03977","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Чем больше подробностей мы добавляем, тем длиннее становится руководство.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"detail"},{"id":"t4","label":"we"},{"id":"t5","label":"add,"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"longer"},{"id":"t8","label":"the"},{"id":"t9","label":"guide"},{"id":"t10","label":"becomes."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"more"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t1"],"explanation":"Обе части используют сравнительную структуру."},{"id":"57ed072e-9e4d-5a7f-a9f8-4e2f6bfc3f31","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The more careful the check, the most reliable the result."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The more careful the check, the more reliable the result."]},"reference_answer":"The more careful the check, the more reliable the result.","incorrect_answer":"The more careful the check, the most reliable the result.","explanation":"Во второй части нужна сравнительная more reliable, не превосходная most reliable."},{"id":"27a13aec-1e62-575b-a2ba-c1caddebc2df","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое ограничение обнаружили при добавлении подробностей?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A team revising a visitor guide noticed a trade-off. The more detail they added, the longer the document became. Initially, this seemed harmless, but some trial readers struggled to locate the instructions relevant to them. The team did not conclude that detail was inherently undesirable. It separated essential steps from optional background and added headings. The relationship between length and difficulty depended on organisation as well as volume. The final report described the observed pattern without turning it into a universal rule that every shorter guide would necessarily be clearer. A comparative construction helped express a relationship, but it did not eliminate the need to specify its context.","options":[{"id":"v230604e87dbc","label":"A longer document could make relevant instructions harder to locate."},{"id":"v488e273fb836","label":"Every extra detail was proved useless."},{"id":"v1ce918744551","label":"The guide stopped containing any essential steps."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v230604e87dbc"},"reference_answer":"v230604e87dbc","incorrect_answer":"v488e273fb836","explanation":"Проблема заключалась в поиске нужного, а не в бесполезности всех подробностей."},{"id":"494e3b2b-a090-5563-b45a-edd9d675c853","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l2d528107852a","label":"correlation"},{"id":"ld06c25ac30ba","label":"clarity"},{"id":"l0d5990dd505d","label":"proportionate"},{"id":"ldf21260af30f","label":"complexity"}],"right":[{"id":"r7aa310d52753","label":"соразмерный"},{"id":"r665ace1a6384","label":"сложность"},{"id":"rc9b98fe50d03","label":"связь между изменениями"},{"id":"r267f0c7070bf","label":"ясность"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l2d528107852a":"rc9b98fe50d03","ld06c25ac30ba":"r267f0c7070bf","l0d5990dd505d":"r7aa310d52753","ldf21260af30f":"r665ace1a6384"}},"reference_answer":{"l2d528107852a":"rc9b98fe50d03","ld06c25ac30ba":"r267f0c7070bf","l0d5990dd505d":"r7aa310d52753","ldf21260af30f":"r665ace1a6384"},"incorrect_answer":{"l2d528107852a":"r267f0c7070bf","ld06c25ac30ba":"rc9b98fe50d03","l0d5990dd505d":"r7aa310d52753","ldf21260af30f":"r665ace1a6384"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: correlation — связь между изменениями; clarity — ясность; proportionate — соразмерный; complexity — сложность."},{"id":"1099e5ad-9d1b-54d3-ac13-ef0ef4e32212","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему нельзя заключить, что любое короткое руководство яснее?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A team revising a visitor guide noticed a trade-off. The more detail they added, the longer the document became. Initially, this seemed harmless, but some trial readers struggled to locate the instructions relevant to them. The team did not conclude that detail was inherently undesirable. It separated essential steps from optional background and added headings. The relationship between length and difficulty depended on organisation as well as volume. The final report described the observed pattern without turning it into a universal rule that every shorter guide would necessarily be clearer. A comparative construction helped express a relationship, but it did not eliminate the need to specify its context.","options":[{"id":"v73aa6f05dfef","label":"Length has no possible relation to use."},{"id":"v1ab4bbe20149","label":"The comparative grammar forbids every observation."},{"id":"v368584ea662f","label":"Organisation and context also affected difficulty."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v368584ea662f"},"reference_answer":"v368584ea662f","incorrect_answer":"v73aa6f05dfef","explanation":"Наблюдаемая связь не даёт универсальной гарантии для всех документов."},{"id":"20c0c432-4bcb-5480-83ff-304ce2f12100","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери согласованную парную сравнительную модель.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Which sentence has the paired comparative structure?"}],"options":[{"id":"vd75f175b03a3","label":"The clearer the headings, the easier the guide is to navigate."},{"id":"v22705616cc87","label":"The clearest the headings, the most easier the guide."},{"id":"vdbcc280955e2","label":"More clearer headings, than easy guide."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd75f175b03a3"},"reference_answer":"vd75f175b03a3","incorrect_answer":"v22705616cc87","explanation":"The clearer ... the easier ... использует две сравнительные формы."},{"id":"f48894de-0e8b-5626-ad17-4eb5d39dffcf","lesson_id":"cc79c78f-d7ab-5078-b478-9b770eee19b1","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The difficulty created by interacting parts is a form of ___.","options":[{"id":"v6f9920774284","label":"certainty"},{"id":"vecdcfa988179","label":"completion necessarily"},{"id":"v26e060bd0086","label":"complexity"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v26e060bd0086"},"reference_answer":"v26e060bd0086","incorrect_answer":"v6f9920774284","explanation":"Complexity — сложность устройства или отношений."},{"id":"ab3a47f4-e9f0-5535-98b7-2dd5a34306c9","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The parcel should ___ by now, but we have no delivery confirmation.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v5017a2b7c6f1","label":"have arrived"},{"id":"vb24d181c4163","label":"has arrived"},{"id":"v29ab375ffd43","label":"having arrived"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5017a2b7c6f1"},"reference_answer":"v5017a2b7c6f1","incorrect_answer":"vb24d181c4163","explanation":"После should нужна форма have arrived; отсутствие подтверждения сохраняет неопределённость."},{"id":"6ef3c5b7-ca85-5c1c-81c8-ddbb98b7f90b","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: checked / check.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"You should have ___ the address before sending it."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["checked"]},"reference_answer":"checked","incorrect_answer":"check","explanation":"После have в этой модальной форме используется checked."},{"id":"c156ca03-2f70-5a85-b770-74c30a2ea255","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Документы уже должны были прибыть к этому моменту.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"should"},{"id":"t4","label":"have"},{"id":"t5","label":"arrived"},{"id":"t6","label":"by"},{"id":"t7","label":"now."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"documents"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Контекст может выражать ожидание; предложение не является журналом доставки."},{"id":"d57edddb-2295-5809-b401-eaa374ace79b","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"She should has checked the attachment."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["She should have checked the attachment."]},"reference_answer":"She should have checked the attachment.","incorrect_answer":"She should has checked the attachment.","explanation":"После should используется have, не has."},{"id":"cc2b2fa9-5884-58fa-bb26-a69f7b208fd7","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую функцию имела первая реплика помощника?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"When the courier had not confirmed delivery, the assistant said that the documents should have arrived by now. The manager initially entered them as received. The assistant clarified that the statement expressed an expectation based on the usual delivery time. It did not establish arrival. In a different exchange, “You should have checked the address” criticised an earlier omission. Both sentences used should have, but their functions differed. The team checked the tracking record before updating receipt status, rather than allowing either the grammatical form or the strength of an expectation to stand in for evidence of the event.","options":[{"id":"v818887b9794b","label":"A confirmed report of receipt."},{"id":"v7599523ea925","label":"A guarantee that no delay was possible."},{"id":"v4348bc1ac974","label":"An expectation based on usual delivery time."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4348bc1ac974"},"reference_answer":"v4348bc1ac974","incorrect_answer":"v818887b9794b","explanation":"Отсутствовало подтверждение; should have передавало ожидание."},{"id":"b7790155-f246-5b84-9365-56f2a6fafd14","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lc84b439f31e5","label":"expectation"},{"id":"l881ff6e94b18","label":"criticism"},{"id":"lc15337ecd067","label":"verification"},{"id":"lb02ab940137a","label":"overdue"}],"right":[{"id":"r799f0cf5d789","label":"проверка"},{"id":"r726b5f3b8de7","label":"просроченный"},{"id":"r1b8b8ce77d19","label":"ожидание"},{"id":"r7ba23bf645f3","label":"критика"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lc84b439f31e5":"r1b8b8ce77d19","l881ff6e94b18":"r7ba23bf645f3","lc15337ecd067":"r799f0cf5d789","lb02ab940137a":"r726b5f3b8de7"}},"reference_answer":{"lc84b439f31e5":"r1b8b8ce77d19","l881ff6e94b18":"r7ba23bf645f3","lc15337ecd067":"r799f0cf5d789","lb02ab940137a":"r726b5f3b8de7"},"incorrect_answer":{"lc84b439f31e5":"r7ba23bf645f3","l881ff6e94b18":"r1b8b8ce77d19","lc15337ecd067":"r799f0cf5d789","lb02ab940137a":"r726b5f3b8de7"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: expectation — ожидание; criticism — критика; verification — проверка; overdue — просроченный."},{"id":"73fe2bef-eb4b-5de5-bf59-70aacde329b8","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что команда сделала перед обновлением статуса?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"When the courier had not confirmed delivery, the assistant said that the documents should have arrived by now. The manager initially entered them as received. The assistant clarified that the statement expressed an expectation based on the usual delivery time. It did not establish arrival. In a different exchange, “You should have checked the address” criticised an earlier omission. Both sentences used should have, but their functions differed. The team checked the tracking record before updating receipt status, rather than allowing either the grammatical form or the strength of an expectation to stand in for evidence of the event.","options":[{"id":"v81335d6b8363","label":"Deleted every record of the shipment."},{"id":"v0ae41da2a654","label":"Checked the tracking record."},{"id":"v147790eb2cc1","label":"Assumed grammar proved delivery."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0ae41da2a654"},"reference_answer":"v0ae41da2a654","incorrect_answer":"v147790eb2cc1","explanation":"Проверка фактического состояния была отделена от модального высказывания."},{"id":"418315d4-bf00-5054-8ed8-7b638326cc72","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Отдели модальное ожидание от проверенного факта.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “The train should have arrived” necessarily establish arrival?"}],"options":[{"id":"vc859d79886b5","label":"Yes; should have always marks a verified event."},{"id":"v08e38ba193f9","label":"Yes; every expectation is a completed measurement."},{"id":"vbf4c99b2cadb","label":"No; it can express an expectation that still needs checking."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbf4c99b2cadb"},"reference_answer":"vbf4c99b2cadb","incorrect_answer":"vc859d79886b5","explanation":"Should have не служит самостоятельным доказательством прибытия."},{"id":"995a239c-ad09-5d2d-b753-8f8059c69982","lesson_id":"b657bf92-2cf9-5381-a893-7ad538a23f63","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An item expected earlier but not yet received is ___.","options":[{"id":"vc627349d8499","label":"verified necessarily"},{"id":"v2e1266b536c6","label":"overdue"},{"id":"v559914fdd3ef","label":"premature"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2e1266b536c6"},"reference_answer":"v2e1266b536c6","incorrect_answer":"v559914fdd3ef","explanation":"Overdue означает просроченный или запоздавший."},{"id":"7a686402-17c2-5b8b-9063-b79dce67b37e","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: They requested a revision, and the editor ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v8d70d2dff50c","label":"did it so to"},{"id":"v761a4b207202","label":"doing so was to"},{"id":"v254bfc0aef1c","label":"did so"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v254bfc0aef1c"},"reference_answer":"v254bfc0aef1c","incorrect_answer":"v8d70d2dff50c","explanation":"Did so заменяет ранее названное действие revision/revise."},{"id":"cdfe3693-2a1f-5b7f-a765-9eb9f0698fdb","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: such / so.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We were asked to notify the applicants and agreed to do ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["so"]},"reference_answer":"so","incorrect_answer":"such","explanation":"Do so замещает названное действие уведомления."},{"id":"7e7685b6-7272-5a98-8b97-6eafc717769e","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Нас попросили пересмотреть черновик, и мы это сделали.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"us"},{"id":"t4","label":"to"},{"id":"t5","label":"revise"},{"id":"t6","label":"the"},{"id":"t7","label":"draft,"},{"id":"t8","label":"and"},{"id":"t9","label":"we"},{"id":"t10","label":"did"},{"id":"t11","label":"so."},{"id":"t1","label":"They"},{"id":"t2","label":"asked"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t11","t1"],"explanation":"Did so относится к пересмотру черновика, а не к любому другому соседнему процессу."},{"id":"35962b72-2002-54e0-9e62-a3e969675867","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"She promised to update the list and has do so."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["She promised to update the list and has done so."]},"reference_answer":"She promised to update the list and has done so.","incorrect_answer":"She promised to update the list and has do so.","explanation":"После has требуется причастие done."},{"id":"e3e71412-0b79-5393-9c27-c95c67c81b6b","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое действие было завершено?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The review asked the team to clarify the eligibility rule. The team did so in the next draft, adding an example beneath the relevant paragraph. A separate recommendation asked for a new appeals process, which required board approval and remained unresolved. A summary later said that the team had “done so” in response to all recommendations. That widened the reference beyond its original antecedent. The editor corrected the account: clarification had been completed, while the appeals proposal was still pending. Short substitutions were useful for avoiding repetition, but they had to preserve the scope of the action actually reported rather than implying completion of an entire list.","options":[{"id":"v59fb82eb2c1f","label":"Every recommendation without exception."},{"id":"v53cb10eafb29","label":"Clarifying the eligibility rule."},{"id":"vd275c08d7f0b","label":"Obtaining board approval for a new appeals process."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v53cb10eafb29"},"reference_answer":"v53cb10eafb29","incorrect_answer":"vd275c08d7f0b","explanation":"Did so первоначально отсылало к уточнению правила."},{"id":"9b2230f6-ec0a-531b-b5fc-f347addb1516","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l7fc9e39f9e91","label":"substitution"},{"id":"l52b6f3a979cc","label":"antecedent"},{"id":"l315bf75f6b8c","label":"revise"},{"id":"laa9e565e182e","label":"scope"}],"right":[{"id":"r30c6bd98e41e","label":"пересматривать"},{"id":"r66232b916eee","label":"область действия"},{"id":"r0b8a26e9fdc3","label":"замещение"},{"id":"rfa6b302c1dd1","label":"предшествующий элемент отсылки"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l7fc9e39f9e91":"r0b8a26e9fdc3","l52b6f3a979cc":"rfa6b302c1dd1","l315bf75f6b8c":"r30c6bd98e41e","laa9e565e182e":"r66232b916eee"}},"reference_answer":{"l7fc9e39f9e91":"r0b8a26e9fdc3","l52b6f3a979cc":"rfa6b302c1dd1","l315bf75f6b8c":"r30c6bd98e41e","laa9e565e182e":"r66232b916eee"},"incorrect_answer":{"l7fc9e39f9e91":"rfa6b302c1dd1","l52b6f3a979cc":"r0b8a26e9fdc3","l315bf75f6b8c":"r30c6bd98e41e","laa9e565e182e":"r66232b916eee"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: substitution — замещение; antecedent — предшествующий элемент отсылки; revise — пересматривать; scope — область действия."},{"id":"70a11b10-20af-56ba-a3b3-70089555702d","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что исказил краткий пересказ?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The review asked the team to clarify the eligibility rule. The team did so in the next draft, adding an example beneath the relevant paragraph. A separate recommendation asked for a new appeals process, which required board approval and remained unresolved. A summary later said that the team had “done so” in response to all recommendations. That widened the reference beyond its original antecedent. The editor corrected the account: clarification had been completed, while the appeals proposal was still pending. Short substitutions were useful for avoiding repetition, but they had to preserve the scope of the action actually reported rather than implying completion of an entire list.","options":[{"id":"veb018fb68888","label":"It extended a substitution for one action to all recommendations."},{"id":"v9f7417ea7aa3","label":"It accurately preserved the pending appeals process."},{"id":"vcb34a48fbad2","label":"It showed that the example was never added."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"veb018fb68888"},"reference_answer":"veb018fb68888","incorrect_answer":"v9f7417ea7aa3","explanation":"Область отсылки была расширена без основания."},{"id":"f850fc5c-d65a-5ed4-8c2e-fd47823fef2d","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Выбери принцип точного сокращения.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"If “do so” replaces “notify applicants”, what should a careful summary preserve?"}],"options":[{"id":"v8f4131307033","label":"The removal of all subjects and timing."},{"id":"vaa78134247ec","label":"That specific action and its actual completion status."},{"id":"vafbd0b209b7a","label":"Every other task as automatically completed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vaa78134247ec"},"reference_answer":"vaa78134247ec","incorrect_answer":"vafbd0b209b7a","explanation":"Замещение не должно расширять объём выполненной работы."},{"id":"6706101d-4d49-599b-a93f-5153c4440469","lesson_id":"3a1b841c-53b9-57b0-8d07-cfbeb2f6d56f","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The earlier expression to which a substitution refers is its ___.","options":[{"id":"vd0bdbde1ab51","label":"antecedent"},{"id":"va83774831249","label":"consequence necessarily"},{"id":"v248fbb8ef223","label":"deadline"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd0bdbde1ab51"},"reference_answer":"vd0bdbde1ab51","incorrect_answer":"va83774831249","explanation":"Antecedent — предшествующий элемент, который подхватывает отсылка."},{"id":"9f1318e6-0f22-598c-a943-5410baeb777d","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The catalogue is far from ___ complete.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v72d69fe9c33d","label":"been to"},{"id":"vecee0786edd6","label":"being"},{"id":"vba34c40e0dc5","label":"be"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vecee0786edd6"},"reference_answer":"vecee0786edd6","incorrect_answer":"vba34c40e0dc5","explanation":"После from как предлога здесь нужна форма being."},{"id":"3095a7f3-3b25-517d-85c9-22f54af382d7","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: solving / solve.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Far from ___ the problem, the first patch created another one."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["solving"]},"reference_answer":"solving","incorrect_answer":"solve","explanation":"После from в этой конструкции используется -ing-форма solving."},{"id":"cf9be91b-c07b-5cb1-8630-132cba3e3544","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Каталог далеко не завершён.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"is"},{"id":"t4","label":"far"},{"id":"t5","label":"from"},{"id":"t6","label":"being"},{"id":"t7","label":"complete."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"catalogue"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Фраза оценивает незавершённость, не утверждая отсутствия всех записей."},{"id":"42086ed6-4d3d-55ab-9ec3-f2d6fb36c3b3","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The project is far from be finished."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The project is far from being finished."]},"reference_answer":"The project is far from being finished.","incorrect_answer":"The project is far from be finished.","explanation":"После from используется being."},{"id":"f07604e1-2e72-53dc-bed4-3c63e4802403","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что означала оценка куратора?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The curator called the online catalogue “far from complete”. Several collections had not yet been described, and some existing records needed checking. A report of the discussion paraphrased this as “The catalogue has no value”. The curator rejected that conclusion. Visitors could already use thousands of reliable entries, even though coverage remained uneven. The point of the criticism was to identify unfinished work, not to deny every benefit of the work completed. The revised report stated both facts: the catalogue was useful in its current scope and still required substantial expansion and verification. A negative evaluation of completeness did not establish total uselessness.","options":[{"id":"v38a6255aa7cc","label":"Substantial work remained, though existing entries could be useful."},{"id":"v4f273bc2bee4","label":"No reliable entry existed anywhere."},{"id":"vb1bd5e4f2ef6","label":"The catalogue was officially complete."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v38a6255aa7cc"},"reference_answer":"v38a6255aa7cc","incorrect_answer":"v4f273bc2bee4","explanation":"Критика полноты не равна отрицанию пользы всех готовых записей."},{"id":"8b222b77-fac2-54c3-b48d-5f0b689e676d","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lc07fdf1d77e5","label":"partial"},{"id":"l1ef3f28ec3f7","label":"incomplete"},{"id":"lf479657f6ebc","label":"useful"},{"id":"l96695e0aaf48","label":"assessment"}],"right":[{"id":"rca2b56432321","label":"полезный"},{"id":"r90adbeed41f6","label":"оценка"},{"id":"r7abb4938aaa7","label":"частичный"},{"id":"r5542c3099601","label":"незавершённый"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lc07fdf1d77e5":"r7abb4938aaa7","l1ef3f28ec3f7":"r5542c3099601","lf479657f6ebc":"rca2b56432321","l96695e0aaf48":"r90adbeed41f6"}},"reference_answer":{"lc07fdf1d77e5":"r7abb4938aaa7","l1ef3f28ec3f7":"r5542c3099601","lf479657f6ebc":"rca2b56432321","l96695e0aaf48":"r90adbeed41f6"},"incorrect_answer":{"lc07fdf1d77e5":"r5542c3099601","l1ef3f28ec3f7":"r7abb4938aaa7","lf479657f6ebc":"rca2b56432321","l96695e0aaf48":"r90adbeed41f6"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: partial — частичный; incomplete — незавершённый; useful — полезный; assessment — оценка."},{"id":"ae82dddd-b87e-5b22-ae58-08177dfeff0c","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что исправили в отчёте?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The curator called the online catalogue “far from complete”. Several collections had not yet been described, and some existing records needed checking. A report of the discussion paraphrased this as “The catalogue has no value”. The curator rejected that conclusion. Visitors could already use thousands of reliable entries, even though coverage remained uneven. The point of the criticism was to identify unfinished work, not to deny every benefit of the work completed. The revised report stated both facts: the catalogue was useful in its current scope and still required substantial expansion and verification. A negative evaluation of completeness did not establish total uselessness.","options":[{"id":"v1d7617201d8c","label":"It removed every mention of unfinished collections."},{"id":"vae7749b43c15","label":"It declared that verification was unnecessary."},{"id":"v8622cc05bafe","label":"It now preserved usefulness and the need for further work."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8622cc05bafe"},"reference_answer":"v8622cc05bafe","incorrect_answer":"v1d7617201d8c","explanation":"Исправленный текст удерживает две совместимые оценки."},{"id":"687e5fc6-87cf-502d-b843-8881b89f36de","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Не усиливай оценку без основания.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can “far from perfect” be paraphrased as “entirely useless” without context?"}],"options":[{"id":"ve5e75bf22558","label":"No; that introduces a stronger and different judgement."},{"id":"v1ae302247ef2","label":"Yes; imperfect and useless are exact equivalents."},{"id":"vb8ac125772b6","label":"Yes; every negative modifier cancels all value."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve5e75bf22558"},"reference_answer":"ve5e75bf22558","incorrect_answer":"v1ae302247ef2","explanation":"Несовершенство и полная бесполезность не равнозначны."},{"id":"62557c0a-a615-587a-be18-253a73307cf5","lesson_id":"ea03e5ae-dd32-5f0c-b0ae-a933caf4d119","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Something finished only in part is ___.","options":[{"id":"v6f9d51301706","label":"complete"},{"id":"v5d3acd809338","label":"universal necessarily"},{"id":"vee61ac477f24","label":"partial"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vee61ac477f24"},"reference_answer":"vee61ac477f24","incorrect_answer":"v6f9d51301706","explanation":"Partial — частичный, не полный."},{"id":"54ac71a2-1c89-5a9a-a16a-4d259b0d71e7","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “It is not merely inconvenient; it prevents access” rejects ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"ve4219fdec3b7","label":"the adequacy of a weak description"},{"id":"vc69f5be6fa28","label":"the fact that access is affected"},{"id":"v672b1df74ae1","label":"all criticism of the arrangement"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve4219fdec3b7"},"reference_answer":"ve4219fdec3b7","incorrect_answer":"vc69f5be6fa28","explanation":"Отрицается достаточность слова inconvenient, а не наличие проблемы."},{"id":"2e113327-c5a9-56c8-b225-c6f423981e9e","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: mere / merely.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The problem is not ___ cosmetic; it affects the whole process."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["merely"]},"reference_answer":"merely","incorrect_answer":"mere","explanation":"Перед cosmetic в данном значении нужно наречие merely."},{"id":"814a0e98-00ee-52f1-9ab3-6999d4ec6776","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Проблема не просто неудобна: оценка этим не исчерпывается.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"is"},{"id":"t4","label":"not"},{"id":"t5","label":"merely"},{"id":"t6","label":"inconvenient."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"problem"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t1"],"explanation":"Not merely отвергает ограничение оценки одним слабым признаком."},{"id":"5727ec4e-e39b-5711-a00a-49bcc3e7dad9","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The change is not mere inconvenient; it blocks the entrance."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The change is not merely inconvenient; it blocks the entrance."]},"reference_answer":"The change is not merely inconvenient; it blocks the entrance.","incorrect_answer":"The change is not mere inconvenient; it blocks the entrance.","explanation":"Для ограничения прилагательного используется merely."},{"id":"1226537b-d540-5a77-b103-40bcd5f51041","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что председатель отрицал в полной реплике?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a discussion of a delayed public notice, the chair said, “It is not merely late; it leaves applicants without time to respond.” A short account quoted only “not late”, making the chair appear to deny the delay. In the full exchange, the chair accepted the lateness and objected to treating it as a minor scheduling inconvenience. The objection concerned the adequacy of the description: it omitted the practical consequence for people receiving the notice. Another member agreed that the delay mattered but questioned whether every applicant had been affected equally. The final minutes retained both qualifications, distinguishing criticism of a weak label from denial of the event and distinguishing a serious consequence from an unsupported claim about every individual.","options":[{"id":"v903e593b2d01","label":"That the notice had been delayed at all."},{"id":"v822990e81ca0","label":"That applicants needed time to respond."},{"id":"v381603f079a9","label":"That “merely late” adequately described the problem."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v381603f079a9"},"reference_answer":"v381603f079a9","incorrect_answer":"v903e593b2d01","explanation":"Полная реплика признаёт задержку и усиливает оценку её последствий."},{"id":"a1a4c901-9546-54d6-aa2e-f556ec0b1b90","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l90942aec4f69","label":"merely"},{"id":"lc3547efa693d","label":"understatement"},{"id":"l51dc680e32cc","label":"severity"},{"id":"ld58bb54ced22","label":"description"}],"right":[{"id":"r00ce24347b49","label":"серьёзность"},{"id":"r444a96473d8a","label":"описание"},{"id":"rae2098b47484","label":"всего лишь"},{"id":"r4a2d7289afbd","label":"преуменьшение"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l90942aec4f69":"rae2098b47484","lc3547efa693d":"r4a2d7289afbd","l51dc680e32cc":"r00ce24347b49","ld58bb54ced22":"r444a96473d8a"}},"reference_answer":{"l90942aec4f69":"rae2098b47484","lc3547efa693d":"r4a2d7289afbd","l51dc680e32cc":"r00ce24347b49","ld58bb54ced22":"r444a96473d8a"},"incorrect_answer":{"l90942aec4f69":"r4a2d7289afbd","lc3547efa693d":"rae2098b47484","l51dc680e32cc":"r00ce24347b49","ld58bb54ced22":"r444a96473d8a"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: merely — всего лишь; understatement — преуменьшение; severity — серьёзность; description — описание."},{"id":"fca8f760-ebf3-5797-9e4d-e42053f71ac9","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую дополнительную границу сохраняют итоговые протоколы?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a discussion of a delayed public notice, the chair said, “It is not merely late; it leaves applicants without time to respond.” A short account quoted only “not late”, making the chair appear to deny the delay. In the full exchange, the chair accepted the lateness and objected to treating it as a minor scheduling inconvenience. The objection concerned the adequacy of the description: it omitted the practical consequence for people receiving the notice. Another member agreed that the delay mattered but questioned whether every applicant had been affected equally. The final minutes retained both qualifications, distinguishing criticism of a weak label from denial of the event and distinguishing a serious consequence from an unsupported claim about every individual.","options":[{"id":"vca6fd2535337","label":"All practical consequences are unimportant by definition."},{"id":"v0276e81c9f67","label":"The consequence may be serious without proof that every applicant was affected equally."},{"id":"v3f261f969f5a","label":"No applicant could possibly have been affected."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0276e81c9f67"},"reference_answer":"v0276e81c9f67","incorrect_answer":"v3f261f969f5a","explanation":"Тяжесть проблемы не доказывает одинаковый эффект для всех."},{"id":"827f6136-7c02-577d-aece-f3cd58b3f7d3","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани область действия отрицания.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can “not merely difficult” safely become “not difficult”?"}],"options":[{"id":"va3bbca39af3e","label":"Yes; merely has no effect on scope."},{"id":"v3b203e5d59d2","label":"Yes; all negative statements deny the entire event."},{"id":"v1aa8511aca55","label":"No; it can reject an insufficient description while retaining the difficulty."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1aa8511aca55"},"reference_answer":"v1aa8511aca55","incorrect_answer":"va3bbca39af3e","explanation":"Удаление merely меняет смысл с усиления оценки на простое отрицание."},{"id":"83d07ec3-7c70-54fc-8d16-93d7a8be2a4b","lesson_id":"f02e0ddc-300b-5809-85ee-54b3882de222","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A description making something seem less serious than it is can be an ___.","options":[{"id":"ve113e18bed3c","label":"independent verification"},{"id":"v236d454fcfc3","label":"understatement"},{"id":"v227554157ff0","label":"overstatement"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v236d454fcfc3"},"reference_answer":"v236d454fcfc3","incorrect_answer":"v227554157ff0","explanation":"Understatement — преуменьшение, противоположное overstatement."},{"id":"355f277e-5933-55f5-87d0-389330e0f3d1","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “We undertake to consider the request” commits the speaker to ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v853295bf6111","label":"granting the request regardless of its merits"},{"id":"v36a9827b985e","label":"having already approved the request"},{"id":"v9b2ed28f543a","label":"giving the request consideration"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9b2ed28f543a"},"reference_answer":"v9b2ed28f543a","incorrect_answer":"v853295bf6111","explanation":"Содержание обязательства ограничено рассмотрением."},{"id":"8de831a3-12f0-56bd-afbc-d6dd70dfab2c","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: considered / considering.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The promise concerns whether the proposal will be ___, not whether it will be accepted."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["considered"]},"reference_answer":"considered","incorrect_answer":"considering","explanation":"В пассивном will be considered требуется причастие considered."},{"id":"9c3edd9b-7b82-5ae7-ba0f-96f99c2dd0f7","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Комиссия рассмотрит предложение.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"will"},{"id":"t4","label":"consider"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"proposal."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"committee"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t1"],"explanation":"Фраза не заменяет отдельного решения об одобрении."},{"id":"1f4be2f6-9b87-5e7c-8c34-b96e53329a73","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"They promised to consider whether to changes the rule."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["They promised to consider whether to change the rule."]},"reference_answer":"They promised to consider whether to change the rule.","incorrect_answer":"They promised to consider whether to changes the rule.","explanation":"После to нужна начальная форма change."},{"id":"a3d37ab2-0585-5fb6-ac8d-b33e65e4ba8c","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что обращение жителей действительно обеспечило?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A committee replied to a residents’ petition by promising to consider a change to the booking rules. The campaign’s next message announced that the committee had committed to making the change. When challenged, the campaign argued that the reply would otherwise have been meaningless. Yet consideration was itself a procedural undertaking: the proposal would enter discussion, while its outcome remained open. The committee had not promised rejection either. In the subsequent meeting, members reviewed access concerns alongside staffing limits and requested further information. A careful account could acknowledge that the petition had secured a hearing without transforming that achievement into a decision that had not been made. The distinction preserved the actual progress while keeping the unresolved policy question visible.","options":[{"id":"vbb68bbc783d0","label":"A promise to reject the request."},{"id":"v6974cbf40c58","label":"A commitment to consideration, not guaranteed adoption."},{"id":"v3692397639f4","label":"Unconditional adoption of the new rule."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v6974cbf40c58"},"reference_answer":"v6974cbf40c58","incorrect_answer":"v3692397639f4","explanation":"Обещание процедурного шага не равно обещанию исхода."},{"id":"ea39ec59-062b-5e8f-94de-ac0867542691","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lcf63290e2a05","label":"undertaking"},{"id":"l790ee27c142a","label":"deliberation"},{"id":"l2747e7240609","label":"endorsement"},{"id":"l0e81e6b85f46","label":"noncommittal"}],"right":[{"id":"r5d2cacdb534e","label":"одобрение"},{"id":"r028053f1ae68","label":"не выражающий определённого решения"},{"id":"rcd8babff62d8","label":"принятое обязательство"},{"id":"rbc5e753e6983","label":"обсуждение перед решением"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lcf63290e2a05":"rcd8babff62d8","l790ee27c142a":"rbc5e753e6983","l2747e7240609":"r5d2cacdb534e","l0e81e6b85f46":"r028053f1ae68"}},"reference_answer":{"lcf63290e2a05":"rcd8babff62d8","l790ee27c142a":"rbc5e753e6983","l2747e7240609":"r5d2cacdb534e","l0e81e6b85f46":"r028053f1ae68"},"incorrect_answer":{"lcf63290e2a05":"rbc5e753e6983","l790ee27c142a":"rcd8babff62d8","l2747e7240609":"r5d2cacdb534e","l0e81e6b85f46":"r028053f1ae68"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: undertaking — принятое обязательство; deliberation — обсуждение перед решением; endorsement — одобрение; noncommittal — не выражающий определённого решения."},{"id":"5d2e8bd7-b660-59d1-a235-1cb758d9ff0e","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему отрицать любой прогресс тоже было бы неточно?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A committee replied to a residents’ petition by promising to consider a change to the booking rules. The campaign’s next message announced that the committee had committed to making the change. When challenged, the campaign argued that the reply would otherwise have been meaningless. Yet consideration was itself a procedural undertaking: the proposal would enter discussion, while its outcome remained open. The committee had not promised rejection either. In the subsequent meeting, members reviewed access concerns alongside staffing limits and requested further information. A careful account could acknowledge that the petition had secured a hearing without transforming that achievement into a decision that had not been made. The distinction preserved the actual progress while keeping the unresolved policy question visible.","options":[{"id":"v51c2bb488797","label":"A hearing had been secured even though the decision remained open."},{"id":"v2d68bf3ca50d","label":"Every undecided issue is automatically approved."},{"id":"v339cef7a0b39","label":"The reply contained no procedural undertaking at all."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v51c2bb488797"},"reference_answer":"v51c2bb488797","incorrect_answer":"v2d68bf3ca50d","explanation":"Рассмотрение — реальный шаг, но его нельзя усиливать до принятия."},{"id":"c059a1f6-83d3-5364-a620-6797dbfee819","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани и обещанный шаг, и неопределённый исход.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"What is the safest report of “We will consider whether to extend access”?"}],"options":[{"id":"v613d965ba025","label":"They have confirmed that extension is impossible."},{"id":"vcdbbdc927a1c","label":"They have promised to examine an extension, with the outcome open."},{"id":"v398ef753d8a0","label":"They have guaranteed extended access."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vcdbbdc927a1c"},"reference_answer":"vcdbbdc927a1c","incorrect_answer":"v398ef753d8a0","explanation":"Рассмотрение не устанавливает ни принятие, ни отказ."},{"id":"8490e149-5f68-59d2-b39c-2beb56c60e87","lesson_id":"1472be16-8ad1-5af2-8f09-949e6255149f","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An explicit promise to carry out a specified action is an ___.","options":[{"id":"v13023a0f4911","label":"undertaking"},{"id":"v9fbc6b464925","label":"completed outcome necessarily"},{"id":"v9e473224c4a6","label":"unrecorded possibility only"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v13023a0f4911"},"reference_answer":"v13023a0f4911","incorrect_answer":"v9fbc6b464925","explanation":"Undertaking — принятое обязательство определённого содержания."},{"id":"8c841f7d-7b45-5a10-9848-ba9ac9b243fc","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: If a narrator says “everyone agreed” but quotes an objection, the text supports ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v8f462b0bd8aa","label":"proving a deliberate lie regardless of context"},{"id":"vc512ed43b124","label":"questioning the universal claim of agreement"},{"id":"vd8994ab24081","label":"proving that every person secretly agreed"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc512ed43b124"},"reference_answer":"vc512ed43b124","incorrect_answer":"vd8994ab24081","explanation":"Одно явное возражение ограничивает everyone, но не устанавливает мотив искажения."},{"id":"4c54a8f1-440b-520d-af49-70b1279eb9d1","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: established / establish.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The quoted objection does not by itself ___ deliberate deception."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["establish"]},"reference_answer":"establish","incorrect_answer":"established","explanation":"После does not требуется establish."},{"id":"3da5242f-f4c4-5474-aaa4-57bcbdc79aa2","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Обобщение рассказчика расходится с приведённой репликой.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"summary"},{"id":"t4","label":"conflicts"},{"id":"t5","label":"with"},{"id":"t6","label":"a"},{"id":"t7","label":"quoted"},{"id":"t8","label":"reply."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"narrator’s"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Конфликт относится к конкретному изложению, а не автоматически ко всем словам рассказчика."},{"id":"6e776d87-0d79-514e-a545-a6cc495df1c2","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The narrator claim that everyone agreed."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The narrator claims that everyone agreed."]},"reference_answer":"The narrator claims that everyone agreed.","incorrect_answer":"The narrator claim that everyone agreed.","explanation":"Единственное narrator требует claims."},{"id":"c2901bd2-5952-516d-ad02-d9dc83bbb014","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как прямая реплика Мары ограничивает вступительное everyone?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"“Everyone welcomed my plan,” the narrator recalls. He describes the warm room, the tea and the pleasing sound of chairs moving closer. Then he quotes Mara: “I can see why you want it, but I cannot support that timetable.” He remembers this as encouragement, dwelling on her first clause and passing quickly over the second. The passage gives readers grounds to question his universal account of agreement. It does not reveal whether he is consciously misleading them, protecting a cherished memory or simply misunderstanding a qualified response. The difference between his recollection and the quoted words is meaningful precisely because both are present. Readers can identify the tension without inventing a private motive that the passage never establishes.","options":[{"id":"vf7291dc69f03","label":"It includes an explicit refusal to support the timetable."},{"id":"v1ded5b38fc2f","label":"It proves unconditional agreement with every detail."},{"id":"ve2f2af3070cc","label":"It contains no evaluation of the plan."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf7291dc69f03"},"reference_answer":"vf7291dc69f03","incorrect_answer":"v1ded5b38fc2f","explanation":"Понимание мотива в первой части не отменяет отказ во второй."},{"id":"6ee8c879-0e30-5398-a86d-b4f3170550e9","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"la46396960b83","label":"narrator"},{"id":"l78b15764953e","label":"perspective"},{"id":"l5316cb1b3554","label":"dissent"},{"id":"l047089524a8c","label":"recollection"}],"right":[{"id":"r988fcb44a2d8","label":"несогласие"},{"id":"rd0de5008734c","label":"воспоминание"},{"id":"r0da87cdf8ebe","label":"рассказчик"},{"id":"r3a9a5cdc66cf","label":"точка зрения"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"la46396960b83":"r0da87cdf8ebe","l78b15764953e":"r3a9a5cdc66cf","l5316cb1b3554":"r988fcb44a2d8","l047089524a8c":"rd0de5008734c"}},"reference_answer":{"la46396960b83":"r0da87cdf8ebe","l78b15764953e":"r3a9a5cdc66cf","l5316cb1b3554":"r988fcb44a2d8","l047089524a8c":"rd0de5008734c"},"incorrect_answer":{"la46396960b83":"r3a9a5cdc66cf","l78b15764953e":"r0da87cdf8ebe","l5316cb1b3554":"r988fcb44a2d8","l047089524a8c":"rd0de5008734c"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: narrator — рассказчик; perspective — точка зрения; dissent — несогласие; recollection — воспоминание."},{"id":"82ceefa3-f575-5f3a-8829-583ec1369d42","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какого вывода текст не позволяет уверенно сделать?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"“Everyone welcomed my plan,” the narrator recalls. He describes the warm room, the tea and the pleasing sound of chairs moving closer. Then he quotes Mara: “I can see why you want it, but I cannot support that timetable.” He remembers this as encouragement, dwelling on her first clause and passing quickly over the second. The passage gives readers grounds to question his universal account of agreement. It does not reveal whether he is consciously misleading them, protecting a cherished memory or simply misunderstanding a qualified response. The difference between his recollection and the quoted words is meaningful precisely because both are present. Readers can identify the tension without inventing a private motive that the passage never establishes.","options":[{"id":"ve00226b89e5c","label":"That his universal summary is questionable."},{"id":"v2c653075ee4c","label":"That Mara distinguishes understanding from support."},{"id":"v2efefdce0709","label":"That the narrator is deliberately deceiving readers."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2efefdce0709"},"reference_answer":"v2efefdce0709","incorrect_answer":"ve00226b89e5c","explanation":"Мотив рассказчика оставлен открытым, хотя несоответствие доступно анализу."},{"id":"f57a1946-adb3-5574-92b8-f6b23948afc1","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани границу между наблюдением и догадкой о намерении.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can we describe a narrator’s account as questionable without claiming access to their intentions?"}],"options":[{"id":"v4c6239c5d2fa","label":"Yes; identify the contradiction and keep the motive unresolved."},{"id":"vad6020eb0f00","label":"No; every contradiction proves intentional deception."},{"id":"vcca96be25fb6","label":"Yes; inventing a motive is required for reading."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v4c6239c5d2fa"},"reference_answer":"v4c6239c5d2fa","incorrect_answer":"vad6020eb0f00","explanation":"Текстовый конфликт можно обосновать отдельно от недоказанного мотива."},{"id":"e2839826-8629-5580-8ef9-a501e1728656","lesson_id":"58aac4e7-291f-5943-85c3-0300512ec05e","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An explicit expression of disagreement is ___.","options":[{"id":"v5e306efd0408","label":"unanimity"},{"id":"v9659c7c828a5","label":"endorsement"},{"id":"v9966b6029674","label":"dissent"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9966b6029674"},"reference_answer":"v9966b6029674","incorrect_answer":"v5e306efd0408","explanation":"Dissent — несогласие, а unanimity — единогласие."},{"id":"cf034655-74c2-556d-b000-9fd05553100d","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “The certificate is necessary but not sufficient for admission” means ___.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"ve9af1945b30f","label":"It is required, but other conditions still matter."},{"id":"v3ae84fa8ee7e","label":"It guarantees admission by itself."},{"id":"v185cc315055a","label":"It is irrelevant to admission."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve9af1945b30f"},"reference_answer":"ve9af1945b30f","incorrect_answer":"v3ae84fa8ee7e","explanation":"Фраза утверждает обязательность сертификата без самостоятельной гарантии поступления."},{"id":"7934156f-df89-597a-b052-85b3b195f49a","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: guarantee / guarantees.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Meeting one condition does not necessarily ___ the outcome."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["guarantee"]},"reference_answer":"guarantee","incorrect_answer":"guarantees","explanation":"После does not требуется guarantee."},{"id":"c92f34ef-731b-54a5-bcef-d329e5fae220","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Соответствие условиям допуска необходимо, но само по себе недостаточно для отбора.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"necessary"},{"id":"t4","label":"but"},{"id":"t5","label":"not"},{"id":"t6","label":"sufficient"},{"id":"t7","label":"for"},{"id":"t8","label":"selection."},{"id":"t1","label":"Eligibility"},{"id":"t2","label":"is"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Допуск и положительный итоговый выбор — разные этапы."},{"id":"12ae0415-2c25-5bee-80bf-f3da848fe339","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The requirement is necessary, but it does not guarantees selection."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The requirement is necessary, but it does not guarantee selection."]},"reference_answer":"The requirement is necessary, but it does not guarantee selection.","incorrect_answer":"The requirement is necessary, but it does not guarantees selection.","explanation":"После does not основной глагол guarantee не получает -s."},{"id":"c34cb930-1ae6-5646-9a01-d9ab5e493767","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что обеспечивал балл выше порога?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The fellowship rules required applicants to score at least eighty in an initial assessment before their proposals could be considered. Places were limited, and the final panel also evaluated the proposals against published criteria. One applicant scored eighty-two and announced that selection was therefore guaranteed. The administrator explained that the threshold established eligibility for the next stage, not a sufficient condition for receiving a place. An applicant below the threshold would not pass that stage under the stated rules, but exceeding it did not remove competition or the proposal review. A precise summary had to preserve both directions: the threshold mattered, and the threshold alone did not settle the outcome. Neither “irrelevant” nor “automatic acceptance” represented the rule accurately.","options":[{"id":"v212e0a0dbe06","label":"Automatic selection regardless of the proposal."},{"id":"v009ba6ae86ba","label":"Exemption from every published criterion."},{"id":"v505714f7c6c5","label":"Eligibility for the next stage, not a guaranteed place."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v505714f7c6c5"},"reference_answer":"v505714f7c6c5","incorrect_answer":"v212e0a0dbe06","explanation":"Порог был условием допуска к рассмотрению."},{"id":"f8054ee7-02d2-5dd8-af14-9136e71b7f14","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lcd39fcaf9afc","label":"necessary"},{"id":"le9cdf75afce0","label":"sufficient"},{"id":"l3eb9d365191e","label":"eligibility"},{"id":"ld482b7e72b15","label":"selection"}],"right":[{"id":"r8f269a3224f8","label":"соответствие условиям допуска"},{"id":"r9fe4f82ca12b","label":"отбор"},{"id":"re020f06d27f7","label":"необходимый"},{"id":"r1957be82dd77","label":"достаточный"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lcd39fcaf9afc":"re020f06d27f7","le9cdf75afce0":"r1957be82dd77","l3eb9d365191e":"r8f269a3224f8","ld482b7e72b15":"r9fe4f82ca12b"}},"reference_answer":{"lcd39fcaf9afc":"re020f06d27f7","le9cdf75afce0":"r1957be82dd77","l3eb9d365191e":"r8f269a3224f8","ld482b7e72b15":"r9fe4f82ca12b"},"incorrect_answer":{"lcd39fcaf9afc":"r1957be82dd77","le9cdf75afce0":"re020f06d27f7","l3eb9d365191e":"r8f269a3224f8","ld482b7e72b15":"r9fe4f82ca12b"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: necessary — необходимый; sufficient — достаточный; eligibility — соответствие условиям допуска; selection — отбор."},{"id":"f5200c16-ed76-51e5-8668-1b1f83aba2dc","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему считать порог неважным тоже неверно?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The fellowship rules required applicants to score at least eighty in an initial assessment before their proposals could be considered. Places were limited, and the final panel also evaluated the proposals against published criteria. One applicant scored eighty-two and announced that selection was therefore guaranteed. The administrator explained that the threshold established eligibility for the next stage, not a sufficient condition for receiving a place. An applicant below the threshold would not pass that stage under the stated rules, but exceeding it did not remove competition or the proposal review. A precise summary had to preserve both directions: the threshold mattered, and the threshold alone did not settle the outcome. Neither “irrelevant” nor “automatic acceptance” represented the rule accurately.","options":[{"id":"v15e2bed727d5","label":"Necessary and irrelevant mean the same thing."},{"id":"v60c778908a44","label":"Applicants below it would not pass that stage under the stated rules."},{"id":"vb3aa513b05ad","label":"Every below-threshold applicant was guaranteed a place."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v60c778908a44"},"reference_answer":"v60c778908a44","incorrect_answer":"vb3aa513b05ad","explanation":"Необходимость порога сохраняется, хотя его недостаточно для итогового отбора."},{"id":"c3c47f22-107b-5940-8ed5-84b6a3ea4ef4","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Различи два логических свойства условия.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How can a condition be necessary without being sufficient?"}],"options":[{"id":"ve4449a69f9c2","label":"It need not be met and always guarantees the result."},{"id":"v35ab8957a4b1","label":"It has no possible relation to the result."},{"id":"v3f28a4a34236","label":"It must be met, but further conditions may also be required."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3f28a4a34236"},"reference_answer":"v3f28a4a34236","incorrect_answer":"ve4449a69f9c2","explanation":"Обязательность одного условия не исключает дополнительных условий."},{"id":"a4d651b1-24c7-5b98-859a-3bfa4b8da273","lesson_id":"d5d90495-3679-5e7a-850a-3eb99ff2a813","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Being allowed to enter a selection stage is ___.","options":[{"id":"vbd20d80ddf80","label":"unconditional success"},{"id":"va6989eaecf01","label":"eligibility"},{"id":"ve01d8df464f8","label":"selection itself necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va6989eaecf01"},"reference_answer":"va6989eaecf01","incorrect_answer":"ve01d8df464f8","explanation":"Eligibility — соответствие условиям допуска, не сам итоговый отбор."},{"id":"60566bf6-8b11-5bbb-b814-1cb37c2b5f03","lesson_id":"e362a84b-efd5-5ceb-bbc3-9e37af48ebc4","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: ___ do you visit the library? — Twice a week.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v7c69dd35602e","label":"How often"},{"id":"v255a66cba55f","label":"Where"},{"id":"v87fd1095ca44","label":"Who"}]},"answer_k