ространство к дождю."},{"id":"19bf4a0b-927e-5777-9650-fb6a2be7ca4c","lesson_id":"d31aa95d-e980-5e5b-9e6e-697e571281cf","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l1c5a73faed7d","label":"despite"},{"id":"l3be46318c9f5","label":"obstacle"},{"id":"l0eb0869bb85b","label":"attendance"},{"id":"lc8f7660585e0","label":"shelter"}],"right":[{"id":"r70e686abbbf9","label":"посещаемость"},{"id":"r4334036d641f","label":"укрытие"},{"id":"rd115436fe92f","label":"несмотря на"},{"id":"rc45dce64433e","label":"препятствие"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l1c5a73faed7d":"rd115436fe92f","l3be46318c9f5":"rc45dce64433e","l0eb0869bb85b":"r70e686abbbf9","lc8f7660585e0":"r4334036d641f"}},"reference_answer":{"l1c5a73faed7d":"rd115436fe92f","l3be46318c9f5":"rc45dce64433e","l0eb0869bb85b":"r70e686abbbf9","lc8f7660585e0":"r4334036d641f"},"incorrect_answer":{"l1c5a73faed7d":"rc45dce64433e","l3be46318c9f5":"rd115436fe92f","l0eb0869bb85b":"r70e686abbbf9","lc8f7660585e0":"r4334036d641f"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: despite — несмотря на; obstacle — препятствие; attendance — посещаемость; shelter — укрытие."},{"id":"a935bfee-8b92-5eb0-86ae-fcd191df02a9","lesson_id":"d31aa95d-e980-5e5b-9e6e-697e571281cf","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что отчёт НЕ утверждал?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"Despite the rain, most visitors stayed for the outdoor exhibition. Volunteers moved the smaller displays under a shelter and offered dry seats. The report praised their response, but did not claim that the weather helped attendance. Rain remained a difficulty that the organisers worked around. Next year, they plan to prepare the covered area before opening.","options":[{"id":"v79c92d406581","label":"That rain helped attendance."},{"id":"v5dcdcba896fd","label":"That rain occurred."},{"id":"vd4a1e5740874","label":"That volunteers responded."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v79c92d406581"},"reference_answer":"v79c92d406581","incorrect_answer":"v5dcdcba896fd","explanation":"Текст прямо отделяет успешную реакцию от пользы дождя."},{"id":"0ae61176-3279-5b79-944f-934d11867f06","lesson_id":"d31aa95d-e980-5e5b-9e6e-697e571281cf","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани уступку.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Did “despite the rain” mean there was no rain?"}],"options":[{"id":"vd4b04eb857c9","label":"Yes, despite means absence."},{"id":"ved8a8b4eb675","label":"Yes, it proves a dry day."},{"id":"vdc799e8f4750","label":"No, the event continued although rain was a difficulty."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vdc799e8f4750"},"reference_answer":"vdc799e8f4750","incorrect_answer":"vd4b04eb857c9","explanation":"Despite не отрицает препятствие."},{"id":"5a49515a-875c-5a84-8547-cd775c8d8033","lesson_id":"d31aa95d-e980-5e5b-9e6e-697e571281cf","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A covered place protecting people from rain is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v76bc0b41bb27","label":"delay"},{"id":"vfec340201f2c","label":"shelter"},{"id":"v675c1984190b","label":"forecast only"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vfec340201f2c"},"reference_answer":"vfec340201f2c","incorrect_answer":"v675c1984190b","explanation":"Shelter — укрытие."},{"id":"31e2d5f0-eb12-5058-aebf-6334fced4b77","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Please return the form ___ Monday; Friday is also acceptable.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v3fde406c550e","label":"by"},{"id":"v48ff0cd277d9","label":"until for"},{"id":"v3e6c03eda64f","label":"during to"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3fde406c550e"},"reference_answer":"v3fde406c550e","incorrect_answer":"v48ff0cd277d9","explanation":"By задаёт крайний срок и допускает более ранний возврат."},{"id":"4a20eeb6-8c73-51be-b551-82d3b1cb507b","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: by of / until.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"You can keep the key ___ Friday."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["until"]},"reference_answer":"until","incorrect_answer":"by of","explanation":"Until обозначает предел продолжающегося состояния."},{"id":"89766c14-ac1c-5327-9cae-3bde9bdcd0e6","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Верните ключ не позднее пятницы.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"key"},{"id":"t4","label":"by"},{"id":"t5","label":"Friday."},{"id":"t1","label":"Return"},{"id":"t2","label":"the"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t1"],"explanation":"By допускает возврат раньше пятницы."},{"id":"230556e0-a8fd-516e-a61a-f2912a1fee78","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"You can keep the book until to Friday."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["You can keep the book until Friday."]},"reference_answer":"You can keep the book until Friday.","incorrect_answer":"You can keep the book until to Friday.","explanation":"После until перед днём недели не нужен to."},{"id":"0dbe62dd-a3b7-5c3e-a467-2ab42a3cf1f1","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему возврат в среду допустим?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The library lets Ella keep a reference book until Friday, but asks her to return it by closing time that day. She finishes her work on Wednesday and brings it back then. The librarian accepts it. The permission covered the remaining days; it did not require her to retain the book for the full period or wait until Friday to return it.","options":[{"id":"v5aeb937fe3d0","label":"Friday was already over."},{"id":"v05023086a868","label":"The book had no return date."},{"id":"v01fe15b81129","label":"The deadline allowed an earlier return."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v01fe15b81129"},"reference_answer":"v01fe15b81129","incorrect_answer":"v5aeb937fe3d0","explanation":"Крайний срок не требует ждать последнего дня."},{"id":"22e7ff41-c567-55c1-8d89-b2336fd4b5e2","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l546ecbd73837","label":"deadline"},{"id":"l22abaef7aa95","label":"retain"},{"id":"l88c6a54e0b1b","label":"extension"},{"id":"l4b7a9e2cc291","label":"due"}],"right":[{"id":"rcff6a43a0903","label":"продление"},{"id":"r453f235eeb73","label":"подлежащий возврату"},{"id":"r566c74462cd4","label":"крайний срок"},{"id":"rc4666fdb0b1d","label":"сохранять у себя"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l546ecbd73837":"r566c74462cd4","l22abaef7aa95":"rc4666fdb0b1d","l88c6a54e0b1b":"rcff6a43a0903","l4b7a9e2cc291":"r453f235eeb73"}},"reference_answer":{"l546ecbd73837":"r566c74462cd4","l22abaef7aa95":"rc4666fdb0b1d","l88c6a54e0b1b":"rcff6a43a0903","l4b7a9e2cc291":"r453f235eeb73"},"incorrect_answer":{"l546ecbd73837":"rc4666fdb0b1d","l22abaef7aa95":"r566c74462cd4","l88c6a54e0b1b":"rcff6a43a0903","l4b7a9e2cc291":"r453f235eeb73"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: deadline — крайний срок; retain — сохранять у себя; extension — продление; due — подлежащий возврату."},{"id":"59fb5203-d40f-5cf1-89e7-bd7ce854ee21","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что разрешало keep until Friday?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The library lets Ella keep a reference book until Friday, but asks her to return it by closing time that day. She finishes her work on Wednesday and brings it back then. The librarian accepts it. The permission covered the remaining days; it did not require her to retain the book for the full period or wait until Friday to return it.","options":[{"id":"v9505c470188a","label":"Keeping the book for the remaining period."},{"id":"v12a6ce3cf32d","label":"Keeping it forever."},{"id":"va053ce5d230b","label":"Returning it only after Friday."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9505c470188a"},"reference_answer":"v9505c470188a","incorrect_answer":"v12a6ce3cf32d","explanation":"Разрешённый период имел определённую границу."},{"id":"3e645cc6-fbb8-5aad-9fe6-945011d2f6a9","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Различи крайний срок и обязательное ожидание.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Must I wait until the deadline to submit?"}],"options":[{"id":"vcfcae45878e8","label":"Yes, by always prohibits early submission."},{"id":"vf82ed3412799","label":"Yes, a deadline means no date exists."},{"id":"v40d80f456c46","label":"No, submitting earlier is allowed."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v40d80f456c46"},"reference_answer":"v40d80f456c46","incorrect_answer":"vcfcae45878e8","explanation":"By ограничивает поздний срок."},{"id":"2e3309dc-f38a-5fd9-9d4d-8b04f509dc0c","lesson_id":"c6b52971-7d89-56d6-9384-cba54bcc17d9","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Extra time formally allowed is an ___.","options":[{"id":"v5b418454e00a","label":"absence"},{"id":"v895657fe33d8","label":"extension"},{"id":"v75696f0bfcac","label":"early return"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v895657fe33d8"},"reference_answer":"v895657fe33d8","incorrect_answer":"v75696f0bfcac","explanation":"Extension — продление."},{"id":"32995950-cce3-5d18-bfd1-ee6e6d913c9a","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The evening route has been discontinued. It is ___ available.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v5ca03857abce","label":"no longer"},{"id":"v29091ff7f598","label":"not no longer"},{"id":"vf9843557b323","label":"longer no"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v5ca03857abce"},"reference_answer":"v5ca03857abce","incorrect_answer":"v29091ff7f598","explanation":"No longer сообщает о прекращении прежнего состояния."},{"id":"d1da74df-95e2-5341-ab58-8617032aa97b","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: longer / longest.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"This entrance is no ___ in use."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["longer"]},"reference_answer":"longer","incorrect_answer":"longest","explanation":"Устойчивая форма — no longer."},{"id":"b0a07542-581d-5a0f-8288-982e03a4d2d7","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Вечерняя услуга больше не доступна.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"service"},{"id":"t4","label":"is"},{"id":"t5","label":"no"},{"id":"t6","label":"longer"},{"id":"t7","label":"available."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"evening"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t1"],"explanation":"Фраза связывает нынешнее отсутствие с изменением прежнего положения."},{"id":"3d373393-bc2b-5692-b602-ead960cee73f","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The entrance is not no longer in use."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The entrance is no longer in use."]},"reference_answer":"The entrance is no longer in use.","incorrect_answer":"The entrance is not no longer in use.","explanation":"Убираем второе отрицание, сохраняя смысл прекращения использования."},{"id":"42fe6127-944b-5298-8ea9-cb36e6b9bc7f","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что произошло с вечерним маршрутом?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The information page said that the evening bus service was no longer available. Several visitors read the notice as meaning there had never been an evening route. The transport office clarified that it had operated until the previous month, when the timetable changed. A replacement daytime service remained available, but did not serve everyone who had relied on evening travel. The corrected summary preserved both the historical service and the current limitation instead of erasing either.","options":[{"id":"v6ece066996dd","label":"It had never existed."},{"id":"va73b715b6c29","label":"It now ran every evening."},{"id":"v1638e0c674a7","label":"It operated before but had recently stopped."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1638e0c674a7"},"reference_answer":"v1638e0c674a7","incorrect_answer":"v6ece066996dd","explanation":"No longer сохраняет противопоставление прошлой и нынешней ситуации."},{"id":"40f0569e-5d7b-526e-a837-9c7f18917bed","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l826df6e47efe","label":"discontinue"},{"id":"l3b00c3f98b0a","label":"replacement"},{"id":"l8f1627f5ccf3","label":"previously"},{"id":"lb9b1db32173a","label":"availability"}],"right":[{"id":"rbb3f61799ef6","label":"ранее"},{"id":"r218f712afe81","label":"доступность"},{"id":"r5ac55c64b65d","label":"прекращать"},{"id":"r25b5c7aec561","label":"замена"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l826df6e47efe":"r5ac55c64b65d","l3b00c3f98b0a":"r25b5c7aec561","l8f1627f5ccf3":"rbb3f61799ef6","lb9b1db32173a":"r218f712afe81"}},"reference_answer":{"l826df6e47efe":"r5ac55c64b65d","l3b00c3f98b0a":"r25b5c7aec561","l8f1627f5ccf3":"rbb3f61799ef6","lb9b1db32173a":"r218f712afe81"},"incorrect_answer":{"l826df6e47efe":"r25b5c7aec561","l3b00c3f98b0a":"r5ac55c64b65d","l8f1627f5ccf3":"rbb3f61799ef6","lb9b1db32173a":"r218f712afe81"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: discontinue — прекращать; replacement — замена; previously — ранее; availability — доступность."},{"id":"a71c8994-f9c3-581a-b589-4155379fa3e5","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему дневная замена не решала все проблемы?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The information page said that the evening bus service was no longer available. Several visitors read the notice as meaning there had never been an evening route. The transport office clarified that it had operated until the previous month, when the timetable changed. A replacement daytime service remained available, but did not serve everyone who had relied on evening travel. The corrected summary preserved both the historical service and the current limitation instead of erasing either.","options":[{"id":"v1fc1a0cb6759","label":"Some users needed evening travel."},{"id":"v5d8291a575f9","label":"It had no passengers in history."},{"id":"vf93e492a022a","label":"It proved the evening route still ran."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1fc1a0cb6759"},"reference_answer":"v1fc1a0cb6759","incorrect_answer":"v5d8291a575f9","explanation":"Другой период обслуживания подходит не всем прежним пассажирам."},{"id":"5ddd4f82-37c0-51b8-a7bc-298489d44e52","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Уточни временной смысл.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “no longer” erase the earlier service?"}],"options":[{"id":"v60eccd3c3fcf","label":"Yes, it means never existed."},{"id":"vfaa9a3bbe429","label":"Yes, it proves permanent future closure."},{"id":"v9673f3b7cfd1","label":"No, it marks a change from the previous situation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9673f3b7cfd1"},"reference_answer":"v9673f3b7cfd1","incorrect_answer":"v60eccd3c3fcf","explanation":"Текущее прекращение не стирает прошлое."},{"id":"1e596ef4-2191-5c54-8388-50946b968301","lesson_id":"7ee9b5c8-7bc6-5537-bdb7-945a9de2f858","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"To stop providing a service is to ___ it.","options":[{"id":"vcacb1a2e6201","label":"extend automatically"},{"id":"vf0e17b740f3d","label":"discontinue"},{"id":"va20ca05a9603","label":"guarantee"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf0e17b740f3d"},"reference_answer":"vf0e17b740f3d","incorrect_answer":"va20ca05a9603","explanation":"Discontinue — прекратить предоставление."},{"id":"0633d888-b42c-5fb7-9372-d2863181be11","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: We regret ___ you that the visit is cancelled.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v8a4a57a201be","label":"to inform"},{"id":"v05a0b2c956e3","label":"inform to"},{"id":"vc7290bf1c3e2","label":"to informing"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8a4a57a201be"},"reference_answer":"v8a4a57a201be","incorrect_answer":"v05a0b2c956e3","explanation":"Regret to inform — формула неприятного уведомления."},{"id":"5c0536b2-81e2-5f75-9917-ace5e9b4be68","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: to shared / sharing.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"I regret ___ the unfinished draft yesterday."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["sharing"]},"reference_answer":"sharing","incorrect_answer":"to shared","explanation":"О прошлом действии после regret здесь нужна форма sharing."},{"id":"d1f81c21-738d-5177-961d-4b28d7660462","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «С сожалением сообщаем, что визит отменён.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"to"},{"id":"t4","label":"inform"},{"id":"t5","label":"you"},{"id":"t6","label":"that"},{"id":"t7","label":"the"},{"id":"t8","label":"visit"},{"id":"t9","label":"is"},{"id":"t10","label":"cancelled."},{"id":"t1","label":"We"},{"id":"t2","label":"regret"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t1"],"explanation":"Это формальное уведомление о неприятной новости."},{"id":"f1c96b31-8d4c-5f51-bbf4-d931348eaf45","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"We regret to informing you of the change."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["We regret to inform you of the change."]},"reference_answer":"We regret to inform you of the change.","incorrect_answer":"We regret to informing you of the change.","explanation":"После to в этой формуле нужен inform."},{"id":"50405d04-6021-542e-be2d-94d32015032d","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что вводило письмо музея?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The museum wrote that it regretted to inform visitors of a cancelled tour. One reader assumed the message meant the museum regretted having sent an earlier announcement. The organiser clarified the difference. This was a formal introduction to disappointing news, not a statement about an earlier disclosure. In a separate note, a guide said she regretted sharing an unfinished timetable the previous day. That sentence did refer to a past action. The two expressions needed different summaries.","options":[{"id":"v78e4b920de58","label":"A confession about sending an earlier announcement."},{"id":"v61f13b75a8a7","label":"A guarantee of an extra tour."},{"id":"v2e7ff33d9dfa","label":"Disappointing news about a cancelled tour."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2e7ff33d9dfa"},"reference_answer":"v2e7ff33d9dfa","incorrect_answer":"v78e4b920de58","explanation":"Regret to inform вводит текущее неприятное сообщение."},{"id":"14255655-acb5-5c39-ab5d-2c45716f8721","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lde464fa6ea4e","label":"regret"},{"id":"ld90cdcbc1d55","label":"notification"},{"id":"l87cfdd85a75f","label":"disclosure"},{"id":"ld9eb86c4fd83","label":"replacement"}],"right":[{"id":"r01b24b9da555","label":"разглашение"},{"id":"r45e81116d604","label":"замена"},{"id":"r35737c97cad5","label":"сожаление"},{"id":"r26f37a4b290e","label":"уведомление"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lde464fa6ea4e":"r35737c97cad5","ld90cdcbc1d55":"r26f37a4b290e","l87cfdd85a75f":"r01b24b9da555","ld9eb86c4fd83":"r45e81116d604"}},"reference_answer":{"lde464fa6ea4e":"r35737c97cad5","ld90cdcbc1d55":"r26f37a4b290e","l87cfdd85a75f":"r01b24b9da555","ld9eb86c4fd83":"r45e81116d604"},"incorrect_answer":{"lde464fa6ea4e":"r26f37a4b290e","ld90cdcbc1d55":"r35737c97cad5","l87cfdd85a75f":"r01b24b9da555","ld9eb86c4fd83":"r45e81116d604"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: regret — сожаление; notification — уведомление; disclosure — разглашение; replacement — замена."},{"id":"9157131d-51f9-53fe-a1b7-7a4f5aafc6de","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какое действие из прошлого упомянула гид?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The museum wrote that it regretted to inform visitors of a cancelled tour. One reader assumed the message meant the museum regretted having sent an earlier announcement. The organiser clarified the difference. This was a formal introduction to disappointing news, not a statement about an earlier disclosure. In a separate note, a guide said she regretted sharing an unfinished timetable the previous day. That sentence did refer to a past action. The two expressions needed different summaries.","options":[{"id":"v14a8e25beab0","label":"Sharing an unfinished timetable."},{"id":"v17a1719749b8","label":"Completing every tour."},{"id":"vb7661be719d5","label":"Withdrawing all messages before sending them."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v14a8e25beab0"},"reference_answer":"v14a8e25beab0","incorrect_answer":"v17a1719749b8","explanation":"В отдельной заметке regret sharing относится к уже выполненной передаче."},{"id":"c2f57abd-f301-518c-9eb7-11f49a364dfe","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Используй форму формального сообщения.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"How do you introduce disappointing news formally?"}],"options":[{"id":"vdca971c86f9f","label":"We regret to informing you."},{"id":"vfbb56e7fbe0a","label":"We regret informed to you."},{"id":"va5d037253c82","label":"We regret to inform you of the cancellation."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va5d037253c82"},"reference_answer":"va5d037253c82","incorrect_answer":"vdca971c86f9f","explanation":"Нужен инфинитив to inform."},{"id":"bc1fbf69-ec59-50b6-83dd-765a588b828f","lesson_id":"f476077e-521b-5bbb-a2b2-6381e5af2ee3","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Giving information to others can be a ___.","options":[{"id":"vefa0326b5162","label":"silence necessarily"},{"id":"v640510f1e27d","label":"disclosure"},{"id":"v776d4f395919","label":"replacement object"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v640510f1e27d"},"reference_answer":"v640510f1e27d","incorrect_answer":"v776d4f395919","explanation":"Disclosure — раскрытие или разглашение информации."},{"id":"ab6f3f76-fcea-558b-af46-8b83d623f88d","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: The editor added a note lest readers ___ mistake the example for a rule.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vbe622b67c026","label":"should"},{"id":"vd9b4ad567ada","label":"to should"},{"id":"v918c7fe0abbf","label":"should to"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbe622b67c026"},"reference_answer":"vbe622b67c026","incorrect_answer":"vd9b4ad567ada","explanation":"В целевой формальной модели lest следует should с начальной формой."},{"id":"8c3d4b68-3898-5c3f-bffa-deee5ab21269","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: misread / misreading.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A note was added lest readers should ___ the example."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["misread"]},"reference_answer":"misread","incorrect_answer":"misreading","explanation":"После should нужна начальная форма misread."},{"id":"f6552908-682f-5a67-8536-3d34071cc5c5","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Редактор добавил примечание, чтобы читатели не поняли неправильно.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"added"},{"id":"t4","label":"a"},{"id":"t5","label":"note"},{"id":"t6","label":"lest"},{"id":"t7","label":"readers"},{"id":"t8","label":"should"},{"id":"t9","label":"misunderstand."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"editor"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Lest вводит предотвращаемый результат."},{"id":"a8e40b68-4cb0-5784-8a2f-f8be86fefce4","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"She added a note lest readers should to misunderstand."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["She added a note lest readers should misunderstand."]},"reference_answer":"She added a note lest readers should misunderstand.","incorrect_answer":"She added a note lest readers should to misunderstand.","explanation":"После should убирается to."},{"id":"99ab9e69-9c69-5664-9a22-8d17ac4db8c0","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какую ошибку хотели предотвратить?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The editor retained a short annotation lest readers should mistake a fictional case for a documented event. A colleague suggested removing the note because the example already sounded plausible. That plausibility was precisely why the annotation mattered. The editor was taking a precaution against misunderstanding; she was not reporting that every reader had already made the mistake. Nor was she trying to prevent readers from understanding the example. The final version kept both the example and its status clearly visible. This preserved the educational purpose while giving readers the information they needed to interpret the case accurately.","options":[{"id":"v4d0ad67fc871","label":"Recognising that the example was fictional."},{"id":"vfaeb7bef60a3","label":"Reading the annotation carefully."},{"id":"v13de9c8c423b","label":"Taking a fictional case for a documented event."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v13de9c8c423b"},"reference_answer":"v13de9c8c423b","incorrect_answer":"v4d0ad67fc871","explanation":"Примечание уточняло вымышленный статус примера."},{"id":"616d31b2-1cdc-5591-b445-94bb38a6998e","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lbffa54820196","label":"lest"},{"id":"l911f89c2fbe9","label":"precaution"},{"id":"ld485b28ad43e","label":"misread"},{"id":"l68f643b81c91","label":"annotation"}],"right":[{"id":"r3315f2f9e7ea","label":"неверно прочесть"},{"id":"r04896d7f6e30","label":"примечание"},{"id":"r4d3a1141fabf","label":"чтобы не"},{"id":"r044cf8ab94ed","label":"мера предосторожности"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lbffa54820196":"r4d3a1141fabf","l911f89c2fbe9":"r044cf8ab94ed","ld485b28ad43e":"r3315f2f9e7ea","l68f643b81c91":"r04896d7f6e30"}},"reference_answer":{"lbffa54820196":"r4d3a1141fabf","l911f89c2fbe9":"r044cf8ab94ed","ld485b28ad43e":"r3315f2f9e7ea","l68f643b81c91":"r04896d7f6e30"},"incorrect_answer":{"lbffa54820196":"r044cf8ab94ed","l911f89c2fbe9":"r4d3a1141fabf","ld485b28ad43e":"r3315f2f9e7ea","l68f643b81c91":"r04896d7f6e30"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: lest — чтобы не; precaution — мера предосторожности; misread — неверно прочесть; annotation — примечание."},{"id":"92b615e7-bcab-590a-8072-0fdd804a60cd","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"reading","prompt":"Доказывает ли предосторожность уже совершённую всеми ошибку?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The editor retained a short annotation lest readers should mistake a fictional case for a documented event. A colleague suggested removing the note because the example already sounded plausible. That plausibility was precisely why the annotation mattered. The editor was taking a precaution against misunderstanding; she was not reporting that every reader had already made the mistake. Nor was she trying to prevent readers from understanding the example. The final version kept both the example and its status clearly visible. This preserved the educational purpose while giving readers the information they needed to interpret the case accurately.","options":[{"id":"vc3961fcacab2","label":"No; it identifies a misunderstanding to prevent."},{"id":"v7337b2a0c3ee","label":"Yes; every reader had been tested."},{"id":"vc35cb153530e","label":"Yes; the editor recorded unanimous confusion."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc3961fcacab2"},"reference_answer":"vc3961fcacab2","incorrect_answer":"v7337b2a0c3ee","explanation":"Цель профилактическая, не отчёт о проверенных реакциях всех."},{"id":"35ceacd6-7710-544e-9a38-9881e6086918","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Используй lest с указанной формой should.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Why keep the label on a plausible fictional example?"}],"options":[{"id":"v72a9af09ed63","label":"Lest readers should to understand it."},{"id":"v3b5052ab9c9a","label":"Because plausibility proves historical truth."},{"id":"v598fa4c9538c","label":"Lest readers should treat it as a verified event."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v598fa4c9538c"},"reference_answer":"v598fa4c9538c","incorrect_answer":"v72a9af09ed63","explanation":"Фраза сохраняет предотвращаемое неверное прочтение."},{"id":"f547ace6-cf24-5f4f-8b91-022db92d3390","lesson_id":"7b40ae52-8555-51ac-b8c8-efb32c34e3de","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An action taken to avoid a possible problem is a ___.","options":[{"id":"ved7cc4100813","label":"guarantee of confusion"},{"id":"vbf5f6ae60dae","label":"precaution"},{"id":"va1e4ac7572bb","label":"proof of a past error"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbf5f6ae60dae"},"reference_answer":"vbf5f6ae60dae","incorrect_answer":"va1e4ac7572bb","explanation":"Precaution — предосторожность."},{"id":"3463553b-ed46-526f-a780-039065da2a0f","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: In the explicit “to the extent that” sense, inasmuch as limits the ___ of a claim.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v3bdf77c66e3c","label":"scope"},{"id":"v512f8c95025a","label":"alphabet"},{"id":"vffe132c7c115","label":"speaker’s name"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3bdf77c66e3c"},"reference_answer":"v3bdf77c66e3c","incorrect_answer":"v512f8c95025a","explanation":"В заданном значении конструкция ограничивает область утверждения."},{"id":"06a1968c-7fcc-509e-86a6-ff825321c48e","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: than / that.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The review is useful to the extent ___ it covers our needs."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["that"]},"reference_answer":"that","incorrect_answer":"than","explanation":"Устойчивая форма — to the extent that."},{"id":"8bbaad58-9713-5750-80b8-993afb278436","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Отчёт полезен в той мере, в какой отвечает на наш вопрос.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"is"},{"id":"t4","label":"useful"},{"id":"t5","label":"inasmuch"},{"id":"t6","label":"as"},{"id":"t7","label":"it"},{"id":"t8","label":"addresses"},{"id":"t9","label":"our"},{"id":"t10","label":"question."},{"id":"t1","label":"The"},{"id":"t2","label":"report"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t10","t1"],"explanation":"Здесь оценка прямо ограничена поставленным вопросом."},{"id":"52c0589d-7e0f-5e89-881e-2fdedaa525da","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The report is useful to the extent than it addresses the question."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The report is useful to the extent that it addresses the question."]},"reference_answer":"The report is useful to the extent that it addresses the question.","incorrect_answer":"The report is useful to the extent than it addresses the question.","explanation":"В этой конструкции требуется that."},{"id":"da98fa3c-3578-5c73-8514-702d48c46e38","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"reading","prompt":"Как контекст определял inasmuch as?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The panel described a report as useful inasmuch as it addressed the narrow question under review. The surrounding paragraph explicitly defined the phrase as meaning to the extent that, then listed several wider questions the report did not consider. A summary removed the qualification and called it a comprehensive assessment. The panel objected: usefulness for a specified purpose did not establish comprehensive coverage. Its correction did not deny that the report helped with the original question. It restored the limited basis of that positive judgement and kept the unexamined questions visible for future work rather than treating them as already settled.","options":[{"id":"v650519af5249","label":"As a claim of complete coverage."},{"id":"vcf4b792d0d77","label":"As a denial of any usefulness."},{"id":"vf78aebea522e","label":"As to the extent that."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf78aebea522e"},"reference_answer":"vf78aebea522e","incorrect_answer":"v650519af5249","explanation":"Значение явно задано окружающим абзацем."},{"id":"10da9910-bd1c-54eb-999d-1242523db36e","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"le4bd9b036809","label":"extent"},{"id":"l9557fdacd557","label":"coverage"},{"id":"l557d390be0c6","label":"qualification"},{"id":"lb50485d0074e","label":"criterion"}],"right":[{"id":"rb1938cc62a07","label":"оговорка"},{"id":"r5a87f3f5d1fb","label":"критерий"},{"id":"rae893df0affe","label":"степень"},{"id":"r4f131c713309","label":"охват"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"le4bd9b036809":"rae893df0affe","l9557fdacd557":"r4f131c713309","l557d390be0c6":"rb1938cc62a07","lb50485d0074e":"r5a87f3f5d1fb"}},"reference_answer":{"le4bd9b036809":"rae893df0affe","l9557fdacd557":"r4f131c713309","l557d390be0c6":"rb1938cc62a07","lb50485d0074e":"r5a87f3f5d1fb"},"incorrect_answer":{"le4bd9b036809":"r4f131c713309","l9557fdacd557":"rae893df0affe","l557d390be0c6":"rb1938cc62a07","lb50485d0074e":"r5a87f3f5d1fb"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: extent — степень; coverage — охват; qualification — оговорка; criterion — критерий."},{"id":"52dbabd4-3762-5a5b-922a-3422f505e603","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что исказило слово comprehensive в резюме?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The panel described a report as useful inasmuch as it addressed the narrow question under review. The surrounding paragraph explicitly defined the phrase as meaning to the extent that, then listed several wider questions the report did not consider. A summary removed the qualification and called it a comprehensive assessment. The panel objected: usefulness for a specified purpose did not establish comprehensive coverage. Its correction did not deny that the report helped with the original question. It restored the limited basis of that positive judgement and kept the unexamined questions visible for future work rather than treating them as already settled.","options":[{"id":"va8cec13133a0","label":"It extended a limited judgement to broader coverage."},{"id":"v99749e02e110","label":"It preserved all the original limits."},{"id":"v20c439ae7c52","label":"It proved the narrow question was irrelevant."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"va8cec13133a0"},"reference_answer":"va8cec13133a0","incorrect_answer":"v99749e02e110","explanation":"Ограниченная полезность не устанавливает полноту охвата."},{"id":"ef6e8c67-e8ff-5411-93ac-25da8b441c34","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани область положительной оценки.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"May we call a narrowly useful report comprehensive?"}],"options":[{"id":"veaa39671ad8a","label":"Yes, usefulness always proves completeness."},{"id":"v4e8be825ebe1","label":"Yes, inasmuch as erases every limit."},{"id":"v9c76c1155545","label":"Only with separate support for that wider coverage."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v9c76c1155545"},"reference_answer":"v9c76c1155545","incorrect_answer":"veaa39671ad8a","explanation":"Для более широкого вывода нужны отдельные основания."},{"id":"33c13115-44c3-5582-a540-c1bbb44e87bc","lesson_id":"101201eb-023d-5865-8843-bad50678d301","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"How much of a subject a report includes is its ___.","options":[{"id":"v322e6dc31b38","label":"author’s identity"},{"id":"vf40626adb3f2","label":"coverage"},{"id":"v3099d1bf7e46","label":"certainty necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vf40626adb3f2"},"reference_answer":"vf40626adb3f2","incorrect_answer":"v3099d1bf7e46","explanation":"Coverage — охват темы."},{"id":"edf81365-4cb1-518f-98ba-5493ad1168d4","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “No access unless authorised; capacity limits also apply.” Does authorisation guarantee entry?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v041f1111798a","label":"No; the stated capacity limit still applies."},{"id":"v5f3c3e2f017a","label":"Yes; unless cancels every other condition."},{"id":"vcfc4586ce2ac","label":"Yes; authorisation means unlimited space."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v041f1111798a"},"reference_answer":"v041f1111798a","incorrect_answer":"v5f3c3e2f017a","explanation":"Нужно сохранить оба явно названных ограничения."},{"id":"0706300c-a83c-5134-b58e-6b603485597c","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: is / are.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Access is restricted unless authorisation ___ granted."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["is"]},"reference_answer":"is","incorrect_answer":"are","explanation":"С единственным authorisation используется is."},{"id":"521daac0-587f-59bc-9727-b7bfebfbb49a","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Разрешение не отменяет указанное ограничение вместимости.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"not"},{"id":"t4","label":"remove"},{"id":"t5","label":"the"},{"id":"t6","label":"stated"},{"id":"t7","label":"capacity"},{"id":"t8","label":"limit."},{"id":"t1","label":"Authorisation"},{"id":"t2","label":"does"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Исключение к одному запрету не отменяет другое условие."},{"id":"b35ca860-e049-5eaf-b50f-7b78d362eab4","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Authorisation do not remove the capacity limit."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["Authorisation does not remove the capacity limit."]},"reference_answer":"Authorisation does not remove the capacity limit.","incorrect_answer":"Authorisation do not remove the capacity limit.","explanation":"С единственным authorisation требуется does not."},{"id":"25d6d981-e729-560b-ba6e-c73a7e3fa361","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что разрешение меняло?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The archive notice stated that nobody could enter the storage room unless authorised by the curator. The next sentence added that capacity limits still applied to authorised visitors. One researcher obtained authorisation and assumed that entry at any chosen time was therefore guaranteed. The curator explained that the exception removed one barrier, not every possible restriction. When the room was full, authorised visitors still had to wait. This did not make authorisation irrelevant: without it, they could not enter under the stated rule even when space was available. A faithful account had to preserve both the exception and the continuing limit. Reading unless as a promise of unrestricted entry would add an entitlement that the complete notice had never offered.","options":[{"id":"v10f87007a5b9","label":"It guaranteed entry regardless of space."},{"id":"vf7cda6b36d61","label":"It made the notice irrelevant to everyone."},{"id":"v41e08bf1b75d","label":"It removed one barrier while capacity limits remained."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v41e08bf1b75d"},"reference_answer":"v41e08bf1b75d","incorrect_answer":"v10f87007a5b9","explanation":"Исключение касалось допуска, но не вместимости."},{"id":"9679f39a-0d86-555a-9df4-cd4b79e0ed29","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lc5de0f9af362","label":"exception"},{"id":"l9192ab4248ee","label":"authorisation"},{"id":"le7fe1ab9c383","label":"restriction"},{"id":"l394d4479d751","label":"entitlement"}],"right":[{"id":"r1dbffd1c4d5c","label":"ограничение"},{"id":"r9deea5a60a1b","label":"право на получение"},{"id":"r980790f8b110","label":"исключение"},{"id":"ra8c022e8905f","label":"разрешение"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lc5de0f9af362":"r980790f8b110","l9192ab4248ee":"ra8c022e8905f","le7fe1ab9c383":"r1dbffd1c4d5c","l394d4479d751":"r9deea5a60a1b"}},"reference_answer":{"lc5de0f9af362":"r980790f8b110","l9192ab4248ee":"ra8c022e8905f","le7fe1ab9c383":"r1dbffd1c4d5c","l394d4479d751":"r9deea5a60a1b"},"incorrect_answer":{"lc5de0f9af362":"ra8c022e8905f","l9192ab4248ee":"r980790f8b110","le7fe1ab9c383":"r1dbffd1c4d5c","l394d4479d751":"r9deea5a60a1b"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: exception — исключение; authorisation — разрешение; restriction — ограничение; entitlement — право на получение."},{"id":"fe27987b-95c3-5894-93e1-9f427bd5f434","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"reading","prompt":"Можно ли входить без разрешения при свободном месте?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The archive notice stated that nobody could enter the storage room unless authorised by the curator. The next sentence added that capacity limits still applied to authorised visitors. One researcher obtained authorisation and assumed that entry at any chosen time was therefore guaranteed. The curator explained that the exception removed one barrier, not every possible restriction. When the room was full, authorised visitors still had to wait. This did not make authorisation irrelevant: without it, they could not enter under the stated rule even when space was available. A faithful account had to preserve both the exception and the continuing limit. Reading unless as a promise of unrestricted entry would add an entitlement that the complete notice had never offered.","options":[{"id":"vbdad846d0393","label":"No, not under the stated rule."},{"id":"vdd0d864e6069","label":"Yes, capacity is the only rule."},{"id":"v110328bea4d3","label":"Yes, unless means authorisation is irrelevant."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vbdad846d0393"},"reference_answer":"vbdad846d0393","incorrect_answer":"vdd0d864e6069","explanation":"Свободное место не отменяет первое условие."},{"id":"a3982407-9a7e-59c3-9db2-5b042c2a6cb2","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Учти весь текст правила.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Why must an authorised visitor wait when the room is full?"}],"options":[{"id":"v9af1c1bba0d9","label":"Authorisation guarantees immediate entry."},{"id":"vfc55d2405b78","label":"Unless erases the next sentence."},{"id":"v64fc8e146509","label":"The notice explicitly retains capacity limits."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v64fc8e146509"},"reference_answer":"v64fc8e146509","incorrect_answer":"v9af1c1bba0d9","explanation":"Второе условие прямо сохранено."},{"id":"c6d12fda-e47b-57d9-bf2c-2151e30dad15","lesson_id":"31079700-aa01-56ca-a5da-c4951ba77844","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A departure allowed from a general restriction is an ___.","options":[{"id":"v2e5cc7ef845b","label":"unlimited guarantee"},{"id":"v8f8e9845f62e","label":"exception"},{"id":"v16dda2dcb546","label":"automatic entitlement to everything"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8f8e9845f62e"},"reference_answer":"v8f8e9845f62e","incorrect_answer":"v16dda2dcb546","explanation":"Exception — исключение к правилу."},{"id":"d12f596c-0b6c-55a9-9c34-be80082cc904","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “The mayor called it flawless; the reviewer disputed that.” Who endorsed flawless?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v321b0e73cc56","label":"The mayor."},{"id":"v370e73e37bc1","label":"The reviewer."},{"id":"v878f094686fd","label":"Both necessarily."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v321b0e73cc56"},"reference_answer":"v321b0e73cc56","incorrect_answer":"v370e73e37bc1","explanation":"Оценка приписана мэру, а рецензент спорит с ней."},{"id":"22b642f5-8561-525d-83b6-7b8d1bfbc8e0","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: at / to.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The phrase was attributed ___ the mayor."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["to"]},"reference_answer":"to","incorrect_answer":"at","explanation":"Модель указания источника — attributed to."},{"id":"660ac0d3-6c4a-5d14-b25f-a6729db02426","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Цитирование оценки не обязательно означает её одобрение.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"judgement"},{"id":"t4","label":"does"},{"id":"t5","label":"not"},{"id":"t6","label":"necessarily"},{"id":"t7","label":"endorse"},{"id":"t8","label":"it."},{"id":"t1","label":"Quoting"},{"id":"t2","label":"a"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Нужны источник и окружающий контекст."},{"id":"6c4b227e-ff92-5bb5-97e1-a5038f52eb50","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The judgement was attributed at the speaker."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The judgement was attributed to the speaker."]},"reference_answer":"The judgement was attributed to the speaker.","incorrect_answer":"The judgement was attributed at the speaker.","explanation":"При указании источника используется to."},{"id":"ddc1dea9-71b4-551b-b243-e0c60d94cbb7","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"reading","prompt":"Кому принадлежала исходная оценка flawless?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A review opened by quoting the organiser’s description of the exhibition as flawless. The following paragraphs questioned that description, pointing to unclear labels and a missing explanation of the central display. A promotional extract reproduced the word flawless beside the reviewer’s name, omitting the attribution and the objections. The reviewer requested its removal. Her article had accurately reported the organiser’s praise before examining it critically; it had not adopted that praise as its own conclusion. Correcting the extract required more than keeping quotation marks around one adjective. Readers needed to know whose judgement it was and how the review treated it. Without that context, an accurate fragment could convey a position opposite to the one developed in the complete article.","options":[{"id":"v03679a9a87e7","label":"The reviewer as her final conclusion."},{"id":"v4ad9d61faacf","label":"Every visitor unanimously."},{"id":"v1e9b3b66a0c4","label":"The organiser."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1e9b3b66a0c4"},"reference_answer":"v1e9b3b66a0c4","incorrect_answer":"v03679a9a87e7","explanation":"Статья приводила слова организатора перед критикой."},{"id":"72d5a77d-98ee-55f7-b787-e22f589a0289","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"laed5b5524d22","label":"quotation"},{"id":"l29af7f57b7ba","label":"endorsement"},{"id":"l39b3b39f0a0c","label":"attribution"},{"id":"l7f4a679ecf2c","label":"rebuttal"}],"right":[{"id":"ra1f4575fc88e","label":"указание авторства"},{"id":"rb9a358930645","label":"возражение"},{"id":"ra76cb0e0c1bd","label":"цитата"},{"id":"r1f10943cb3c8","label":"одобрение"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"laed5b5524d22":"ra76cb0e0c1bd","l29af7f57b7ba":"r1f10943cb3c8","l39b3b39f0a0c":"ra1f4575fc88e","l7f4a679ecf2c":"rb9a358930645"}},"reference_answer":{"laed5b5524d22":"ra76cb0e0c1bd","l29af7f57b7ba":"r1f10943cb3c8","l39b3b39f0a0c":"ra1f4575fc88e","l7f4a679ecf2c":"rb9a358930645"},"incorrect_answer":{"laed5b5524d22":"r1f10943cb3c8","l29af7f57b7ba":"ra76cb0e0c1bd","l39b3b39f0a0c":"ra1f4575fc88e","l7f4a679ecf2c":"rb9a358930645"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: quotation — цитата; endorsement — одобрение; attribution — указание авторства; rebuttal — возражение."},{"id":"1b782658-ec0c-5daa-9479-79eec5ac96f8","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему одних кавычек недостаточно?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A review opened by quoting the organiser’s description of the exhibition as flawless. The following paragraphs questioned that description, pointing to unclear labels and a missing explanation of the central display. A promotional extract reproduced the word flawless beside the reviewer’s name, omitting the attribution and the objections. The reviewer requested its removal. Her article had accurately reported the organiser’s praise before examining it critically; it had not adopted that praise as its own conclusion. Correcting the extract required more than keeping quotation marks around one adjective. Readers needed to know whose judgement it was and how the review treated it. Without that context, an accurate fragment could convey a position opposite to the one developed in the complete article.","options":[{"id":"vdf1c7bfbbe4d","label":"The source and the critical treatment are also needed."},{"id":"v35003627d076","label":"Quotation marks guarantee endorsement."},{"id":"v249de832f41f","label":"Every isolated adjective proves the full argument."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vdf1c7bfbbe4d"},"reference_answer":"vdf1c7bfbbe4d","incorrect_answer":"v35003627d076","explanation":"Фрагмент без источника и контекста может исказить позицию."},{"id":"d1c1e890-fe4e-5d97-ad18-90d5022e5910","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани источник и отношение автора.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can we put the quoted praise beside the reviewer’s name as her verdict?"}],"options":[{"id":"v1d64d1831eee","label":"Yes; quoting always means agreement."},{"id":"v50c4f279b825","label":"Yes; objections cancel attribution automatically."},{"id":"v34dfc3863a31","label":"No; her article attributed it to someone else and disputed it."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v34dfc3863a31"},"reference_answer":"v34dfc3863a31","incorrect_answer":"v1d64d1831eee","explanation":"Цитирование чужой оценки не передаёт её авторство рецензенту."},{"id":"2a1a057a-6e95-564d-a6ff-af29700faace","lesson_id":"1aaf1f8d-e861-5fe7-89fe-0109b0d24cc9","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Naming the source of a statement is ___.","options":[{"id":"vcc9b07bbc3b3","label":"silence"},{"id":"v7dec74cc82dc","label":"attribution"},{"id":"v0128eeb528bb","label":"endorsement necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7dec74cc82dc"},"reference_answer":"v7dec74cc82dc","incorrect_answer":"v0128eeb528bb","explanation":"Attribution — указание источника высказывания."},{"id":"232e39ea-ea4f-53fe-86e0-28609d8af356","lesson_id":"e63ff879-616a-5140-be10-a0d478a93592","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Both bags are blue. They are ___ colour.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"vd9a5f79e8f8a","label":"the same"},{"id":"v925c9290e8a5","label":"different of"},{"id":"v602e25837e24","label":"a two"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vd9a5f79e8f8a"},"reference_answer":"vd9a5f79e8f8a","incorrect_answer":"v925c9290e8a5","explanation":"Один и тот же цвет — the same colour."},{"id":"e506eb0c-5631-574d-952c-8dc998ea6ba7","lesson_id":"e63ff879-616a-5140-be10-a0d478a93592","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: different / s