:"В этих контекстах: spend — тратить; duration — длительность; task — задача; remaining — оставшийся."},{"id":"7cc1e4f8-72ac-5e2e-8002-56ba35d2cecc","lesson_id":"9cb798a6-690c-5e83-aff9-6076376e3289","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что журнал сохранял кроме времени?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The volunteers spent two hours checking the old catalogue. They corrected several entries, but a large section remained unchecked. In the activity log, the coordinator recorded both the time spent and the work still outstanding. A shorter summary claimed that the whole catalogue had been verified. The coordinator restored the distinction between time devoted to a task and its completion.","options":[{"id":"v1e3afa36513b","label":"The work still outstanding."},{"id":"v09ca767124e2","label":"A claim that nobody worked."},{"id":"v52fd1658e770","label":"A guarantee of complete accuracy forever."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1e3afa36513b"},"reference_answer":"v1e3afa36513b","incorrect_answer":"v09ca767124e2","explanation":"Остаток работы был указан отдельно."},{"id":"e065ee70-43ec-56c6-be5c-36aee15712b6","lesson_id":"9cb798a6-690c-5e83-aff9-6076376e3289","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Различи длительность и завершённость.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does spending an hour on a task prove it is finished?"}],"options":[{"id":"v9cfa2c078907","label":"Yes, every hour completes every task."},{"id":"v408fe7444a83","label":"Yes, spend means finish completely."},{"id":"v8f4ff2a57691","label":"No, completion needs separate information."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8f4ff2a57691"},"reference_answer":"v8f4ff2a57691","incorrect_answer":"v9cfa2c078907","explanation":"Spend сообщает о затраченном времени."},{"id":"758e5df3-662c-53cd-a780-b5a38e93b906","lesson_id":"9cb798a6-690c-5e83-aff9-6076376e3289","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Work that is not finished yet is ___.","options":[{"id":"vd4dafe93cf30","label":"irrelevant necessarily"},{"id":"vb707f45827d6","label":"remaining"},{"id":"vb6aae25816ac","label":"completed necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb707f45827d6"},"reference_answer":"vb707f45827d6","incorrect_answer":"vb6aae25816ac","explanation":"Remaining — оставшийся."},{"id":"c8c09b33-610b-576b-ad9c-4661802eac5b","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: I was about ___ leave when the phone rang.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v3c3ae9f71db4","label":"to"},{"id":"vbb4227643ad5","label":"for"},{"id":"v3b01bd6955cf","label":"of"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v3c3ae9f71db4"},"reference_answer":"v3c3ae9f71db4","incorrect_answer":"vbb4227643ad5","explanation":"Be about to требует инфинитив с to."},{"id":"617e58d2-77dc-5c21-afa1-6850f4badf67","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: begin / begun.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The show is about to ___."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["begin"]},"reference_answer":"begin","incorrect_answer":"begun","explanation":"После to нужен инфинитив begin."},{"id":"ba1a447a-0e0c-53ee-883f-acdebf98f806","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Она собиралась вот-вот уйти, когда зазвонил телефон.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"about"},{"id":"t4","label":"to"},{"id":"t5","label":"leave"},{"id":"t6","label":"when"},{"id":"t7","label":"the"},{"id":"t8","label":"phone"},{"id":"t9","label":"rang."},{"id":"t1","label":"She"},{"id":"t2","label":"was"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t9","t1"],"explanation":"Фраза помещает звонок в момент перед ожидаемым уходом."},{"id":"78ad5064-4ec3-5342-9e95-a261a0c10c3c","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The train is about leaving."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["The train is about to leave."]},"reference_answer":"The train is about to leave.","incorrect_answer":"The train is about leaving.","explanation":"Для значения ближайшего действия нужна модель about to leave."},{"id":"348ebbd7-8d59-52cd-95aa-fac0ea22e1b8","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что прервало закрытие?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The caretaker was about to lock the hall when a volunteer noticed a bag under a chair. They paused to find its owner, who returned a few minutes later. A brief incident report said the hall had already been locked before the discovery. The caretaker corrected the sequence. Preparations to close were under way, but the final action had been interrupted. The eventual closure happened only after the bag was collected.","options":[{"id":"ve8e4975f2968","label":"A completed closure before anyone noticed the bag."},{"id":"v6b694019fc8c","label":"The cancellation of every future event."},{"id":"v1ac2844dd756","label":"The discovery of a bag."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v1ac2844dd756"},"reference_answer":"v1ac2844dd756","incorrect_answer":"ve8e4975f2968","explanation":"Сумку заметили до окончательного закрытия."},{"id":"b399ce94-a8b4-55c4-9fd9-5cfe87ee8696","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"lc5c7b4ea85ea","label":"imminent"},{"id":"l2e800b7e60e1","label":"interruption"},{"id":"l36d0c136b63f","label":"departure"},{"id":"la8aa56ff15b2","label":"preparation"}],"right":[{"id":"r51a1e0be252a","label":"уход или отправление"},{"id":"r00fc5ce17bb7","label":"подготовка"},{"id":"rcf78d4ad1f40","label":"ожидаемый в ближайшее время"},{"id":"ref19b984103b","label":"прерывание"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"lc5c7b4ea85ea":"rcf78d4ad1f40","l2e800b7e60e1":"ref19b984103b","l36d0c136b63f":"r51a1e0be252a","la8aa56ff15b2":"r00fc5ce17bb7"}},"reference_answer":{"lc5c7b4ea85ea":"rcf78d4ad1f40","l2e800b7e60e1":"ref19b984103b","l36d0c136b63f":"r51a1e0be252a","la8aa56ff15b2":"r00fc5ce17bb7"},"incorrect_answer":{"lc5c7b4ea85ea":"ref19b984103b","l2e800b7e60e1":"rcf78d4ad1f40","l36d0c136b63f":"r51a1e0be252a","la8aa56ff15b2":"r00fc5ce17bb7"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: imminent — ожидаемый в ближайшее время; interruption — прерывание; departure — уход или отправление; preparation — подготовка."},{"id":"b67d79c5-d8d9-5f0a-a6cc-fb4581ad98af","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"reading","prompt":"Когда зал в итоге закрыли?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The caretaker was about to lock the hall when a volunteer noticed a bag under a chair. They paused to find its owner, who returned a few minutes later. A brief incident report said the hall had already been locked before the discovery. The caretaker corrected the sequence. Preparations to close were under way, but the final action had been interrupted. The eventual closure happened only after the bag was collected.","options":[{"id":"v7aafc98ed32b","label":"After the owner collected the bag."},{"id":"v6c44d03cce44","label":"Before the bag was discovered."},{"id":"v616385087295","label":"The text says it never closed again."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v7aafc98ed32b"},"reference_answer":"v7aafc98ed32b","incorrect_answer":"v6c44d03cce44","explanation":"Окончательное закрытие произошло после передачи сумки."},{"id":"23b0a94d-3875-5c5b-b831-b386bb9a8b45","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани временную последовательность.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does “was about to lock” prove the door was already locked?"}],"options":[{"id":"v6a11ef5532fb","label":"Yes, about to always means already completed."},{"id":"v35acb38e6ea2","label":"Yes, it removes all later events."},{"id":"v2c7cc17a4563","label":"No, it describes an imminent action that may be interrupted."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v2c7cc17a4563"},"reference_answer":"v2c7cc17a4563","incorrect_answer":"v6a11ef5532fb","explanation":"Ожидаемое действие и выполненное действие различаются."},{"id":"69aad70e-0637-565f-9470-5ad1cbaa2b86","lesson_id":"8ce7c056-17c3-5c05-b3c9-8d247670c0ac","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Something expected very soon is ___.","options":[{"id":"vae624bd31dd7","label":"historical only"},{"id":"vebda21646aaa","label":"imminent"},{"id":"v389d8aa0cc5e","label":"completed necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vebda21646aaa"},"reference_answer":"vebda21646aaa","incorrect_answer":"v389d8aa0cc5e","explanation":"Imminent — ожидаемый совсем скоро."},{"id":"604e8dac-fa21-57d8-9544-e152afcfca74","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: Choose the past-form pattern: It is time we ___ home.","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v027c16042aab","label":"went"},{"id":"v52e144370c8e","label":"goes"},{"id":"v2e95f1504cb6","label":"going"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v027c16042aab"},"reference_answer":"v027c16042aab","incorrect_answer":"v52e144370c8e","explanation":"В заданной модели после we нужна прошедшая форма went."},{"id":"6c2b6ed6-2b6c-5520-98db-21de2d6e83f1","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: takes / took.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"It is time she ___ a break."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["took"]},"reference_answer":"took","incorrect_answer":"takes","explanation":"С отдельным подлежащим she здесь используется took."},{"id":"e69cad9e-17e2-5977-b12a-36b4782606af","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Нам пора уходить.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"time"},{"id":"t4","label":"we"},{"id":"t5","label":"left."},{"id":"t1","label":"It"},{"id":"t2","label":"is"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t1"],"explanation":"Форма left не утверждает, что уход уже произошёл."},{"id":"43031559-2685-53a2-a15c-0262486a33d8","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"It is time we leaving."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["It is time we left."]},"reference_answer":"It is time we left.","incorrect_answer":"It is time we leaving.","explanation":"Для заданной модели нужна форма left, не leaving."},{"id":"a9d79cc0-ea1f-5e26-913b-a2691596bb64","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что Лео сделал своей репликой?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a long planning meeting, Leo said it was time they took a break. A colleague reading the minutes later assumed the phrase recorded a break that had already happened. The chair explained that Leo had been making a suggestion about what should happen next. The group actually continued for another ten minutes before stopping. The revised minutes separated the suggestion from the later action, preserving the difference between grammatical past form and the timing of the event.","options":[{"id":"v175f9860b401","label":"Confirmed a break that was already over."},{"id":"v41fdbb010819","label":"Cancelled every break for the day."},{"id":"ve648082a2bfd","label":"Suggested that they take a break next."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve648082a2bfd"},"reference_answer":"ve648082a2bfd","incorrect_answer":"v175f9860b401","explanation":"Реплика предлагала действие, а не фиксировала его выполнение."},{"id":"c3f6e163-1b8f-5b90-af18-e693ca35d9a3","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l7c9cceeaae4a","label":"overdue"},{"id":"l8e77a1290bcf","label":"urgency"},{"id":"la29222ac8a66","label":"suggestion"},{"id":"l62debf68a82b","label":"departure"}],"right":[{"id":"r756e41aeb87d","label":"предложение"},{"id":"r74f63c308b73","label":"отправление"},{"id":"rc83dcee93762","label":"давно ожидаемый"},{"id":"r78d4cbbd9862","label":"срочность"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l7c9cceeaae4a":"rc83dcee93762","l8e77a1290bcf":"r78d4cbbd9862","la29222ac8a66":"r756e41aeb87d","l62debf68a82b":"r74f63c308b73"}},"reference_answer":{"l7c9cceeaae4a":"rc83dcee93762","l8e77a1290bcf":"r78d4cbbd9862","la29222ac8a66":"r756e41aeb87d","l62debf68a82b":"r74f63c308b73"},"incorrect_answer":{"l7c9cceeaae4a":"r78d4cbbd9862","l8e77a1290bcf":"rc83dcee93762","la29222ac8a66":"r756e41aeb87d","l62debf68a82b":"r74f63c308b73"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: overdue — давно ожидаемый; urgency — срочность; suggestion — предложение; departure — отправление."},{"id":"28aa1af9-4425-5c7b-a1a7-300cb60127b1","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"reading","prompt":"Когда группа остановилась?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"During a long planning meeting, Leo said it was time they took a break. A colleague reading the minutes later assumed the phrase recorded a break that had already happened. The chair explained that Leo had been making a suggestion about what should happen next. The group actually continued for another ten minutes before stopping. The revised minutes separated the suggestion from the later action, preserving the difference between grammatical past form and the timing of the event.","options":[{"id":"v0caafb6d2363","label":"Ten minutes after the suggestion."},{"id":"v6165a9881310","label":"Before Leo spoke."},{"id":"v2ce89966710b","label":"At no point according to the text."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v0caafb6d2363"},"reference_answer":"v0caafb6d2363","incorrect_answer":"v6165a9881310","explanation":"В тексте указано продолжение на десять минут."},{"id":"85e3d198-affb-5840-9ed1-29bf6e1f170b","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Учитывай указанную грамматическую модель.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"In “It is time we left”, has departure necessarily happened?"}],"options":[{"id":"v46aeb60e5d1e","label":"Yes, left always records a completed departure here."},{"id":"vc1c4feca5782","label":"Yes, the phrase is a travel receipt."},{"id":"v70d746938e28","label":"No, the past form expresses a present need for action."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v70d746938e28"},"reference_answer":"v70d746938e28","incorrect_answer":"v46aeb60e5d1e","explanation":"Форма прошлого не определяет фактическое время действия без контекста."},{"id":"c406b7fc-0dee-57ce-ae2b-805b2f406edf","lesson_id":"5f4a0f57-e139-55aa-a4f7-1228a866eccf","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"A proposal about what people should do is a ___.","options":[{"id":"v6882432c1f24","label":"record of departure necessarily"},{"id":"v99763d56683f","label":"suggestion"},{"id":"vf9fa53356d53","label":"proof of completion"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v99763d56683f"},"reference_answer":"v99763d56683f","incorrect_answer":"vf9fa53356d53","explanation":"Suggestion — предложение действия."},{"id":"d6cf6b1a-6c75-5d46-a7c8-d2d952066cc1","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “All but two members agreed.” Which meaning is accurate?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"v74f97595b631","label":"Every member except two agreed."},{"id":"v203b495f48ec","label":"Exactly two members agreed."},{"id":"v35f72e1f5f93","label":"Every member agreed without exception."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v74f97595b631"},"reference_answer":"v74f97595b631","incorrect_answer":"v203b495f48ec","explanation":"После all but названо числовое исключение."},{"id":"3477a84b-b72e-5b1c-b016-38e4010920cb","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: but / than.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"The work is all ___ complete: only one label remains."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["but"]},"reference_answer":"but","incorrect_answer":"than","explanation":"All but complete означает почти завершён."},{"id":"c4f13b97-b7e1-55e2-8d63-0ecdd27ee099","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Все участники, кроме двоих, согласились.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"two"},{"id":"t4","label":"members"},{"id":"t5","label":"agreed."},{"id":"t1","label":"All"},{"id":"t2","label":"but"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t1"],"explanation":"Оговорка исключает двоих из согласившихся."},{"id":"1acb1b4d-d3a8-5780-9d8b-194278543a5a","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"All but two members agrees."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["All but two members agree."]},"reference_answer":"All but two members agree.","incorrect_answer":"All but two members agrees.","explanation":"Множественное members требует agree."},{"id":"d717506b-9605-5b3d-9c99-99760794ae2e","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"reading","prompt":"Сколько участников исключено из поддержавших?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"The draft minutes stated that all but two members supported the new timetable. A summary converted this into unanimous support, while another reader assumed that only two members had supported it. Both readings changed the numerical exception. The same minutes described the room preparation as all but complete, with one label still to be installed. There, the phrase marked near completion rather than an exception involving two people. The secretary retained both statements and added clearer paraphrases. Accurate interpretation depended on the structure surrounding all but, not a single replacement meaning that could be applied mechanically to every occurrence.","options":[{"id":"v1777c37a2759","label":"None."},{"id":"v402088a6093f","label":"All except exactly two supporters."},{"id":"vb5654ba4b0eb","label":"Two."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vb5654ba4b0eb"},"reference_answer":"vb5654ba4b0eb","incorrect_answer":"v1777c37a2759","explanation":"All but two означает всех за исключением двоих."},{"id":"2773c969-d3c9-5972-9757-8e8a6d8cfae1","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l99d317dd1d28","label":"exception"},{"id":"lc2a7414f60b1","label":"nearly"},{"id":"l2efc13f47053","label":"unanimous"},{"id":"ldd35314d57c7","label":"outstanding"}],"right":[{"id":"rcb360536638e","label":"единогласный"},{"id":"rc425a54eb833","label":"ещё не выполненный"},{"id":"rcf6f06a997e2","label":"исключение"},{"id":"r47ff3b5de3dd","label":"почти"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l99d317dd1d28":"rcf6f06a997e2","lc2a7414f60b1":"r47ff3b5de3dd","l2efc13f47053":"rcb360536638e","ldd35314d57c7":"rc425a54eb833"}},"reference_answer":{"l99d317dd1d28":"rcf6f06a997e2","lc2a7414f60b1":"r47ff3b5de3dd","l2efc13f47053":"rcb360536638e","ldd35314d57c7":"rc425a54eb833"},"incorrect_answer":{"l99d317dd1d28":"r47ff3b5de3dd","lc2a7414f60b1":"rcf6f06a997e2","l2efc13f47053":"rcb360536638e","ldd35314d57c7":"rc425a54eb833"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: exception — исключение; nearly — почти; unanimous — единогласный; outstanding — ещё не выполненный."},{"id":"fc30d3a5-7a29-5d9f-9aa8-6db233c908e5","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"reading","prompt":"Почему подготовка была all but complete?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"The draft minutes stated that all but two members supported the new timetable. A summary converted this into unanimous support, while another reader assumed that only two members had supported it. Both readings changed the numerical exception. The same minutes described the room preparation as all but complete, with one label still to be installed. There, the phrase marked near completion rather than an exception involving two people. The secretary retained both statements and added clearer paraphrases. Accurate interpretation depended on the structure surrounding all but, not a single replacement meaning that could be applied mechanically to every occurrence.","options":[{"id":"v31a3ea26274d","label":"One label still remained to be installed."},{"id":"v3fcfa3dee8a1","label":"Exactly two members had opposed the room."},{"id":"v0296bfde667e","label":"No preparation had begun."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v31a3ea26274d"},"reference_answer":"v31a3ea26274d","incorrect_answer":"v3fcfa3dee8a1","explanation":"Во втором употреблении описана почти завершённая работа."},{"id":"5e3a2c8f-17b2-5ac7-9aab-1f01bb815059","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Проверь грамматическое окружение.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Can all but always be replaced with except?"}],"options":[{"id":"v9ab486b83381","label":"Yes, regardless of structure."},{"id":"vecf7e94535d2","label":"Yes, complete is always a number."},{"id":"v140e3993a7df","label":"No, all but complete has the meaning nearly complete."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v140e3993a7df"},"reference_answer":"v140e3993a7df","incorrect_answer":"v9ab486b83381","explanation":"Одна замена не покрывает оба употребления."},{"id":"882f14dd-9df3-5699-9434-5d7814411645","lesson_id":"eaa3f994-f7f5-55bd-9ee8-360519f0c6f1","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"Agreement by every member without exception is ___.","options":[{"id":"veb2aa6fff85c","label":"outstanding"},{"id":"v50bb916b84e4","label":"unanimous"},{"id":"v8004c4c5651e","label":"nearly complete"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v50bb916b84e4"},"reference_answer":"v50bb916b84e4","incorrect_answer":"v8004c4c5651e","explanation":"Unanimous — единогласный."},{"id":"864a34ad-af2e-5622-8f9a-6c649c3bc685","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"single_choice","prompt":"Выбери точный вариант: “It is not faster; if anything, it is slightly slower.” What is the correction?","position":1,"public_payload":{"options":[{"id":"ve5bfc76db7a4","label":"The tendency is towards being slower, not faster."},{"id":"v02c7cc9962e2","label":"It is certainly much faster."},{"id":"v2de7d70f475a","label":"There can be no comparison of any kind."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"ve5bfc76db7a4"},"reference_answer":"ve5bfc76db7a4","incorrect_answer":"v02c7cc9962e2","explanation":"Оборот поправляет направление, а slightly ограничивает величину."},{"id":"0cb3f300-e03a-5d31-95c2-5e388086506f","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"gap","prompt":"Вставь слово из пары: nothing of / anything.","position":2,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If ___, the revised process is slightly slower."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["anything"]},"reference_answer":"anything","incorrect_answer":"nothing of","explanation":"Устойчивый вводный оборот — if anything."},{"id":"ca0edf3c-6896-504d-b357-dc12c4ae712d","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"sentence","prompt":"Собери предложение: «Если уж на то пошло, изменённый процесс немного медленнее.»","position":3,"public_payload":{"tokens":[{"id":"t3","label":"the"},{"id":"t4","label":"revised"},{"id":"t5","label":"process"},{"id":"t6","label":"is"},{"id":"t7","label":"slightly"},{"id":"t8","label":"slower."},{"id":"t1","label":"If"},{"id":"t2","label":"anything,"}]},"answer_key":{"value":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"]},"reference_answer":["t1","t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8"],"incorrect_answer":["t2","t3","t4","t5","t6","t7","t8","t1"],"explanation":"Сохраняется осторожная небольшая поправка."},{"id":"71196cba-b5cb-5119-8643-b037265e3c33","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"correction","prompt":"Исправь ошибку в указанной конструкции, сохраняя остальные слова и смысл.","position":4,"public_payload":{"sentence":"If anything, the revised process are slightly slower."},"answer_key":{"accepted":["If anything, the revised process is slightly slower."]},"reference_answer":"If anything, the revised process is slightly slower.","incorrect_answer":"If anything, the revised process are slightly slower.","explanation":"С единственным process требуется is."},{"id":"eeabe6a5-4371-5adc-8605-2fabe33b8973","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"reading","prompt":"Какой вывод поддерживала формулировка координатора?","position":5,"public_payload":{"passage":"A team expected a revised filing process to save time. After a small trial, the coordinator wrote that it was not faster and, if anything, was slightly slower. A later headline called the trial proof of a dramatic collapse in efficiency. The coordinator objected to the scale and certainty of that claim. Her wording offered a modest correction to the expected direction, based on a limited trial. It neither supported the original promise of improvement nor established a large effect across every future setting. She recommended a larger comparison before deciding whether the procedure should be retained or changed again.","options":[{"id":"v1e7b51479f71","label":"A dramatic collapse proved in every setting."},{"id":"v7a659e2d723e","label":"A confirmed substantial speed improvement."},{"id":"vc7618575c1b8","label":"A limited tendency towards slightly slower work in the trial."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc7618575c1b8"},"reference_answer":"vc7618575c1b8","incorrect_answer":"v1e7b51479f71","explanation":"Slightly и малый пробный запуск ограничивают силу оценки."},{"id":"0355ef11-a35c-5b3d-8367-05a111998eda","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"matching","prompt":"Соедини слова с переводом в контексте урока.","position":6,"public_payload":{"left":[{"id":"l16ee89026fe7","label":"qualification"},{"id":"labfad093375f","label":"tendency"},{"id":"l684dce5cd559","label":"revision"},{"id":"l74459ff02d97","label":"modest"}],"right":[{"id":"re30ec49179ab","label":"пересмотр"},{"id":"r0e5e80994833","label":"небольшой по масштабу"},{"id":"rabce5d3284b2","label":"оговорка"},{"id":"r7d9a8e1eb100","label":"тенденция"}]},"answer_key":{"pairs":{"l16ee89026fe7":"rabce5d3284b2","labfad093375f":"r7d9a8e1eb100","l684dce5cd559":"re30ec49179ab","l74459ff02d97":"r0e5e80994833"}},"reference_answer":{"l16ee89026fe7":"rabce5d3284b2","labfad093375f":"r7d9a8e1eb100","l684dce5cd559":"re30ec49179ab","l74459ff02d97":"r0e5e80994833"},"incorrect_answer":{"l16ee89026fe7":"r7d9a8e1eb100","labfad093375f":"rabce5d3284b2","l684dce5cd559":"re30ec49179ab","l74459ff02d97":"r0e5e80994833"},"explanation":"В этих контекстах: qualification — оговорка; tendency — тенденция; revision — пересмотр; modest — небольшой по масштабу."},{"id":"15121cf7-83f1-50c7-a4ca-2b7dea0d750a","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"reading","prompt":"Что она предложила перед окончательным решением?","position":7,"public_payload":{"passage":"A team expected a revised filing process to save time. After a small trial, the coordinator wrote that it was not faster and, if anything, was slightly slower. A later headline called the trial proof of a dramatic collapse in efficiency. The coordinator objected to the scale and certainty of that claim. Her wording offered a modest correction to the expected direction, based on a limited trial. It neither supported the original promise of improvement nor established a large effect across every future setting. She recommended a larger comparison before deciding whether the procedure should be retained or changed again.","options":[{"id":"vc15aef705e14","label":"A larger comparison."},{"id":"vdc19ee440c0c","label":"Ignoring all observations."},{"id":"vd589a983281f","label":"Claiming a universal result immediately."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vc15aef705e14"},"reference_answer":"vc15aef705e14","incorrect_answer":"vdc19ee440c0c","explanation":"Для решения нужны более широкие сопоставимые данные."},{"id":"f77c20dc-0188-538e-850a-6e6831e2f722","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"dialogue","prompt":"Сохрани размер и уверенность оценки.","position":8,"public_payload":{"lines":[{"speaker":"Собеседник","text":"Does if anything justify replacing slightly with dramatically?"}],"options":[{"id":"v1f1506d9d9b9","label":"Yes, the phrase always intensifies every adjective."},{"id":"v40b65af1ae83","label":"Yes, modest trials prove universal effects."},{"id":"v8efd389bcb22","label":"No, that would strengthen the claim beyond its wording."}]},"answer_key":{"value":"v8efd389bcb22"},"reference_answer":"v8efd389bcb22","incorrect_answer":"v1f1506d9d9b9","explanation":"Вводный оборот не отменяет ограничение slightly."},{"id":"fdec3d0c-7538-561b-88cf-8aec0541e782","lesson_id":"7f1ef112-cb7e-5e33-9b77-a11754e9be93","kind":"context_choice","prompt":"Выбери слово по смыслу контекста.","position":9,"public_payload":{"sentence":"An effect described as small in scale is ___.","options":[{"id":"vf61c391fc4f5","label":"universal necessarily"},{"id":"vfe5ff649c13b","label":"modest"},{"id":"vd6556db572eb","label":"dramatic necessarily"}]},"answer_key":{"value":"vfe5ff649c13b"},"reference_answer":"vfe5ff649c13b","incorrect_answer":"vd6556db572eb","explanation":"Modest — небольшой по масштабу."},{"id":"b9a5023d-fb01-5dc3-9b